INSERT INTO `comments` VALUES (1,1,3,'Do any of the lights work at all? Are both of the FCMs doing the same thing?',1449171720),(2,1,17,'No lights at all on the first FCM, the second FCM is working as it is supposed to.',1449171769),(3,1,3,'Can you power off the FCM and leave it off for 10 seconds. Then plug it back in and turn it on. Check if the lights work.',1449171840),(4,1,17,'Powered off the FCM for about 30 seconds, but the results are the same. No LEDs on.',1449171883),(5,1,3,'It seems that the FCM hardware is not functioning properly, we will ship a replacement to Lincoln SKF and they will coordinate with the installers and replace the hardware.',1449172110),(6,1,3,'The hardware has been shipped to Lincoln via UPS. The tracking number is :1Z5S56516S1S651',1449172174),(7,1,7,'Awaiting arrival of Hardware',1449172186),(8,1,7,'Hardware has arrived: Install is scheduled for December 5th, 2015',1449172196),(9,1,17,'This will work for the shop',1449173285),(10,1,17,'Everything is working perfect now. Thank you',1449173349),(11,2,19,'Can you dispense oil?',1449604244),(12,2,21,'Yes ',1449605013),(13,2,19,'Can you find a small black wire coming from back of the display and fallow it and see if it is plugged into an outlet?',1449668222),(14,2,21,'That was it, plugged it in. Everything is working',1450102677),(15,4,2,'Confirmed this issue, we will work on it',1456320712),(16,5,2,'Confirmed this is an issue, we will work on it.',1456320748),(17,6,2,'Confirmed issue, we will work on it.\n',1456320828),(18,7,2,'We will improve the placement of logo and give details on specifications',1456320926),(19,9,2,'Confirmed this, we will take care of it',1456321128),(20,4,2,'Issue has been resolved on our end and will be released with the next testing version \"LQD_T_2_16\"',1456826512),(21,5,2,'Issue has been resolved on our end and will be released with the next testing version \"LQD_T_2_16\"',1456826615),(22,7,2,'Issue has been resolved on our end and will be released with the next testing version \"LQD_T_2_16\"',1456826661),(23,8,2,'Working on this',1456827184),(24,10,2,'This is being worked on',1456827423),(25,10,2,'Issue has been resolved on our end and will be released with the next testing version \"LQD_T_2_16\"',1456827620),(26,11,2,'This has been resolved',1456827897),(27,8,1,'Issue has been resolved on our end and will be released with the next testing version \"LQD_T_2_16\"',1456839647),(28,9,1,'Issue has been resolved on our end and will be released with the next testing version \"LQD_T_2_16\"',1456839693),(29,3,2,'This was completed, can see in LQD_R_2_17',1459541616),(30,17,2,'This has been fixed.',1460381635),(31,6,2,'Completed',1460383392),(32,21,20,'\nOK i will send you a new seal',1460555595),(33,21,21,'Thank you!!',1460555655),(34,20,2,'I believe this issue has been resolved. I have been able to connect systems to oilcopsupport.com. please confirm',1460744372),(35,26,2,'Yes, if they are on version LQD_R_2_18 or later',1464426723),(36,23,2,'On version LQD_R_2_18 and with the latest firmware you should no longer have any issues with Reels locking up and just in case there is an off chance it may happen there is also a reset reel button',1464227477),(37,25,2,'Currently it is not something that can be done in a simple manner, this may be released in a future release.',1469498459),(38,22,2,'This issue has been resolved in the latest version, LQD_R_2_18',1464229477),(39,15,1,'User Error. ',1470235647),(40,19,1,'Resolved. ',1470235673),(41,26,1,'Resolved. ',1470235997),(42,27,138,'The Demo Manager is setup with Demo1-Demo5 ready to simulate, and initial setup required for Demo6-Demo10.\n\nTo verify that there is not an issue with the system, which Demo system was you having difficultly getting to work?',1472484516),(43,27,138,'Just checking up to see if you are still having the same issue, or if this has been resolved to your satisfaction.',1473195587),(44,29,1,'We are looking into this issue again. this problem was fixed on the old yellow controllers. If the new software is downloaded to the old yellow controllers, then the time is working fine. Somehow there is a difference in old and new controller. The new controller is still showing the 1 hour difference. Since this issue was already fixed before, it should be some kind of a file mismatch. We are looking into this issue right away and will resolve it as soon as possible and update you here. ',1473264670),(45,28,1,'I contacted Andrea this morning and was able to update the controller to a Test version. This has been taken care of at 7 this morning.',1473265468),(46,31,6,'Kevin @Liquidynamics test',1473346541),(47,30,138,'We are currently researching on what is causing the FCMs to drop communications. We are currently looking at all possibilities. One possibility is an error within the routing of the signal. \n\nThere is a way to monitor the signal strength it will take time to implement that in the current version of software.\n',1473348600),(48,32,138,'This is a test discrepancy.',1473690998),(49,33,1,'----testing comment -----',1473776192),(50,33,1,'test again with notification user change',1473777839),(51,29,138,'This particular issue with the system time moving forward by one hour has been resolved in version LQD_T_2_25. All other time related errors will be resolved in the next software update.',1473880685),(52,30,138,'This issue with the signal dropping has been resolved with a combination of a software and firmware fix. Please update to software LQD_T_2_25 and the newest firmware for the FCM, Tank Monitor, and TAC . Please update and confirm that this has resolved the issue.',1473880945),(53,34,62,'We are looking into this. Could you please tell us what software and firmware version you are using. Thanks. ',1475098169),(54,34,138,'We have found and was able to correct this issue. The fix will be in the next Test Release that is scheduled for released on Sept 30, 2016.',1475241651),(55,35,1,'Testing commenting mail  - \"add link to comment email as well\"',1475320011),(56,35,1,'yes.... update done. Once please check the emails . ',1475320054),(57,36,2,'Hello Sebastien, There is a newer test version released. LQD_T_2_26. Updating may resolve this issue, we are looking into this and will get back to you shortly.',1476180286),(58,37,2,'Hello Sebastien, There is a newer test version released. LQD_T_2_26. Updating may resolve this issue, we are looking into this and will get back to you shortly.',1476180294),(59,37,80,'Hello Angel\nI am test version T_26 now small improvement! (no communication ERROR!)\n,but it shall not work Like this\nLet me explain. We are Mutli produced by W/O\nI make a transaction on the Station 1 Product # 1 Reel No. 1 and leaves open my OR.\n\nI want to resume a transaction with the product # 2. it do not work\n\nIt puts me systematically on Station 1 product and 1 reel\n\nAlso from PC it\'s work you can choose your station your product and your reel\n\nI think it is a firmware problem TAC\n\nRegards\n\nSébastien',1476191115),(60,38,2,'When the technician is trying to close the work order, is this on the TAC or the web? Also what is the error code you are receiving? ',1476191203),(61,37,2,'Is the work order being created on the web or the TAC? Also are you doing an open dispense amount or preset? You also mentioned you have Multi product ON, do you have Multi dispense ON as well?',1476191669),(62,36,80,'Hello Angel\n\nConcerning Load Job Recepies. I think it work, but I think it will take for the reports to the sum of jobs by products. I prepare a report\n\nThanks\n\nSébastien\n',1476191761),(63,37,80,'W/O created on the TAC and open on preset\n\nMulti product ON\nMulti dispense ON\n\nit works well with version R_17\n\nSébastien',1476192029),(64,38,80,'Angel\nThe work order is on the TAC\nthe manager tried to open it but it did not work. he removed the W / o\nthe technician tried to connect to the TAC and the technician code no longer worked\nThe manager removed the technician and to recreate this to work there and it can connect',1476193594),(65,37,138,'The issue was with the software and we will be releasing an update soon so that the TAC load work order logic will match the website load work order logic.',1476265231),(66,39,138,'Will release a fix to the way W/O Opened Today & Closed Today are tallied in the system in the next T update along with other fixes.',1477425369),(67,40,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found. Please attach to Oilcop Support any relevant documentation on this particular error.',1479218439),(68,41,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found. Please attach to Oilcop Support any relevant documentation on this particular error.',1479218461),(69,42,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found. Please attach to Oilcop Support any relevant documentation on this particular error.',1479218475),(70,43,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found. Please attach to Oilcop Support any relevant documentation on this particular error.',1479218488),(71,44,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found. Please attach to Oilcop Support any relevant documentation on this particular error.',1479218502),(72,45,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found. Please attach to Oilcop Support any relevant documentation on this particular error.',1479218516),(73,46,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found. Please attach to Oilcop Support any relevant documentation on this particular error.',1479218532),(74,46,81,'FULL DISCREPANCY TITLE\npossibility to select a station even if the product set by manager is not available in that station',1479218930),(75,42,81,'FULL DISCREPANCY TITLE\nno open WO mentioned in \"WO status\" and \"summary report - normal view\"',1479218999),(76,41,81,'FULL TITLE:\npreset quantity exceeds \"max product dispense per WO\"',1479219381),(77,46,81,'(description continuing...)\ndispense.\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.2.2, §1.1.2.5, §1.1.5, §1.2.4.2, §1.2.4.3, §1.2.4.9, §1.2.4.11\nsee also \"dispensing procedure test\" report\'s notes #1, #2 and #3',1479219791),(78,49,81,'FULL TITLE:\nautomatic switch to first product of the selected station when the set product is not available',1479219955),(79,49,81,'FURTHER COMMENTS/NOTES:\n1) From my tests, because of the system configuration I created, I could only check that system was automatically selecting product #1 (in products loading, admin configuration). But with Sébastien we checked a different configuration, where product #1 was not present in all stations (like in my configuration). We found out that system is automatically selecting the first product/reel of the station, not caring of the products list and order.\n2) remind that the manager created the WO in the system with some details like product and preset, but the user could have simply been told to go and dispense WO#xxxx, without knowing which kind of product he have to dispense..so he can select any of the stations he finds in the list, and he does not know/care if the product the system shows is different from the one selected by manager',1479219971),(80,49,81,' check \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.2.2, §1.1.2.5, §1.1.4.2, §1.1.4.5, §1.1.5, §1.2.4.2, §1.2.4.3, §1.2.4.4, §1.2.4.10',1479220155),(81,40,138,'Can you please confirm the Administrative settings for: Auto Close Work Order, Multiple Products per Work Order, & Multiple Dispense.  Along with the WO Management settings for: Lock Dispense Amount & Preset Amount.',1479220837),(82,41,138,'Can you please confirm the Administrative settings for: Auto Close Work Order, Multiple Products per Work Order, & Multiple Dispense.  Along with the WO Management settings for: Lock Dispense Amount & Preset Amount.',1479220958),(83,49,81,'see pictures TAC - TA1-005 - correct windscreen but open dispense: this is the screen if I select the correct station where the preset product (windscreen) is available',1479221429),(84,49,81,'see picture TAC - TA1-005 - automatic switch to 10W40: this is if I select a different station',1479221457),(85,40,81,'all of the discrepancies I\'ve added and that I\'m going to add soon have been found with the following configuration:\n   \ntop-off ==> OFF   \nauto close ==> OFF   \nmultiple products ==> OFF   \nmultiple dispense ==> OFF   \n   \nlock dispense amount ==> left on default ON\n   \nwhen specified, scenario 1 is with preset specified and scenario 2 is with preset blank (open dispense)   \nall specific values for presets are specified in the pdf document that I will send at the end (I\'m adding all discrepancies to oilcopsupport, so that I have their numbers and I can put all of them into the document for easy reference)',1479222808),(86,46,138,'Is it possible to get a photo of the error and a copy of reports §1.1.2.2, §1.1.2.5, §1.1.5, §1.2.4.2, §1.2.4.3, §1.2.4.9, §1.2.4.11',1479222886),(87,40,81,'system configuration on pdf attached',1479222936),(88,41,81,'check discrepancy #40',1479222955),(89,46,81,'the picture of the error is impossible: check the attached picture, you have the full list of stations to select...but it does not mention the WO# or the product..',1479223133),(90,46,81,'all reports will be available on pdf full report once finisched the loading of the discrepancies and having updated consequently the number of the discrepancy in each paragraph',1479223216),(91,47,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479223827),(92,50,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479223861),(93,46,138,'Can you verify what version of Firmware you are using on the TAC? You can check by power cycling the TAC or pressing Stop at the sign in screen.',1479226096),(94,48,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479226138),(95,50,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479226189),(96,49,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479226208),(97,51,2,'Andrea,\nWe are currently working on a way to allow distributors to have distributors underneath them, after this is implemented you will no longer have issues with this. Currently we cannot have one email set up with multiple accounts. I can for now change the email that is on the gartec/gitec account but need to know what email to use.',1479230496),(98,51,81,'Hi Angel, please use a.simonetto@gartec.it\n\nand switch on Gartec account from this email to tecnico@gartec.it if possible',1479281478),(99,46,81,'it\'s 1.3, all the devices have the last firmware that have been sent to us for testing purpose',1479281601),(100,52,81,'FULL TITLE:\nuser can select a WO that he should not be able to see',1479282972),(101,54,81,'CORRECT TITLE: WO automatically assigned to user/station',1479289553),(102,58,81,'in order to select a product, I had to change station value to \"all stations\", then again to a specific station and then the product dropdown menu returned to work properly - see picture (2)',1479295694),(103,52,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479308687),(104,53,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479309025),(105,54,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479310259),(106,57,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479315040),(107,58,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479315968),(108,59,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479317133),(109,60,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479323728),(110,61,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479324781),(111,62,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479327336),(112,63,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479329215),(113,64,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1479751860),(114,65,138,'We are currently working to resolve this and will update as soon as a resolution is found.',1480343323),(115,65,27,'please I need some comments and answers by tomorrow, the customer is thinking to dismount the whole system!',1481796031),(116,66,27,'this is TOP urgent since it\'s a brand new system, where we already needed to replace a controller after one week.',1481796563),(117,66,144,'As discussed with Andrea, Angel and I will be changing Saudi\'s system controller from R_19 to R_17, since that customer has TAC v1.1 which is not compatible with R_19. We are scheduled to update December 16th, 6am CST.',1481819101),(118,65,144,'We completed the export bug fix and are testing it right now. As you mentioned in your email, the customer updated to R_19. So what we can do is release an R_20 version that applies the export fix. If that solution is okay with you, we will have the R_20 version up today before 5:00pm CST.',1481819810),(119,66,2,'The controller has been changed back to version R_17. I have also uploaded the DB that was provided by Andrea. This was completed this morning.',1481894084),(120,50,1,'Testing the Issue\ntesting in process',1484044795),(121,68,1,'Thanks for the information. It looks like one of the database additions did not update properly. I\'ll re-upload the LQD_T_2_27 to oilcopsupport with the patch right now. If you have already downloaded LQD_T_2_27, what you will need to do to get the patched version is go into winscp and navigate to /var/www/oilcop/UPDATES and delete the LQD_T_2_27.zip. Then you can go into maintenance and download/install the patched version like you normally do through oilcop\'s maintenance page.. I will switch this discrepancy to test when I have uploaded the patched LQD_T_2_27.',1484752218),(122,69,1,'This is related to discrepancy 68',1484752279),(123,68,6,'Thank you, I have uploaded two other discrepancies that may also be affected by this same issue.',1484752576),(124,70,144,'This is most likely related to discrepancy 68 as well.',1484752681),(125,68,144,'I have changed it to testing, please follow the instructions from the default admin post.\n\n-Thank you.',1484752717),(126,70,6,'I figured it was but wanted to make sure you saw these before the patch was uploaded in case there was more work needed to be done to it.',1484752886),(127,68,6,'Followed instructions and downloaded the patch. It switches to the Manager menu now but there is a red box PHP error at the top of the page. See attached \"Select User Manager 2 T_2_27\"',1484753344),(128,68,144,'Looks like there is still a database addition that did not update properly. Can I teamviewer into your system, so I can look at update logs? Then I\'ll fix any remaining database update issues, and we\'ll add one more patch.',1484754518),(129,68,6,'yes i will send you the info for teamviewer\n',1484754682),(130,68,144,'Okay, we figured it out. We will provide another patch that you can install the same way. I will update you and set this discrepancy to testing when the patch is updated.',1484756280),(131,68,6,'Thank you',1484756505),(132,68,144,'Okay, please follow instructions from the default admin post please.',1484757315),(133,69,144,'This should be fixed now.',1484757608),(134,70,144,'This was related to discrepancy 68, and should be fixed now.',1484757642),(135,66,138,'Wanted to verify that the change that were made corrected the issue the end user was have and checking to see if the issue was resolved satisfactory.',1484760514),(136,71,144,'Okay, we are investigating if the CDM file is wrong or controller. We are thinking the CDM file is acting up. Currently, re-testing it. I\'ll update a different one here and name it CDM_3_0_1 if we end up having the same issue.',1484762026),(137,71,144,'It looks like it was the CDM file. I\'ve attached the hex file here.',1484762446),(138,71,144,'Actually, I\'ll upload it in Oilcop Files/firmware and replace the old zip. It won\'t let me upload hex files here.',1484762523),(139,71,144,'Hex uploaded.',1484762571),(140,72,144,'Can you provide me the following admin options that you are using:\nMultiple Products per Work Order	\nMultiple Dispense\nEnable Work Order Config',1484850410),(141,72,6,'Multiple Products- ON, Multiple Dispense- ON, Work Order Config- OFF',1484850530),(142,72,144,'Okay, I was able to replicate it. It is happening after entering in the work order number, correct? I\'ll work on fixing it, and plan to have it out in today\'s update at 5pm cst.',1484850812),(143,72,6,'yes it was after trying to input the WO number. Will that be just Software or will this be a firmware update?\n\n',1484850942),(144,72,144,'Online software update',1484851100),(145,72,6,'this was not switched to Testing but i have tested the issue with T_2_28 and it is fixed. Am I good to close the discrepency?',1484927063),(146,72,144,'Yeah, it was meant to be under testing.',1484927838),(147,73,144,'So I\'m looking into the communication error on the dispense. Can I get an example of what the workorder configuation was and the multi dispense and mutliproduct options that were selected?\n\nCan you also elaborate on what the difference between the TAC and website were with that workorder because it sounds like they do the same thing, but the TAC just had that communication error?\n\nThank you.',1484935655),(148,73,6,'Bryan, i was testing this more and changing the different admin options to see exactly what the combination of admin options and WO settings caused what issues. There are too many variables to do this on the fly so i have a copy of the excel spreadsheet that Adam did a few months ago that test every possible WO configuration. I am going to go through all 182 of them and will upload the spread sheet here when finished. With all the configurations i  may not be able to finish it today.',1484936668),(149,73,6,'Attached is an excel spreadsheet showing the different combinations and results. All of these work orders were created on the website and then selected by a user on the TAC. I will go through repeat the same process but loading the work orders on the website instead of TAC to check if it is just a TAC problem or both. \nThe biggest issue is when a product is not assigned to the work order, that is when we get a lot of RED in the results. \nSome other issue are small but need to be addressed.\n\n1. If the product selected when creating the WO is only available at 1 station, then there should not be an option to select a station when at the TAC. This is an issue cause it allows you to pick a station, but if you pick a station that does not have the product you want then it automatically selects a product at that station that is incorrect. We either need the system to recognize the product is only available at 1 station or have an error message telling the user at the TAC that the station they have selected does not have a reel with the product that was selected when the WO was created.\n\n2. If the preset amount is left blank when creating the WO, then it automatically goes to an open dispense when the WO is selected at the TAC. This does not happen when selecting the WO from the website, there is allows the user still to set a preset if they want to. There needs to be an option for the user to select a preset at the TAC even if the WO was created without a preset value.\n\n',1485364946),(150,73,144,'Thank you Kevin. I\'ll work on getting the issues in the excel sheet resolved.',1485365480),(151,73,6,'Correction on number 2 with the preset on the website, if you Create the WO on the website and leave the preset value blank and select the WO on the website it does not allow you to set a preset. So there actually isn\'t anything wrong with this, but we need to discuss for preference if still want preset to be an option even if it is not selected when creating the WO. Discussed with Mark a little bit and he thinks that it should be an option at the TAC. So if the WO is created in the parts room but the person creating doesn\'t know how much fluid they need they can leave it blank and then the technician can set the preset at the TAC when they select the work order. Let me know how much work will be needed to make this happen. If it looks like a lot and would require software and firmware updates we made want to go another route with the issue.',1485374772),(152,73,6,'Note for the issue of the product only being available at one station but the TAC ask to pick a station- If you select the WO on the website it automatically takes you to the dispense page for the product instead of asking for a station like on the TAC. (If the product is available on more then 1 station then it ask you to select a station on the website)',1485376039),(153,73,144,'Regarding the preset, the reason why it functions how it currently does now was to reduce the number of screens or operations that the technician would need to configure. \n\nI believe we got around the scenario you described was by having that \"Lock Dispense Amount\" button. If \"Lock Dispense Amount\" button under adding a new work order is ON (which it defaults to ON), it forces the technician to do whatever is set by the manager. If the preset is blank, then it makes it an open dispense.\n\nIf \"Lock Dispense Amount\" is OFF, then it allows the technician to change the value (set a preset).',1485376773),(154,73,6,'ok thanks, i didn\'t mess with the lock dispense button, i will check it against the issue\n',1485376940),(155,73,6,'You are correct about the lock dispense button, it works correctly on the TAC and the website. After discussing with Mark we need to make that default OFF. Also how hard would it be to move the button underneath the Preset Amount input box? ',1485378935),(156,73,144,'Not an issue. We can move the button below the preset amount input box, and default it to OFF.',1485379453),(157,73,1,'The red sections in your TACOPTIONS.xlsx have been addressed with LQD_T_2_29 update.\nWe are testing the yellow sections as well as finishing up the UI changes for Lock Dispense Amount.',1485904543),(158,40,81,'tested with T_2_28, fixed',1486054379),(159,41,81,'tested with T_2_28, fixed',1486054419),(160,77,27,'when it\'s written\n\n(with Y<x?X)\n\n\"?\" digit means minor or equal...I pasted the symbol but it\'s not recognized',1486995342),(161,76,6,'I was able to recreate the issue and yes, if you select an amount, through history drop down, that is higher than the allowed preset amount it will save the WO, but it does not allow the user to dispense the amount. At the dispense page when the user hits the start button a message appears telling the user that the preset amount is greater than what is allowed and that a manager\'s pin is required to continue. So the system will still not allow a higher preset to be dispensed. We will look into getting this bug fixed by having the system check the amount again before the WO is saved.',1486998133),(162,49,81,'discrepancy not fixed\ntested today, vers. T_2_29\nall new firmware\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.2.2',1486998428),(163,46,81,'discrepancy not fixed\ntested today\nvers. T_2_29\nall new firmware\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.2.2\n',1486998572),(164,42,6,'LQD_T_2_29- The WO now appears in \"WO status\", \"summary report- normal view\" and \"daily report\" even if it has not been selected yet. The only place it still does not show is in the Recent Word Order window on the manager\'s dashboard (it shows up only after it has been selected by a user).',1486999015),(165,52,81,'discrepancy not fixed\ntested today\nvers T_2_29\nall new firmware\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.2.2',1486999156),(166,77,144,'We see the issue. We are updating it right now. Hope to have it resolved tomorrow 5pm CST.',1487026877),(167,76,144,'We plan to have this solution fixed by 5pm cst tomorrow',1487026908),(168,75,144,'Figured out the issue. Going to provide an update T_30 tomorrow 5pm cst to fix it.',1487026964),(169,74,144,'Still having issues getting this error to come up on our test system. Going to look into it more tomorrow. Can I teamviewer into your system, and you can replicate it while I have the logs going?',1487027053),(170,74,6,'No problem, ill message you first thing in the morning\n',1487027222),(171,73,144,'Still working on the excel sheet for yellow issues. T_29 fixed the red issues, and T_30 that is planned to release tomorrow will make the locked dispense ON as the default, and have lock dispense moved under the preset box.',1487027258),(172,65,144,'Did the R_20 versions end up fixing the export issue?',1487027306),(173,42,144,'We are working on getting the view updated. It should be on T_30\'s release that is planned for tomorrow.',1487027523),(174,49,144,'Do you mind if I get a backup of the database your are using? I want to load it on our system to see all the settings being used as well as be able to replicate it quicker.',1487027659),(175,66,138,'Again, I wanted to verify that the change that were made corrected the issue the end user was have and checking to see if the issue was resolved satisfactory.',1487030051),(176,52,138,'Is it possible to get a copy of your database to further trouble shoot this error and resolve it?',1487030146),(177,65,138,'Works with T_29 and R_19',1487030285),(178,49,81,'I\'m trying to upload the database (even in compressed folder) but it\'s giving a database error page',1487061746),(179,52,81,'I\'m trying to upload the database (even in compressed folder) but it\'s giving a database error page',1487061766),(180,55,81,'it seems fixed, but there is a particular situation where there is a difference. Please check new discrepancy #78, then it\'s up to you to verify if this is closed and only #78 must be fixed or if this is still to be checked.',1487065513),(181,42,81,'version T_2_29 ==> this is fixed as the brandly new created WO appears both in WO status and Summary report reports\n\nrecent WO window should be a different discrepancy, please check and in case you can close this.',1487065863),(182,43,81,'version T_2_29 ==> this window is still having issues.\nSorting seems to be ok, as it looks like the default sorting is by date then time, correctly\nI don\'t understand the logic of which open WO are shown is the list: I have 17 open WO (1 dated November 2016, 1 dated December 2016, 2 from January 2017, 3 dated February 1st 2017, 2 dated February 9th 2017, 6 from February 13th 2017 and 2 from February 14th 2017): the list is only showing one single open WO (dated February 9th 2017) independently from what I\'m setting in admin options (daily, weekly, monthly, custom 120days are showing always only that single open WO)',1487066483),(183,44,81,'T_2_29 ==> sorting seems to be ok, but since I can check only the list when showing also closed WO (only one open WO is shown - check discrepancy #43) I cannot assure this is totally fixed.',1487066712),(184,45,81,'T_2_29 ==> discrepancy fixed',1487067877),(185,47,81,'fixed',1487068028),(186,48,81,'fixed',1487068652),(187,50,81,'it seems\nto be\nfixed',1487071126),(188,51,81,'2 separate accounts yet',1487071234),(189,44,6,'Andrea- from what i see testing this, the Recent Work Order window on the manager dashboard shows open/closed work orders in order from when there was a transaction/dispense done with that work order. So the work order at the top is the latest work order to have been used in a transaction. The order may look out of date because if a user created the work order on 2/9, but does not dispense under that work order until 2/14, it will show at the top of the list but with the date it was created on 2/9. So other work orders that dispensed on 2/10,2/11,2/12 and 2/13 would be below it even though they show a later date under date created. The reason it is like this is so a manger can look at that window and see the most recent work orders that have been used. So if they see a work order from a few days ago on there, they know that a dispense was done off of it and can find out why it has not been closed by checking the work order number in the transaction report to get the details.',1487084035),(190,44,6,'I guess the question is do we want it to keep working like this or do we want to adjust it? I like the idea of the window showing the most recently dispensed work order, this lets the user know what work has been done recently. If they need more details or want to see the work orders in order of when they were created/closed they can go to Work Order Status under view logs. If they need to see details of the transaction under a specific work order then they can go to Transaction Report.',1487084461),(191,44,6,'Adam/Bryan- can you guys check this, as i am testing this i am finding that my first comment is not 100% true. There does seem to be a date range that even if i open a work order that was closed and dispense from hit and leave it open it does not show up on the recent work order window. I am trying to find out if there is a specific date range for this. The work orders that seem to fall into this unknown date range are sorting the way i described in my first comment.',1487086557),(192,57,6,'Andrea- Tested this on T_2_29 and seems to be fixed but would like to you confirm. I loaded the WO with a product and preset of 10. Selected the WO on TAC and PC but did not dispense. Then went to manager and changed the preset to 5 (product stayed the same). Then loaded the WO from TAC and PC and the preset changed.',1487087818),(193,51,144,'Just so I can confirm before I make a change: you want to have the Gartec user\'s email (gartec@gitec.com) under Gitec switched to a.simonetto@gartec.it? This way you can see discrepancies that Sébastien adds and Sébastien can see ones you add, correct?',1487104847),(194,44,144,'This is a strange issue we have seen as well. On T_2_29 and even before then, there was some weird conditions where the sorting wouldn\'t go by date first even if you filtered by date. We\'ve been working on it, and believe we have it fixed for the next version as we cannot replicate it now. It will come out on the T_30 version for testing. We are going to continue testing it. If you find the same issue with the database you are using on the next update, I would like to see it.',1487105659),(195,78,144,'So on this the web seems to be assigning the work order still on some cases. We have your database, and were able to replicate it. We are now checking to see where the underlying issue is.',1487105767),(196,38,144,'There is a comment that says the TAC works. Is this work order closed?',1487105903),(197,77,144,'Please check with LQD_T_2_30',1487114163),(198,76,144,'Please check with LQD_T_2_30',1487114172),(199,75,144,'Please check with LQD_T_2_30',1487114182),(200,74,144,'Please check with LQD_T_2_30',1487114193),(201,73,144,'One thing that came up for the lock dispense is that I could see the default lock dispense being an issue for some customers where some will want it to default to ON while some will want to default to off. Maybe we need an admin option for what the default for lock dispense for managers should be?',1487114280),(202,44,144,'T_30 should address this issue. There could still be issues. We are testing different configurations ourselves as well.',1487114450),(203,75,6,'Fixed on LQD_T_2_30',1487177763),(204,74,6,'Fixed on LQD_T_2_30',1487177787),(205,73,6,'That is a good idea, but still want the option to change it for a specific work order, so if the default is set to OFF, they can still turn it ON when creating the work order',1487177970),(206,80,138,'We are changing the verbiage on the PC to match that on the TAC',1487353386),(207,76,27,'fixed with T_2_30',1487582921),(208,77,27,'fixed with T_2_30',1487582975),(209,43,81,'T_2_30\n\nit looks like it has been fixed: open work orders are all shown indipendentely from \"purge WO\" settings in admin options; closed WO are shown correctly only if they are contained in the range allowed by admin options.',1487584949),(210,44,81,'I think that open WO should be sorted by date by default, with T_2_30 this seems to happen and I guess it could be considered fixed.\n\nI agree that, as Kevin was writing, it could be good to have them sorted by date of last dispense, but:\n1) all the not-dispensed needs to be sorted by date of creation (until 2_29 it was not this way)\n2) there is no possibility to re-sort by date of last transaction after you make a different sorting using arrows on a column title: that\'s why maybe is better to follow only date of creation by default\n\nplease let me know, personally for sorting I\'m good with 2_30 fixes.',1487586975),(211,51,81,'Yes, I need to follow this \"account \" gartec@gitec.com (not existing address) from my email a.simonetto@gartec.it, so that I can receive alerts, see what Sébastien adds and add things that Sébastien can see\n\nMore generally, the best would be to have Gitec under Gartec;\nif not possible, to have the possibility to have 2 different accounts with the same email address, same user under Gartec and under Gitec',1487588383),(212,53,81,'T_2_30 fixed',1487589031),(213,54,81,'T_2_30 fixed, the WO is no more assigned to a specific user when this user selects it withoput dispensing\n\n(take care about discrepancy #78)',1487589602),(214,56,81,'T_2_30 fixed',1487666758),(215,57,81,'T_2_30 fixed',1487666879),(216,65,27,'version T_2_30\nWhen you click on \"download\" the result is different depending on the browser:\n\n1) GOOGLE CHROME\nit works, the browser opens a window that automatically closes and a pdf file is downloaded\n\n2) MOZILLA FIREFOX\nthe browser opens 2 windows, a popup requesting to open or save a file is open.\nThen you can download a file with no extension. If you open it with a pdf reader, it\'s ok (similar step if you click directly on open\nIn my opinion, needs a little more fixing\n\n3) INTERNET EXPLORER\nit works similar, browser is asking you to save or open. If you open, automatically opens the pdf on a new window\n\n\nWARNING! it allows you only to download a pdf file - what about a csv/txt/xlsx file? I can consider this fixed, but opening a new discrepancy',1487667860),(217,58,81,'T_2_30 same as before, not fixed',1487669585),(218,59,81,'T_2_30 fixed',1487669682),(219,60,81,'T_2_30 fixed',1487669953),(220,61,81,'T_2_30 fixed',1487670334),(221,39,6,'Fixed on LQD_T_2_30',1487687184),(222,67,6,'Tested this on T_2_30- This seems like a timing issue. If you let the counter go down to 1, a message comes up saying \"dispense successful\" but the counter stays at 1 for about 30 seconds and then will reset to 59, the start button resets right away to green. If you click the start button fast enough right after \"dispense successful\" the relay will turn on and the counter will start counting down but the start button does not turn yellow. I also noticed that if you start 2 dispenses on two tanks at the same time and let it count all the way down the counter does not reset back to 59 until you refresh the page, this is only when doing 2 at the same time. (Note- none of this happens when hitting the stop button to stop a dispense, only when it counts all the way down)',1487688987),(223,79,144,'We found the error. Currently fixing it. Should have a release soon that fixes this issue. We were seeing that it was working if it dispensed first on the website, but doesn\'t if it hadn\'t been dispensed from the website at all. Thank you.',1487800172),(224,81,138,'We will add this change for the next release that is coming soon.',1487866745),(225,67,144,'Figured out the issue. It is indeed a timing issue which messes with the logic. The timer does indeed refresh back to 59, but it takes about 10 seconds after it counts all the way down to 0. This will be fixed in the next update.',1488361861),(226,82,138,'Since this is a logic issue with the dispense procedure, changes to how autoclose workorder will take a while for some scenarios in order to make sure the changes are done properly. However, some of the ones listed in the document, we should be able to make changes fairly quickly. We are first focusing on the other discrepancies, but if a change is made to any of the autoclose workorder scenarios, we will comment on this open discrepancy.',1488921842),(227,51,144,'My team said they made the change. When you get a chance, please confirm. Thank you.',1488927606),(228,51,81,'Hello Bryan, I received an email that a new discrepancy has been opened (discrepancy #82), but not receiving any comments when someone commented on old discrepancies.\nI received the email about new discrepancy opened, but Sébastien no\nHe received email about comments, I did not',1488964375),(229,63,6,'Tested on LQD_T_2_30 and issue is fixed. I could not get a user to select a work order (on TAC or PC) that could only be used at a station where the user was not assigned. ',1489007627),(230,43,81,'I\'m sorry, I have to re-open the discrepancy since it looked like it had been fixed. but it\'s not.\n\nI found out today (this week I did not make any test because of time) that all recent still open WO are not shown in the list...no matter which \"purge WO\" settings you make, you can only see closed WO (in case they\'re in the time range allowed by purge WO settings)\n\nI think that open WO are shown only in case they were opened in the same month? Month changed, I can\'t see any old still open WO',1489073357),(231,43,81,'if you click on \"view details\", you can see all open WO (check attached pictures)',1489074096),(232,44,81,'WARNING, sorting is not fixed in T_2_30!\ncheck new attached pictures',1489074601),(233,44,81,'correct on dashboard, not correct in \"view details\" window',1489075013),(234,62,81,'T_2_30\n\nsystem returns the same error \"you are not assigned to any station\"',1489075476),(235,63,81,'T_2_30\n\nit\'s acting differently from earlier, user can\'t dispense the product he cannot dispense, but the system is asking him to chose the station (showing only the stations the user is assigned to) and if he selects one of them the system is switching automatically the product to first product of the selected station (discrepancies 52, 46 and 49 still open).\n\nActually...it\'s like #63 has been fixed, because the issues are already reported in other 3 discrepancies',1489076419),(236,37,6,'Sebastien- I have tested this issue on T_2_30 and from what i see it is fixed. I loaded a WO from the TAC, was able to dispense, kept WO open, then selected it again and dispensed a different product on a different station with no issue. Please check this as well and if you find that it fixed we can close the discrepancy.',1489158200),(237,85,81,'I don\'t know if it\'s a software problem (algorythm) or a hardware problem (probe\'s sensitivity/range of working pressures...).\n\nIt has been found with 5 different probes, coming from 2015, 2016 and last 2017 shipment',1489505361),(238,87,6,'I can not re-create the issue here. I have tried switching to liters and using European instead of USA but everything seems to be working. Check to make sure the latest hardware is loaded to the remote display, sometimes this can happen if it is not up to date. Can you send me a copy of your database so i can look into this further and match your exact setup?',1489509438),(239,89,144,'When you switched to US Central time, the system accounted for Daylight Savings Time in the U.S. If the time in London was 16:25 and you changed it to Central, the true time is 11:25am and not 10:25am. Daylight Savings Time for the U.S. just started this last weekend (time went forward an hour), so the (-6) for US Central Time is going to be (-5) and the (-5) for Eastern US time will be (-4).',1489511172),(240,88,144,'It seems as though the controller system time got set to Central for the system time instead of UTC which can cause time issues. Is there any chance I could teamviewer into this controller?',1489511451),(241,85,144,'This would be a software issue when the probe is in an empty or empty enough tank where the bottom half is not submerged in liquid. We should be able to change the algorithm to fix the issue at that level.',1489511781),(242,89,6,'I think daylight savings time has come into play here. When i wrote this it is 11.45 Central standard time. London is 5 hours ahead of us at 16.45. So even though the GMT is -6 from London to US Central, the correct time is being displayed by the system when switching between different GMT time zones. I test this a little bit and checked it with real time around the world and what i have found is that even though it says GMT-X, the value for X does not always equal the difference in real time between two different time zones. If you switch the time zone to GMT-5 Lima, it gives the same time as GMT-6 US Central, which after googling what time it is in Lima this is correct, but if you switch it to GMT-5 US Eastern the real time is 1 hour ahead of both Lima and US Central.\n\nThe \"do you want to update time\" button does not apply to changing the time zone, the time that is set will adjust accordingly when you select a different time zone. Selecting the button only allows you to change the physical clock on the system. So if it reads 16.30 but for whatever reason you need it to read 15.30, you can adjust the time on the system while still staying in the same time zone. ',1489511830),(243,42,144,'You have discrepancy 43 for the recent work order, so I\'m assuming that this particular discrepancy can be closed. Please close if this is correct. Thank you.',1489513554),(244,87,144,'I was also not able to duplicate. If I can teamviewer into your system or get your latest database, we can try to replicate it.',1489518794),(245,86,144,'At a first glance, this could be a more difficult thing to do then adding an extra field. I\'ll look into it after taking care of some of the pressing discrepancies and see what the best solution could be.',1489519003),(246,88,81,'yes, it\'s here in my office\n\nbut the same is happening on Sébastien controller, so I think it\'s something you can check directly on yours?\n\nI\'m on skype anyway today!',1489565847),(247,89,81,'ok, I did not consider that DST is coming in different weeks between here and US\n\nbut system is considering daylight saving time also for other countries? I mean it will change automatically also here in Europe in 2 weeks?\n\nI will test by changing date',1489566053),(248,89,81,'ok, tested. For me it\'s closed (never to be open, sorry!)',1489576161),(249,51,144,'Please check now if both you and Sébastien are receiving update emails for discrepancies opened by either Gartec user or Sébastien. Thank you.',1489577254),(250,90,138,'We are gathering together a completed Translation File now.',1489611096),(251,79,81,'we succeded in testing jobs.\nQuestion is: does the TAC require a firmware update to work complety properly?\n\nSituation: we can work with jobs assigned to technicians assigned to all stations.\nCommunication error if a tech assigned only to 1 or 2 stations (not all) tries to select a job assigned to all technicians\nCommunication error if same technician tries to select a job assigned only to him.\nIn both cases the oil configured in the job is present in at least one of the stations assigned to tech\n\nfrom PC everything seems to work, that\'s why I\'m asking if to test correctly TAC needs a firmware change',1489760950),(252,42,6,'Tested on T_2_31- created a new work order but did not select it by any user, the open work order showed up in all the reports and on the manager dashboard in the recent work orders window. (also shows if you click \"view details\" or \"work order maintenance\") Andrea if you can confirm we can close this discrepancy.',1489762153),(253,43,6,'This is fixed on T_2_31- purge work orders is set to daily, all open work orders are showing in the recent work order window, some dated from two months ago. Andrea if you can confirm we can close this discrepancy.',1489762874),(254,44,6,'Fixed on T_2_31- Work orders are sorted by date they were opened in all windows. Closed work orders do not show if they were opened outside of the purge work orders time setting. Andrea can you please confirm then we can close this discrepancy.',1489763600),(255,49,6,'The initial issue with this discrepancy seems to be fixed, it no longer allows a user who is not assigned to a station where the selected product is available to select an assigned station and a different product is then turned on, but there is still some issues. \n1. This discrepancy is directly tied to discrepancy 46, so i don\'t think we can close this until that discrepancy is also fixed.\n2. On the TAC- the user can select the work order, then select an assigned station (even though the product is not available), the TAC then pauses for a minute then returns a error code 255. This is good that it does not allow the user to continue, but i think we need to have descriptive error code appear. I.E- \"Product not available at selected station\", or we need to have one appear when the user selects the work order saying \"Product for this WO is not available at assigned stations\".\n3. On the PC- When the user selects the WO, a message comes up saying \"you are not assigned to ANY station\". Again good that they cannot continue, but the message is misleading. The user is assigned to stations, just not the ones with the product for the WO. We need to look at changing this message to \"Product for this WO is not available at assigned stations\", then it would match the TAC as well.',1489766820),(256,55,6,'Andrea- I am going to close this discrepancy since one of the issues is being addressed on discrepancy #78, and this is a very broad discrepancy that is generally fixed. If any new issues come up with the TAC vs PC procedure that needs to be addressed then a new discrepancy should be opened.',1489767602),(257,90,144,'The translation file was updated in the Dropbox/Oilcop Files/Translations 2016/Translations 2016 file. The ones that need translations for the web are highlighted blue and the ones that need translations for the TAC are highlighted in dark green.',1489777640),(258,90,80,'Hello Bryan\nThe file is updated for the French part.\nThere are a few lines where I cannot translate\n\"Legacy Sensor\", \"Sensor Amount\", \"Tank Monitor Dispensing\", \"Tank Monitor solution\"\nI would like to have some additional explains\n\nOn the TAC part, I modified some transaltions (in red)\n\nThanks you,\n\nSébastien',1489841521),(259,38,81,'it happened also to me on R_2_17.\n\nBasically, the technician is blocked and everytime you try to log in on TAC, system always brings you to the dispensing page asking you if the dispense is complete or not.\nIt happened with auto-close on, but also with auto-close off: in this second case, I tried to close the WO from TAC (dispense complete ==> close WO ) but on the PC it stayed open.\nI tried by closing the WO from PC, logging with same technician it always brought me to same page...\nSolved only if you delete the technician and create it from scratch...',1490090856),(260,38,81,'with version T_2_30 and 31 it never happened.\nWe can consider this closed for the moment. If it happens again during these days, we will re-open it',1490091038),(261,42,81,'we also tested with T_2_31, yes Kevin we can close this discrepancy',1490091401),(262,43,81,'confirmed, tested with T_2_31\nopen WO are all shown not depending on purge settings, closed WO are shown depending on purge settings.\nClosed',1490092848),(263,44,81,'confirmed, it\'s closed\n\nPS we will add a new discrepancy about the recent WO window, but the sorting by date of creation and time of creation is ok',1490093935),(264,46,81,'tested with T_2_31, fixed\n\nWO: all technician, specified product, all assigned stations, specified preset\n\n- if logging with a tech assigned to all stations, with a product present only in a single station ==> system automatically goes to dispense page with the only reel available, OK\n- if logging with a tech assigned to all stations, with a product present in multiple stations (but not all) ==> system asks to select a station only showing the list of stations with the product, OK\n- if logging with a tech assigned to a single station, with a product present also in other stations ==> system automatically goes to dispense page with the only reel the tech is allowed to open, OK\n- if logging with a tech assigned only to stations where the product is not present ==> tech can select the WO but system returns communication error, BUG (but it\'s discrepancy #52, not this one)\n\ndiscrepancy closed',1490097520),(265,49,81,'Tested with T_2_31, since it\'s tied and coming directly after #46, this is now fixed.\nnote n°2 by Kevin, this is discrepancy #52\nnote n°3 by Kevin, this is discrepancy #62\n\nso we can consider #49 closed',1490104327),(266,51,81,'ok, I\'m receiving emails and notification both if I update/close or if Sébastien does modify the discrepancies.\n\nthis is closed, my question is if I could work from Gartec account and see what\'s making Sébastien from Gitec account (like having Gitec under Gartec). If it\'s not possible, this can be consider closed and I will continue to work using 2 different accounts',1490104703),(267,52,81,'test on T_2_31, not fixed.\n\na technician assigned only to stations where the product is not available can anyway select the WO. Later system will return communication error, but the bug is earlier, since the tech should not see the WO in the selectable list',1490105723),(268,58,81,'T_2_31 same as before.\n\nIf you create a WO giving a specific product and a specific station',1490107336),(269,58,81,'(sorry my laptop clicked some buttons all alone and closed the discrepancy whileI was writing....)\n\nT_2_31 same as before.\nYou create a WO giving a specific product and a specific station and save it, then if you click the button to update the WO, the product name changed to \"all products\" and the dropdown menu is only showing \"all products\"\n\nwe made a video for your reference',1490107510),(270,52,81,'same problem both on TAC and PC',1490108191),(271,62,81,'T_2_31\n\nsystem acts in the same way.\n\nonce discrepancy #52 will be fixed, this will be fixed automatically, because it won\'t be possible to face this situation',1490108315),(272,58,81,'link for the video:\nhttps://www.dropbox.com/s/silzz3vq1pyku5o/%2358%20-%20product%20filter%20not%20working.mp4?dl=0',1490108819),(273,63,81,'T_2_31\n\nwe can consider this issue fixed. System is not allowing you to dispense the product configured by the manager if the station field is on \"all assigned stations\". System allows the user to select stations (product is available only in the station not listed), then it returns communication error ==> it\'s discrepancy #52, so this is closed',1490109230),(274,98,81,'update:\nwe have station 3 which is composed by 3 reels, connected to ports 2-3-4 of FCM 3.\nWe made same test on station 2, reel connected to port 1 of 3rd FCM.\nSame results! The system gives communication error if we try to select the WO using a user assigned to station 2 and other stations.\nNo problems if we select the WO with user Tech02, the only one who is assigned only to station 2.\n\nFor unknown reason, FCM 3 is not allowing to communicate with users assigned also to other stations!\n',1490116478),(275,98,81,'update 2:\nwe tried to use a 4th FCM, disconnecting the 3rd. Using same address and connecting same solenoids/pulses simulator.\nIt\'s happening exactly the same thing.\n\nFrom PC, no problem is found',1490117200),(276,98,81,'since you have the full complete backup, we are now going to delete the whole configuration, because we need to continue testing',1490117252),(277,79,81,'T_2_31 test on TAC:\n\n1) product available in all stations\n - tech assigned to all stations ==> OK\n - tech assigned only to a single station ==> COMMUNICATION ERROR\n - tech assigned to more than one station (2) but not all ==> COMMUNICATION ERROR\n - tech assigned to station 1 and 3 is different from the others ==> he can choose between stations (all, and not only 1 and 3) and he does not receive communication error even if he chooses 2; he can dispense\n\n2) product available only on a single station (X)\n - tech assigned to all stations ==> OK\n - tech assigned only to station X ==> OK\n - tech assigned to more than one station (one is X) but not all ==> OK\n - tech not assigned to station X ==> COMMUNICATION ERROR (WARNING! he should not see the job!)\n\n3) product available on multiple stations but not all (2 out of 3, X and Y)\n - tech assigned to all stations ==> system asks for station selection ==> OK if you select both X or Y\n - tech assigned only to station X ==> COMMUNICATION ERROR\n - tech assigned only to station Y ==> COMMUNICATION ERROR\n - tech assigned to more than one station (one is X OR Y) but not all (so not to Y OR X) ==> COMMUNICATION ERROR\n - tech assigned to X+Y ==> system asks for station selection ==> OK if you select both X or Y\n - tech not assigned to X and not assigned to Y ==> COMMUNICATION ERROR\n\n\nthis is a complete test on TAC very quick, please just confirm that is only because TAC requires a firmware update or not',1490123559),(278,79,81,'test on PC ==> works perfectly in all cases',1490123594),(279,90,144,'\"Legacy Sensor\" means a type of sensor probe. Yes means it is an old type of sensor probe and No means it is a new type of sensor probe\n\n\"Sensor Amount\" has to do with a report that is being currently worked on. It has to do with how much fluid is measured from the sensor probe during a certain amount of time that the a tank was increasing or decreasing in fluid.\n\n\"Tank Monitor Solution\" means that the system will only be configured to use the tank monitor part of the full system (no fcms, no work orders, no jobs, etc.) It just monitors tank contents using sensor probes and TSM.\n\n\"Tank Monitor Dispensing\" means that the system will be able to turn on relays and dispense to dispense fluid while it is in the \"Tank Monitor Solution\" mode.',1490126490),(280,98,144,'Thank you for the information. Looking into it now.',1490126530),(281,98,144,'Changed it to engineering',1490126549),(282,51,144,'Having a distributor under a distributor is currently under development. After getting an Oilcop release for the end customer, this will be something we will continue to finish. I will close it the initially problem is solved.',1490126777),(283,79,144,'As long as you have the latest TAC update (v1.4), then this is not a firmware update.\n\nI will look into the communication errors you are getting, and I will move this back to engineering for now.',1490126945),(284,87,144,'Is this something you are still seeing? Is it possible that it is a firmware problem? Can I get more information like was it wired/wireless? Is this for the test version or one of the release versions?',1490127060),(285,46,81,'ERRATA CORRIGE\n\nthe discrepancy is not fixed and must be re-opened\n\nyesterday we tested with configuration G (autoclose off, multiproduct and multidispense on) ==> system was ok and discrepancy seemed to be fixed\n\ntoday we are testing the system with a different configuration (B = autoclose on, multiproduct and multidispense off) ==> problem occurred again\nwe tested also with configuration C (autoclose off, multiproduct on, multidispense off) ==> problem occurred again\n\nthis means that for some reason the multiproduct switch is causing the problem...if it\'s ON, system acts correctly, but if it\'s OFF it gives problem, giving the possibility to select a different station where the product configured by the manager is not available, and switching to first product if selecting that station (discrepancy #49 re-opened too)\n\nthis happened with a WO with a product available only on station 2, logging with technician assigned to station 1 and 2. It asked to select station, if you click on station 1 it switched to first product.\nSame conditions but with configured product availble only on station 1, no problems: no asking to selct the station and directly addressed to correct dispensing page.',1490175825),(286,49,81,'ERRATA CORRIGE\n\nthe discrepancy is not fixed and must be re-opened\n\nyesterday we tested with configuration G (autoclose off, multiproduct and multidispense on) ==> system was ok and discrepancy seemed to be fixed\n\ntoday we are testing the system with a different configuration (B = autoclose on, multiproduct and multidispense off) ==> problem occurred again\nwe tested also with configuration C (autoclose off, multiproduct on, multidispense off) ==> problem occurred again\n\nthis means that for some reason the multiproduct switch is causing the problem...if it\'s ON, system acts correctly, but if it\'s OFF it gives problem, giving the possibility to select a different station where the product configured by the manager is not available, and switching to first product if selecting that station (discrepancy #49 re-opened too)\n\nthis happened with a WO with a product available only on station 2, logging with technician assigned to station 1 and 2. It asked to select station, if you click on station 1 it switched to first product.\nSame conditions but with configured product availble only on station 1, no problems: no asking to selct the station and directly addressed to correct dispensing page.',1490175887),(287,90,3,'Bryan,\nDoes Legacy Sensor mean the 6\' probe and new type means the 21\' probe and 30\' probe?\n',1490202303),(288,90,144,'Legacy Sensor means 6\' probe and new type means the 21\' probe.',1490202881),(289,46,81,'link for the video about this issue\nhttps://www.dropbox.com/s/s7zu11oen4hhqer/%2346-%2349.mp4?dl=0',1490256423),(290,90,81,'is it possible to change \"yes\" and \"no\" with a quick description/reference?',1490256618),(291,102,138,'We are working to correct these errors.',1490301364),(292,103,138,'Are you having this error only on the System Language & Time page or is it on a different page/report? Also, what version are you working with?',1490365297),(293,90,144,'It\'s possible to change \"yes\" and \"no\" to something else. Just need to know what would be the best descriptions.\n\nIn addition, we found 8 more words that need to be translated. I updated it in the Dropbox/Oilcop Files/Translations 2016/Translations 2016.',1490366443),(294,58,138,'We are currently working to resolve this.',1490385869),(295,78,138,'We are currently working to resolve this.',1490385887),(296,93,138,'We are currently working to change the verbiage.',1490385984),(297,94,138,'We are currently working to change the verbiage.',1490385998),(298,96,138,'We are currently working to make this change.',1490386047),(299,95,138,'We are currently working towards our next release and want to resolve all discrepancies first before discussing this idea further.',1490386261),(300,97,138,'This will be corrected once Discrepancy 58 has been resolved.',1490386315),(301,98,138,'Replicated. Have not pin pointed the bug yet.',1490386389),(302,92,138,'We are currently working towards our next release and want to resolve all discrepancies first before discussing this idea further.',1490386467),(303,91,138,'We are currently working towards our next release and want to resolve all discrepancies first before discussing this idea further.',1490386480),(304,88,138,'We are currently working to resolve this.',1490386530),(305,99,138,'We are currently working to resolve this.',1490386541),(306,100,138,'We are currently working to resolve this.',1490386549),(307,101,138,'We are currently working to resolve this.',1490386555),(308,91,80,'Hello,\n\nThis is a priority request we had asked for the next realease.\n\nWe need to have a new printer firmware (correct translation, correct time, 1 Dispense = 1 print)\n\nThanks',1490597974),(309,110,138,'We are working on setting up oilcop@gartec as the address the system uses. Can you provide password, incoming/outgoing ports and servers directly to bryan@viaanelectronics.com',1490713874),(310,128,27,'database sent by email on March 28 to Bryan and Angel',1490716343),(311,128,144,'Thanks Andrea. We\'ll look into it, and plan to Teamviewer into their system Thursday morning (CST). Do you know if there a specific time(s) Teamviewer would be available?',1490716722),(312,110,81,'email sent',1490775098),(313,134,81,'to be checked also later when it will be possible to export in csv/txt format (only for reports that could be exported in this format)',1490777712),(314,128,144,'Hello Andrea, after looking into the database today, we didn\'t find anything inherently wrong with the dispenses. There were some out of place dispenses though. For example, on average the work order dispenses were around 0-10 Liters, but there were some work orders that were around 25-40 liters. So the thought is the technician is using a different work order that was not closed out. For some of the 0 dispenses, I also can\'t be sure if it wasn\'t a timeout.\n\nHowever, since this is a downgraded controller, (from R_19 to R_17), I\'ll compare the files they have on their controller to the normal R_17 files we have to make sure they are matching. There are some additional logs I\'ll also be able to look at on the controller itself to help. I can be available tomorrow (Thursday) for 3 hours starting at 6am (CST). Otherwise, Angel and I can also be available Friday.',1490833017),(315,128,27,'I asked them id and password, so that we can start even if there\'s noone in the office.\nOtherwise they will be available from 7am CST\n\nDo I need to ask them to download winscp?',1490856179),(316,128,144,'I was able to teamviewer in this morning.\n\nFirst, there were 2 dispenses from a long time ago that were never completed (the work order was closed, but the dispense was still open). Those 2 dispenses were closed. That could have been the main issue.\n\nSecond, the sync is enabled and has the sync issue due to being R_17. This could have caused an issue later down the road, so did a patch to fix it.\n\nI did a file comparison and they match up with a stock version of R_17. Also, more logs were enabled in case the issue comes up again. Let me know if they experience the issue again.\n\nThank you.',1490877997),(317,136,6,'Andrea- in talking with Bryan we think this may be a sync issue with the controller, this can be fixed through winscp by deleting the sync files. If you can get the customer to set up teamviewer we can get in and fix the issue.',1490883521),(318,139,144,'My team compiled a list of TAC engineering error codes and their translations.\nLet me know if you have any questions.\n\nThank you',1491350937),(319,138,3,'This is not an uncommon procedure with car dealerships...\n \nCustomer brings a car in with a complaint and while at the dealership request them to change the oil.\nMechanic investigates the problem and finds they need to replace a defective part, however they do not have the replacement part so they order it from the factory. Typically it takes 1 -2 days for the part to arrive..  Meanwhile while waiting for the part the service manager will have the Express Lube department perform the oil change so when the part arrives the only have to install the part.\n',1491488310),(320,136,1,'Is the End User still having issues with accessing this controller or has this issue been resolved?',1491593055),(321,140,144,'I\'m checking this now to see if this is an issue with the online update or the TAC firmware.\nIf it is still communicating, but not displaying green on the website. It sounds like it is a UI issue. I\'ve got the controller\'s files, and will compare them to ours.\n\nIn addition, there was discussion regarding the job recipe top off. There is a request to either turn off top-off for jobs or have a separate option to disable/enable top offs for jobs.\nYou can currently turn off top-offs for jobs using the \"Top Off\" option in administrative options, but there are the cases where some customers will want top-off for their normal work order dispenses and not have top-off for jobs.\n\nWhat I need to know are their customers right now that currently use top offs with their jobs? If so, then we will want to have a \"Job Top Offs\" option in admin options separate from the normal \"Top Off\" options. Otherwise, we can disable top offs for jobs entirely.',1491773350),(322,81,6,'Problems with the logs after downloading them in CSV. Action Journal has weird character at the after the column header. In transaction and tank adjustments some of the dates are replaced by ########. See attached files for all three reports.',1491841671),(323,81,6,'* tried to load the excel spreadsheets here but it would not let me. I will attach screen shots instead.',1491841919),(324,91,1,'Sebastien and Andrea,\n\nI\'ve been looking into how to get this feature included in a timely matter. Right now, there are a lot of variables with printing after every dispense.\n\nCan I get more information on how this needs to be implemented for the customer. \n\nCurrently, we can do this relatively quickly if after every dispense we print regardless of whether it is a top-off, normal dispense, or a job.\nThis means if I do a normal dispense, it will print. Then if I do a top-off afterwards, it will do another print.\nIs the above okay?\n\nIf you are needing the normal and top-off dispense combined for every dispense, I\'m wondering how the logic needs to go. It seems that you would need a print button on the dispense page itself, and if we add it on the dispense page, then we also need it on the TAC. This would add quite a bit of logic/UI changes which would take a while.\n\nAlso, with the current setup of printing after closing the work order, you are able to reprint by opening the work order and closing it again from the manager menu.\nIf we print after after every dispense, we do not have a spot to do a reprint unless we add a re-print button somewhere. This would need to be advised where to go.\n\nThere are also a few other thoughts on would the ticket need to change at all for these type of dispenses or can they remain the same:\nCompany Name\nDate/Time of Dispense\nW/O #\nProduct Name and Amount Pumped\nTop Off and Amount Pumped\nTotal and Combined Total Pumped.',1491862703),(325,91,6,'I wanted to add to this discussion on changing the way the system prints. Currently we have customers using the printer and they prefer the current logic on printing. The way they operate is the printer sits at the desk of the person who does the billing for the work orders, so once all the dispenses attached to that work order are completed and the work order is closed, they receive a printed ticket showing the total amount of all fluids that were dispensed under that work order number and can bill the work order out. This works well for them as some of these shops have multiple dispense on the same work order at different times, even days apart for bigger jobs. If the logic were changed to where the ticket printed after every dispense, and the work order ended up having multiple dispenses over a span of a few days, then instead of one final ticket at completion, they would have to track and save multiple tickets and manually add them up for billing. They also would need a way to be told that the work order is finally \"complete\" when as it works now when the ticket prints they know the work order is done and they are good to bill it out. I think instead of completely changing the logic of how the system prints, we may need to find a way to make it an option that can be selected to print on dispense complete or on the work order being closed. Please comment here and let me know what you think so that we can come with a solution that works for everyone.',1491922064),(326,46,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491941851),(327,49,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491941954),(328,79,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942003),(329,80,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942180),(330,81,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942225),(331,82,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942347),(332,88,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942378),(333,90,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942412),(334,93,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942459),(335,94,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942822),(336,96,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942889),(337,99,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491942913),(338,100,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943033),(339,101,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943050),(340,102,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943080),(341,104,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943110),(342,106,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943159),(343,107,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943186),(344,108,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943288),(345,109,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943312),(346,110,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943334),(347,119,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943364),(348,120,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943389),(349,121,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943403),(350,122,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943450),(351,123,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943472),(352,124,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943497),(353,125,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491943510),(354,128,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491944109),(355,130,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491944247),(356,131,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491944305),(357,132,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491944324),(358,133,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491944353),(359,134,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491944369),(360,135,138,'Changes made via Version LQD_T_2_32',1491944403),(361,140,144,'The TAC  status problem is fixed. I uploaded the updated hex for the TAC in firmware_LQD_T_2_32. It is named TAC_3_0_2. It will still show version v1.5 when booting the TAC.\n\nWe decided to add the admin option for turning job top-offs ON/OFF instead of disabling Job Top-Offs entirely.\n\nAlso, Sebastian. Is there a chance I can get access to your controller to reset your controller to T_31 then retry the update to T_32? It looks like 2 files were missing on your controller, so I want to see why that could be.\n\nThank you.',1491944589),(362,46,81,'I just tested with T_2_32 and it\'s happening exactly the same thing!\n\nI created a WO for 0W30, available only in a single station.\nI log as user assigned to all stations, I can select all 3 stations and if I select the 2nd station, it\'s allowing to dispense 10W40 (1st product of the selected station).\nIt opens the 10W40 solenoid valve and I dispense 10W40.\n\nThe ticket printed is saying I dispensed 0W30!!!\nReport is saying I dispensed 0W30 from 10W40 reel!!!',1492004387),(363,46,81,'firmware TAC_3_0_1.hex, TAC is saying v1.5',1492004449),(364,46,81,'tested also with firmware 3_0_2, same',1492007549),(365,141,3,'When the Start button is pressed, Mechanic performs 1st dispense – “Standard pre and post dispense timeouts apply” after the 1st preset dispense is complete/PSM valve closes, system immediately reloads the defined preset amount and opens the PSM valve. All dispenses that occur after the 1st dispense will need to have an additional time out “Multi Dispense Timeout” that begins when the PSM valve is opened. If the Multi Dispense timeout is allowed to expire, then Dispense Complete time out countdown begins to count down, when dispense complete time has elapse display returns to Mechanics home page. The mechanic can either choose Select Work Order or “Close Work Order”.',1492014721),(366,82,138,'We discovered a few bugs and are working to correct them, this is not fixed as of today. ',1492015591),(367,131,80,'T_2_33\nNot fixed, in schulder email.\n\nThe date is correct but time is shifted of 1 hour (correct time is 12:15, title time 13:15 in file and title.pdf\n',1492512488),(368,142,144,'As discussed on skype, this will take some time to change as it changes some of the selection and after dispense logic.\n\nIt is somewhat related to discrepancy 138 in the sense that once it is pumped, that work order gets assigned to that technician, station, and product unless multi-product is turned ON.\n\nThis logic will change slightly anyways as when Autoclose is ON, multidispense is ON, and multiproduct is OFF. The work order would close automatically after the dispense (or after top off dispense if it is ON) according to discrepancy 82. This means the manager would have to go in there and re-open the work order anyways.\n\nSo my questions here before we move forward with this change is: \nDo we want the technician to go through the selection process each time for the same product if it is on different stations, or once created with multi-dispense ON and multi-product OFF, have them be able to skip the selection process after the first time they dispense? Or do you just want it so once the manager changes it back to all assigned stations, then the technician has to go through the selection process again?',1492524424),(369,143,144,'This sounds like 2 bugs:\n\nOne is the bug related to discrepancy 78 where once selected on the PC, it changes how it is selected on the TAC.\n\nI\'ll check this configuration with the user only assigned to a single station. That may be able to be fixed today before the release today that adds the job top off button and fixes a few more translations.\n\nHaving the work order not show up if the user cannot select will take a little bit more time because we need to look into it and isolate where to make the change.\n\nThanks for the feedback.',1492524945),(370,144,144,'We are looking into this right now. Just to confirm, the time you are giving us is based off the controller\'s system time, correct?',1492525370),(371,145,144,'This change makes sense. Should be able to add it fairly quick.\n\nThank you for the feedback.',1492525434),(372,142,80,'if Tech select its WO it must be possible to go to search the product on all the stations where the product is present (Autoclose = ON, multiproducts = OFF, multidispense) without intervention of the manager I think.\nAfter Autoclose = ON then the Manager must open the Wo and can modify the station',1492529293),(373,144,80,'Yes controller\'s system time',1492529437),(374,147,1,'I\'ve seen the TAC take up to 3 minutes before reconnecting after a controller reboot. \n\nHow long are you waiting for the TAC to show up before power cycling the TAC?\n\nAnd is this for the latest test version and firmware?\n\nThanks.',1492700560),(375,147,80,'Waiting more 3 minutes. It\'s sure and very regularly not reconnecting. I must disconnected and reconnected.\nLast firmware TAC_3_0_2.hex\nT_2_35',1492755791),(376,91,80,'Hello Kevin,\nWe would have a button in the administration menu to set up the print mode\n1 dispense (dispense + top off) = 1 printing\nOr current operation',1493013479),(377,96,80,'this discrepancy seems fixed',1493018193),(378,46,80,'I tested with T_2_35\nI created a WO for OW30, available only in a single station.\nI log as user assigned to all stations, I select WO : OK possibility to dispense 0W30 in first station.\nBUT if I log as user assigned station 2 or 3 BUG I can chosse WO ( it must impossible to do it) and the TAC make me choose other products (on station 2 or 3) with open dispense',1493020562),(379,80,80,'This discrepancy seems fixed (Becareful the translation is not done)',1493021176),(380,88,80,'This discrepancy seems fixed',1493021246),(381,140,80,'this discrepancy seems fixed',1493033226),(382,139,80,'Thanks for the listing.\nIt will be very helpful in determining errors in customers',1493033376),(383,93,80,'This discrepancy seems fixed',1493033714),(384,94,80,'This discrepancy seems fixed',1493033771),(385,99,80,'T_2_35\nThis discrepancy seems not to be fixed',1493034911),(386,100,80,'This discrepancy seems not to be fixed',1493035140),(387,91,144,'Even if it is an option, I still need to know more information before we proceed to implement this logic.\n\nThere are 2 main concerns that I have for printing after each dispense if you want to include the related top off with the dispense for printing.\n\n1) What happens if the user does not want to do a top off for that dispense? Should they be forced to start the top off then dispense complete it in order to print?\n\n2) What happens if the user needs to reprint a ticket from a previous dispense? Where should the button for reprinting go?\n\nRegards,\nBryan',1493053377),(388,91,80,'1 ) If the user doen\'t want to do top off for the dispense. On the Tac He presses \"no top off and there is printing (if top off is ON in admistration menu)\n2 ) I think when we are in 1 dispense = 1 printing configuartion the user cannot reprint a ticket from a previous dispense \n\nWe should be to keep the possility for reprinting with the current configuration (re open WO and close in WO maintenance)\n',1493055279),(389,91,144,'On the virtual TAC, if the user does not want to do a top off, how do we wish to handle that? Would we print it when they hit the back button?\n\n-Bryan\n',1493077243),(390,91,80,'Yes with the back button seems to be a solution.\n\nOn the TAC\nwithout top off (in adminstration menu)\ndispense complete = printing\n\nWith top off (in administration menu)\ndispense complete\nno top off = printing\nor\ntop off\ndispense complete = printing\n',1493098693),(391,147,80,'Hello,\nFeedback on my customer with T_2_35\nAfter power cut\nCTR restarts : OK\nFCM connected but TAC are not reconnected\nWe must disconnect and reconnect the TAC\nPlease provide us with a solution\n',1494314674),(392,147,144,'The most recent hex files for t_35 are in Dropbox/Oilcop Files/firmware/firmware_LQD_T_2_35.zip\n\nThe new TAC hex is TAC_3_0_3.hex. This file should fix the TAC reconnection issue.\n\nThe CDM also got an update unrelated to the TAC reconnection issue. This just strengthens the network, so there are fewer dropped packets on larger systems. This CDM update is not required.',1494339846),(393,147,80,'The new TAC hex do not work.\nAfter power cut on TAC and FCM\nFCM reconnect immediatly\nTAC is not reconnected\nIt would seem that it is worse than before impossible to reconnect it\nNow we have to disconnect the CDM and reconnect it\nThank you for finding a solution, if the customer has a power cut the TAC must reconnect without customer intervention',1494345462),(394,147,144,'Is the CDM using hex version 3_0_1 or 3_0_2? Have you tried the latest TAC hex on multiple different TACs to see if they are doing the same thing?\n\nI was seeing the problem on TAC hex 3_0_2, but after the update to 3_0_3, the problem went away. I just want to get more information to see if the problem that you are seeing is with the CDM or TAC\n\nThanks',1494386734),(395,147,80,'with CDM hex version 3_0_1\nIt would seem that this is a problem on the TAC.\nTAC S / N: 022616-73 does not reconnect (tried several times); We must disconnect and reconnect the CDM\nTAC S / N: 121316-01: no problem after cut it reconnects without problem.\nWhy? TAC\'s Hardware has changed?\nI fear that this problem often happens with our customers who have old TAC when I make updates\n',1494419858),(396,147,144,'The radio hardware for the TAC would not have changed. We\'ll check with one of our older boards to see if we can replicate. \n\nMy initial thoughts are that there are some bad radio chips that were manufactured. We\'ll contact the chip manufacturers to see if any changes were made between that time.\nWhat are the serial numbers of the FCMs that are connecting fine? I want to check to see if they were around the same time as the TACs that are not reconnecting.\n\nAlso, can you try with CDM hex version 3_0_2? There is some network strength logic that might help the issue even though it was not intended for this specific TAC issue.\n\nThank you',1494446613),(397,147,80,'Hello Bryan,\n\nWith CDM hex version 3_0_2\nThe same problem, impossible to connecting the TAC ( S/N : 022616-73 ). We must disconnect and reconnect the CDM\nFCM\'s test : \nS/N : 031216-10\nS/N : 020817-04\nFCM of my customer (Audi Garage)\nS/N : 031716-17\nTAC of my  customer (unable to connect)\nS/N : 081915-05\nS/N : 031316-18\nTAC of my customer WV Garage (unable to connect)\nS/N : 020516-07\nS/N : 020516-02\nS/N : 081915-15\n\nThanks\n',1494494172),(398,147,144,'I\'m waiting on a response on the manufacturer. In the mean time, I made another hex file with a slightly different radio code than the others for the TAC. If you could try it on a TAC that is not reconnecting, it may fix the issue. It will be located in dropbox \"Oilcop Files/firmware/LQD_T_2_36_test_firmware/TAC_3_0_4.hex. If you have TACs that are reconnecting just fine, don\'t reprogram them. This TAC hex is for the ones that are not connecting okay. If the issue is not resolved, there are a couple options to try.\n\nFirst, if we can setup some sort of anydesk or teamviewer setup, and have a pickit connected to a TAC and the computer that is remote controlled, then I can try debugging those. We would want to setup a time.\nSecond, is replacing the ones that are not reconnecting, and we can look into more detail on why those are not working like the others.\nThird, wait for the manufacturer to get back. They may be able to shed light on the issue.\nFourth, if I can get one TAC that replicates the issue, that would speed up a solution.',1494814260),(399,91,144,'Added in LQD_T_2_36',1494814821),(400,82,144,'Added in LQD_T_2_36',1494814842),(401,149,144,'The error occurs when there is a station with no reels on it. The error is handled when multiproduct is OFF, but not when multiproduct is ON that is why a communication error is happening after you enter the work order name is. The solution in the mean time is to either add a reel to the empty station or delete the empty station. We will come up with the software fix for multiproduct ON case. The same problem occurs on previous versions as well (T_36 to T_38). \n\nCan you please confirm on your side that deleting the empty station or adding a reel to that station fixes this issue?\n\nThank you\n-Bryan',1495720509),(402,150,144,'Is the error still happening every once in a while or is it happening at a specific spot? For example, last time the communication error was happening everytime they pressed start for a dispense.\n\nI\'ll talk with Angel about the Minnesota system.',1496930970),(403,150,3,'It happened once after he installed the new TAC.. During the original phone call i asked if they had power cycled the CDM after they installed the TAC he had not, so i asked him to do that. Ron from Jobbers called back and said that power cycling the CDM seems to have fixed it.\nI will monitor and keep you updated on the situation..\n',1496931996),(404,46,81,'tested with R_21, with multiproduct ON and OFF, it works ==> discrepancy closed',1497428930),(405,49,81,'tested with R_21, in all configuration mentioned in \"errata corrige\", it works ==> discrepancy closed',1497429123),(406,52,81,'tested with R_21, discrepancy is not fixed\n\nwhen logging on TAC:\n1) multiproduct ON ==> user can select the WO, while he should not see it in the list; if he selects the WO, system returns communication error\n2) multiproduct OFF ==> user can select the WO, while he should not see it in the list; if he selects the WO, system asks for product selection in the station assigned to him (if it\'s only one) or asks for station selection (if assigned to more than one); in this last case he can select a station and select one of the products available in this station\n\nwhen logging on PC:\n1) multiproduct ON ==> user can selects the WO, while he should not see it in the list; he\'s asked to select the products, and if he selects any product system returns an error message \"You are not assigned to the stations where the product is present\"\n2) multiproduct OFF ==> user can select the WO, while he should not see it in the list; system returns an error message \"You are not assigned to the stations where the product is present\"\n\nfrom PC system is almost working ( ==> not completely correct, but at least user cannot dispense), while from TAC is still totally wrong.\n\nBasically, user should not be able to see in the list the WO they cannot dispense',1497430759),(407,58,81,'tested with R_21, it\'s fixed ==> discrepancy closed',1497435408),(408,62,81,'tested on R_21, #52 still open, so this is still open',1497435493),(409,64,81,'tested on R_21, impossible to replicate the situation since other discrepancies have been fixed ==> discrepancy closed',1497435883),(410,78,81,'unfortunately there still are some cases (#52 but also we will need to open new discreapncies) where system acts differently when working on TAC or on PC\n\ntested on R_21, discrepancy not fixed',1497436033),(411,79,81,'tested on R_21, fixed ==> discrepancy closed',1497442506),(412,85,80,'With version R_21 ===> fixed\ndiscrepancy closed',1497445720),(413,87,80,'Test Version R_21 ===> fixed',1497446092),(414,90,81,'R_2_21: some words are still to be translated ==> check if the translation file is complete or needs to have those words/sentences added to the file and then translated\n\n(examples: admin option menu ==> Work Order Top Off, Work Order Top Off Limit, Job Recipe Top Off - sensor configuration ==> meters in cable length - email scheduler ==> minute in the minute column)\n\n\nfor LEGACY SENSOR, must change on and off into \"6\' probe\" vs \"21\' probe\" - then they would need to be translated into \"sonda 2m\" vs \"sonda 6m\" (ITA) and \"sonde 2m\" vs \"sonde 6m\" (FRA)',1497446749),(415,150,3,'Appears power cycling the CDM resolved the issue. \n',1497449694),(416,151,144,'Thank you for bringing this to our attention. We will attempt to reproduce the issue then try to get a fix as soon as possible.',1497471266),(417,52,144,'Can I get the R_21 database you are using to test please? I want to start with the same setup to speed up the debug process. Thank you.',1497471463),(418,90,144,'Understood. We\'ll have the team look over the pages again to see if there are some other words not translated as I know I saw some after the R_21 release.',1497471673),(419,152,144,'Error code 9 comes up on the TAC when a user goes to \"Select Work Order\", but there are no open work orders for that user.\n\nMaybe they dispenses then closed the work order, then they went to select that work order again. That would have brought up error code 9.\nThe other way it could have been brought up is if the Manager made the work order for a specific technician, and a different technician logged into to try and select that work order.\n\nI\'ve attached a excel of the error codes and a brief keyword map for their meaning. ',1497534501),(420,153,3,'Emergency Stop works from the Technician dispense page (web)',1497894108),(421,52,81,'hi Bryan, please find attached database',1498027976),(422,52,81,'(I think it has been saved before all tests we made last week...but unfortunately my colleague \"played\" a little with the controller and deleted some reels 2 days ago, so I\'m not able to give you the actual database in the same conditions of last week..)',1498028126),(423,154,144,'Hello Andrea,\n\nSo we have a new hex file in order to get a fix out quicker for you and your customers that have more than 9 reels per station. It will be uploaded in dropbox under \"Oilcop Files/firmware/firmware_LQD_R_2_21\" as \"TAC_3_0_4.hex\". It will show up as version number \"1.5.2\" on boot up. None of the other hex files change. In addition, we are also checking to see when this problem was introduced.\n\nAs a side note, we are standing by to aid with import/export. We\'ll do an initial check in the mean time.\n\nThank you,\nBryan',1498582645),(424,83,3,'This somewhat related to Indexing Jobs records/.csv file.',1498828112),(425,24,3,'Check out the screen shot from 1 and 2 hourly variance report, note the 9:00 AM and 12:00 PM data points.\n9:00 AM Inventory before dispense was 560.1 Q,  inventory after dispense 949.1 Q , Sensor Amount -389\n12:00 PM Inventory before dispense was 928.5 Q inventory after dispense 903.6 Q, Sensor Amount -386.6\nSeems unusual to have two tank fills three hours apart.\nWhat is this telling us?\nOnly able to upload one file, so uploaded a zip file containing 5 screen shots.png \n',1498829364),(426,156,144,'Hello Tommy,\n\nThis is with tank monitor mode set to ON, correct?\n\nDo you happen to remember what browser this was happening on (chrome, firefox, internet explorer?)\n\n-Bryan',1499265351),(427,157,3,'FCM 7 was down',1500044219),(428,157,2,'Did you happen to get the MAC address for the controller, we would like to make sure it is on oilcopsupport.com. Just to confirm since you moved the range extender the devices are now up and running, correct? If you happen to get another call about the devices going down could you try adding an additional range extender and placing one in view of FCM 6 and one in view of FCM7.',1500044633),(429,157,3,'The Sedgwick County Fleet controller is displaying Green on support.com the mac address is 00:f1:f3:1f:af:bf.\nYes everything was working in this morning. \nWill add an extra CDM if the problem persist. \nA little concerned installing another range extender in such a small area (150\' x 150\') might cause more problems.\nIt will be a good test to see what happens.\n\n',1500045624),(430,157,144,'Hey Mark,\n\nI have teamviewer logs of a failed install and am going to work with Teamviewer support to see if they know why the installs sometimes fail. It may be as easy as just using a slightly older version of Teamviewer 12. I\'ll keep you updated.\n\nAlso, for FCM 2, how far is it away from the CDM compared to FCM 6 and 7? Does it have walls/obstacles in the way that would possibly justify 2 bars?',1500055730),(431,157,3,'As of today everything appears to functioning correctly.\nFCM 6 & 7 are located in the north shop CDM to Range extender is about 80\' through 3 cinder block walls.\nFCM 2 is about 60\' from the CDM though 1 cinder block wall and recessed inside of a 5 sided metal box, one side of the metal pocket side is shadowing the FCM.\nWill try to upload a drawing time permitting..\n',1500565742),(432,158,144,'Hello Mark,\n\nLooking at the data, it actually looks like it last synced about an hour ago. To confirm, is the MAC address correct: 00:e0:4c:ae:83:9a? \n\nLet me work with the web development team to see why it is coming up as System Error. The network doesn\'t look like it needs anymore ports open on their end though. As for a response going back to the controller, the controller is able to tell whether it made a connection and is transferring. What would need to be added is a proper UI to display if it didn\'t make that connection or a different error occured.',1500581096),(433,158,3,'Hi Bryan,\nYes, that is the correct Mac address.\nFood thought....  This is a 10. wide area network like Cassens and Walser.\nWalser had the issue with tank monitor UI not updating tank volume info.\nHave the Walser CTR, CDM and TMM plugged into our network for about a week,  tank volumes have been updating properly. \n',1500583378),(434,92,80,'fixed',1501484102),(435,97,80,'Fixed',1501484253),(436,160,144,'Hello Mark,\n\nIt looks like a certain configuration of changing colors/fonts/bold/italic can cause the html formatting to mess up for the formatter. Can you take a snapshot of the following box: on the administrative options page for the company name editor click Tools->Source Code. We\'ll need to mess around with it to get the order or what is the exact cause, but to do a sort of reset to the name, click on tools-> source code: then delete everything in that text box, and hit apply. That essentially resets the format box. You will have to start the format from scratch though after doing that.',1501601002),(437,160,3,'In the test wrote: Walser BMW/MINI OilCop Tank Monitor',1501601941),(438,164,3,'TESt',1503609878),(439,169,3,'Maybe the cleanest way would be to display a line graph of each tank, top of the graphic select the series Daily or Weekly or Monthly, then select the appropriate time frame for the cart. \n\n- Daily: 5 min or 15 Min or 30 Min or 45 Min or 60 Min\n- Weekly: 60 Min or Daily\n- Monthly: 60 Min or Daily or Weekly\nIf the customer needed tabular data they would perform an .csv export  \n',1504039136),(440,171,144,'Hello,\nCan you send a picture of which LED you are referring to for sensor 4 error? I\'m not seeing that label on the FCM.\n\n-Bryan',1506356607),(441,169,215,'Your system has been updated.\nTank History report can be viewed from the Manager or Administrator desktop go to System Log/ View Log/ Tank history.\n',1509119717),(442,172,3,'Relocated range extender #2 to upstairs, only improved signal for Station #5.\nIts as if the antennas are some what directional not so much omnidirectional.  ',1510228752),(443,174,144,'Hello Mark,\n\nI currently added extra logs for the auto fill/dispense detection. The first dispense or fill tomorrow, we should be able to see why it is not showing.\n\n-Bryan',1510295974),(444,174,3,'Something else to consider.. When dealing with Used Oil and Used Coolant, the opposite condition is occurring they slowly accumulate used fluids from various point in the shop, then when the Used fluid tanks are full the fluid is pump out and hauled off.\nWould be nice to come up with a evacuation/extraction/removal report. ',1510321031),(445,175,3,'\nWe can send replacements and you send back the FCMs. My only concern if its related to existing hardware damaging the FCM  could damage the replacement  FCMs. I think it would be better, if you have the time, send the effected FCM\'s back to engineering for root cause determination. They can turn them around in 24 hours. Instead of replacing the equipment.\n\nI know this sounds typical for big manufactures to say but, as you know we are not a big manufacture, we have had no production issues with the FCM firmware or hardware for the last 283 FCMs shipped / 58 installations in USA and Europe.\nLet me know how you would like to proceed..\n  ',1510323076),(446,174,3,'Wired range extender is no longer communicating.\nWill check with the personal if they can determine if either the extender or TMM is begin turned off Friday evenings.\nAny idea ETA  for wired range extender Updated?',1510419506),(447,168,3,' \nAsked customer to check if PSM bypass is partially open.\n',1510419794),(448,176,2,'I am currently working on this. I am doing a few tests, I have added myself as a user on the controller to test. I will update the discrepancy once more when I figure out the cause and solution',1510602888),(449,177,2,'The necessary tables are not currently scheduled to be synchronized.  This will require a controller update, this is currently being tested.',1510603239),(450,173,2,'I am looking at the Action Journal and it seems this all occurred on Wednesday November 8, 2017. Is this correct? Have there been any issues after that day? ',1510603698),(451,175,26,'I have removed one of the two effected FCM\'s and will send it to you.  Let me know if I need an RMA# or should address it to someone specific.\n\nI will be sending FCM#2 minus the plastic back mount and terminal blocks.  It does not count on ports 3 & 4.  All FCM\'s are connected to new Piusi K400 pulse meters and old existing fluid solenoids.',1510603894),(452,173,3,'I believe it occurred Wednesday.\nNo issues after that day.',1510603952),(453,175,3,'Please use RMA# 472895M attn: Mark.. \n\nI will take directly to engineering, not only will they determine root cause, good possibility they can replace the effected component!\nWill advise.',1510604222),(454,176,2,'How long has this been an issue? Have emails and notifications been an issue since the installation? Also does this locations network admin block any of the following ports? Port 80, 8080, 465',1510677209),(455,178,144,'You can skip to T_2_38. There was an issue with T_2_37 where it would have an error that made it difficult to go back to the maintenance page, so the files for that updated were removed. We\'ll work on removing T_2_37 from the list of updates that show up when updating a T controller.',1510841278),(456,178,3,'Thank you!',1510842178),(457,167,3,'This was fixed during the Untied BMW installation.\n\nThis location may be out of service for an extend timed due to hurricane.',1510849262),(458,166,3,'This is completed in T41 update..',1510849305),(459,158,3,'Note: Need to also confirm Ports 480, 465 are open for outbound traffic.',1510850751),(460,179,2,'I have removed the MAC Address (00:e0:b4:54:6b:1d) from the system. Can you please try to assign the MAC Address once more? Let me know if there are any issues.',1511277725),(461,179,80,'Angel\n\nit doesn\'t work \n\nMacaddress already exists.Please enter correct macaddress.\n\nSébastien',1511278341),(462,179,144,'Hello Sebastien,\n\nCan you check to see if you are able to re-add the system now?\n\nThank you,\nBryan',1511360749),(463,179,80,'Hello Bryan,\n\nok, it works\n\nThanks you',1511474742),(464,180,2,'I logged into the system and checked the stations and reels but do not see a reel that is constantly on. Can you verify this? I am logging into the controller with MAC Address: 00:e0:b4:54:3b:20',1511970029),(465,180,144,'I reset this reel yesterday from the Manager menu. One thing that needs to be tested is can it be reset from the admin dashboard to see if the error described comes up. Another task is figuring out how the reel remained in the On state even though the work order was closed.',1511970245),(466,180,3,'Bryan & I were logged into the location Monday.\nBryan was able to able to reset the reel from manager desktop.\nDon\'t know why it wouldn\'t let me reset.\nWill observe to see if it occurs again. ',1511970272),(467,175,26,'The repaired FCM #2 was reinstalled on Friday Dec 1st.  I tested Reel #7, port #3 and it counted properly.  We will monitor this FCM to ensure that the same problem does not occur again.   If it continues to operate properly, we will remove FCM #1 and send it in for repair.',1512412674),(468,181,3,'Tank history bug.\nCan not set Start Stop time for 24 hr.\nOnly 12:00AM - 11:00PM or less',1512746832),(469,182,3,'Forgot to say was able to power cycle the system to communicate, checked back a couple of hours later and returned to the original symptom.\n',1512747472),(470,174,3,'New range extender with updated firmware is connected to the #2 tank monitor.\nattempted to calibrate 0W/20 and Used Coolant tanks by changing specific gravity values however did not change the tank values.\nDoesn\'t appear tank values are being updated.\nWill try to find someone to power cycle the TMM.\n \n',1513088009),(471,174,3,'Cycled the TMM power no change in symptom.\n\ntried to opening ManInTheMiddle, HW_CONFIG_INFO_DEBUG  = \"HW_CONFIG_INFO_DEBUG\" not found.\n\n',1513090626),(472,184,144,'This could have been an issue because the controller was never restarted after it was updated to the latest version.\n\nWe just restarted the programs that needed to be restarted, so give it about 15 minutes and you should start seeing data for the tank adjustments and inventory reports show up.\n\n-Regards\nBryan',1513090911),(473,174,144,'First, can we confirm that their is a light on the tank module that is blinking? The range extender is communicating, but the sensor board readings are not coming in.',1513091590),(474,184,192,'View the location from support.com can only view Tank inventory, none of the other reports are available.\n\n',1513270382),(475,182,3,'Appears from the tank adjustment reports the tank monitor quit working 12/16/17.\n\n',1513806840),(476,185,3,'EH Wolfs customer information:\n Michels Corp., twschnei@michels.us  pw:123456',1514992261),(477,185,144,'The controller is not making a proper remote connection to transfer the data which I assume has to do with the network\'s firewall.\n\nCan we have them unblock port 3306 and 443 for the following IP: 52.24.203.205 (oilcopsupport.com)?\n\n-Bryan\n\n\n\n',1514998200),(478,185,3,'This is the customer we already sent the following email to:\n\nIP address 52.24.203.205 for OilCopSupport.com  \n\nThe following ports need to be unblocked from outbound traffic  80, 8080, 480, 465? \nWe use these ports to communicate with oilcopsupport.com to back up the OilCop system each hour, monitor of the system is running and to send email notifications and reports. \n\nI will resend the email asking them to confirm.\n\n\n',1515001834),(479,185,144,'In addition, add 443 and 3306 to that email. 3306 is a port used for direct database communication and 443 is for https (secure http).',1515002322),(480,185,3,'Just noticed you added port 3306 and 443 is that in addition to 480 & 465?\n',1515002431),(481,185,3,'You must have been writing when i sent this. \nWill let them know.',1515002521),(482,182,3,'Changed CDM and serial cable 1/3/18\n',1515172071),(483,184,3,'Dennis, to view the other reports first must select the location from the drop down menu at top of the page.',1515174819),(484,187,26,'2 additional photos',1515454344),(485,187,26,'(10) Photos total and (2) layouts. Red annotations were added to aid in identification of OilCop components.\n\nThe file labeled \"UniversalMitsubishiLayoutOilCop\" is to scale but placement of OilCop components are approximate and Controller/CDM is not pictured.',1515455066),(486,187,3,'Shawn,\nThank you for the write up, photos and drawings. \nGive the team a little bit to digest this.\n\nMy first thought is to install the range extender in the south west corner of the east shop and note the RSSI values for all devices. Then move the extender to in the middle of the east shop and note the RSSI values for all devices. Then locate the extender at the location that gave you the best reception during your test.\nThen unplug the CDM and power all of the oil cop devices. Then plug in the CDM and Range extender and note there RSSI values, next turn on in this order the tank monitor, FCM#3, FCM#1, FCM#2 noting the RSSI values as each device is added. After each device is added give the system 10 minutes before reading the RSSI values and turning on the next device.\nIt will be interesting to see if the overall values improve as the other modules come on line.  \n\nTo set up the range extender set the physical address and then go to Admin/System Configuration/Hardware Configuration and manually add the range extender by pressing the + Add button and enter the range extenders address. \n',1515504073),(487,52,81,'TEST JANUARY, 10th 2018 - T_2_42\n\nscenario: multiproduct OFF, multidispense ON, autoclose ON\nWO: WO# = DIS#052, created from PC, all technicians,all assigned stations,75W90 (available only on station#2), preset 3 liters, quantity blocked\n\ntechnician TEST1 (assigned only to station#1) logs in, presses #1 for WO selection: he finds in the list WO# DIS#052, while he should not be able to see it!\nIf he selects this WO, system asks to select one of the products available on station#1.\nPreset is not asked, as system is using the configured preset, even if we are dispensing another product.\n\nthis discrepancy is still waiting to be fixed.',1515570452),(488,62,81,'TEST JANUARY, 10th 2018 - T_2_42\n\nscenario: multiproduct OFF, multidispense ON, autoclose ON\nWO: WO# = DIS#062, created from PC, all technicians,all assigned stations,75W90 (available only on station#2), preset 3 liters, quantity blocked\n\ntechnicia Test1 logs in on PC, ask for WO selection and select the WO.\nSystem returns the error \"You are not assigned to the stations where the product is present\" ==> OK\n\ndiscrepancy closed',1515570744),(489,78,81,'TEST JANUARY, 10th 2018 - T_2_42\n\nscenario: multiproduct OFF, multidispense ON, autoclose ON\nWO: WO# = DIS#078, created from PC, all technicians,all assigned stations, all products, quantity blocked\n\nthe technician selects the WO from PC, selects a station but aborts the WO before starting the dispense ==>\n-the WO is still assigned to all users and can be selected by any other user (OK)\n-the WO looks assigned to all stations and configured for all products, while if it is selected by someone on TAC this user is automatically brought to dispense page, with the previously selected product and on the previously selected reel.\n-on PC the behavior is correct, user can selects the WO and choose any other station and any other product\n\ndiscrepancy not fixed',1515571456),(490,86,81,'concerning this, we would need to know the situation for mini-remote display...otherwise this will become a little more urgent.\n\n(anyway, this modification will be required even after mini-remote displays will be available, as in some case the customer does not want to use mini-remote displays but prefers to have standard display.',1515571641),(491,95,81,'we would like to discuss this, because we find in new releases some new features not requested like tank monitor solution (not requested, useless for European market) and like tank history report (which is by the way not explained anywhere, we don\'t know how it works, how it has to be used), while somediscrepancies are still waiting to be fixed and while there still are some bugs in \"standard\" use',1515572507),(492,98,81,'it looks like it is closed, we are not able to replicate the issue at the moment',1515572967),(493,99,81,'TEST JANUARY, 10th 2018 - T_2_42\n\nscenario: multiproduct OFF, multidispense ON, autoclose ON\nWO: WO# = DIS#099, created from PC, all technicians,all assigned stations, AdBlue (available only on station#3, on 2 reels - FCM and PSM phisically connected to a real pump in our testing room - k-factor around 1.005, so REAL situation), preset 8 liters, quantity blocked\nstock: actual stock 55 liters (before dispensing), shutoff level = 50 liters.\n\nthe system allows the dispense (see discrepancy#101)\n\nthe system stops automatically the solenoid once we reach 5.0 liters (OK) but in the dashboard we still see the tank as in RE-ORDER level, while it should be red for shutoff.\nThe system does not allow to make topoff or another dispense, ok. (error 006 - amount error)\n\ndiscrepancy still to be fixed.',1515574229),(494,100,81,'TEST JANUARY, 10th 2018 - T_2_42\n\nsame as for discrepancy #99\n\nif you try to make a dispense after you reached the shutoff level (but system show yellow re-order level), the system does not return an error 006 like from TAC, but simply states \"starting the pump was unsuccessful\"\n\ndiscrepancy still to be fixed',1515574423),(495,101,81,'TEST JANUARY, 10th 2018 - T_2_42\n\nthe system allows you to dispense with a preset amount which is greater than the difference between the actual inventory and the shutoff level.\nIt must return an error, or at least a warning message stating that the max quantity available to be dispensed is X\n\ndiscrepancy to be fixed',1515574521),(496,105,81,'still open since March 2017 without any comments. To be fixed urgently, as all discrepancies concerning report area, since we have a lot of customers asking these reports to work',1515574617),(497,112,81,'wait for comments and fix',1515574645),(498,113,81,'this has been fixed, even if double filtering with date + name is not working.\nI will close this and open a new one for this',1515574735),(499,114,81,'for this we can find now the reported action when a WO is deleted, which is good also because is reporting the WO#.\nPlease comment about other actions on WO',1515574878),(500,116,81,'still need to be fixed.\nWe are wondering where the odometer information asked before dispensing is going to...',1515574965),(501,118,81,'still waiting to be fixed',1515575009),(502,126,81,'wait to be fixed',1515575037),(503,127,81,'fixed for dropdown research.\nmust make a standard name for the \"product\" column, why here is different from other reports?\nPRODUCT is ok instead of PRODUCT NAME.',1515575209),(504,129,81,'it shows more than 50 WO using the pages logic, which is ok for us.\nwe can close this discrepancy',1515575313),(505,142,81,'what is the status of this discrepancy?\nwe are still in the condition that the tech can\'t decide where to take the product if it ahs been already dispensed.\nAs Sébastien answered, if we are on multidispense the tech should be able to decide each time where to take the product (obviously following the configuration of the system, meaning that he can choose only between the stations he is assigned to).\n\nIf we are with autoclose OFF and noone closes the WO, he must be able to select the station each time, unless the station was assigned by the manager from PC.\n- WO created from PC bu manager, assigned to all tech and to all assigned stations ==> WO stays assigned to all assigned stations, but it is assigned to the tech who selected it.\n- WO created from TAC by user ==> WO is assigned to this user, user can select the station each time he selects this WO from the 2nd dispense on\n\nIf we are with autoclose ON, manager must each time a new dispense is required go to re-open the WO, which stays always assigned to the user and to all assigned stations (if it was so at the beginning).\n\nIn all cases, manager can decide to change user, in this case the first user won\'t be able to see it (unless manager switch again to all users)\nIn all cases, manager can decide to assign a specific station, in this case the WO must be dispensed from this station',1515576162),(506,143,81,'we close this discrepancy as it is the same of #78.\nthe 2nd bug it was reported in the past...maybe discrepancy #49 or similar... I think that fixing the #78 the second one won\'t appear.',1515576340),(507,147,81,'communication tested with rebooting the controller: all components recognized quite immediately ==> ok\n\ntested with disconnecting one device, it took about 30s to recognize it was disconnected, but ok\n\ntested with reconnecting the device, recognized quite immediately, ok\n\n\ndiscrepancy closed',1515576719),(508,148,81,'still waiting for this discrepancy.\n\ntested again with multiproduct, returning \"T. Unknown\" on the ticket most of the times.\n\nNot understanding why sometimes it\'s reporting the correct user and sometimes no, we tried 3 similar events but not found out a logic. Need to test deeper this.',1515577593),(509,151,81,'TEST JANUARY, 10th 2018 - T_2_42\n\nscenario: multiproduct OFF, multidispense ON, autoclose ON\nWO: WO# = DIS#151, created from PC, all technicians,all assigned stations,85W140 (available only on station#2), preset 3 liters, quantity blocked\n\nuser selects the WO, makes the dispense and asks for topoff. The quantity reaches the max topoff allowed value and the TAC returns to login page, like the autoclose worked. But on software the WO results still open and the WO can be selected again (automatically on open dispense but closing at the previous preset value). Reached that quantity and not asking for topoff, the WO is closed automatically.\n\nTested the same againtwice , the WO has been closed. Exactly with same steps!\nso first time we tested it was not working, then 2 times it worked...honestly I don\'t know what to say...\n\nI will close the discrepancy, but with the possibility to re-open it immediately if it happens again during the tests...',1515578367),(510,163,81,'same with T_2_42, range extender must be added manually because it\'s not recognized by auto-scan',1515578677),(511,187,26,'On Wednesday, I tested each situation described above except power cycling each component in the order described since getting to FCM1 & FCM2 is very difficult.\nResults of testing with range extender:\n\n1.Powered cycled FCM#3 and TMM\n   -FCM#3 & TMM would not connect\n2.Plugged Range Extender into Southwest corner of East shop\n   -3 Bars on FCM1, 2 & range extender / FCM#3 & TMM not connected\n3.Plugged Range Extender into middle of East shop\n   -3 Bars on FCM1, 2 & range extender/ FCM#3 & TMM not connected\n4.Plugged Range Extender into tank room\n   -3 Bars on FCM1, 2 & range extender / FCM#3 & TMM not connected\n5.Power cycled CDM\n   -3 Bars/ FCM#3 came online, TMM not connected\n6.Moved TMM out of tank room and temporarily installed in service bay next to FCM#3\n   -TMM not connected\n7.Reinstallled TMM in tank room and changed address to 4\n   -TMM connected\n8.Repeated 2-4 above\n   -Same results as above except with the extender in the southwest corner of the East shop, FCM2 andFCM3 dropped to 2 bars and everything else was 3 bars.\n\nLong story short it seems changing the TMM from address 1 to 4 allowed it to reconnect.  I did this so every component no matter its type had a unique address.  I deleted the range extender from the system since it did not seem to help.  We will see if this continues to work.  ',1515801619),(512,189,3,'TSM_3_0_0 is the current TMM firmware version, however we do have a small update to T_2_42 that has some modifications to probe definitions that will be available for down load by end of the week.\n\nWe have found the specific gravity values for lubricants vary from what lubricant manufacture published, consequently we have found to achieve best accuracy use the specific gravity setting as a “calibration factor” used adjusted to make the display read correctly when setting up the tank for the first time.\nCalibration instructions are on page 29 of the tank monitor installation guide that can be down loaded from the User Manual tab on oilcopsupport.com \n',1516113104),(513,187,3,'Noticed FCM 1 (East Shop) has a weak signal would it be possible to add the range extender back to southwest corner of the shop for a week or so. \nAfter the range extender has been installed, would like to power cycle (FCM-1).\n',1516115161),(514,189,81,'ok, then there is a big problem: did you ever check the 21\' probes? We tested 2 and both gave a value of 72cm while it had to be 0!!! it\'s too big to be an accuracy error, it\'s an offset, don\'t know if due to wrong algorythm, wrong signal conversion, wrong scale...\nIn any case, we need this to be fixed at soonest then, we cannot accept a probe that reeds 0.7m wrong!',1516115426),(515,189,3,'Yes, we have tested and have installed 21\' probes and they functioning properly.\n\nYou will need to install a small update to T_2_42 that has some modifications to probe definitions that will be available for you tp down load before end of the week.',1516116084),(516,175,26,'I have removed FCM #1 to send in for repair.  Please provide RMA#.',1516179284),(517,175,3,'Please use RGA 973758M\nThank you,\n',1516281662),(518,189,81,'hello, we installed the new firmware, but this issue is still the same.\nWe tested firmware 3_0_1 with R_22 and with T_42\n\n21\' sensor is giving a signal different from 0. We tested 3 different probes.\n\nIf you use a working 6\' sensor and set it as 21\', the signal changes, from 0 to something different (and high, not a small change).\nIf you set the 21\' probe tas 6\', the signal becomes 0.\n\nSo this means that it\'s not a problem due to defective sensor or to a defective channel on TSM, it means that the algorythm for 21\' is converting the tension/current equivalent to 0 inot something different from 0.\nI don\'t know if the sensor is giving a signal 0-5V or 0-20/4-20mA or something else. But when it is giving the lower level of signla, the 21\' setting on the software makes it changing into a signal different from 0.\n\nI have a 21\' probe working on R_21 and this was not happening, unless I didn\'t notice when I made that configuration.\n\nIn any case, please check now this with new version and new firmware and with 21\' probes and check what happens.\n\nWe tested this with 2 different systems, one here in my office and one in France (on customer\'s site, not for testing, it\'s urgent) and it\'s happening always the same.',1516630503),(519,189,144,'Hello - you said that you tried withT_42 and R_22. There was a new T version pushed out (T_43). Can you try with that version if you have not already. If that doesn\'t work, can I get the tank configurations and sensor configurations',1516679405),(520,189,81,'hi Bryan, updated to T_2_43 (it gave me a database error the first time, re-updated and went well - I will send you an email with pictures just for check)\n\nthe signal is correctly 0 now with probe configured as 21\' sensor\n\nwe need a R version at soonest because the customer has 3 tanks over 8\', and it\'s very important he can have the tank monitoring working',1516696227),(521,175,26,'The 2nd repaired FCM has was installed Feb 7th but could not be tested until yesterday.  The FCM now functions properly.',1521744883),(522,187,26,'A wired Range Extender has been installed on the TMM and was working flawlessly as of yesterday.  However the FCM for the Oil Bar would not connect until it(FCM #3) and the CDM were powered cycled.  I will keep this discrepancy open until the customer can confirm the fix holds.\nAttached image of RangeExtender',1521747205),(523,190,3,'ok',1524845543),(524,182,3,'Customer has called several times to inform us the tank monitor has not changed all tank value for several days. Reboot the system fixes it temporally. CDM and serial cable replacement did not change symptom.  \nChanged Controller problem reoccurred 2 days after replacement, reinstalled original  controller.\nTank Module-2 device status has had red device status last few times when i checked in, reboot seems to clear the error.\nThis morning reboot cleared up the error however the Used Oil made a 269 gallon deduct adjustment. Luckly this error is in our favor this time, however this could have gone the other way and overfilled the tank! \n\nWill replace TMM-2, should clear up the intermittent red status for TMM-2 maybe resolve the issue   \n ',1525869669),(525,192,3,'Turned on Auto close work-order feature because techs were not closing work orders.\n\nAlso found the 5W/30 Eco and 5W/20 XHD product labels were flip flopped corrected labels and updated tank type and size.',1526565258),(526,193,144,'At want point or points are they getting 255 errors? For example, are they seeing a majority of 255 errors at login, when selecting the work order, or when starting a dispense?\n\nWere the TAC and FCM was showing green status for connection during this time as well?',1526661476),(527,192,3,'Received call this AM (5/24/18 7:45 and :47) dispensed with out registering, found broken wire connection at the pulses.\nJim Taylor mentioned yesterday afternoon 5/23 4:16 PM transact log) he tried to dispense 5.0 qt but the system stopped at 4.8Qt, the log says 5.0Qt.\nhe said it also happened to him yesterday morning (5/23 10:18) he tried to dispense 5.0 qt but the system stopped at 4.8Qt., the log says 5.0qt.\n\nMight be a good location to test the solution..',1527176930),(528,194,3,'Shawn, Thank you for taking the time to write this up..\nThe team will look in to this tonight.\nDo you think its possible the  PSMs was bypassing even-though the bypass was closed?\nWe have had a couple PSM bypass even-though the bypass valve was securely closed, ever since we discovered this we have been testing 100% of the PSM we ship out. ',1527617054),(529,194,26,'No, I tested the PSM numerous times when I was trying to get the Alemite in line meters to match as close as possible to the PSM\'s which required numerous dispenses and each time the PSM shutoff as expected.(With the meter being held open)  ',1527628769),(530,194,3,'So far what we have figurged out:\n\n R.O. numbers were mixed up. First, the 86035 was the one that showed no dispense, and 86001 was the one that had 2 dispenses.\n\nFor 86001 (the one that showed 2 dispenses), how the current settings are multiproduct ON and multidispense ON, this allows the technicians to dispense the same product multiple times. The preset that is set by the manager in this mode just makes it so that the technician is not able to dispense more than that amount in a single dispense. It does not stop them from redoing the dispense though. There are a few options to go. One is turn multidispense OFF and leave multiproduct ON. This lets the technician only dispense a single product per work order once, so this makes it so that the technician will not be able to dispense extra of that fluid without the manager intervening. The other option is to turn multiproduct OFF and leave multidispense ON and Autoclose OFF. This configuration will let the technician pump the same fluid that the manager setup until the preset is reached. Once the preset is reached, the work order closes. However, they will not be able to setup multiple products per work order. We saw they do have some cases where they end up have multiple products per work order, so I don\'t know if this configuration will work for them.\n\nAs for 86035, we are still searching through the 1.4GB log file that would have the collection of dispenses since the last time the controller reset. I\'m seeing if any of the information collected there can give me insight as to why 86035 did not show up with a dispense.\n',1527767212),(531,196,1,'Can you please reply with the MAC address you are trying to set up.',1528987378),(532,197,1,'It appears the email is currently in use by a customer under Arrowtech Marketing. I have attached a screenshot showing this. Would you like me to delete this customer so you may update the new distributor\'s email?',1528987892),(533,182,3,'Root cause: Controller was plugged into the same 115 Vac outlet the compressed air refrigerated dryer was plugged into. Plugged controller into different outlet problem resolved..\nYay!\n ',1529065678),(534,198,3,'Transaction Journal report has a lot of PHP errors, Work Order Status: is it possible to reduce the margins to reduce some of the Text wrapping and if its not to much trouble maybe see if we could the line between Product name and Amount Dispensed?   Attachment',1530108905),(535,198,3,'Summary Report- after page one each page 1-10 displays on tank per page .',1530109147),(536,198,3,'When reports and notifications are emailed the first page is a 8 1/2\" x 11\" OilCop Logo.\nCan we make smaller or remove the logo?  ',1530109399),(537,198,3,'Daily Report - Not sure where the delivery data is coming from but its not correct.\nFor now lets remove Variance until we have time to fix and further testing.',1530110623),(538,198,3,'When attempting to download Tank History report - \"This Page isn\'t working\"',1530111041),(539,198,3,'Tank History report will will only print top graph, not any of the data on bottom of the page',1530111225),(540,198,3,'Print - Daily Report bottom data does not appear.',1530111785),(541,198,3,'Print- Summary Report- Is it possible to have a page break between pie graphs and current inventory ',1530111911),(542,198,3,'Regarding daily report- Delivery data appears to be from manually added inventory. Will not display delivery when tank monitor is installed.',1530112293),(543,198,3,'Print - Tank Adjustments Is it possible to reduce Manual/Automatic Column and make the Amount column wider?',1530112506),(544,198,3,'Print - Action Journal can right left margins be smaller, maybe add a little margin on the top and bottom.',1530114465),(545,199,3,'If Manager selects product and leaves preset open, with Unlock- ON, the system forces user to open dispense even though users capabilities is only set for preset. Modify to force preset.\n\nUser Capabilities: Preset, Load, Select \n\nAdmin dispense settings settings:\nWork Order Top Off - Off\nJob Recipe Top Off - Off\nAuto Close Work Order - Off\nMultiple Products per Work Order - On\nMultiple Dispense - ON\n\n',1530204114),(546,199,3,'Clarification- Currently the system allows a dispense to be deleted from (adjust work orders page by pressing the minis sign right of the row with name of product and preset amount), need to modify so after any product is dispensed the system will not allow that product to be deleted from the work order.',1530207356),(547,199,3,'Zach is testing combinations of Admin dispense settings along with Tech Capability settings. Most configurations have been OK, however this configuration needs a little work not sure how simple or difficult the fix will be. See attached report. \nAlso created system database back up  6/28/18  1:52PM on the NADA test system.\n\nController Test 5- \nThe system added transactions that did not happen which, in turn, cause products to reach MAX that truly had not and, worse yet, removed product that had not been dispensed. At first, I thought that ATF wasn’t being allowed to reach MAX for some unknown reason, but debunked that by checking, via ADMIN, the max dispense per work order. I saw that I was reaching said max and adjusted accordingly. I did not run into any issues after that. \n\nThe other 3 work orders worked exactly as they should have and reacted as expected from previous testing. The main issue, as with the other tests, is deleted previously dispensed products from a work order. The reports will delete the information of deleted dispenses, but the tanks will read the same. You have made a dispense and the tanks agree, but the reports do not so you would somehow ‘gain’ product that isn’t there. \n\nAlso, is there some sort of trigger that engages Auto Close even when disabled? Is an order meant to close itself when a product reaches MAX dispense? Even when there are other products on the work order to be dispensed, but they have not yet been? \n',1530211628),(548,199,3,'Was testing to see if Multiple user update was installed and experienced what Zach described in the controller Test 5-. \nWO multipaluser 08:30AM - See screen shots and backed up the system 6/25 8:37. ',1530280412),(549,198,3,'Summary Report - Default work orders to All Work Orders must select split.\nWhen printing tank volumes they do not fit inside of margins. Please check all reports format so all printing fits inside of margins\n',1530303108),(550,198,3,'Transaction Report Export 2 - Pages need to have same format, columns missing on some pages. The first and last page of the 72 page report are the pages filled with printing. Consolidate pages.\n',1530303754),(551,198,3,'Daily Report 2 - Report needs to be formatted with columns and rows. Daily report should only show information for one day maybe get open and close information based on Shift set up by setting Daily Open and Close times.\n\nConfirm delivery amount is calculated correctly - tank monitor should provide net delivery amount, that is calculated by recording tank volume before delivery and recording tank volume after delivery net change equals delivery volume. System needs to subtract any product that was pumped from the tank while filling the tank. - If not using tank monitor record the amount managers manually adds to the tank. \nInstead of only using the word delivery use the word Tank Delivery.\nAdjustments = Manual Subtractions or Additions made by the manager.\nShow Work Order Summary and list all Open work orders and Closed for the day. \n ',1530305462),(552,200,3,'T_46_Test_7_TAC\nAdministrative Options: \nOff/On/On/Off \n\nWith this configuration, from the TAC, having Multi Dispense disabled does not seem to matter unless you are trying to Multi Dispense to very last product line item.\n\nFrom W/O: Off/On/On/Off 6, I dispensed one product successfully, went back into the work order and changed the original product to a different product. The new product, on the same line item within the order, could not be dispensed. It had not been dispensed previously, but I think the system saw that line item number one had been dispensed and could not be again. The fact that it was a new product did not matter. When Multi Dispense is enabled, does it focus on the line item or the product? I then reverted the first line item back to its original product and added a second line item and product. The system reacted strangely and pumped 10W/30 when it should have been 0W/20. The second line item worked as it should. It seemed as if the system was remembering what the work order USED to be before being changed, i.e. not dispensing a new product from the same line item thinking it was the same product as before and dispensing the previously changed line item when the line item had been changed back to its original product. It’s like a lag in information maybe?\n\nStated previously and shown in the work orders, if there are multiple products on a work order multi dispense does not matter until you reach the last product line item. All other products were dispensed until MAX. \nAuto Close is also strange from the TAC. You always have the option to either Keep Open or Close. Unlike completing orders from the Controller where if Auto Close is enabled a pop-up will appear stating Work Order Closed. If you click Keep Open with multiple products you can keep dispensing, except for the last product. Sometimes, though, if you click Keep Open and you attempt to open the order again it will display Error 009. Is this the TACs version of Auto Close? Possible to have the same pop-up saying Work Order Closed and must hit Enter on the TAC to acknowledge?\n\nLike other tests, deleting a work order puts the previously used product back into the tank. The exception to this rule is if one deletes a product from the work order before deleting the work order. The deleted transactions will disappear from the journals but stay removed from the tanks. Any transactions that are deleted prior to deleting the work order will not be returned to the tank and the readings will be inaccurate. Also, why are transaction journalized if there is no dispense? Is it necessary to show a dispense of 0 in the journals?\n\n',1530641269),(553,200,3,'I think it would be a good idea to to see zero dispense transactions to aid trouble shooting. Pre-dispense time out to fast, or reed switch failed in the pulser/meter.',1530641711),(554,200,3,'OilCop T_46 Test 8\n\nVery simple configuration that is hard to mess up. Once a work order is loaded and a product is chosen it cannot be changed but can be dispensed multiple times until that product has reached its MAX dispense point. You cannot change the original line item from one product to another. Unlike the previous configuration, the Auto Close feature does engage after each dispense from the TAC. Once a product has reached MAX, the work order can no longer be re-opened. Like other tests, when a work order is deleted from the system, any dispensed product is then returned to its respective tank. Zero issues within the journal system with this configuration. Worked exactly as it should have. ',1530810344),(555,200,3,'OilCop T_46 Test 9\nWhen used correctly, this configuration worked as it should. Again, when messing around with a work order and changing line items to different products, deleting products and then adding them back in is when things start to go awry.\n\nWhen running a work order as All Products and All Stations and a TECH picks the product and station they want those parameters can no longer be changed. The system will always think that what the TECH is dispensing is the first chosen product and station, even if the order was closed and re-opened and different product and stations were selected.\n\nRan into a weird bug where I added products to an order that was previously All Products and All Stations. After products were dispensed the TJ did not log them into the system. The WOS did, however. I cannot think of a reason why the TJ did not tally those dispenses.\n\nDeleting products should still be avoided. Doing so removes those transaction from the logs, but does not get returned to its tank as it would if the entire work order was deleted. \n',1530814311),(556,200,3,'Job Recipes Testing\n\nPutting in either the MGR or ADMIN pin to override the MAX dispense point does not work. The system still does not allow a dispense over MAX.\n\nFrom the TAC using a job recipe with no preset the TECH could Open Dispense without the capability set up via the ADMIN. Using the same recipe from the controller, the TECH is forced to put in a preset. I did change the TECH capabilities and turned Open Dispense on to test from the controller and it did work.\n\nAll job recipes were set up for and performed by Tommy Tech, but in the Transaction Journal some of the dispenses don’t have the TECH name attached to them, but say they were completed by All Technicians.\n\nIt didn’t seem to make a difference, but I did run job recipes from all four of the configurations that we previously tested. The recipes only run one product at a time and close after every dispense so the configuration doesn’t seem to matter regarding recipes. \n',1530887379),(557,201,3,'\n8:44a extender 2 and 3 red for 5 -20 min, rebooted the system had to have them cycle the power to get team viewer up. They plugged the controller into the UPS for their server.\n11:07a wo 123123-123 pump 300 Qt everything worked properly,\n11:22 wo123123-123 #2 RED quit updating just before 49.2 quarts\n11:49 TAC 1 255 error when loading pass word and loading work order, at 11:50a  wo 569531-000 second try was able to dispense 300.6 qt. \n\n11:50 Debugger screen shot- notice new display values in order- 298.7, 299.9, 300.1, 299.1, 299.3\n\n11:59 Debugger Screen shot – watiching the debug feed HE-3 seemed to pause, Ctrl C serail port fail then Serial port open\n\n1:42p wo 274965-001 TK-3 reel #52  1st attempt successfully started did not pump anything, 2nd attempt 1:50 wo 274965-001 TK-3 reel #54  pumped 40 Qt., 3rd attempt/dispense 1:58p wo 274965-001 TK-3 reel #54 pumped 3qt. From workorder Maintenance screen it shows the 1st attempt and combined the 2nd and 3rd dispenses (43qt).\n\n3:07 Ctrl C – 3:07 Debug Screen Shot watiching the debug feed noticed RM: annot remove ‘/var/www/files/syncronize/*’: No such file or directory. Pressed Ctrl C indicated serial fail, then serail Port Open.\n\n4:00P Ctrl C again.. did not get screen shot.\n\n',1531436746),(558,201,3,'When \"CDM Timeout. Restarting Serial, Serial port open\" occurs it reprints  the message 20 times.\nSee 7_12_CDM Timeout Screen Shot',1531486473),(559,198,258,'Exporting Work Order Report the formatting is off. Pages only display one transaction per page until the last couple of pages. These last couple of pages look good in parts and others the columns do not match the info displayed and the info extends past the last column. The same issues exist for the Transaction Report, also. The Action Report, however, looked to be in order.\n\nAlso, is it possible to add to the header or footer of each page the name of the report you\'re looking at? Currently the header displays the location and date/time and the footer has the page number. The only way to know what report you are looking at is to find the name on the very first page. ',1531505640),(560,201,3,'Generally a slow day at the oil ranch, oil hung out in the tanks today only 14 Qt. dispensed. Observed the debugger and device status screen thought the day. RSS values seem more stable. RED-1 dropped one time, range extender 1 and 2 both turned red 8- 10 times, one of those times both were red for about 10 minutes. about 5-8 FCMs flipped from green to red a couple of times, wireless printer was offline all day which is not unexpected because it is located two pre-stress concert walls away, need to see how feasible it would be to modify the range extender to be hard wired to a printer as we do with the TMM. \nWill be interesting to see how things do Monday.. \nNoticed no 10th in volume readings displayed on the work order screen, like in the transaction screen. We should work towards having 10th displayed. WO 260687-042 7/13 3:51 80 Qt. displayed, 80.2Qt. actually dispensed, verified in the transaction journal.  \n ',1531516351),(561,201,3,'7/16/18 Monday.\nRange extender 1, 2 and occasionally range extender 3, wiil turn red and remains off up from 30 sec. to 7 minutes before turning on.\n\n8:00A 115.00Qt 115.3Qt.\n****\n12:46p RE-1 Off, 12:53 On\n12:48p RE-2 Off, 12:51 On\n12:56p RE1 & RE-2 Off, RE-1 ON 1:03p, RE-1 Off 1:04p, RE-2 on 1:05p, RE-3 Off 1:06p, RE-1, RE-2, RE-3 On at 1:08pm same time.\n1:10p  TM-1, RE-1, RE-3 (4 bars), 1:12 RE-3 (3 bars), 1:13 RE-3 (4 Bars)\n1:11 RE- 2 Off, On 1:18\n1:17 RE-1 off, On 1:21\n1:22 RE-2 Off, On 1:27 – 4 bars\n1:26 RE-1 Off, On 1:27 – 4 bars\n1:30 TAC-11 off, On 1:32 – 4 bars\n1:36 FCM-1 off, On 1:36 – 4 bars\n2:08 TAC-11 off, On 2:08\n3:00p\n3:27 TAC-11 off, On 3:27\n3:48 RE-1, RE-2 off, On 3:53\n\n3:53 RE-1 off, On 3:58\n3:57 RE-2 off, On \n4:00 RE-1 off, On\n',1531843605),(562,201,3,'7/17/18 Tuesday\nBoth range extender 1 and 2 will turn red the same time, some times both turn green at the same time, other times they will turn green separately. When they turn red will remain off from 30 sec. to 7 minutes before turning on. \n\n7/17/18 10:56a wo 272422-002 while dispensing product CDM timeout occurred around 30 qts. , after reset system continued to pump until 43.1Q',1531859526),(563,205,3,'Had customer reboot the controller and that recovered ability to use terminal desktop.\nOpened the debugger it shows Serial Port Open, the next line says Purging files. Device status shows all devices have 4 bars?\nIs the serial port open or is normal when opening the debugger?',1532092561),(564,205,3,'When leaving the debugger screen open and then close Team Viewer session does the debugger consume memory and if left running eventually effecting performance?',1532093112),(565,202,258,'Setting controller IP to: 192.168.0.221',1532097215),(566,201,3,'Dispensing from the tank room is problematic, they can not login intermittently, will try to login again within minutes an can not. Wait 20 minutes try again will work.\n\nLooks like we will have to hard wire all of the device in the lube room back to the CDM and let all of the other devices remain on radio.. ',1532122040),(567,207,3,'1. The next update will include delivery amount, for now tank inventory can be viewed from manger or admin go to  System Logs/Tank History Report, select Weekly time frame and press submit. Line graph and daily inventory amounts are listed at the bottom of the page appears 7/24/18 11:00 the inventory was 718.3, 7/24/18 it was 72.5 thus approximately 645.50 gallons were delivered.\n\n2. It is must be turned on from Admin settings. \n\n3.Give me a little time to look into this will advise..\n',1532980244),(568,215,3,'**the amount currently in the TJ match those that were added back into each tank, but the tanks do not match the starting amounts before the testing began meaning that product was lost due to making amendments to the w/o via deleting and re-adding previously dispensed products**\n\n**was there any plan to disable the ability to delete previously dispensed products from a w/o?**\n\n\nNotes: Sort of ran into many of the same issues as the previous round of testing. I think there is a tad too much freedom in this configuration and there should be more restriction when making amendments to work orders. If a work order is created and dispensed I think the option to delete anything from that work order should be disabled and the user should only be allowed to add line items to the work order, even if that means having the same product on two line items. The total amount dispensed between the two, or however many instances of the same product, would combine until MAX is reached and another work order would have to be made for that product. Is there any possibility of disabling the subtract button for dispensed products? In some cases when I deleted products and re-added them in later I was able to dispense past MAX and in some cases I was not, but what happens in between all of that is the journals get mixed up and numbers start to not match up and so forth. When finished testing I deleted the work order and the tanks did not get back all of the product that was dispensed. \n See Controler_Test_2_R2.docx',1534249800),(569,215,258,'From Controller_Test_3_R2\n\nNotes: Two main concerns regarding this configuration. What is multi dispense tied to, product or line item? If it is supposed to concern the product then it does not work as it should as it is very easily ignored by moving a previously dispensed product to a new line item. If it is only concerned with the line item then it works a bit better, but it still wouldn’t be working properly due to using All Products and All Stations on the same w/o 3 times using a different product each time. I’m not sure I’m understanding correctly how multi dispense being disabled should work. In my opinion, it should be only concerned with the product. No matter the line item, if that product has been dispensed then it can no longer be dispensed again on that w/o anymore at all.\n\nSecondly, and again, deleting previously dispensed products should not be an option. As we’ve seen on other tests deleting line items from a w/o causes serious problems with the journal systems and if, for whatever reason, an order gets deleted wholly from the system the numbers are more than likely wrong and inventory will be incorrect.\n',1534254671),(570,215,258,'From Controller_Test_4_R2\n\nNotes: Not much testing to be done here as this is a very limited config. Once an order is made it cannot be modified except for the amount of product to dispense. If the w/o is first opened as All Products and All Stations and the user chooses whichever product or station they want, when re-opening the w/o it will now be set to those parameters and cannot be changed. Only one product can be used per w/o and dispensed until MAX and then a new order is required to continue.\n\nThis config works as it should. There is no option to add or delete products which takes away the largest concern, in my opinion, from the other configs in that product can get lost when fooling around with the w/o too much. Product from deleted w/o go back into their respective tanks and the journal coordinate nicely.',1534260452),(571,215,258,'From Controller_Test_5_R2\n\nNotes: This config worked quite a bit better than what I can remember. All seemed to work well until, again, I began deleting products and line items from the orders. The system handled changing between products and flip-flopping them just fine. The Auto Close feature is a little strange as it closes orders when a product reaches MAX and it completely disregards that there are other products yet to be dispensed. The system will close the order anyway. This horse is dead by now but deleting dispensed products from an order should 100% not be an available option. I think it will solve most of the issues that have been found during testing.',1534282934),(572,215,258,'Uploaded Exported Report from OilCop. Spreadsheets still only show one or two lines before moving to next page.',1534340015),(573,215,258,'When clicking \'Download\' button on \'Daily Reports\' page it does not download the report, but instead opens a new internet tab that takes you to the OilCop dashboard.\n\nMark also noted that the \'Delivery\' section of the \'Daily Reports\' is empty. Should it be showing something for all of the tank adjustments I\'ve been making during testing?',1534340563),(574,215,3,'Tank Adjustment Report will not sort by date and time.\nIf there is more than one page for a report multi-pal page numbers are listed on the bottom of the page however the font needs to have a color such as Black.. \nSee Page number button picture',1534941626),(575,215,3,'Summary Report - Can 3 pages be consolidated into 1 or 2 pages?\n\nTank History report has extra blank page\n ',1534947146),(576,215,3,'When printing OilCop Work Order Status reports top header names are not lined up with their perspective columns, volumes are not on the same line as unit of measure and AM/PM are not on the same line as time. \nWork order status displays each transaction within a work order, how much of an issue would it be to have the web team change “Role” to “Dispense”, then column under Dispense change from “Technician” to “Date” / “Time” of the particular transaction within the work order. Or something for a future update? \nAttch: WorkOrder Status\n',1534970070),(577,215,3,'Need to disable ability to delete transaction from a work orders once product has been dispensed.\n\nTested six variations all but two configurations seems to function correctly.\n\nMP- ON, MD-ON, AC-ON\nMgr. can load multiple products, Tech. can dispense one of the two products loaded by Mgr. multiple times as long as they don’t dispense the other product, once the second product is dispensed, system auto closes WO.   Not OK** hummm, not sure how to handle. Need to discuss. \nTech. can load multiple products, Tech. can dispense one of the two products loaded multiple times as long as they don’t dispense the other product, once the second product is dispensed, system auto closes WO.   Not OK** hummm, not sure how to handle. Need to discuss.\n\nMP- ON, MD-OFF, AC-ON\nMgr. load multiple products, Tech. can dispense multiple products. loaded by Mgr. one time. OK  \n(Note: Need to disable ability to delete transaction from work order once product has been dispensed).\nTech. can load multiple products, but Tech. can only dispense one of the products they loaded.  Not OK** Can only dispense one product, should be able to dispense each product one time. \n  \n',1535115692),(578,215,3,'Regarding MP-ON, MD-ON, AC-ON above, seems there is a logic conflict with  MD-ON and AC-ON. \nMaybe we should program to prevent this combination from being selected?',1535135650),(579,216,3,'Reviewing the daily report, what is the time period for \"Amount Dispensed\"? Should display the last 24 hours (Daily Report), or do we need to set up daily start and stop times? \nThere are two sets of \"Current Inventory\" one is a bar graph indicating a certain amount that dose not agree with another amount in the same current Inventory row? are they the same value?\nUntil we understand better how/if the Variance works maybe we should only display Zero.\n\n \n',1536587960),(580,207,26,'I have confirmed OilCop has been updated and is showing Increase and Decrease in reports.   Delivery amounts can be seen in the Tank Adjustment report as \"Automatic\" \"Increase\"',1536599657),(581,216,62,'There are multiple things here: \n1. Reports Displaying incorrect value (going above capacity)- By end of October \n2. Adjusting the tank inventory when automatic fill-up happens when a probe is pulled out and tolerance needs to be adjusted. - Needs to be discussed as this will require to create logic, process and will require testing. \n',1538497168),(582,216,62,'Second Para graph of the discrepancy moved to new discrepancy 218',1538497818),(583,216,62,'The third paragraph - Created a new discrepancy 219 for that issue. ',1538498054),(584,219,62,'For an Automatic system to work these two settings need to be set:\n1. Delivery Acknowledgement timeout\n2. Tank monitor solution timeout. \nAdmin>system settings> timeout configuration>\n\nPlease check with these settings and update if needed. ',1538498292),(585,218,62,'This needs more discussion on what\'s needed. Will schedule it on Friday meeting. ',1538499136),(586,221,315,'This record was saved even though an error was thrown, see # 222',1538658379),(587,218,315,'What triggers tank adjustments in the Tank Adjustment report to be made Manual or Automatic? Tank Adjustment reports for United BMW Atlanta, Ga and Don Hattan Chevrolet both show “Automatic” all tanks are on the tank monitor whereas the NADA test system shows all “Manual”, even though one tank is on the monitor and three tanks are not on the monitor. Additionally Bakersfield truck center has three tanks using the monitor and two tanks not using the monitor and their reports only show manual update.. Would it be a difficult thing to show automatic updates for any tank using the monitor, even though some of the tanks are not using the monitor?',1538663594),(588,224,315,'Looks like the users are not getting an email to reset their password even though site states it was successfully sent to the user.',1539705929),(589,224,3,'The customer would like an update resolving this issue, the salesman can not login into to his customers system to see if they need to send them some oil..\n',1540315582),(590,224,144,'Mark - Oilcopsupport was updated with new email code about 15 minutes ago and we are now receiving on emails outside of Gmail. Some of the emails still go to spam which we are still working on. However, the customer should be able to request the password and get the email. Sometimes the email is sent instantly and sometimes it takes a few minutes (let them know to check their junk mail).',1540387631),(591,226,144,'The reports are set for quarts and the reels are set to dispense liters. It looks like it did dispense with liters. 7.5 Quarts does equal the 7 liters they would have had set. It must have dispense 7.1 liters as it logged 7.5 Quarts. He also do another dispense (not a top off) at 0.3 Quarts (or ~0.3 liters) for a total of 7.4 liters or 7.8 quarts. Could the car still have had oil in it because the logs are showing that it didn\'t reach 8.1 Liters like it was intended to. Another thought would be could the reels also need calibration? Are there other known instances of the work orders at PAG going over significantly?\n\nAs for the numbers not showing up, the device may have momentarily lost communication and picked it back up as soon as he went to re dispense.\n\n',1542204618),(592,227,144,'Teamviewered in this morning and I am seeing the range extender and tank monitor online (no flashing lights). If a range extender was switching between red and green, then that means it has a TMM attached to it and the range extender is not able to connect to the CDM wirelessly. Where is this range extender located in relation to other devices? Could there have been something environmental like a vehicle that was parked in front of that range extenders spot momentarily? ',1542205148),(593,227,3,'Note from the customer: Installer came out this morning and fixed the issue that we had. We encountered a power distribution issue that was causing the extender to go up and down. He moved the extender and everything is functioning as normal.\nI suspect they had the range extender plugged into 220 Vac. ',1542296344),(594,226,3,'The PSM K factor was based on SAE 30 at 70 Deg. so when pumping fluids that are thinner i.e. 0W/10, 0W/20, 0W/40 ATF more fluid will slip by the engineered tolerance of the meter chamber and oval gear compared to SAE 30. Or less if pumping a thicker fluid than SAE 30.\nThis why we have the ability to calibrate, so ordered a 2.5 Gallon measure graduated in both quarts and litters, will ship this to several different locations and calibrate different fluids. With this information will add a table of K factors of various fluids that can be manually updated in the calibration desktop. ',1542296988),(595,228,3,'Something to consider for possible new feature. \nTag a work order to be keep open for a settable time, monthly- annually?? Then allow other work orders to be automatically closed. If auto close is turn on in Admin.\n',1542297237),(596,225,316,'For your request of multi-product dispense, selecting back takes you back to the products page. That will only work for locations that dispense multiple products from a single bay.  Customers that move between bays to dispense different products depending on what work they have done, would request the current functionality.  Therefore at this time, if you would like this feature please raise a separate ticket and label it as \"Future Release.\"',1542751888),(597,231,144,'Hello Zach - it seems as though the password was changed. This could have been done due to having to give the password out to the customer for some reason. In teamviewer properties for Enterprise Oil - Rack\'m, I added the password you need to use to login not as guest.',1544649737),(598,230,144,'One of the tables for email scheduler locked up (t_user_email_map). Ran a repair script for that table. It is back online. That table would have had the the relationship of who will be getting what type of email. I don\'t know exactly when it locked up, but it was fine 7 days ago as it was able to get a normal backup of that table at that point (it hadn\'t been used at that point).',1544652660),(599,233,316,'Would it be possible to forward the logs to this email address:\nliquiddynamics@viaanix.com',1545258156),(600,236,144,'Are the power supplies provided with these controllers the exact same as the ones previous provided. Sometimes strange things with PCs getting stuck on bios sometimes means there is a power supply issue. If they started giving you the bad power supplies or cables again, then that could be what is causing an issue.\n\nSometimes there are also hidden boot items in BIOs that cause it to stall. Maybe they provided a different version of the bios installed in which case there is possibly a setting in BIOS that needs to be turned off or on.',1549379608),(601,236,258,'The BIOS changes on the controllers pretty much every batch we receive. The power supplies did change this most recent shipment, as well. We asked that they include euro plugs with the controllers now, so we now have those along with the US plugs. The US plugs, though, have changed from having been 2 prong to now being 3 prong.',1549394888),(602,237,315,'Sales order created, VXSO-000016, waiting on PO before sending copy',1549414788),(603,237,315,'Received PO 16285',1549664696),(604,235,315,'Per Emilio\'s troubleshooting:\nInitial observations:\n	• The oilcop controller (.71) here has been emailing a daily report up until Jan 30th.\n			§ Able to open it in Firefox\n			§ Able to open it up in Adobe Acrobat Reader DC, Version 2019.010.20069\n		? But it could be that the controller is off and that\'s why is hasn\'t transmitted since Jan 30th\n\nPossible course of action:  Take SQL file from the customer controller and download the controller version to another controller.  And see if results can be copied\n	Take screenshots of settings - maybe something there is causing the issue.\n\n• Downloaded Teamviewer 12, logged into \"MNC 2\"\n• After attempting to log in for the first time, I was kicked out and then got the message that Teamviewer wasn\'t running on the other controller.\n\nCurrently Teamviewer site shows that the unit is offline so we are unable to do anything.  Require customer contact information so that we can find out how we can access the controller or at least walk him through some steps to help us troubleshoot the system.\n',1549668504),(605,235,3,'Contacted the customer had them cycle the power Monday, this allowed me to remote in, add my name to the list.\n Received the transaction journal and daily report this morning via email. Everything appears to be working for now.\nThe unanswered question is what caused it and will it happen again?\nWill monitor the location for a month before closing the issue..\n',1550011867),(606,237,3,'Problem resolved, Bryan installed patch from T version.\n\nMike should i close or do you want to close after you process your sales order??\n',1550012102),(607,235,316,'Troubleshooting update\nWe created a new Admin user in the MNC 2 controller in order to try to copy what the customer saw.  Logged in as this new Admin user, we generated an email with an attached Daily Report PDF.  There were no issues in opening this Daily Report PDF.  As a result we asked the customer if they had issues opening the PDF on another PC, if any other users reported similar issues with attached PDFs, and if they could forward an email with a PDF that can\'t be opened.',1550012130),(608,241,315,'Some questions that need to be answered.\nHas the following basic troubleshooting steps and data collection been accomplished:\n1.	How long has the crashes been going on?  DR was raised on 2/19 which was 3 days ago which is not enough time to explain two times a week.\n2.	Has the controller been swapped out with another one?\n3.	Has information been collected from the customer detailing any symptoms they observed before the controller started to crash?\n4.	Has it been confirmed that the controller has the latest software release installed?  If not what version of software is on the controller?\n5.	Has the controller OS been updated?  If not what version of OS is on the controller?\n6.	Was any software update performed prior to the crashes being observed? \n7.	Has another controller been configured with the same software and using the customers DB tested to see if it also crashes?\n8.	Is another controller available to configure to the match the customers controller that can be sent to them?',1550839349),(609,241,3,'Some questions that need to be answered. Has the following basic troubleshooting steps and data collection been accomplished: 1. How long has the crashes been going on? DR was raised on 2/19 which was 3 days ago which is not enough time to explain two times a week. \n\n  The email I received from the customer was sent to me a week ago, he was referring to the week of 2/11. He was advising me of the anomaly. \n\n2. Has the controller been swapped out with another one? \nYes, Bryan assisted in the exchange.\n\n3. Has information been collected from the customer detailing any symptoms they observed before the controller started to crash? \nThe controller did not crash.\n\n\n4. Has it been confirmed that the controller has the latest software release installed? If not what version of software is on the controller? \nYes, when Bryan assisted in the exchange he installed the latest\n\n5. Has the controller OS been updated? \nSee answer question 4. \nIf not what version of OS is on the controller?  \nTo my knowledge we have not changed/updated OilCop OS.\n\n6. Was any software update performed prior to the crashes being observed? \nNo\n\n7. Has another controller been configured with the same software and using the customers DB tested to see if it also crashes?\n \nNo, don’t believe this course of action is required at this time. Bryan and I have found a couple of isolated cases it appears for some unknown reason the serial port will open thus the CDM goes off line. We have been able to mitigate this issue by installing a patch Bryan made, installed on the old NMC controller, since then we/Bryan swapped the controller with one that TeamViewer and everything has been working since then (1-2 months). So this leads me to my question above, Did we add the open serial port patch to the new controller? \nAs i indicated in the post I did observe open serial port on the debugger….  If we didn’t, then we need to install the patch to see if this takes care of the problem. If Bryan applied the open serial port patch on swapped controller then it’s a good indication open serial port is not the issue, so if they experienced more problems this week then we would know to start asking the customer more probing questions about why they felt it was necessary to power cycle the controller.\n\n8. Is another controller available to configure to the match the customers controller that can be sent to them? \nWe delivered the first controller that experienced the “open serial port issue” with NMC to you last month, so Bryan could further evaluate the issue. Will be interesting to know what Bryan finds..\n\n',1550842734),(610,241,315,'[8:31 AM] Bryan Brumm\nThe patch was added to the new controller before the lockup.\nSo right now the logs for check hardware status is left on. Has it always been left on? If it was left on while the terminal was not, then it could have filled up the memory of the controller (by having it stored in logs) which ultimately would cause the controller to stop working until a reboot occured which would wipe those logs freeing up the memory again. By controller locking up, were they still able to get on the website or just that it would not pump?\n',1550846335),(611,241,144,'Was the USB cable or CDM at NMC ever changed out? Strange issues like this tend to be related to power supply or loose connectors/connections. The fact that it keeps coming up at this location makes me think it is still related to power or connectors.',1551329439),(612,236,258,'The power supplies are not the same as they were in the previous batch of controllers. The BIOS also changes with just about every new batch of controllers. I looked through it and could not find anything that looked like it might have to do with this issue.',1551821416),(613,241,315,'Per discussion at LQD this morning engineering support is no longer needed.  Closing VXSO-000029',1552069468),(614,241,3,'Fix email notification system.\nLearn how to view, turn on and off logs for check hardware status. \nIs HW_CONFIG_INFO_DEBUG  what you are referring to turning on/off check hardware status?\n \nAdd questions to trouble shooting list,      Re: locking up, able to get on the website or just that it will not pump.',1552225740),(615,243,144,'Mark - I am trying to teamviewer in, but I am getting authentication rejected. Are you able to connect, or are you connected right now? Sometimes it seems teamviewer can get a little wonky with multiple connections on the same controller. If you are not connected, can they restart the controller?',1552420115),(616,243,3,'Have already powered cycled controller three times and cycled power on all devices.\n',1552420581),(617,243,3,'Bryan, I will log out of TV now',1552420707),(618,243,3,'Bad CDM? i.e. radio ?',1552421507),(619,243,3,'Bad CDM? i.e. radio ?',1552421519),(620,243,144,'Has the CDM itself been power cycled (physically unplugged and plugged back in from USB)? It is connecting to Serial just fine and it is communicating back and forth on USB between the controller and CDM. If it hasn\'t, go ahead and power cycle the CDM. If the CDM has been power cycled already, then disconnect the CDM from power for 2 minutes. This would be enough time for the other devices to fully disconnect from the ZigBee network completely and attempt to join a new one. After 2 minutes, plug the CDM back in.',1552421704),(621,243,3,'Yes, had them unplug it from the controller for 15 minutes.',1552422019),(622,243,144,'Hey Mark,\n\nI do think it is a radio issue with the CDM. I would go ahead and replace it.\n\nIf it turned out to be a software issue on the ZigBee module, then need to get with HopeRF as they don\'t let us have access to their firmware. It won\'t be a software issue on the CDM microcontroller itself because the CDM does not save anything in non-volatile flash, so when it is power cycled, that is essentially factory restarting the CDM and I doubt all the other board\'s radio just failed.\n\nIf it is a hardware issue, then we could take a look at the board. Possibly a surge somehow screwed up components on the CDM which included the RF module? If that is the case, we could add some additional protection circuitry or could probably use some off-the-shelf device that can go in between the CDM and USB port to isolate power and protect against surges.',1552424731),(623,242,315,'Created VXSO-000034',1552476392),(624,244,258,'Printed all reports in landscape and, although they do look better, there are still issues with column titles not lining up with the correct information and the tables get wonky between pages. All the information does fit the page much better, tho.',1552921614),(625,241,315,'This is till an issue so reopening VXSO-000029 to continue work',1553025058),(626,241,315,'Talked to Bryan about this issue and determine that his confidence level is high it is a hardware problem as he has done all he can do troubleshooting it remotely but just what it is we are unsure what type of hardware is failing but believes it is a power issue so suggests starting in that area.  \n\nFrom our conversation you mentioned that the controller was connected to an  UPS, if it is not a true sine wave UPS then it could be causing the problem.  Bad ground in the computer room could also be causing the issue as well as the USB booster or the USB cable.  He is very busy at the moment with other tasks so has not gotten a chance to look at the controller sent here. \n\nThere is a lot of articles talking about how WiFi can interfere with ZigBee transmissions so this may be another area you want to investigate.  https://support.metageek.com/hc/en-us/articles/203845040-ZigBee-and-Wi-Fi-Coexistence.\n\nMaybe you could ask the question on whether or not their wireless is transmitting on 2.4 GHz or 5 GHz.  Are any of the Oilcop devices with ZigBee near a wireless router?  If so maybe moving them farther away or having them setup their wireless to transmit only on 5 GHz frequency to test to see if the erratic communication loss goes away.',1553176384),(627,244,258,'T_2_52\n\nExported reports look good.\n\nPrinting from View Logs page:\n     Work Order Status still a bit wonky on the Open Work Orders graph. Both portrait and landscape.\n\n     Transaction Journal graph becomes jumbled in portrait mode.\n\n     All other logs look fine.',1553618942),(628,245,315,'Can you confirm that the updates from R21 to R24 were accomplished in the following order and a reboot/power cycle was done to the controller between all of them:\nR21 to R22\nR22 to R23\nR23 to R24\nThe error describe would occur if one of the updates was done before a required one as there were table updates done.  After R24 code was put in so that a jump to a higher R number could be accomplished without going through each R version consecutively.',1554120923),(629,245,315,'Created SO VXS)-000036 for reference',1554124768),(630,245,316,'Teamviewered into the Chantilly PDI controller and ran a command to correct the corrupted \"t_administrative_options\" table, then ran a query to populate the \"t_administrative_options\" table with it\'s previous fields based on a previous backup.  After this was done, the controller was successfully reverted to R_2_21, then updated to R_2_22, then R_2_23, then R_2_24 and rebooted after each update. Please log in to confirm that the controller is working properly.',1554142401),(631,241,3,'4/04/19 - received call, system won\'t open reports again and system won\'t start. had Mat backup system and reboot.\nMat sent pictures of the controller installation inside of the server room, reviewing the pictures shows the Ethernet cable, 65\' USB cable with amplifier and 24Vdc power cable are routed on top of a 20 year old Bogen intercom system. Discussed with Matt that potentially this old of an intercom system could radiate a couple of different kinds of interference, when ever the paging system was active.\nMatt is having the IT department relocate the controller on the server rack and runthe cables away from the intercom system. \nSee 8 Pictures.\nMark ',1554917486),(632,247,315,'Can you confirm the following:\n1. Do they remember the version they were on before they tried the update to R_24?  Did they jump any updates?\n2. Can you provide the login/names of the users that the system does not seem to be working correctly for?  We would like this information so that we can see what the users are experiencing.\n3. Can you provide a Admin and Manager password?\n4. Do they only have one controller?  Team viewer show just this one \"Cassens Dodge 2 - Neumyer\"\n5. Do you remember the previous discrepancy number that was raised for the previous problem?  Will try searching after posting this myself but just encase you know it off hand you can post.\n\nBryan is currently unavailable at this time and am unsure what time today he will be free.  \n',1555521988),(633,247,3,'@#$Q#$^@#^Y%!!\n Now i remember some avoid using discrepancies i spent about 30 minutes writing a response, only to hit update and noting updated lost everything! I will start writing my responses in a word document and paste later. ',1555523279),(634,247,3,'1.	I updated from R_23, No.  “I did not remember we had this issue otherwise would not have done it. Note: to self, note these kinds of issues in team viewer notes”.\n\n2.	Did not take time to have parts department manager test and record all the users at the time because, we both knew this was the same issue Bryan had when he elected to revert back to R_23. You will not be able to reproduce the errors when logging in with Team viewer because it works when we remote in with team viewer like mentioned above. Technician pass word i tested was 1896. The error seems to only occur when the logging into the system from one of their computers. I believe Bryan was thinking it had something to do with how the controller was working with their network.  If you want to further research the error will need to contact the Parts Manger name is Bryan also, his number is 681.656.6070 ext.261 and have him tell you what he is seeing, or ask if you can install Anydesk so you can view what they are seeing.\n\n3.	You can TV into the system using the master password and access all of those pass words\n\n4.	They only have one controller. #2 is because they updated from the original controller installed in 2016 to a current version controller,,,, sometime last year.\n\n5.	Don’t recall if a discrepancy was made..\n',1555526108),(635,247,315,'So I have no clue why the daily report is not working and the summary report and tank adjustments aren\'t working either. Because there has been so much back and forth with updating it up R_24 then back down then back up, I am having a hard time on where to actually look. \n\nSo what I did was delete the sections of the database that get added when you update from R_23 and R_24. Then I copied the exact backup of what I did for the oilcop controller and replaced the files. They should be able to select a station and dispense. We will need the web team to actually go in and see why there is an error happening. It did look like it initially was an error where the memory filled up trying to select too much data from the database, but I ended up changing the php.ini file and that got rid of that error but the internal server error is still happening on the those reports. I imagine with all the messing around with changing the versions up and down and up another bug may have been introduced.\n\nBut I have already spend 2.5 hours on this, and now I think it comes down to troubleshooting the web files for the reports which the web team is going to be much better at doing then me.',1555672415),(636,241,3,'Regarding the weird intermittent communication error at NMC, as with most things it all becomes clear in the fullness of time.\n\nThere are two problems, blue Ethernet cable connecting the controller to the customers network and the gray USB cable connected to the Communication Data Module are laying on top of an 20 year old Bogen paging system, so whenever they use the paging system it is inducing noise causing the serial port to quit communicating to the CDM and possibly interrupting communications to the customers network.\n\nRemedy move the cables away from the intercom equipment..\n\nStupid devil needs to quit messing around with details..\n\nSee 3 Attached pics',1556136605),(637,241,3,'\nRegarding the weird intermittent communication error at NMC, as with most things it all becomes clear in the fullness of time.\n\nThere are two problems, blue Ethernet cable connecting the controller to the customers network and the gray USB cable connected to the Communication Data Module are laying on top of an 20 year old Bogen paging system, so whenever they use the paging system it is inducing noise causing the serial port to quit communicating to the CDM and possibly interrupting communications to the customers network.\n\nRemedy move the cables away from the intercom equipment..\n\nStupid devil needs to quit messing around with details..\n',1556136650),(638,241,3,'This discrepancy can be closed, didn\'t hit the closed button so everyone interested could see the final resolution.',1556136834),(639,249,258,'Please change work order status with work order maintenance in the original post.',1556568407),(640,250,3,'Updated NMC customer, did not save correctly. Deleted and re-added customer when adding MAC address says already exist.\nPlease add Mac address, so customer can access system via support.com.   ',1557836605),(641,246,3,'This customer does not Pre set transactions they only open dispense',1558014998),(642,251,315,'At this time it is not recommended for them to update to R25.  Bryan will look into the uniqueness of the code for this customer when he gets a minutes.  Once we have the info we will review how much effort it will take to integrate into the current R25 version.',1558026623),(643,252,315,'Requesting a level of effort from web team.',1558040999),(644,250,315,'It looks like the column Bryan mentioned is the “mac_address” field in the “system_location” table.  If this is the correct one, I’ll just delete the MAC address from this field.  Just to be clear, I’ll just remove the MAC address, I won’t delete the line this field is in.',1558093824),(645,250,315,'Please confirm it is now working for you.',1558093879),(646,250,3,'Added the system to support.com, everything looks like its is functional now.',1558096720),(647,253,3,'Or would it be better to have their customers install something like AnyDesk on a desktop for remote access?\n',1558098033),(648,253,315,'I see a structure in Teamviewer for Gartec Controllers, so it is not quite clear just what your request is asking for.  Added an attachment showing the directory structure we are seeing in Teamviewer.',1558098275),(649,254,3,'See Attachments',1558197980),(650,254,315,'Is there any way you can find out what version of the software they were running at the time the tanks were not correctly registering quantities pumped?  We know there was a bug intermittently where transactions were not recorded.',1558350581),(651,254,3,'They were using R-24 at the time, since them then they have updated to R_25\n\n',1558355003),(652,254,315,'We believe there was an issue that was fixed in one of the T version from the October mass of fixes but was never released to an R version but is now included in the R25 release.  \n\nHard wiring would be a step we strongly suggest being done at the two places listed as this would be the first step in the troubleshooting process if they do report issues again and this would speed up troubleshooting should the issue return with them being on R25.  \n\nSuggest we do not spend any time on this at this time but you should ask the customers to monitor for any more missed transactions now that they are on R25 and hard wire the two systems.',1558358111),(653,254,3,'Due to how expensive it will be to hard wire, might be best to let them operate with R_25 see if the problem occurs again. If the problem persist will have to hard wire the system. ',1558359797),(654,257,315,'Not clear as to what this is referring to I\'m afraid, can you provide more details/use case as to what this question is referring to please.',1558541948),(655,257,315,'We did no changes to anything in this area for the R25 release.',1558541978),(656,258,1,'Cannot find the demo user jim@oiljobber.com.  Where would this user be located since it is a Demo.  Demo Manager has no features to view any emails assigned.  Can you provide a little more information on this user and what demo this user is assigned to or where this user was created.\n\nIs there a document on how demos are setup and used.  I see two active demos in the demo manager but unsure how the demo is supposed to work to answer your question.',1559058031),(657,259,3,'Tested the power restart on R_25 9 times worked correctly each time. What ever its worth when restarting the database throws an database error:  See below\n\n  A Database Error Occurred\nUnable to connect to your database server using the provided settings.\nFilename: /var/www/oilcop/third_party/MX/Loader.php\n\nLine Number: 98',1559676997),(658,259,3,'Tested Power Off 3 times work correctly each time.\nAnd has the same data base error..',1559677255),(659,259,3,'Confirmed using \"Parks Ford - ADG\", set up \"inventory\" report, instead of sending inventory report the system sends the tank adjustment report.\n',1559679246),(660,259,316,'Hello Mark, in using version LQD_R_2_25 for our testing, it seems that this database error occurs when clicking a link a few seconds after clicking on either \"Power Restart\" or \"Power Down\".  Can you confirm that this is when the database error appears for you?',1559683602),(661,259,3,'Hi again,\nconcerning email scheduler, looks like we have another problem: we have 5 users added in email scheduler and configured to receive a specific report, but only 2 of them (one is our Gartec address) have received the email. The other 3 contact have not received anything, spam checked too.\nWhat could be the cause? Is there something their IT can check? Is there a possibility to see if the emails have been forwarded?\nAndrea',1559735476),(662,259,3,'The error shows after the button was pressed, after the system ask are you sure, wait 10 seconds and press the browser refresh button.\n ',1559735849),(663,259,3,'Emilo, \nI am testing the issue Andrea brought up this morning, about five email accounts, going to set myself , Zach, if its ok would like to also add you and mikes email as well and a fifth person in our office.',1559736063),(664,259,3,'if an email address is entered from the email scheduler it is not added to the user page and can not be added to the user page.\n\nWhile testing the email scheduler added my name from the scheduler by selecting the drop down add new user. It sent email properly however, my name does not show up in the Add/Modify user page. When trying to add my name it would not let me save my name, it asked “Please Enter New PIN”.  ',1559737976),(665,259,3,'Using the bench system added five users from Add/Modify users page for a total of six users in the system, set all six to receive email. The system sent emails to all six users correctly.',1559740220),(666,225,315,'Closing this DR is no longer valid as we are at R25 now.',1559743776),(667,258,3,'These are not demo users as in simulating oilcop system.\nThese are accounts set up for potential customers to login to oilcopsupport.com to remotely viewing data from there OilCop system that is communicating with oilcopsupport.com.\n\nTo better understand please login as calvin@customer.com, password:123456, then put in date range for data is November 2017 - September of 2018. this will show you what a customer can expect to see when they login. Then login as dan@distributor.com, password 123456, then put in date range for data is November 2017 - September of 2018 . This will show you what distributor/installer will see when they login. Then when you figure out how to unblock jim@oiljobber.com you will see that the Oil Jobber can only see the customers inventory.\nI think Angle is the one who originally set this up.\n',1559744688),(668,248,315,'VXSQ-000011',1559744783),(669,252,315,'VXSQ-000012',1559744926),(670,254,315,'VXSQ-000013',1559745221),(671,255,315,'VXSQ-000014',1559745385),(672,257,315,'VXSQ-000015\n',1559745519),(673,258,315,'VXSQ-000016',1559745620),(674,260,3,'The system used for the testing can be accessed with Team Viewer see    LDI Bench LQD_T_2_56',1559764397),(675,260,3,'My mistake should have said to see    LDI Bench R_2_25',1559764485),(676,260,315,'VXSQ-000018',1559771918),(677,260,3,'Yes, agree the amounts are correct. Big red truck ????  Quarts versus Gallons idiot.. lol \n\nThe other issue when the system is configured as a fluid management system that has tank monitoring, with admin settings Tank Monitor Solution is NO and Tank Monitor Time out is  NO and Delivery Acknowledgment is YES. Tank monitor information is not updated in the Admin journal, Tank Adjustments, Summary Reports, Daily Reports or Tank History.\nThe work around is YES Tank Monitor time out and set the time same as Delivery Acknowledgment time out setting, then everything works properly for exception of  Tank History report the graphic up dates however the tabular data does not. \nThis test was on the LDI R-25 bench system if you would like me to demonstrate it to you.\n',1559855367),(678,257,3,'Yes, Tank Monitor Solution and Delivery Acknowledgment must be set to Yes for reports to include tank monitor information.\nSee Discrepancy #260.. ',1559909488),(679,263,315,'Please confirm you are saying that installing software R_2_25 is changing this information or are your referring to installing the image R_2_25 is what you are referring to and not the software installation from the website.',1560784281),(680,263,316,'Regarding the IP addresses, these settings came from an email from Mark on May 21st.  Regarding the passwords for the default usernames, they came from a backup of a Bench System.  If they\'re are incorrect, they can be changed in a new image.',1561399448),(681,258,316,'This account has been unlocked.  Please check if there are any issues logging in.',1561400027),(682,264,3,'see attachments',1561560485),(683,265,3,'Attachemnts',1561564462),(684,266,315,'this site is using R24 and they need to update their controller prior to assigning to engineering to investigating any problems with this controller.',1561633491),(685,266,39,'Is this R24 a special release of R24 for them for multiple techs and multiple dispenses on a single work order? Is there anything you know of in release 25 that could resolve the issue?',1561635615),(686,266,3,'R24 was not a special release. Bryan had to remote in to modify the R24 code to allow multipal users per work order. Plan was to to add a switch in Admin, options.',1561637875),(687,266,3,'If they update the system to R-25 they will lose the ability to have multipal users per work order. \nWill need to have some one standing by to modify the system before they update to R25.',1561638064),(688,266,315,'For future reference this would be considered a custom software load and this MUST be clearly stated in the discrepancy title field to ensure it is clear to the technicians troubleshooting a customers system the customer cannot just update to latest software releases.  Will investigate with engineer as to what is different that they had to change code instead of just setting the WO\'s to All Technicians.   \n\nWill need PO to begin work on this issue.',1561639592),(689,254,315,'What are the results of this customer operating with R25 as it has been over a month now?  Has this problem continued?  If so will need a PO to begin troubleshooting.',1561639948),(690,255,315,'Will need PO to begin work on this.',1561640003),(691,258,315,'Please confirm functionality and send PO for this issue.',1561640140),(692,264,315,'Please send PO for this when you would like us to start work on it. ',1561640223),(693,254,316,'We can confirm that plasma cutters do cause radio interference and that it will be necessary to hardwire the system.',1561642913),(694,266,315,'We need a PO to begin work on this as well as need TeamViewer fixed on their system as of right now we cannot connect using TeamViewer.  \n\nAlso confirm that ASE Milwaukee 2 EH Wolf has the same custom software.',1561645880),(695,265,315,'Please send PO so we can investigate this issue as well has Teamviewer is reporting that it is off line so cannot access the controller.',1561646462),(696,266,3,'Confirmed can not remote into Wausau however, can remote into Milwaukee.\n Yes, it has the same multi user per work order tweak, that we have on hold for a more convenient time.\n\n-- > Mr. Young could you get someone to power cycle the Wausau controller so we can try to remote in.\nThank you!',1561649086),(697,266,3,'cycle the power... Dyslexia moment !',1561649262),(698,263,258,'Emilio - I spoke with Mark about the IP settings and it was a typo on his end. The IP should be set as stated in the discrepancy. Please change the default user passwords to match as well.\n\nMike - all settings I mentioned in the discrepancy that are incorrect are from installing the R_25 image from the usb via Clonezilla.',1561736090),(699,266,315,'Still unable to Teamviewer into ASE Wausau',1561739795),(700,263,316,'Understood, will make another image.',1561740457),(701,263,316,'The image is ready.  If possible, I will drop it off Monday morning.',1561751918),(702,266,39,'System was rebooted yesterday. Can you guys get in?\n',1562170607),(703,266,315,'Teamviewer shows system is offline with a comment when connecting that teamviewer is not running the remote computer.  Could mean that it is not available outside the local network or teamviewer has stopped',1562172379),(704,269,3,'Just saw this, remoted in appears 10W/30 is working.\nIs there anything we can do to assist?\n\nMark\n ',1563200145),(705,252,316,'This has been resolved with the LQD_T_2_57 release',1563283325),(706,262,316,'This has been resolved with the LQD_T_2_57 release.  Please check this release.',1563283561),(707,269,26,'10w/30 at the moment is not an issue after my visit on the 9th.\nHowever we still do have a problem that any action taken on OilCop can take up to a minute or more to complete.  For example if you \"Adjust a Work Order\" by changing the tech it is assigned to, it can take 60 seconds or more from the time you click \"update\" until the time it says, \"Work Order Successfully Updated\"  I pinged the OilCop controller while this delay was happening, from the same computer, and received less than 1ms pings with no packets dropped.  In other words a perfect network connection.',1563301562),(708,269,3,'This sounds familiar from another location, had two devices OilCop controller and a mechanics automotive scanner using the same IP address. Quick way to test this is find another computer that is working properly, copy the network settings from this computer and power down the computer.\nThen install those settings on the controller and see if things are better, if they are return the controller setting to the way they were, turn on the other computer and notify the IT Administrator.\n',1563394597),(709,216,1,'testing testing',1563457401),(710,273,1,'test comment mails',1563540749),(711,273,1,'testing comments second time',1563540876),(712,273,1,'testing 1234',1563540940),(713,273,1,'12345',1563541001),(714,273,1,'qewq',1563541142),(715,273,1,'ewrewrewrewr',1563541266),(716,273,1,'123457679909',1563541708),(717,273,1,'dfsfdsfsdfdsf',1563541803),(718,273,1,'sadsadsadsa',1563541948),(719,272,315,'Please do not include multiple issues in a single discrepancy.  Each issues requires a separate discrepancies to be raised otherwise it becomes very difficult to track which issues have been resolved.',1563799575),(720,272,3,'How would you like to handle cataloging testing results, so we all can track the status.',1563878446),(721,271,3,'Basically the API referenced is so far out of date that it is not useful with the current software version.  We are investigating the best approach to update this and initial consensus is that we move away from this restrictive API as it requires 3rd part vendors like Karmak to use a python library and integrated into their API.  The more robust, easier to maintain and more flexible route of API develop would be to use web base development.\n\n',1563887135),(722,252,316,'This discrepancy has been resolved with the LQD_T_2_57 and LQD_R_2_26 releases; please confirm functionality.\nA PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563894683),(723,255,316,'This discrepancy has been resolved with the LQD_R_2_26 release; please confirm functionality.\nA PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563894795),(724,258,316,'A PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563894942),(725,260,316,'The issue regarding the Tank History report\'s tabular data not updating correctly has been resolved with LQD_R_2_26; please confirm functionality.\nA PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563895175),(726,274,316,'This is from the June 27th email.',1563897357),(727,274,316,'This has been resolved in recent updates to the oilcopsupport.com production website.\nA PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563897459),(728,275,316,'These points have been resolved in recent updates to the oilcopsupport.com production website.\nA PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563897737),(729,262,316,'A PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563904586),(730,277,316,'This was resolved with the LQD_T_2_57 and LQD_T_2_57; please confirm functionality.\nA PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563905364),(731,278,316,'This point has been resolved with LQD_R_2_26; please confirm functionality.\nA PO needs to be issued before this Discrepancy can be closed.',1563906504),(732,279,316,'Please issue a PO for this and then assign to \"Engineering\".',1563907184),(733,282,315,'Have web team looking into this and hopefully will be fixed by tomorrow.',1566318262),(734,282,316,'Mark, the web team resolved a bug in the sync feature.  Please look over the account and confirm that the correct information is showing up in the Reports and respective Homepages.',1566400507),(735,261,315,'This was removed as an option',1567168372),(736,266,315,'Mark can this be closed since they no longer use custom code?  If not need a PO',1567168475),(737,281,315,'Sent Quote',1567168503),(738,282,315,'This has been cleared',1567168617),(739,284,315,'Mark I have this on the books with an note saying a quote was sent 6/15/19.  Is this something your still pursuing?  If so I need a PO for this one and if not close this discrepancy.',1567170506),(740,285,315,'Mark I have this on the books with an note saying a quote was sent 6/15/19. Is this something your still pursuing? If so I need a PO for this one and if not close this discrepancy.',1567170683),(741,254,315,'Since there was a PO issued for this I\'m closing this as resolved.',1567171803),(742,255,315,'Closing this DR as it was resolved.',1567171862),(743,258,315,'Closing as this was resolved.',1567171908),(744,260,315,'Closing as this was taken care of in the latest release',1567175660),(745,263,315,'closing as this issue was resolved.',1567176307),(746,274,315,'Closing as issues were fixed and PO issued',1567176380),(747,266,315,'We would still need a PO for the work put into troubleshooting this issue prior to the resolution of having them upgrade and using the dashes in their WOs.',1567176873),(748,283,3,'Found issue with the probe used to test.\nPlease cancel this PO.\n',1567177840),(749,286,3,'PO 16836 ',1567184442),(750,285,3,'Yes, we received your quote VXSQ-000009. \nCurrently we are waiting for Getec/ Renault to set up accounts for your development team.\nMark',1567186412),(751,284,3,'Yes, we received your quote VXSQ-000010. \nCurrently we are waiting for Getec/ Mecca to set up accounts for your development team.\nMark',1567188999),(752,286,3,'Interesting..\nCompare the 20\' probe specific gravity setting of 0.2458 used to calibrate the starting point of the test at 240” with the 6’ probe specific gravity setting of 0.975 used to calibrate the  starting point of the test at 73”.\nCalibrated the 20’ probe to water 1.0  by lowering the specific gravity value to 0.2458 from the default specific gravity setting for oil  0.88 to match what the actual water level indicated on the tape measure, then calibrated the 6’ probe to water 1.0  by raising the specific gravity value to 0.975. Raising the specific gravity value makes more since 0.88 = oil and water 1.0. Because specific gravity is different for different grades of oil need ability to calibrate the probe for different specific gravity to display the correct level. \nAttached pic of the test setup.',1567259715),(753,286,3,'Interesting..\nCompare the 20\' probe specific gravity setting of 0.2458 used to calibrate the starting point of the test at 240” with the 6’ probe specific gravity setting of 0.975 used to calibrate the  starting point of the test at 73”.\nCalibrated the 20’ probe to water 1.0  by lowering the specific gravity value to 0.2458 from the default specific gravity setting for oil  0.88 to match what the actual water level indicated on the tape measure, then calibrated the 6’ probe to water 1.0  by raising the specific gravity value to 0.975. Raising the specific gravity value makes more since 0.88 = oil and water 1.0. Because specific gravity is different for different grades of oil need ability to calibrate the probe for different specific gravity to display the correct level. \nAttached pic of the test setup.',1567259719),(754,288,315,'Mark if you would like us to look into this can you please provide a PO and reference VXSO-000071',1571153814),(755,288,315,'Mistakenly put in the wrong SO reference.  Should be VSO-000288 reference along with the DR# in your PO.when you want us to start working on this.',1571234698),(756,289,315,'Per Bryan\'s email: System is updated to R_2_30. Looks like there were a few database entries for manual tank adjustments that had commas instead of periods which messed up one of the upgrade queries. Future versions don\'t allow this to happen.  Please close this DR once you are confident no further action on our part is required and we see that it is close will send invoice.',1571244743),(757,291,315,'Old code use to use 0 and 1 for sensor info to populate the sensor page.  New code no longer uses 0 so change 0 to 3, 20\' probe, and now senors page populates correctly.  \n\nCustomer will have to re-calibrate their system as new formulas are in place and probe mapping has been corrected.\n\nWill need PO for this DR.  Reference VXSO-000291 and DR 291 in the PO please.',1571245021),(758,290,315,'canceling PO associated to this DR per Mark M and closing DR as it is a duplicate of DR 286',1571248002),(759,289,3,'This is most definitely a hard drive issue. I tried doing a command that checks the disk and tries to fix any bad sectors, but it won\'t work unless I unmount the affected drive. I won\'t be able to do that remotely as I need access to the bios which means teamviewer can\'t run. \nEven if it fixes the disk, I don\'t know how much we can trust the hard drive afterwards. I was looking to see when the controller restarted. Did anyone from Bus Company restart it? I am wondering if it has been getting power surges that causes unintended resets that could have caused the disk to get damaged.\nAs for the reason it was showing R_2_30 until after the reboot occurred. It seems as though the controller can store some of the changes in cache memory (not the main drive), but it never successfully writes to the drive. So once the reboot occurs, the cache is erased and it uses data from drive. The drive is damaged to a point it is in read only mode to reduce any other loss of data hence why it is stuck on R_22. I assume they were using the reset button on the website to reboot the controller after an update. If so, I would want to look into if there is something in addition (like a program) that needs to be shutdown before the reboot command kicks in. If they were powering it off by unplugging and plugging it back in, then that could be a cause for failure. I have the latest database from today, but it is going to just contain data from R_22. If we get the controller back, I\'ll be able to run the disk command to try to recover any additional data.\n-B\n',1571693099),(760,289,3,'Andrea was preparing to ship the controller to the customer, he found the system was was not showing up on support.com and the rebooting procedure is not working... It shuts down the controller, and immediately reboots it.. but then you cannot reach the website page and pinging the IP is giving no answer.... but I can see the LAN port\'s LEDs blinking...\nThe controller is view able on teamvierwer as Bus Company 2\n',1571834145),(761,289,3,'Forgot to mention mac address (00:e0:4c:28:ee:68) for the new Bus Company 2 controller that Bryan transferred data from the original Bus Company controller with a bad hard drive. This one will not communicate with support.com..',1571834588),(762,292,3,'Received Quote  VXSQ-292\nThank you.',1573483531),(763,288,3,'Regarding how tanks are displayed on the desktop.\nBefore someone decided to display tanks in alphabetical order on the desktop, it was according to the tank number (left-right in numerical order) tank number was automatically assigned when the product was assigned to the tank, tank would adopt the product number. The product number was assigned in chronological order according to order the product name was entered into the system. \nFor various reasons this seemed to cause quite a few different issues, only way installers/customer can fix is to do a factory reset and start over.\nI believe the easiest fix maybe when to add a new field when “Add New Tank” the field could be located above the “Tank Name” field called “Tank Number” when adding tanks. The tanks would be displayed left – right in numerical order. Also let the programs know that this field maybe subject to change i.e. its not uncommon to move products to different tanks and move tanks for more tanks to be installed over time as new oils are introduced to the market.\n',1573497634),(764,288,3,'Also please include this fix.. When setting up Custom Shape Tank in “Update Tank” and Centimeters is selected the height of tank is in inches not Centimeters.',1573498508),(765,288,3,'PO VXSO-288',1573583480),(766,293,3,'VXSO-293',1573583552),(767,295,315,'Figured it out. It was upgraded to R_30 which has the cable length add or subtract for cable length. They had a cable length set for each tank which ended up subtracting values anywhere from 5 inches to 47 inches from the calculated value depending on the sensor.\n \nSet them to 0 and now it is showing up correctly.',1574870375),(768,295,315,'PO 17062 VXSO-295',1574870399),(769,298,3,'As mentioned to Tommy Young this is most likely a radio reception issue.\nNeed to evaluate radio environment more thoroughly, possible move TMM out of a reception shadow caused by steel tanks, racks, beams.\nMay need range extender or hard wire TMM to range extender or direct to CDM.\n ',1576190224),(770,298,3,'Devices at both locations appears to have a steady 4 bar radio strength.\nrelays are not used at both locations.\n \n',1576256077),(771,299,3,'Was able to add Building 28 system and Mac address. System is now displayed on the site but offline.',1577553167),(772,298,3,'Jim sent me these pictures see attached, noticed TMM 2 is mounted directly behind TMM 3. Maybe the two modules mounted back to back is having some kind of cause and effect thing happing??\nEe disconnect TMM 2 from the mounting bracket lay it face down where it is, to see if that keeps TMM 2 from going off line?\n',1577553383),(773,294,315,'Discussing with Bryan we believe this was a fluke and would be very hard to reproduce.  The answer to your questions is that there should be no particular order to what needs to happen outside of following the current directions and should be able to change it on the fly.  We believe at this time it would not be cost effective to troubleshoot this further by us unless this start to happen on a regular bases so suggest closing this DR.',1577980967),(774,298,3,'Found #2 TMM was mounted back to back with another TTM with Uni-Strut.\nRemoved #2 TMM cover and let hang seems to have resolved the issue.\n',1579720836),(775,299,3,'1/22/20 System is now on line',1579721033),(776,236,3,'Sent OilCop Controller to Bryan\'s house for him to evaluate',1579721772),(777,219,3,'Yes, Delivery Acknowledgement timeout and Tank monitor solution time out were both turned on and set to the same 1 minute timeout setting',1579724465),(778,301,315,'I installed a backup on another controller and it seems as though the DB is causing the issue.  Two options.\n1. Delete significant number of records in the t_adjust_workorder, t_systemlog, t_actions, t_dispense, t_tank_adjustments, t_tank_reports, t_workorder_details\n2. Have code written where the total number of DRs is limited to some criteria.  For example, when Work Order Maintenance page is selected from the Managers tab it only pulls enough records to fill the page and fetches only enough to fill each page if another page is selected.  Currently it looks like it is pulling every record from the DB.  This is the preferred method.\n\n',1580261368),(779,301,315,'Used the following query to close the work orders > 30 days.\n\nUPDATE `t_adjust_workorder` SET `f_workorder_completed` = 1, `f_closed` = 1580256657 WHERE `f_created` < 1609203575\n\nTested accessing the Work Order maintenance menu and did not get script error and also there now only shows 17 pages of work orders compared to 87 pages prior to closing WOs using aforementioned query.',1580265960),(780,301,315,'Sent VXSO-301 for reference for PO request.',1580266605),(781,302,3,'Can we get a backup of the system from support.com?\n',1580913514),(782,303,3,'Tried to attached the complete DB backup.sql file, did not let me attach it to the discrepancy\n ',1581372475),(783,303,315,'Bryan: I cleared up the memory. It was the logs for the python under /var/www/logs named cronlog. Deleted it and restarted the python.\n\nNote:  type ctrl+shift+t which is the shortcut for terminal\n\nQuery used to close WO\'s after attached backup was done.\nUPDATE \'t_adjust_workorder\' SET \'f_workorder_completed =1, \'f_closed\' =58129800 WHERE \'f_created\'<1577836800.',1581394283),(784,302,315,'Attached complete system backup file.',1581442535),(785,302,315,'Web team said the error when accessing the logs is because the /tmp directory is too full but df -h shows that it should have plenty of space.  Waiting to hear back.',1581539089),(786,304,315,'Added sales map link to About Us page, Change Company link to \"About Us\" to match directions in catalog, enabled SSL on site and started work on implemented captcha to reduce spam.\n\nPlease send PO for VXSO-304',1581765956),(787,302,315,'All seems to be fine with this customer now.  I did a complete backup and then restored an older file but stopped before completed and then restored the latest backup I created before doing anything today.  Everything started working fine once I rebooted the controller, including accessing the logs.\n\nI have attached the cronlogs and the latest backup to this DR.',1581963473),(788,302,315,'Cronlogs would not upload, there must be a limit on the number of files that can be attached to a DR.',1581963571),(789,305,3,'PS.. Installer thinks the system has been this way from the beginning..',1582142579),(790,305,315,'Initial investigate has pointed to two possible issues or a combination of both.  The controller runs normally it would seem if on any page but the dashboards which are graphic intensive web pages which seem to be updating at a very rapid pace.  With one or two tanks this is not seen as an issue but with a large number of tanks there may be too many calls to the DB in a given amount of time causing other process from executing in a timely manner giving false indications on device status.\n\nWeb team has been notified and requested they configure their test bed to simulate a site with more devices than specified at EHWolf to help narrow down the cause of the issue and come up with a solution for the issue.  Will update after meeting with them to tomorrow.',1582149448),(791,306,315,'Mark can this controller be updated to the latest software version?  It is currently at 2_28 and would like to update to 2_31 but customer would have to re calibrate',1582889859),(792,306,3,'Apologize for not catching it was not using the current version.\nAnyway, updated to  R31 everything went smoothly. Only thing that needs to be done before up date, is to confirm the cable length is set to zero in sensor configuration.\nUnfortunately the symptom is the same..\n  ',1582899973),(793,306,315,'I didn\'t expect it to fix the issue per say, just wanted to rule out any DB changes being the cause of the issue between the two versions.  I asked the team before I posted my comment to look into it and have meeting to discuss at 10:30 cst so will updated you afterwards.',1582904851),(794,306,3,'Remoted into the system today and noticed the software version is LQD_R_2_29, on 2/28 shortly before 14:26 upgraded the system from R_28 to R_29 and then upgraded from R_2_29 to R_2_31. Appears the update didn\'t finish correctly or maybe the team needed to revert back to _29 anyway i didn\'t try to update today in case its part of the trouble shooting in progress..',1582996836),(795,308,3,'Noticed another issue, tank named DEF Cart has a 60 gallon capacity, however it has 375.1 contents. system will not let manager to subtract inventory. Tank is not connected to a tank monitor',1583169771),(796,308,3,'Resolved issue with DEF cart tank, subtracted larger amount 320 gallons seemed to work',1583169962),(797,308,3,'Rebooted the controller seems to have helped a little. Maybe something to do with needing to turn off the logs?\n',1583245286),(798,308,315,'found controller on 2_24 and upgraded to 3_31, all seems to be working fine.  Still need to confirm there are not any excessive logs enabled.',1583251285),(799,306,315,'Upgraded to 2_31 today, will see how things work',1583251369),(800,309,315,'This is possible, please provide specification for the report/log.  For example report will be in table format with the following columns: Date Created, Product Name, Preset Amount, etc.  Whether or not there should be a summary by tank showing current tank inventory and expected end of day inventory, etc.  \n\nGuesstimate would be that would take about a week to release.',1583508184),(801,309,258,'Spoke with Mark about this and he will contact the customer to collaborate whatever details need to be hammered out.',1583522157),(802,311,3,'Is the OilCop code different to operate with Zigbee radios made for < 15 nodes vs Oilcop code made for > 15 nodes.',1584048672),(803,310,3,'EH Wolf is going to hardwired the FCMs using 2 wire RS-485 communication to eliminate radio communications as the cause.\nWill update when the change is made.   ',1584455077),(804,313,315,'AEG Petroleum is the site I went to to see error presented.  Upon logging in saw a web page with the error message but once I opened the login screen and logged into the system could not get the error when access logs.  Could access logs without errors.  Was the system rebooted by chance or was anything done to the controller prior to my logging in?',1584479200),(805,313,315,'Misread discrepancy and was able to reproduce error but only when logs Tank Adjustments report was selected as describe in the Description.  Did a complete system backup and it created a zero length file.  Could not log into phpMyAdmin and could not bookmark a page or get the start page to save.  Firefox also seem to have other issues.  Rebooted the controller and everything seems to work correctly.  Was able to save the login page as the start page, create bookmarks, complete a system backup that produced a 6MB file, back button in Firefox worked correctly now but still produced a DB 126 error when the Tank Adjustments log was accessed.  All other logs opened correctly.   Noticed that when looking at the DB backups it looks like the last two backups before today are also zero length and were data back in Jan 2020.  \n\nWhen was the last time the customer accessed the Tank Adjustment report successfully?\n\nTroubleshooting continues.',1584481764),(806,313,315,'Exported Tank Adjustment data using csv export feature and attached to DR.  Had error from Ubuntu while working on controller which indicated there was a space issue but running the command df -h showed that there was enough free space.   Received other Ubuntu errors and then again another Ubuntu error on reboot.  Troubleshooting continues.',1584483788),(807,313,315,'csv did not upload on last DR update',1584483847),(808,313,315,'Seems to be a limit to the number of attachments or total bytes that can be attached to a DR so cannot upload csv file.',1584483931),(809,313,315,'After rebooting the 3rd time no longer saw any error messages from Ubuntu and successfully accessed the Tank Adjustment logs without issues multiple times from both Admin and Managers dashboards.\n\nIs there any directions to the customers to reboot controllers?',1584484412),(810,313,3,'We have not given instrucrions to reboot contollers. Thinking to preserve the issue and possabley to backup system before cycling the pwr.',1584485833),(811,305,315,'Updating FireFox from v28 to v66 improved performance of the admin and managers dashboard pages.  There is still somewhat of a lag but it may be tolerable now and now the top command show that it is Web Content taking up most of the resources and Firefox is sitting around 8% when on the dashboard.  \n\nWeb team probably noticed this same improvement when they suggested testing out Chrome on one of the controllers at the office.',1584652513),(812,314,315,'Please update controller, confirm that Tank monitor should be set to off in Admin Options and confirm that if Tank monitor is set to off no sensor will show on sensor page.  Please confirm all other settings are correctly set for tanks/stations/etc.\n\nSend PO if you would like us to look at it further.',1585173257),(813,313,3,'Received call from Lorenzo he said the tank monitor quoit reading tanks sometime 3/7/20 according to the tank adjustment report. I attempted to use the debugger tool however the system says HW_CONFIG_INFO_DEBUG not found.\nI checked my syntax couple of times same result??\nAttached screen shot.  ',1585853275),(814,313,315,'ManInTheMiddle file had 0 size, pulled R31 from Oilcopsupport.com and copied ManInTheMiddle from zip file to controller and all worked after restarting.',1585856946),(815,313,3,'Appears the system still is not working correctly, tank level information is not being processed by the system. Opened the HW status debug made setting selections and saved. Then went to run the python to view the information – “killall python”          -  “python /var/www/ManInTheMiddle_v8.py”\nSystem replied python:  no process found.\nUsing ls -l command  looks like  BackAPI.py and launcher.sh and pytz-master.tgz  have 0 file size.\n\nSee attachment\n',1586010727),(816,313,3,'Updated the system to R31 for a second time, to see if it would update the files. Tried to open HW status debug came back and said not found....\n',1586011626),(817,313,3,'Rebooted the system a second time. Everything seems to be functioning properly now.\n',1586012676),(818,317,3,'Should have been more clear above.. tank monitor solution \"timeout\" must be enabled and tank monitor solution in administration setting should be turned off.',1586439285),(819,316,315,'I have tested the power down and restart procedure on 4 different controllers and it worked as designed.  There is however an issue with the controllers when using the Ubuntu power down and restart option where the controller locks up on boot up.  Unsure at this time why the controller locks on the boot screen and does this whether you use the ubuntu or the Oilcop power down and restart options.\n\nWhat version of software and what controller was this issue discovered on?',1586785044),(820,305,3,'Changed man in the middle settings LEVEL_CHECK_TIMEOUT setting from 1sec. to 3sec. and CHECK_TANK_TIMEOUT setting from 1sec. to 3sec. \n\n1 second settings = mysqld 26.33% CPU usage and python 22.05% CPU usage.\n3 second settings = mysqld 18% CPU usage and python 16% CPU usage.\n',1587060876),(821,320,315,'Zigbee chips from mini display will not work with other hardware, returned hardware to LQD.',1589918850),(822,311,315,'mini-display zigbee chips do not work with other hardware, returned hardware to LQD.',1589921949),(823,321,3,'This is a test version not to be used.',1590165809),(824,321,385,'According to Bryan version numbers were never really thought out all the way.  His intention was not to have the version number change except for major updates.  This is something we will have to address in the future so that it is all thought out and documented correctly so that all have the same understanding.  As of now it would be best to ignore versions showing up on the TAC.\nThe following hex files are the most current for the TAC:\nTAC_3_0_6g removes Gartec and Liquidynamics from the welcome screen, but keeps Oilcop (Italian translation still has Oilcop)\nTAC_3_0_7n - removes Gartec, Liquidynamics, and Oilcop from the welcome screen (Italian translation still has Oilcop)\nTAC_3_0_8a - removes Gartec and Liquidynamics from the welcome screen then switches Oilcop with Admiral APU (Italian translation used to still have Oilcop. It now has been removed)\nThese files need to be confirmed all is working as expected.\n\nCurrently also working with Bryan to make sure the source files associated to these files are available and up to date.',1590777751),(825,322,385,'System would throw the 130 error due to a corruption of the t_adminstrative_options table.  The datetime of the system was July 31, 2017, year may be off.  Databases are very particular at times with datetime info being off from realtime too much and during one of the updates the db would complete something due to a datetime mismatch but didn\'t report the error correctly.  Verified there were backups in the DB directory.  The size of the most recent DB that matched the controller datetime were no very big.  Determine that they are basically empty backups, basic table structure at the most.  Only option was to use the the latest larger DB.  Dropped the current DB and imported the backup.\n\nAfter importing the backup the system acted normally upon login..  Tried to duplicate issue by going back to R_17 then installing all revisions in order till the most latest was installed R_25',1591065641),(826,322,385,'Last entry should have said R_31.',1591065724),(827,318,385,'Changes have been pushed to production and tested good.',1591211881),(828,324,385,'The admin table again was corrupted.  Was the controller at a lower version than R_24 when you started to update?  If so I believe this is the 2nd controller the failed after updating to R_24 to R_25.  For the life of me I cannot remember if it is R_24 you can start to jump over releases, can you confirm.  If so then next time try going to the latest version instead of installing R_25.\n\nI installed R_26 and everything seems to be working fine.  \n\nSomething else I notice, if you did start from a lower version than R_24 then the backups are not being performed before updating so if at all possible manually back up the DB and confirm the file is larger than say 80 kb, it really should be in the MB range.  Another check is to make sure that the latest backup is larger than past backup files sizes. \n\nUse the SQL code in the attached file to generate a new table structure and single record, so you will have to correctly set Admin options for this customer.   ',1592447200),(829,126,1,'This is fixed I do believe.',1592447878),(830,324,3,'This controller was sold to the customer last year with R_24 installed, they are just now installing the system. Had them send the controller back for us to update and confirm it was working properly and to install their network settings.\nPer Bryans instructions any version prior to R_25 requires the system to be rebooted after each version update, and the must be done sequentially. After R_25 is installed we can jump versions and does not require rebooting between updates.\nOne of these days would like for you to show me how to use the SQL code.\n',1592484378),(831,325,3,'Entering Odometer dose not work when entering from the webpage.\n',1592484608),(832,324,3,'Updated the system to R_32 everything appears to be working properly.\nUpdated the network settings to the customers specifications then rebooted the system.\nChecking network settings now displays two network settings tables. Settings in the top table are incorrect settings in the bottom table are the correct settings.\nHow should we address this? See attached pic, i\'ll leave everything in its current state for your review.',1592486642),(833,324,385,'I can\'t access the controller through Team viewer so not sure exactly how to proceed but here is a shot\nClick the \"start\" button and search for the Network Connections program by typing in network in the search field, see attach pic Find Network Connections program\nThe box should be blank, if it is not delete the connection that does not match the customer\'s settings, see attachments .216 controller network settings  and 2.png\nNot exactly sure how you will test since the customer network settings will not work on your network. \nIf you have teams on your phone you can call me and then share your screen on your phone which basically shares your camera so I can see the controller since I can\'t use Teams.',1592490566),(834,324,3,'Went back to where we have the controller benched, logged back into the system now its showing the normal network setting page with one set of network settings. It dawned on me that after i changed the network settings it will not show up on team viewer until its plugged into the customers network using their settings or i change it back to our network settings. I will ship the unit back to the customer. What is the charge for your time i\'ll issue a PO.',1592491303),(835,325,385,'Ok there is something else going on here.  On the .216 development controller the odometer enters correctly in the DB.  I put in 12345678 and it stored in the DB as entered.  \n\nWill have to compare the python file as well as the webpage files to see why it works on .216 and not on yours. Revision control is not well established yet for the oilcop controller web files and it is lucky there are only 3 or 4 python files, so it is possible that at one point in time a file was not documented as required to be include in a release.',1592530592),(836,325,385,'Per Marks test of E_54 and R_32 and verified that entering an odometer reading from web does work. ',1592935410),(837,319,3,'PO #17563 issued.\n',1592942505),(838,325,385,'Bryan release an E and T version of the fix.  Please check and confirm there are no issues.',1594642445),(839,319,385,'Pushed changes to Production and tested good.',1594642845),(840,315,385,'These boards were sent to Liquidynamics for them to build.',1594643034),(841,327,385,'Found that the only way to program the devices was to have batteries installed or have an external power supply providing power to the boards.  All correctly programmed as long as batteries or external power was applied to the boards.',1594648057),(842,327,385,'Request PO for $61.25.  Please reference DR 327 on PO',1594648135),(843,325,3,'RE test version 66.\nOne new bug we found is that if you have time&date configured to MM/DD/YY, no matter if you have admin options set to “liters” both for transactions and reports, but the exported txt file will send the data with “quarters” units…',1594651005),(844,316,385,'Found that the lockup does not always happen when using the buttons on the Manager screen, it sometimes locks up when using the Ubuntu power button also.',1595599926),(845,325,385,'Please confirm odometer fix is working from TAC and ignore export issues.\n\nIssues posted about a bug is not related to this fix since that is a web page issues and not a python issue which this fix is concerned with.  Export feature for Oilcop system has had the mentioned bug all along of not exporting units consistently which was discovered when auto export was being developed and was told at that time not work any standard export issues discovered during the work for the auto export work..  The values exported are correct for liters, pint etc but units are not being exported correctly.  ',1595600318),(846,328,385,'Request PO be issued for 10 hrs @ $35 = $350 and reference DR 328 in PO.',1595833260),(847,327,385,'All work completed and invoice sent',1596030273),(848,326,385,'Andrea\'s Customer controller has been updated.  All work completed and invoice sent',1596030322),(849,319,385,'All work completed and invoice sent',1596030366),(850,322,385,'All work completed and invoice sent',1596030383),(851,324,385,'All work completed and invoice sent',1596030427),(852,325,385,'All work completed and invoice sent',1596030448),(853,312,385,'This is taken care of by security update',1596030502),(854,308,385,'Logged into controller and no excessive logging is happening.',1596030597),(855,306,385,'All seems to be working fine.  WO are being closed and only show 5 open WO as of today.',1596030755),(856,305,385,'Could not connect today but believe issues have been resolved by hardwiring system',1596030835),(857,316,385,'Need PO if work is going to be done on this.',1596030881),(858,304,385,'All work completed ',1596030908),(859,300,385,'Need PO if work is going to be completed on this',1596030944),(860,297,385,'Need PO if work is to be done on this.',1596030978),(861,296,385,'Quote was submitted',1596031035),(862,288,385,'All work completed and invoice sent',1596031354),(863,293,385,'Will need PO if work is to be started',1596031394),(864,287,385,'PO will need to be sent for work to begin on this',1596031422),(865,272,385,'Need to discuss this DR so we can appropriately break out the issue into individual DRs so that PO can be sent covering items',1596031803),(866,331,385,'Attached quote',1596669956),(867,331,385,'Found usb drive was corrupted causing issues with customer builds.  Built new image for controller builds based on R32 and security updates to ubuntu software.  Created image from controller with security updates and R32 configured for Gartec controllers for controller builds for Gartec.  Tested initial upgrade to ubuntu softwware version 18.xx and troubleshot issue with Teamviewer after upgrade.  Found that version originally being used on for builds was somehow incompatible with ubuntu but downloading the last version of teamviewer 12 from the website installed correctly.',1596670203),(868,330,385,'Tested written procedures on multiple controllers to ensure users would not have any issues.  Rewrote sections and added necessary steps for issues found during testing.',1596670263),(869,330,385,'Added version of procedure that can be open on ubuntu',1596670346),(870,330,385,'Added MS word version of procedures',1596670412),(871,330,385,'Failed to add ubuntu version of attachment so doing it again.',1596670487),(872,330,385,'System will not allow ubuntu version to be uploaded, trying after zipping up the ubuntu version',1596670644),(873,330,385,'It would seem that some file extension are not allowed to be uploaded.  Suggest creating a new DR if there is a requirement to allow for more files types to be uploaded.  Sending invoice for this DR as work is completed and closing DR.',1596670720),(874,333,385,'Logged into controller and saw normal dashboard tanks info.  Please provide more details as to what exactly is not being seen.  Please be specific how to navigate to the area/web page that the data is missing from.',1598549188),(875,333,363,'I cannot see bulk tank inventories online either. ',1598553389),(876,333,363,'Mike, When I select American State Equipment and the Wausau location nothing comes up at all, just a blank screen.',1598553808),(877,333,1,'Disk drive was full, removed unnecessary files to free up 1.6GB of space.  Force sync\'d ASE Wausa and could view info on oilcopsupport.com for that customer under Inventory.',1598575121),(878,333,1,'Disk drive was full, removed unnecessary files to free up 1.6GB of space.  Force sync\'d ASE Wausa and could view info on oilcopsupport.com for that customer under Inventory.',1598575122),(879,333,385,'Please send PO for SO.  Please reference DR 333 and discrepancy title on PO line item description.',1599868307),(880,331,385,'Please send PO for attached invoice.  Once received will send invoice to finance.',1599868498),(881,335,385,'Instructions and correct IDE and compiler info has been provided.  Compiler files are located in OilCop - Documents\\OilCop Jr\\Tools on SharePoint and the instructions are attached.',1601515255),(882,333,3,'Hardwire system resolved issue',1602703678),(883,340,3,'After coming back from holidays, once again I had issues with frozen\ncommunication: in one day, 2 different systems, both version 2_30.\n\nAlways the same thing: all devices are green, signal strength is shown as\ngood (4/4, or 3/4).. but if you try to do anything, on TAC you have\ncommunication error and FCM is returning \"starting pump unsuccessful\"... no\nway to fix it unless you make a factory reset...\n\nLuckily, on one system, they had a version 2_30 backup dated July: I was\nable to upload this database after factory reset and fix it. I am sending\nyou both databases:\n07-14-2020 ==> working database\n08-25-2020 ==> database of the system not working\n\nTransactions/actions/WO apart, they should be exactly the same... hope this\ncan help to find the reason of why this issue is continuously happening...\nIt was my understanding that it was supposed to happening only with R_2_25,\nbut apparently is continuing to appear with newer versions too...\n',1602706842),(884,340,3,' Andrea,\n We continue working on trapping the TAC communication error with no success yet. While testing it occurred to us maybe the error has to do with timing related to the latency found with radios. This could explain why the error occurs even though the radio has four bar strength, we can eliminate this possibility by hard wiring one of TAC communications to the CDM and turn on dip switch 8 in the TAC which turns off the radio and changes the device address. As you know dip switch 8 on = address 128 so would need to reassign the address. Ideally if we could test with a location that had multiple TACs, hard wire only one of the TAC to see if the problem no longer occurs on the wired TAC but continues to occur on the TAC with the radio turned off.   \n',1602707236),(885,340,3,' Hi Mark,\nit looks like you did not understand what the error is… It’s not a problem of TAC communication!!! It’s not a problem of communication at all!!!\n When this problem occurs, anything in the system appears not to communicate anymore:\n1.	If you go on TAC, when entering PIN code it returns communication error\n2.	If you try to calibrate or to dispense, it returns that starting the pump was unsuccessful (like there was no communication)\n But this error is related to something into the database, and not with hardware communication.\nIn fact:\n1.	If you make the backup of a system with this issue and load this backup on a working system (with same version), the working system stops to work and gives the same issue\n2.	If you have a system with this issue, and you make a factory reset:\na.	If you add manually the hardware, it returns to work\nb.	If you load the backup made while the system was having the issue, the system returns to have the issue\n Therefore, there must be something different in the database, something that changes the behavior of the system. But it’s not a TAC communication problem.\n',1602707308),(886,340,3,'Andrea,\n Restored the 08-25-2020 data base to a test controller with R 30, set address on the CDM and two FCMs to match addresses used in the data base. Was able to simulate multiple dispenses with no problems.\nWe will continue to test using controllers with older software versions.\n',1602707392),(887,340,3,'Andrea,\nI understand how frustrating it is, would It be possible the next time this error occurs to allow us to remote into a controller that is not working. Maybe have you do the restore on a controller, confirm it is not working after the restore and then allow us to log in. \nWe would walk though some troubleshooting step, i.e. reboot the controller, cycle power on the CDM, etc even if it has been tried in the past, at first and then we can use the July data, for the tables I mentioned above, to replace the data in the tables on the non working controller entry by entry to see which one fixes the issue.  Then if we can make it work just by changing the values in the DB we can start looking at the code to find out what section of code is changing the values.\n',1602707447),(888,340,3,'Andrea,\n \nHave been working through the system trying to understand what could be causing the communication issues you are having. In light of the fact we have not received any similar complaints in America, I have been reviewing how the system is set up from the data base you sent line by line, only thing that is different, all of the systems we have installed in America the CDM is always set to address 0 (zero), whereas the data base shows the CDM is set to address 1 (one).  This is hard to believe it could be cause of the problem but would explain why all of the communications fail, as if the controller forgot the CDM address?\nWould it be possible to set the CDM address at the location having this problem to address 0 as a test ?\nI know this is a stretch, it the only thing I can think of at the moment.\n',1602707494),(889,340,3,'Hi Mark,\nI obviously hope it won’t happen again, but will try this way from now on: will always set CMS address to 0 on new installations.\nThis issue happened both on system set to Italian, English or French language.. The other different configuration between our systems and yours is about liters/quarts.. but I remember we had same issue on a Colombian system, and they’re using quarts…\n \n',1602707536),(890,336,385,'Found the issue to be a flaw in the circuit design for input power.  Not connecting external power and using the programmer to supply the power to program the board allowed for programming of all failing modules.  See OneNote for detailed troubleshooting and other notes. CDM programming issues in the OIlcop Notebook - OilCop - CDM programming issues page.',1603156238),(891,352,385,'After trying a number of items it looks like the network this controller is on is not allowed to access site on the internet.  Tried to get to oilcopcupport.com and could not, just keeps saying Policy Login Redirect on the tab and near the status bar is shows \"transferring data from 192.168.0.11...\"  Not sure how they got the R_30 update on this computer without being able to connect to the internet.  Since the file is there the update can happen but for some reason it puts blank info into the DB because it could get info from oilcopsupport.com.  \n\nBefore the controller can be fixed the customer has to allow this controller to access at least the oilcopsupport.com site.  Once this is allowed work can continue on the controller.',1603231102),(892,353,1,'Disabled a crontab script that was failing. I do not know what that command was used for.\n*/1 * * * * /usr/bin/php /var/www/html/index.php crons deactivate_demo\n',1603929329),(893,357,3,'Received daily report the header has PHP errors.\nSee attached daily report',1611237602),(894,361,3,'See Attachement',1611239200),(895,357,3,'Received “Send Daily Report Now” daily report. see second attachemnt',1611423071),(896,356,385,'Found that there was a PHP error when ever a complete DB was updated as well as when the system is updated.  Found that there was an extra table that no longer exists t_hardware_main.  Not sure where that table came from as it is not in any version after R_21.  Could be in the DB before but haven\'t taken time to locate it.  \n\nNot sure that this will fix their auto closing problem but it was causing an error.  Will look again tomorrow to see if the system is closing WO\'s as it should and if so then having this table in the DB was causing the issue.  If not then further troubleshooting will have to be accomplished.\n\nNote:  t_hardware_main would not show up if a complete backup was performed, only when you used phpMyAdmin to export the oilcop DB would it show up.',1611797450),(897,363,3,'Notified customer the email address he is trying to use is 27 characters in length. Asked if they could reduce the number of characters. He is checking..\nIs this a Hard limitation or can it be modified to 30 characters? ',1611869976),(898,363,3,'Password is United1864\nNote if entering using team viewer don\'t for get to backspace after entering n, because after entering uppercase U the next letter will also be uppercase. Must backspace the reenter n.',1611870267),(899,363,3,'tested using OilCop@penskeauto.com appears to have worked!!',1611871295),(900,368,385,'Attached quote, waiting on PO.',1616632765),(901,350,385,'Scheduled Daily report emails are working on the E68 code that includes the 7\" tablet enhancements.  Compared files and there are a lot of differences between the two releases due to the changes.  Narrowed down to the following file to test first /oilcop/application/modules/admin/controllers/admin.php.\n\nInstalled on test controller and Daily email was sent at the correct time.  Attempting the same file change on Gartec controller.',1617977264),(902,329,385,'Released  T_2_69 version with the following commits:\nset calculator so it will scroll on screens too small. …\nEmptied directories and placed .gitkeep file so the directory gets co… …\nRearranged buttons so everything fits on screen in landscape mode. …\nRemoved hyper-link when no workorder is found. …\nAble to scroll screen to show hidden items. …\nRemoved formatting issues with showing a semicolon. \nTechnician name shows on all screens …\nCenter footer on all screens. …\nChanged body text color to lighter value. …\nAdded space after \'Welcome\' …\nCorrected logic/bugs for the preset amount. …\nAdded RTC to mobile footer\nRemoved unused/will error paramaters in .htaccess file. …\nFiles changed on test server and imported into Git repository. …\nOther mobile page view changes …\nload-workorder mobile changes …\nEnabled \'use strict\' again. …\nFixed language files …\nRemoved ZWSP non-printable character in the English translation file. …\nCopyright change on mobile footer. …\nMobile login screen change. Removed text box. …\nCorrected a missed line to change the desktop version back to what it… …\nSyntax issue should of been a string.\nTLS issues corrected, missing variables, unknown functions.\nFixed 404 resource errors.\nTablet corrections\nFixed keypad popup on mobile.\nUpdated phpmailer to include security fixes\nUpdated git of phpmailer\nExtra parentheses removed. …\n7inch tablet modifications\nUpdated .htaccess file for https redirection.\nCorrected console error loading http over https message.\nTech Dashboard and header display modification\nDispense Page modified for display on all screens to be the same.\nFixed button display issue.\nChanged email address in test files.\nCRLF to LF!\nRemoved erroneous test data that was on the screen.\n7inch Dispense pages updated.\nRollback tech-dashboard.php\nRollback tech-dashboard.php\nUpdated IDE project. tech-dashboard.php incomplete modified\nAdded bootstrap 4.0.0 dist library\nInitial Commit R_2_33 w/database',1618499156),(903,370,385,'Duplicate see DR 371',1619533886),(904,369,385,'Duplicate see DR 371',1619533895),(905,371,385,'Looked up information on all the vulnerabilities listed in the attached file.  Basically Ubuntu, Apache, code ignitor and PHP will all have to be updated to pass the scans done by this customer.  This unfortunately will require a massive rewrite of the Oilcop Controller web code due to newer versions of PHP have deprecated a lot of the php commands in use in the current code base.  The rewrite would be similar to what had to be done on the Liquidynamics.com site.',1619534696),(906,355,385,'Found issues with DB permissions on 3rd parting hosting system.  Corrected permissions, test good.',1620175223),(907,356,385,'Waited over a week for response on whether or not the system was working correctly after fixing DB issues.  There was no access to the controller to do further troubleshooting due to being on a closed network.  Had downloaded the DB and system files prior to losing the ability to connect.  Installed files and DB on local system and continued to test auto close feature.  Could not duplicate the issue with the limited hardware test bed. Tried numerous scenarios but could not duplicate the issue.  Suspect was not able to produce if issue still was a problem was due to no having the right hardware as Jordan.  Issue was re-reported but could not get access to the system so closing DR until issue is raised again.',1620176234),(908,357,385,'After working on the controller it was found that when the controller is set to European it will not send the daily emails.  This will require a web programmer to troubleshoot and fix the issue.',1620178327),(909,367,385,'Troubleshoot system and found that there was a bug in code.  Was fixed only on the controller for clearwater by fixing the system files instead of fixing the python/web code for DHCP.  Closing this DR since this site was fixed and need a python or web programmer to fix all the other systems so that DHCP will function correctly.',1620178760),(910,372,399,'Found that a space had been removed from the MITM making the DHCP variable al 11 instead of just a 1.  Added space back into code line and all works.  Will release fix in next update.',1624967241),(911,366,399,'Found that image had a record in the the tables that should not have been there.  Cleaned up image DB and recreated new image.',1624967291),(912,365,399,'Installation of equipment was being blocked due to being installed to low lossing line of sight with other devices.  Reinstalled devices to a more appropriate height.  All started working as designed.',1624967421),(913,364,399,'Closed all WO that were opened. ',1624969709),(914,374,399,'Set reel back up, FCM2 port 4 and all started working.  Not sure how the reel disappeared, no action log entries showing any changes.  Updated controller to R34, backup DB and attached files.',1627310434),(915,373,399,'This customer was not in DB, which is a separate issues that needs to be addressed.  The issue was the range extender fell off the wall and power disconnected preventing the signal from gettting to the TMM.  Once the range extender was reconnected to power all work as designed.  This customer was in a city north of wichita, maybe McPherson.',1627310943),(916,362,399,'Found that this was caused by a single orphan record in the adjust work orders table.  Removed orphan record on new image and all checked good.',1630520190),(917,358,399,'The controller had a logo file that was too large and just confirmed that a Wasua re order email does not have a huge image in the email.',1630521323),(918,24,399,'This was written up against R21 and since then the variance report was thoroughly worked are R30, so am closing this DR',1630521662),(919,25,399,'You can put an entry in the hosts file on the local computer or have the customers IT department put an entry in their DNS file.  On a windows machine the hosts file is located in the following directory:\n\nC:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\etc',1630524024),(920,52,399,'Since we are at R34 now, this issue no longer exists',1630524066),(921,126,399,'This shows up on the Work Order Status page of R34',1630524869),(922,375,399,'During calibration of all reels the system would not show any pulses for reel #2.  Had them move the wires from port 2 to port 1 and port 1 to port 2.  They also mentioned that port 3 was probably bad which is why it is not used on FCM #2 but port 4 is used.  After moving the wires recalibrated Reels 2 and 3 and now both were showing pulses so suspect there may have been a loose pulser wire for Reel 2.  Change software to show that reel 2 was now using port 2 and reel 3 was now using port 1.  All checked good and system correctly stopped when preset was reached.  They will continue to monitor.',1631718379),(923,376,399,'Murphy tractor does not use tank sensors, TMM, and they didn\'t know due to personal change that they had to go in and add inventory manually when they receive it.  Explained how to add and subtract inventory which solved this issue.',1631723994),(924,377,399,'Asked that the FCM be power recycled.  After power cycle express lane fcm started working fine.',1632343004),(925,378,399,'Could not find any 10W/30 reels that dispense over 2 quarts today as there was only 1 work order with a 10W/30 dispense.  All other dispenses today were on 5W/30 and MERC-LV where the max dispense showed 7 quarts.  Did a calibration on station 10, 10W/30 reel, and it correctly dispensed a preset of 2.5 afterwards.  Ask tech to get more specifics since there was only one dispense today for 10W/30 and it showed only 2 quarts being dispensed.  Suggested to tech that all reels be calibrated more accurately, do calibration and try to limit the amount of air in the prover container during calibration to more accurately calibrate the reels.',1633016392),(926,379,399,'Irvin asked if we could send out an IT person to setup there system on a VPN.  Explained to him what ports were needed if they wanted remote support, email without using their servers and db backup to oilcopsupport.com.  He said he would pass it on to their IT department so they could set it up to work.',1633720418),(927,380,399,'it looks like it happens anytime you click on the View Logs.  This error normally indicates that there is a lack of disk space for a queries to run.  The system starts to output data to a temp table and then runs out of disk space.  Check the system and it should have enough free space as only 81% full using the df -h command.  Since the swap partition is not used I decreased the size it and increased the overall size of the working partition /sda.  Had to reboot but the system didn\'t come back online.  When first logged into the system there were numerous Ubuntu errors that may have caused an issue during reboot that it didn\'t come back online.  There are some controllers that will hang at the bios screen when rebooting which may also be why it didn\'t come back online.  Trying to find contact info to call the location to have them power cycle the controller. ',1636490158),(928,380,399,'After reboot didn\'t get error when accessing the logs.  Performed a bit more cleanup of old files by compressing them.',1636492014),(929,381,399,'This issue was reported last week and again today.  Rebooted the system took care of the issue both times.  Will leave this DR open for a week to see if it reoccurs and if so will need to look cron log and hope it is showing some errors.  If there is enough disk space will restart MIM with debug options on to gather more info.',1636492213),(930,383,399,'Looks like usb port is bad or the cable is bad.  Asking that they first move the cable to a different port.  Phone number to headquarters is tel:402-891-8600.',1638910345),(931,382,399,'Returned controller with new power supply to them.',1638910407),(932,380,399,'Reported problems with accessing reports again but they had already rebooted it twice today and had no problems accessing the reports when initially looked at the system for issues on DR 383',1638910496),(933,383,399,'Sending 65\' usb cable to Dan at Service Express 6959.  Will log into controller in the morning to clean the cronlog as it will fill the disk by morning more than likely.  Will leave DR open until we have heard back that are is functional after cable installation.',1638914412),(934,383,399,'Looks like replacing the usb cable fixed this problem though they didn\'t call me to let me know they had replaced it just checked myself cause I hadn\'t heard anything and all look like it is working.',1639075060),(935,384,399,'Was able to connect to all 4 EH sites without issue.  Issue must have been with their local network.',1639592397),(936,384,3,'Why is Michels Building 28 - EH wolf not shown on team viewer?\n',1639593096),(937,385,399,'disk space usage is excessively high. Cronlog is over 5.2 GB which is not normal, Created new cronlog and archive old log..  System did not come back online after rebooting so email Mathew to see if he could reboot manually so I could finish looking into the issue.',1641840399),(938,385,399,'The reason the cronlog was so huge was due to the error messages produced by the system when it cannot communicate to the CDM. This 65Ft usb cable was replaced around Dec 7, 2021.  Mathew moved the cable to a different port and all started to work correctly again.  Monitored for a few more minutes and then rebooted but the system locked up again on reboot so email to have him power cycle manually.   Will leave this DR open for a couple of days to monitor if the issue comes back.',1641843279),(939,386,399,'Had them cycle power to FCM 13 and corrected the issue of it being red after it came back online.  Also explain and send manual for how to calibrate reels.',1641848182),(940,387,399,'Went through a list of user and deleted the ones that no longer worked there added two users and Al as a manager.  Reset all tech rights from all capabilities and removed just Open dispense.',1648041760),(941,388,399,'There were no Admins in the system besides the default so set him as manager from just being a technician.',1648041865),(942,389,399,'Contacted Jim, installer for Tommy Young, about how things are wire and to ask when someone could go to Greenbay to troubleshoot the system.  He said he would call me back once he determines when he or David can get up that way.',1649086475),(943,390,399,'The location is Porche of Wichita.  Tech brought TMM by and it was confirmed to work correctly with Radio and wired.  Did not check ports during visit.\n\nTech went back but still had the same issue.  Ask tech to bring all equipment by to check.  Found CDM radio was inop and port 2 on the TMM was bad.  Provided replacement TMM board but not CDM as he would wire the CDM to TMM since they are located only about 3 feet apart.\n\nTech returned to location and began troubleshooting the sensors.  Found that the sensor connected to port two caused the entire board not work, once removed the other ports worked as they should,   \n\nTech is returning for new sensor to replace bad one.  ',1649700965),(944,391,399,'Connected through TV and all seems fine.  Disk space is only at 57% and systems shows it was rebooted in the last hour.  Tim is going to contact their IT support company to see what they have to say since it is working normally from TV point of view. ',1649855455),(945,385,399,'Cronlog did not increase in size filling up disk.  All seems to be good as of today 13apr22.  Closing DR.',1649877117),(946,381,399,'System was all green today but the tanks did not show they were updating when you hover over them.   Looked at the tank adjustments and the system seemed to track one day ok and then go a week or a day without any entries in the logs.  Customer is not complaining though this is not right and there must be some interference that happens only once in awhile.  Recommend that they hardwire the TMMS or at least extend the wiring to the Range extenders to get them out from where they are currently located to see if that solve the issues of the intermittent adjustments.  ',1649877636),(947,381,399,'Noticed in the cronlog that there are a lot of CDM connection errors but without dates it is hard to say when these were written to the log.  They rebooted 2 days ago.',1649877862),(948,380,399,'Checked today and could access report no problem.  Closing DR.',1649877995),(949,391,399,'Have not heard back from Tim, called and left a message asking him whether or not their IT support found anything that would cause their connection to the system to be slow.  Closing DR since they have not responded.',1649878127),(950,389,399,'Walked the techs through how to troubleshoot the system.  They found that TMM 12 was causing the issues when connected to the buss.  They also discovered that another TMM failed on two ports.  Sent replacement TMMs to them.',1649878208),(951,391,399,'Tim called back and confirmed the issue was with a DNS server.  All is good.',1649879959),(952,392,399,'Gary C will contact their IT people and have them call me to arrange how to go about getting at least access to a local computer to look at the system through the web pages.  Getting access to the controller will require us to send them a cellular dongle for them to plug into the controller which should allow us to see that Teamviewer is online giving us access to the controller to view more details about the logs and cronlog.',1650395574),(953,392,399,'Facility pics are located under the Team ADG in the Clearwater Toyota channel files.\n',1650397257),(954,392,399,'While waiting for Clearwater\'s IT dept to get schedule a time they can be at the location did some testing to confirm that the system will stop dispensing if MIM crashes or the CDM fails to communicate with the FCM.  \nSet preset from the managers menu and \"crashed\" MIM while it was dispensing.  RED was incrementing still and the system stopped correctly at the set preset value.\nSet preset from a loaded WO and \"crashed\" MIM while it was dispensing.  RED was incrementing still and the system stopped correctly at the set preset value\nSet preset from the Techs menu on WO created from Managers menu and disconnected the CDM while it was dispensing.  RED was not incrementing but system stopped correctly at the set preset value.\n\nConclusion it seems that the CDM may have code to keep the RED incrementing instead of MIM keeping the RED incrementing.',1650462438),(955,392,399,'Sent an email to Gary asking for a backup of the DB.  He said I would have to walk him through the process to email so waited for him to finish up work he had to get done.  Gary called about 3pm and I walked him through the backup process, how to zip a file and then he emailed it to me.  Had issues importing it into phpmyadmin as a stand alone db, so attempting again.',1650489769),(956,392,399,'Gary received replacement equipment on 27apr22 and will be calling on 28apr22 to do some test dispenses and confirm the cell dongle will work for us to get into their system.',1651153025),(957,381,399,'Looked at cronlog today and saw a couple of instances where the CDM timeout occurred.  Unfortunately there are no date and time stamps associated with the entries to confirm that they are happening the same time as the tanks are not reading.  If the assumption is made that the latest is at the bottom then it is currently showing a CDM timeout which may explain why the \"hover test\" on the tanks is not showing the small movements in the inch values.  There is a bug that the devices will show green even though they are not communicating with the controller and that may be due to the web pages not seeing changes in the status so leave them at their last known state which was that they were green. Currently the system is constantly showing a CDM timeout but the customer has not called to complain as they seem to still be able to process dispense as just seen as a prompt that a pump start from the web page entry. ',1651157177),(958,393,399,'This is the first controller where 100% of swap disk is being used as well as it is maxing out of RAM almost and CPUs are below 25% utilization which it not normal compared to all other controllers.  It does seem to react slow but that could be their internet connection.  All reports work as designed for version of software installed.',1651177711),(959,393,399,'Testing with their DB after updating 224 controller to R34 the techs with limited capabilities seem to get an error that the pump start was unsuccessful even though you can hear the system \"click\" using simulator boards on the first attempt.  Clicking Start a 2nd time the system worked fine.  Used tech 7662 for first test. On 2nd test using 2061 it worked fine. 2nd time using 7662 system worked fine.  Using 2323 admin all cap worked fine on the first dispense but failed to start pump successfully on the top off dispense the first time Start was pressed.  2nd time Start was pressed it worked normally. 2nd test using 2323 all worked normally.  2323 3rd try normal, 2323 4th try normal, 2323 5th try normal dispense but printer didn\'t print, 2323 6th try normal and printed normal, 2323 7th try normal, 8th try normal but didn\'t print on close wo, 2323 9th try normal.  7662 3rd time work fine but when topoff reached value set in admin had to click dispense complete instead of it automatically changing to the keep wo open/close screen cronlog showed that auto dispense complete happened but didn\'t really, 7662 4th try normal, 7662 5ht try normal but waiting on o/c screen for a few minutes the system didn\'t print, 7662-6 try normal including print, 7662-7 try normal waited on o/c screen for 1 minute.  Issues with it not printing may have been due to the devices being too close together so spread them out and move printer, tmm, and fcm to the workbench in the other room. 7662-8 try normal, 7662-9 try normal..\n\nNothing found during this testing justified why they had to put the entire system into bypass for it to function.  The issues experience during this test can be explained away due to communication corrupt since the devices  were technically to close together.  Once they were moved apart everything worked as normal.',1651248987),(960,394,399,'Also told Martin to get ahold of Quags as they were the distributer and they needed to send techs out to do the work on the dripping psm and confirm warranty.  \n\nDuring troubleshooting found that Station 9 and 3 were offline.  Cycling power to FCM for station 9 brought it back online but doing the same for Station 3 didn\'t bring it back online.',1652289984),(961,392,399,'Troubleshooting station 9 with Chris at Clearwater Toyota showed that the FCM at station 9 had two bad ports, ports 3 and 4.  Port 3 was being used by the 0W/16 reel and port 4 was not wired to any reel.  The ports failed due to miswiring sometime during installation of the PSM to the FCM board.  Once the FCM board was replaced, the 0W/16 reel began working as designed and correctly incremented on the screen during dispenses and correctly stopped when the preset was achieved.    \n\nGary confirmed that Station 9 is correctly counting fluid and stopping at the correct presets after replacing the FCM board at station 9 so am closing the open discrepancy.\n',1652795802),(962,395,399,'Bob cycled power to TMM and it came back online.  He told me that TAC has not worked since installation but said they didn\'t use it.  He later called back saying the system was not working and that he would like me to look at it again.  All devices were green except the TAC.  I looked at the user and saw that most of the user had only preselect rights other had just select wo so made them all the same.  Bob said he was going to go by there and call me when he arrived but he didn\'t call back so suspect it must have been user rights they were complaining about because Bob could not give me any details of exactly what they were saying wasn\'t working. ',1653686618),(963,397,399,'David will call back to see how they want to handle replacement.  Suggested they send the controller overnight to us so that we can move the HD to a new controller saving them the time and effort to set everything backup since they have never backed up the HD.  \n\nSystem is on an UPS so it is strange the the power circuit failed on the controller.',1656429375),(964,398,399,'He had pulled the sensor out of the tank and saw that one of the ports was had \'gunk\' in it so he blew it out.  The TMM showed offline on the dashboard so had him cycle power.  After plugging back in he said that there was not power light so had him pull the box from the wall and look to see if any leds were lit on the board and they were not.  He found that the power supply was connected to a GFI outlet and found it tripped.  After resetting the outlet the system showed the correct leds on the pcb and the power light on the TMM was also lit.  System showed TMM back online and the correct tank level for just being filled showed correctly on the dashboard.',1656512076),(965,399,422,'For some reason can attach file',1657894539),(966,401,399,'Sent new pcb on RGA 081122-1MS invoice 174121',1661288152),(967,402,399,'Again at Zimmer Monroe another system stop counting while dispensing but this time it was on FCM port 1, the other issue on the 11th was on FCM port 2 which was found that the reed switch was bad and replacement pcb was sent.  This time it was just the fuse.  Explained to him that this was very abnormal that the fuse should blow after the system has been working just fine.  Asked him to keep an eye on it and he ordered 10 fuses for stock.  He will let us know if it blows again.',1661288392),(968,403,399,'Christopher called from Santa Fe and I walked him through some TS-ing steps for the relays on the single TMM they have.  We swapped the wires from relay port 2 to port 2 and port 2 to port 2 then changes the relay configuration so that when dispensing 5W/20 relay 1 would activate instead of activating relay 2.  Used Reel Calibration to dispense 0W20 which is activated when relay 2 on the TMM would energize and it dispensed properly.  Used Reel Calibration to dispense 5W/20 which is activated when relay 1 on the TMM would energize and it would not dispense.  Christopher swapped the wires back to their original locations and software relay configuration was reset back to original configuration.\n\nExplained to Christopher to trace the wire from relay to to the hardware it was connected to and explained that either the wire was bad or the component the wire connected to was bad.  Explained that if the ATF tank had the same piece of hardware that 5W/20 tank had that the relay wire was connected to then he would swap the hardware from the ATF tank with the hardware on the 5W/20 tank and all should work on the 5W/20 tank and then he could order a replacement component for the ATF tank.  ',1661363721),(969,403,399,'While waiting for Christopher to call me back, notice that station 9 kept going offline and then back online every few minutes.',1661365166),(970,405,399,'Peacock Ford has about 1000 more WO then Leith Acura yet it doesn\'t get the web page is slowing down your browser error message.   Both controllers are quad core  Celeron and both have the same amount of memory.  Peacock Ford response more quickly loading web pages and the CPU\'s never go above 25% usage.  Web content is at 100% on this controller where as Peacock Ford doesn\'t show this resource much in the top list.',1661777721),(971,405,399,'both systems are running the same OS 14.04 and all other software is the same on both controllers.',1661777995),(972,406,399,'Provided Dave with the default IP and gateway info that the controller should have had prior to being sent.  TV properties were not filled out so assume that it had the default info.  Gave him the Admin default password to access the controller once they can establish the connection.  He will call if they have any further questions.',1661796631),(973,403,399,'Customer reported that system just blows air through the system pump. 21094T-S2 purchased 8/9/20. PO# KC1156. ',1662045179),(974,402,399,'The board they sent back on RGA 081122-1MS checked good here so called Jeff to confirm he sent me back the board that he pulled out of PSM 2.  He also got the fuses in for the PSM 1 FCM port 1 and said all is working fine.  Suspect a wiring/connection issue that caused these problems so asked him to let me know should there be more issues of fuses blowing or products stop counting.  Closing DR .',1662471818),(975,409,399,'Receiving paperwork has a note that the wrong PN was lasered on the 10\' probes, so they may be the correct probes but when Dave went through writing down all the PN\'s he wrote down the PN that was incorrectly lasered on the probe.  Will confirm they are correct 10\' probes using manufacture PN and SN and comparing it to the calibration sheets sent by manufacturer.',1662579513),(976,410,399,'Emptied the application/logs folder of all .php files but that didn\'t put a dent freeing up disk space.  Saw that the cronlog was about 6GB but was unable to open to look at contents due to it size and slow connection to device.  Deleted the cronlog. Ran the top command and saw that it has been 88 days since last reboot, should be rebooted at least monthly as it is good maintenance practice.  Device had an old image file taking up 1.5GB of space so deleted that also.  When looking for more files that were taking up space the system locked up and kicked me out and didn\'t come back online tp reconnect.  Asked Mark to contact them to do a power cycle on the controller.\n\nNeed to recheck system next week to see if the cronlog is larger that it should be.  System was on R36 so should not have been filled up with php error files.',1662756086),(977,411,399,'see DR 410',1663010064),(978,410,399,'Was able to log in today and found that all hardware was showing as failed.  Saw disk space again was very low and found cronlog had grown to over 5GB.  Looked at what was in the cronlog and it showed that MIM could not detect the CDM as being connected.  MIM kept trying to connect to CDM and since it can find the CDM the cronlog will again grow huge and limit the disk space.  While logged in updated firefox due to issues with the login screen showing the actualy numbers when entered and but was never able to get past the login screen until upgrading firefox.',1663010279),(979,410,399,'System either has bad usb cable or bad usb ports as they have already moved the cable once before to another port for the same issue of all devices being offline.  Asked Mark to backup the DB to a usb drive so that he has a copy just encase we have to send them a new controller.',1663015545),(980,412,399,'They received new controller but GW was incorrect in the old db file used to update system before sending it to them.  Connected to the controller using ssh through one of their local computers through TV and manually fixed the interfaces file so GW would be correct to allow connection through TV.  Troubleshot 5W/30 tank showing low level shutoff.  All devices showed green so suspect tank sensor bad or port bad.  Set tank to manual tank without tank monitor and deleted sensor from system so they could at least pump until ADG could get down there to troubleshoot the system.  Contacted ADG and left message with details of issue they need to troubleshoot.  Asked ADG tech to call me when finished so tank and sensor could be setup correctly if they didn\'t know how.',1663170376),(981,408,399,'Waiting on EH Wolf to get Green Bay fully working to check this fix.',1664194461),(982,416,399,'Found no issues, probably slow connection either on there side to the internet or our side.  I have slow connections to controllers here in the same building.',1664894131),(983,414,399,'Fix published in release R_39',1664903200),(984,399,399,'implemented in version R38',1665146231),(985,397,399,'Their controller is working, has a mac address of   e4:3a:6e:4c:25:16 so we must have sent a replacement.',1665146478),(986,412,399,'Tech is schedule to troubleshoot 5W/30 tank probe 10/7/22',1665146530),(987,412,399,'Found port 4 bad on TMM SN 22720-1.  Sending new board on SO 144632 as soon as PO is received from ADG',1665152077),(988,418,399,'Didn\'t do anything but open a browser.  Disk space was only at 42% utilization and controller has only been up for 21 days.  Andrew said he had hard reset it a couple of times without the issue improving.  Ask him to give me a call if it should happen again since it is hard to troubleshoot something when the issue is no present.',1665431909),(989,415,399,'Closing as the system is working fine for now, misread the permissions.',1665431960),(990,419,399,'checked site as it was raised that the TMM was not working but it was working, green, when I logged in and only station 8 and 11 cycled on and offline.',1665597955),(991,419,399,'Mark said they are going to drop the CDM lower, and there may be an issue with the air handler inducing noise causing the radio signal to be intermittent. ',1665598157),(992,421,399,'Based on what the mail is describing the FCM may have a bad port that is constantly energized or the PSM is stuck open or the bypass valve is engaged.\n\nThe distributer will have to send someone there to troubleshoot the system.  Suspect PSM over FCM. Station 28 only has one reel and station 29 only has one reel and use the same FCM. Can\'t find that that port 1 and 3 are used for anything else so if it is the FCM then there are ports available to use instead of getting a replacement FMC.',1666038600),(993,400,399,'Added to E_2_86 and T_2_78 for testing',1666189839),(994,423,399,'Saw that on the 20th over 200 gallons were removed from the tank so asked him to confirm that the sensor wasn\'t accidently pulled out of the tank a bit and that it was resting on the bottom of the tank.  Watched as he went to confirm and saw the inventory value for the tank jump to over 200 gallons so it looks like someone had accidently pulled out the tank senor cable so that it was no longer on the bottom of the tank.',1666642646),(995,381,399,'Haven\'t seen the cdm timouts in the cronlog.',1666798778),(996,403,399,'This must have been fixed as they did not mention any issues yesterday when they called about the tank showing improper level which was fixed by them putting the probe correctly in the tank.',1666799001),(997,148,399,'This is so old and haven\'t heard of any issues concerning printer.',1666799127),(998,158,399,'This is really old and no updates have been added since 2017, no controllers show up in TV for this customer, nor mac address in comments.',1666799325),(999,160,399,'This is very old so closing.',1666799352),(1000,176,399,'This is really old, closing.',1666799434),(1001,193,399,'This is really old, closing',1666799506),(1002,196,399,'Very old, closing',1666799585),(1003,197,399,'Closing as no update since 2018',1666799632),(1004,198,399,'We are so past this T version release, closing',1666799686),(1005,199,399,'We are so past this T version release, closing',1666799699),(1006,200,399,'We are so past this T version release, closing',1666799715),(1007,202,399,'This is so old closing.',1666799777),(1008,205,399,'no update since 2018, closing',1666799803),(1009,210,399,'This is so old, closing',1666799836),(1010,208,399,'No updates since creation, closing',1666799868),(1011,213,399,'This is so old without updates, closing',1666799900),(1012,214,399,'Closing since no updates since creation in 2018',1666799935),(1013,215,399,'So far past this version closing.',1666799959),(1014,216,399,'So far past this version, closing',1666799981),(1015,217,399,'Do you mean high level alert?  If not what is an overfill alarm as I don\'t see that option.',1666800093),(1016,218,399,'so old, closing',1666800143),(1017,219,399,'so old closing.',1666800173),(1018,222,399,'so old closing.',1666800206),(1019,223,399,'so old closing.',1666800229),(1020,229,399,'this is so old closing.',1666800314),(1021,232,399,'so old and not enough data',1666800336),(1022,233,399,'so old closing',1666800362),(1023,236,399,'so old closing ',1666800397),(1024,244,399,'so far past this release closing',1666800514),(1025,246,399,'so old closing',1666800539),(1026,249,399,'so old closing',1666800587),(1027,257,399,'closing as we are so far past this release',1666800632),(1028,271,399,'so old, closing ',1666800662),(1029,272,399,'closing as this is so old',1666800770),(1030,284,399,'closing ',1666800798),(1031,285,399,'closing',1666800815),(1032,287,399,'Closing',1666800853),(1033,293,399,'This will be fix with the new version release',1666800905),(1034,296,399,'This was already done.',1666800930),(1035,301,399,'Doesn\'t seem to be an issue checking today.',1666801090),(1036,303,399,'no issue accessing reports.',1666801203),(1037,307,399,'closing since there have been no updates since creation.',1666801278),(1038,314,399,'all seems to be working',1666801476),(1039,321,399,'Jr will be completely redone in the future.',1666801568),(1040,329,399,'done',1666801638),(1041,337,399,'Which one should be deleted?',1666801865),(1042,338,399,'This does not have enough info to understand where to start or how to check, closing',1666801987),(1043,339,399,'This is very old but setup self to get emails, once confirmed receiving emails will close.',1666802823),(1044,340,399,'no updates since 2020 assuming last fix solved issue.',1666802981),(1045,341,399,'This is very old and no updates, controller is using customer smtp. ',1666803159),(1046,342,399,'This is very old and have tested this and seems to work correctly.',1666803591),(1047,343,399,'Current release for V1 is outputig the correct values not matter what the date format is set to.',1666804234),(1048,345,399,'This is old',1666804254),(1049,346,399,'checked macs and all show they are online. DR 346 confirming issue is resolved.',1666804604),(1050,347,399,'very old and no updates, closing.',1666804653),(1051,348,399,'very old closing',1666804676),(1052,349,399,'This is a duplicate of one already closed.',1666804700),(1053,350,399,'There is no controller on TV with this mac, closing.',1666804751),(1054,351,399,'This is very old and are far past the mentioned releases, closing.',1666804779),(1055,357,399,'Since there is no info on which controller this is for closing the dr as this was fixed in +R34 releases.',1666805133),(1056,421,399,'Emailed, phoned and talk with Tim Hill stating that he was arranging for tech but wouldn\'t give me any more details or estimation.',1666805232),(1057,419,399,'They must have moved the CDM as the stations are not cycling between online and offline like they did the day the issue was observed.',1666805375),(1058,339,399,'Getting some emails but not daily report.  Asked Web programmers what the possible cause could be.  Could be the server still but need web team to see what may be different between the other emails and daily report.  Last email received was 30oct22.',1667218418),(1059,339,399,'Getting daily reports now without doing anything on the controller.  Possible there is something with the email server as to why occassionally it stops some emails but haven\'t a clue since we have no ability to look at the email server or had anything to do with setting it up.  Changing f_from_name to see if that makes a difference from oilcop.com to gartec.it',1667477289),(1060,421,399,'Kody England called to say with the new solenoid it still gets hot and the system constantly allows the user to pump.  Based on the info from the last tech that did the troubleshooting it was narrowed down to the solenoid.  Kody confirmed that the only light lit on the FCM is the power light.  He pulled it off the wall to confirm that the LED for port 4 is not lit on the pcb.  Pic sent by Kody shows that pulser wire on port 2 for station 29 was not connected and touching the psc mounting screw.  Kody said the wires were not secure in the plugs for port 2 and secured them.  Move the wiring for station 28 to port 3 and the system still allowed oil to pump without activating the solenoid from the FCM.  \n\nFurther troubleshooting proved that the wire from the FCM to the PSM had to be shorted someplace in the route of the wire so had Kody trace the wire and he found the spot where the wire had chaffed and was arcing again the metal.  He fixed the wire and tested the system and all tested good.',1668109389),(1061,413,399,'We found that the specific gravity on the product they were over filling pretty consistently was extremely high for oil, set at 1.34 and I think that was a typo.  I set it for .934 guessing it was a typo and explained to Taylor how specific gravity affects the changes in oil quantity and that he can contact his supplier for the exact SG values of each of the oils.',1668110533),(1062,427,399,'Last time right after connecting with TV the system started to work normal for the customer.  This time the exact same thing happened.  Suspect maybe some sleep issues so edited the file /etc/default/acpi-support and changed SUSPEND_METHODS=\"none\" and ran the command sudo /etc/init.d/acpid restart from this site https://askubuntu.com/questions/949063/disabling-sleep-mode-on-14-04.\n\n\n',1668540073),(1063,428,399,'Controller for NMC is not configured to send Daily reports as non of the users in the listing have the Daily report selected to be sent.  Check all users so they will received the daily report.  If you don\'t get a daily report tomorrow then please update this discrepancy stating this.',1668693677),(1064,428,399,'Sent Daily report manually, please confirm users received the email.',1668693745),(1065,412,399,'Check site and all seems to be working for the TMM.',1668706836),(1066,428,399,'Found that another reason for emails not showing up was due to email provider blocking less secured apps automatically.  Switch it to ON and emails started working.',1668706895),(1067,429,399,'Troubleshot with John the TMMs and based on his responses to troubleshooting questions it was determined that both TMMs had been damaged during installation somehow.  Sent 2 replacement TMMS on SO 145221 original SO 137077 Inv 169565 on RGA 110822-1.  On 11/17/22 he had recieved and installed the replacement TMMS but things were still not working correctly.  When probes for waste oil was out of the tank it still showed 300+ gallons.  Configured new oil tmm replacement and all tanks correctly started reading the sensor info and seemed accurate.  Explained to John how to calibrate the tank readings by using a tape measure and adjusting the specific gravity.  Explain there is an inverse relationship to the tank level in inches.  Gave an example that if he read 48\" on his tape measure and the sensor was showing 47\" he would have to lower the specific gravity value.  He asked about the red vent tubes in the sensor wiring and explained what they are for.  He mentioned not seeing them on some of the probes and confirmed with him that all probes had them.  This is when he discovered that the sensors were not wired correctly on the TMM for waste oil and coolant.  He said something about the ground not being wired and after he fixed the wiring the sensor began reading more accurately on the waste product tanks.  \n\nAt the end of troubleshooting he mentioned that the customer told him there was a station that was not counting pulses so gave him some troubleshooting steps what to do to narrow down the issue.  Explained that checking wiring was the most important as a number of times during installation the psm gets wired incorrectly and damages the reed switch in the PSM or the FCM port.  I informed him that the system currently is only using 3 of the 4 ports as each FCM so if he finds that the FCM port is bad he should be able to use the extra port so that customer is not impacted.  Asked him to let me know what he finds out after troubleshooting so I can mark in these notes what fixed the issue.',1668708349),(1068,429,399,'John called back and he said that it looks like the pcb board is bad in the psm and there are 2 stations which are not counting so he is going to do some more troubleshooting to confirm it is the psm board and not the spare ports on the fcms.  Will send pcbs for psm if it is determined they are bad on the same RGA 110822-1MS.',1668713203),(1069,429,399,'John confirmed that he needs two psm pcb shipped.  Shipped today UPS ground.',1668716248),(1070,430,399,'Looked into system and could not find the system in TV.  Customer setup TV on a computer and was able to see that the FCM was offline.  Was able to SSH into the controller from the computer customer provided TV access on and found that the disk space was at 100% used.  Rebooted and disk space used dropped to 36%.  Updated their system to R37 and FCM came back online which I suspect was offline due to no diskspace since but took awhile for it to come back online, almost an hour.  Found the controller did not have TV installed on it and was able to find directions on how to install through the ssh session I had established.  Setup and confirmed that all is working for customer including TV on our side so in the future we can access it.',1669065001),(1071,430,399,'Customer info:  Distributor could be Midwest but could not find any invoices with a oilcop system listed.  Jared Getz 605-228-5900 is there IT guy.  ',1669065134),(1072,418,399,'Andrew called again today saying the system was slow again when accessing work orders but as soon as I connected with TV it responded normally without ever logging in.  Andrew will install TV on his computer and will connect to his computer instead of through the cloud to see if I can figure out what is going on since as soon as I connect with TV the issue goes away.',1669731488),(1073,418,399,'IP Address of controller is 205.190.94.93 with gateway of 205.190.94.126 for next time to see if ssh-ing into the controller also fixes the issues.  DNS is 8.8.8.8 so maybe ask next time if they have a DNS server of their own. System is running R37 which updating hasn\'t improved the issue and it still reoccurs eventually.  Going to leave up system monitor to see if having an app loaded that doesn\'t consume many resources has any effect.',1669732941),(1074,418,399,'Andrew called again which was the fastest time the issue returned.  This time however the system did not speed up as soon as I logged in using TV.  I was connected through ssh from his computer and was TV into his computer.  Local resources didn\'t show anything that would cause the issue so brought up the top program and saw that when he submitted a new WO  the mysql service was over 100% of CPU usage and had an TIME+ of over 666:02:22.  The system has only been up for 15 days which is only a litter more than 340 hours and would have suspected that once the controller was rebooted the time would have reset.   Going to monitor it for the next couple of days to see if mysql shows significant cpu usage and depending on what I find I may create a cronjob to restart the mysql service on a weekly bases outside of their working hours of 7am to 6 pm.',1669741392),(1075,418,399,'Controller has\nphp = 5.5.9\napache2 = 2.4.7\nmysql = 8.42 Distrib 5.5.46\nubuntu = 14.04 LTS\n',1669750764),(1076,418,399,'Commands to get software versions\nphp -v\napache2 -v\nlsb_release -a       \nsudo mysqladmin -v\nsudo python2 -V',1669753028),(1077,418,399,'look logs in the following directories\n/var/log/mysql/error.log\n/var/log/mysql.err and mysql.log\n\nuncommented the following lines in /etc/mysql/my.cnf\n# Here you can see queries with especially long duration\nlog_slow_queries	= /var/log/mysql/mysql-slow.log\nlong_query_time = 2\nlog-queries-not-using-indexes',1669754201),(1078,418,399,'References used:\nhttps://www.eversql.com/export-slow-sql-queries-to-slow-log-file/?utm_medium=referral&utm_source=blog&utm_campaign=p20004\nhttps://www.eversql.com/how-to-fix-mysql-high-cpu-usage/\nFor creating a cron job\nhttps://askubuntu.com/questions/451839/shell-script-issu\n',1669757417),(1079,433,399,'Called Robert and he said that he was able to figure it out.',1669997299),(1080,434,399,'Logged into the Wassau site and saw that they had both a TMM and an FCM offline.  We discussed how to go about troubleshooting but explained it was difficult to give more accurate troubleshooting info without knowing more about the issues since the site is wireless.  The only info given to Dustin was that the light on the TMM was a bit dim compared to the other others.   The site had already swapped the power supply to the faulty TMM.  Asked if Dustin wanted to have us ship a TMM and FCM prior to him going to the site so that once he was there if it turned out that the FCM and TMM were bad he would not have to wait for replacement parts.  He mentioned that they had 3 demo cases and was going to call Mark P to ask whether he could just take parts from the demo cases instead of us sending other since new devices would be coming out in the next few months.  I mentioned that it should not be a problem using those devices but there may be a small issue with the radio bars not showing if they had old firmware but if they had <16 ZigBee chips there shouldn\'t be an issue using them.  He will call if he needs any further troubleshooting help.',1669997754),(1081,432,399,'Haven\'t heard anything from Peacock Ford or ADG concerning this DR, but will leave it open for a bit longer.',1669998321),(1082,431,399,'Contacted Quality Mazda\'s IT company and found that they had given an computer on the network the same IP address as they allocated for the controller we sent.  Asked Bob the next time he went there to plug in the original controller and confirm it works and that we can connect using TV.  If all is good he will send back the 2nd controller we sent back and will credit them as necessary.  Will leave DR open until controller is returned.',1669998456),(1083,429,399,'Have not received any devices back yet.  Waiting on two TMMS and two psm pcbs to determine if they are warranty items but based on troubleshooting info from the tech they were incorrectly wired and thus are not warrantied.  Leaving DR open until parts are returned and testing can be done.',1669998588),(1084,426,399,'This will require a firmware programmer to fix this issue and one will not be available until they finish with the new hardware designs so it may be well into next year before this issue can be fixed.',1669998660),(1085,425,399,'This fix is in release R37.',1669998798),(1086,424,399,'This fix is in R38 but R38 has an issue with the login page refreshing making it difficult to log into the system so it is not suggested to update to R38 at this time.  Fixes for all issues will be in R39 ',1669999247),(1087,436,399,' Don\'t have much hope with this as if I can\'t access the controller it will not tell me whether it is a network issue or whether the controller\'s IP address was accidently changed.  This is the site that Tim had me call last week to explain how to change the tank levels so if they were exploring they could have accidently changed the IP address of the controller and the only way to fix would be to send a new controller configured for their network so it would eliminate the controller as the issue and then they would have to contact their IT department to troubleshoot which would mean they would be out of service for at least 3 or more days and that doesn\'t seem feasible.  ',1670247124),(1088,437,399,'Logged into controller through TV and gave them the IP address to put in their browsers.  They confirmed all was good.',1670248723),(1089,436,399,'Controller \'magically\" came back online itself.',1670251541),(1090,438,399,'We will get someone out to see what’s going on.\nDon Opland, President \nDows Equipment Service Inc.\nO: 734-722-3697\nC: 734-216-3147\nEmail: don@dowsequip.con\nwww.dowsequipment.com',1670344262),(1091,438,399,'WO 494046 at station 2 had an estop done twice according to the action journal.  The tech Michael Moore is the only tech who has open dispense capabilities.  If this is the WO which the \"over fill\" happened on then it is possible that a preset was not set and since he had open dispense rights the system would not have stopped until he manually stopped the flow.  This WO does not show that any product was dispensed though so it may not have been the overfill issue.  There is one WO with 9 quarts 492408, the next highest dispense amount is 6 and below.',1670344845),(1092,418,399,'Checking to see if issue of slow WO pages is there yet but all was working as designed.  Added indexes to WO tables.',1670354304),(1093,417,399,'In R39 release',1670421560),(1094,408,399,'Fix in R39',1670421624),(1095,438,399,'Saw Mark had changed techs rights and since there has not been any further communications on this issue closing DR.',1670853964),(1096,435,399,'Haven\'t heard back from Corky so assuming they do not use the REDs that didn\'t come back online so closing DR.',1670854006),(1097,432,399,'Haven\'t heard anything back on this issue, closing DR.',1670854046),(1098,418,399,'Checked today and saw that mysql was again consuming over 100% of CPU resources and wo maintenance page was extremely slow loading so ran the command to restart the mysql server.  After restart web pages responded normally.  Downloaded files from /var/log/mysql to see if web team can figure out why the queries are running so slow.  Disk space was checked after restarting mysql and was at 45% used.  Will have to check before restarting mysql so see if disk space is a factor.',1670854762),(1099,409,399,'Have not heard back from EH Wolf concerning the TMMs that are still offline at this site nor that they have confirmed the probes.',1670854840),(1100,406,399,'See that controller is online and have not heard anything back or of any issues.  Closing DR.',1670855047),(1101,406,399,'updated controller to R39',1670855158),(1102,405,399,'Updated controller to R39.  Also notice that web content when loading the wo manger pages was slow.  restarting mysql didn\'t seem to have any effect like it did at Parks Chevy.  Changed admin option to purge wo weekly instead of monthly but still didn\'t seem to help with the cpu resources be less for web content, though mysql didn\'t  show high uses for more than a few seconds.   There are still a lot of wos open but script error only shows for a few seconds instead of showing multiple times.  They still have 44 pages of open work orders all the way back from 2019.  Closed all wos that were older than Oct 1 2022 so now they only have 4 pages of open work orders.',1670856675),(1103,439,399,'Disk space 47% used, updated firefox and controller to R39 and downloaded latest backup file.',1670857755),(1104,440,399,'Change from monthly to weekly the purge wo option in admin options.  updated controller to R39, closed wo\'s older than oct 2022. backed up controller files, ',1670858585),(1105,404,399,'Controller was replaced due to failure so this issue is no longer presetnt.  Update controller to R39, disk space at 20% usage, took backup of controller.',1670858866),(1106,339,399,'Andrea has confirmed emails have been received for all accounts so updated this controller from R34 to the latest R39 and will wait to hear back whether this controller still has an issue.  if it does it perhaps my be an internal network issue and the customers IT department needs to be contacted to troubleshoot.  Emails are set to be sent out daily at 2300 hours and have an entry to show so that I should get an email when this happens.  Site has a slow internet connections.  Found that all FCM are showing offline also.  Last open workorder created was on 9/12/22 but wo table shows wo\'s as recent as 12/10/22',1670859588),(1107,339,399,'Disk space was at 72% due to old img file on controller, removed and disk space is now at 44%.',1670859848),(1108,337,399,'TV shows only one controller with mac address  00:e0:4c:28:ee:a5 but is offline and oilcop support shows that there was a controller that was syncing with that mac address oilcop-00e04c28eea5.  The last WO that shows up on oilcop support is dated 11/30/21.  Since this is a very old DR and have not received any info back from Andrea, closing DR and we can raise a new DR with updated info as to what the problem is since this controller shows offline.  ',1670861098),(1109,309,399,'Have not seen any update to this DR but will leave open for development of report in new versions and updates.',1670861208),(1110,339,399,'Received emails from this controller that have was not getting before controller update.  Suspect issue has been resolved but will wait till tomorrow to close after confirmation that a daily report from this controller is received.',1670861372),(1111,339,399,'Successfully received daily report on schedule, attached.  Closing DR.',1670936292),(1112,441,399,'Troubleshooting showed that FCM SN 82118-3 had a bad port 2 on the board.  Ray said they ordered a PSM but when they installed it the system still did not stop at preset.  Original SO# 114506 Inv# 144268 bought by Professional Maintenance & Supply INC but it was Universal Distribution Group that called for help on the system.  System is out of warranty but they need an FCM sent.',1671139306),(1113,441,399,'Shipped FCM pcb for this DR on SO 145876.  Will close DR when installation of PCB has been completed and functionality of system is confirmed as good.',1671468579),(1114,442,399,'I sent a link to the OilCop manuals for Jeff to look at and explain that if they are having issues with the loss of communications to a specific station they could hardwire it to the CDM.  He will call me if he needs any further help.',1671638834),(1115,443,399,'Called Mike back since we were off Friday and he said all was good after they rebooted.  Logged into their system and notice that their TMM for new oil was offline.  Sent Mike an email asking him to power cycle the TMM when he gets a chance to see if it comes back online.  Mentioned that it will not stop them from dispensing but they cannot rely on the tank quantities.  Will check later to see if it is back online.',1672150100),(1116,431,399,'Still waiting on controller to be returned.',1672150428),(1117,429,399,'Still waiting on devices to be returned.',1672150479),(1118,418,399,'Checked system today and it was loading the pages normally.  Did not have to restart mysql. Will monitor for a few more weeks to see if the issue returns.',1672150756),(1119,409,399,'Sill have not heard anything back from EH Wolf concerning the rest of Green Bays TMMs in other building.  System does have R39 installed.',1672150973),(1120,444,399,'Had to do a sudo service mysql restart command for it to start working correctly.  Need to keep an eye on it.  There are not alot of WO open, only one page but the page seems longer than normal.  This system in on R39.',1672177199),(1121,445,399,'Tested controller and all USB ports seemed bad as it would not detect a keyboard or mouse when connected to the system.  Was able to get system to recognize a keyboard only once at which time I enable the BIOS diagnostics to display errors.  After saving changes and exiting system would not recognize the keyboard or mouse no matter what port they were attached to so could not get past the diags screen.  Removed the HD from the Pantropic\'s controller and installed in the Jobbers controller.  The Jobber\'s controller would not recognize the network port so had to reimage the drive and then install Pantropic\'s DB on the newly image controller.  Verified all network by updating controller and confirmed that it communicated with the Bench CDM.',1672947804),(1122,445,399,'Pantropic\'s received the controller and installed but could not access the system.  IT was called and they had to set the new mac address in their firewall before system could be accessed.  The system devices were all still showing red as the system could not communicate with the CDM.  Had Juan change usb port the CDM was connected to but did not help.  Ran command dmesg | grep tty to determine if the system was recognizing when the CDM was connected.  It was so the assumption is that the CDM was bad.  Called Jobbers and talked to Ron who said he replaced the CDM the other day so the assumption is that the CDM he replaced doesn\'t have the correct firmware on it.  Sending out a newly tested CDM on SO 146182 UPS NDA by 8am with a <16 ZigBee chip on it since this site only has 3 devices after testing to make sure it would communicate and recognize hardware through the FCM and TMM RS485 ports as well as detect wireless devices.  \n\nRon will go by and pick up CDM and send it back along with the original for us to check out on RGA 010523-1MS.  \n\nJuan will contact me in Teams when he gets the CDM so that we can make sure there are no further issues and hope that the FCM that Ron replaced is compatible with the current controller software as I have been told it is from a Sears site that closed down..',1672948330),(1123,444,399,'System was responding normally, keeping DR open for another couple of weeks at least.',1672948730),(1124,443,399,'TMM new oil still offline.',1672948834),(1125,442,399,'Station 12 still shows failed FCM-16, user defined name FCM 15.  Station 6 seemed stable today which used FCM-6 and FCM-13 port 2.',1672949528),(1126,441,399,'Have not heard anything back on whether or not they installed the new FCM pcb as of yet.',1672949671),(1127,434,399,'Have not heard back on this issue but checked site and saw FCM-2 was offline as well as TMM-3.  Updated system to R39 while logged in.',1672949899),(1128,431,399,'Still waiting on controller to be sent back.',1672949926),(1129,429,399,'Still waiting on devices to be returned.',1672949953),(1130,418,399,'Checked system today and it was responding normally.',1672950198),(1131,445,399,'After installing the new CDM the system if working except for the segment display.  When power is cycled it does not light up with all zeros which it should.  Ron is going to the site to test the power supply to see if it is the power supply or the segment display that is bad. ',1673013602),(1132,445,399,'Juan wrote back to say that the display is bad and the meter is bad.  I asked for clarification on whether or not when he stated the meter is bad that it doesn\'t stop at a preset amount.  Waiting on his reply.',1673014351),(1133,445,399,'Juan said their meter is burnt and not working at all.  Ron is go to change out the damaged parts using parts I\'m assuming he has in stock as currently he had not requested any parts from us.  Waiting to hear back.  Also notice that their calibration k-factor is way off from normal and is currently set at .266 and normally it should fall between .8 and .9.  Sent an email to Ron recommending that he calibrate their reel after he replaces the bad meter.',1673015283),(1134,446,399,'Had Jeff confirm that the outlet the controller uses has power available.  He said that the outlet didn\'t have any power and would investigate if a breaker tripped.  He would call Automotive Equipment if they need further assistance.  Leaving DR open for a day and if they do not call back by tomorrow will close DR.',1673988268),(1135,447,399,'When I was logged in to troubleshoot the issue, Mark also logged in and began changing screens on me so I told Tom it looks like someone else in his company was also talking to someone here about the issue so I disconnected.  Not sure what Mark did but did see just as I logged off that he was changing the custom WO options to numeric from what looked like Alpha but unsure if it was the alpha setting that allowed for both numbers and alpha characters or whether it was the setting which only allowed alpha characters.',1674228015),(1136,447,399,'Tom called again and said that the system worked the first time but was now giving them the same message and he asked was there a way to disable the system so that they could just pump oil because he had 14 cars he had to get out.  I told him we could try disabling the custom work order setting for the time being and he confirmed it was working for what they needed.  Talking to Mark to find out what he had done it may be that they were trying to load a RO that was already entered in the system.  Will have to confirm the error message is clear that when they enter a duplicate it states that the user is trying to load a work order that already exists instead of just invalid work order.',1674228755),(1137,446,399,'Haven\'t heard back from customer so assuming that they were able to solve the power issue without needing anything from us.  Closing DR',1674229866),(1138,447,399,'Called Tom and explained to him why he was getting the invalid WO message and told him what to do when that happens, was to select the WO from the Select WO screen instead of putting it in through the Load WO screen.  Re-enabled the custom WO configuration.  Closing DR.',1674246288),(1139,422,426,'Logic behind remaining days to empty column in inventory page oilcopsupport :-\nproduct average dispense of the week(past 7 days) = sum of dispense amount of the product/7;\nremaining days to empty of the tank = sum of inventory of the product(tanks content)/product avg dispense of week(7days); \n\nSome controllers are showing that field blank because there is no dispense data.',1674281368),(1140,448,3,'Update 9:31 AM Saturday..... \nFCM 1,3,4,5,16,17,18,19,20,21,Range extender-1, Range extender-2 (WI-FI Red)\n\n12 wired set to wireless is (RED), 14 set to wired is (RED)',1674314099),(1141,448,3,'Update 10:45 AM Saturday.......\nLogged in all devices Green..\n',1674319135),(1142,450,399,'Sent new TAC panel, warranty item on SO 146536 PN 100819',1674501338),(1143,448,399,'All hardware showed green except FCM address 21 was red.',1674501443),(1144,448,399,'Billy from their IT department called about 10:30 am but didn\'t get the message till now that they were having issues with their system and wanted a call back.  Called back at 402-681-2758 and left a message.\n\nLooked at their system and saw that FCM-15, wired, and FCM-21, radio, are offline.  All other devices showed online.  FCM-15 came back online while I was looking.  ',1674585775),(1145,448,399,'After accidently hitting the scan for new hardware button the system then showed FCM-8 wired, FCM-10 wired, FCM-14 wired, and still FCM-21 radio offline.  After refreshing the screen a couple of times.  Only FCM-14 wired and FCM-21 were still offline.  Refreshing the screen every so often it looks like the wired devices are intermittently going offline but unsure how that is affecting them but have already discussed with Mark that the wired communications should be rewired as a series bus instead of being wired with parallel busses.',1674586151),(1146,448,399,'Billy called because they forgot the admin for H&H Recon so he was not calling about any issues at this site.',1674588593),(1147,448,399,'Mike called to day as they were having issues with Station 3 and cycling power and rebooting the controller had no affect.  They currently have Stations 2,3,17,18.19.21 all radio not working.  Wired stations are still intermittently dropping randomly offline also but they at least come back online within a few seconds.',1674660790),(1148,451,399,'Attached backup file pins were provided from.  Kevin is going to connect using a network cable hooked directly into the controller.  Will call Kevin back later to get new IP info and update properties in TV.  Current values are as follows but are confusing as there are multiple IP addresses and there are 2 TV devices shown for for Reliable Chevy.\nReliable Cheverolet - Quags\n\n172.18.131.165\n172.18.131.54 XX\n255.255.255.0\n172.18.128.254\n10.255.16.22\n\nReliable Chevrolet (2) - Quags 00:e0:4c:28:ee:8c\nIP: 172.18.128.15\nNetmask: 255.255.255.0\nGateway: 172.18.128.254\nDNS: 10.255.16.22\nDHCP: ON\n',1674663861),(1149,451,399,'Kevin called back as he was not able to connect through ethernet cable but saw it was online again so was able to go in and set the IP address to static.\nIP: 10.58.2.15\nNM: 255.255.255.0\nGW: 10.58.2.1\nDNS: 192.168.226.12',1674681679),(1150,448,399,'Called Colton, 402-681-2758, and left him a message that I needed to talk to him about the issues that are happening at this site. ',1674681755),(1151,448,399,'Colton still has not called back yet but Mike and Tom from H&H Chevy have called multiple times.  All radio stations have been down since yesterday and wired stations are intermittently going on and off line.',1674741553),(1152,445,399,'Juan chatted with me about this issue Wednesday and asked him to cycle power but it seemed as though he didn\'t understand but he never chatted back.  The picture he sent yesterday of the FCM looked like it was a wired so assumed that the TAC was also wired because he responded that it was wired but it is actually using radio based on the pic he sent today of the TAC so set it back to Radio and it turned green.  Juan confirmed in chat that it was now green but didn\'t respond that his issue he sent an email for now was fixed.  it has only 2 bars on the radio so his site may benefit from a RAN.  Will monitor.',1674832422),(1153,448,399,'Colton called back and confirmed that there were 4 RANs installed and what he remembers their addresses were set to so added those missing devices to the hardware list.  Adding them didn\'t help much but there were a few more radio stations that came back online, 19, 20, 2 and 21.  1,3,4,5 still show offline though.  \n\nCalled Tom and let him know that the tech will be up next week sometime and he said that they were making it work with the stations that do stay online.  They still have issues with the wired stations and the system really needs to be rewired so that the RS485 buss is a series bus and not wired in parallel.  Suggest all stations be wired, see marked up drawing attached.',1674832960),(1154,452,399,'Logged into system and confirmed all hardware was green.  Then went to reel calibration and activated the reel for UDT-2 and it gave a successful pump start message.  Canceled it on my end and Jeff tried and successfully pumps oil from the reel calibration menu.  Not sure what the cause of initial issue was but HD space was ok, controller was up for over 258 days and suggested maybe to reboot a bit more often, every other month or so.  Otherwise he said there were no other issues with the system.',1675107359),(1155,451,399,'Kevin called again today and said that the system has not been working since the IP change.  Did some troubleshooting with him and the only thing that was seen by the system was the CDM but the CDM intermittently only communicated with the other devices but mostly wasn\'t able to see them.  They used a shorter USB cable for TS-ing and it was able to pick up the closest FCM but again it was intermittent so it is highly possible that the CDM is bad.   CDM seems to be intermittent or the cable is.  Also the controller is cycling power on its own.  Sending CDM, 6\' USB and power supply.  Bob will use the controller we sent for Quality Mazda for testing also after he gets either me access to the controller to change IP address to match customers or he has his IT person use the guest account on the controller to change it.  Sending spare parts on RGA 013123-1MS',1675193890),(1156,448,399,'Colton moved the CDM and RAN 6 to lower positions and other angle as much as he could but it did not help any of the radio devices.  Highly suggest all FCM be rewired into a serial bus.  Logged in at 0630 and looked at all devices, there was some slight improvement, see attached Device Status 2feb22 0640.docx.  Watched for a bit longer and then refreshed the screen and all devices were offline at 0651. Refreshed the screen and most wired and some two radio, 4 and 5 were back online.  Refreshed again and some more devices came back online.  Strangely station 20 showed online, this station has solidly been offline since they opened for business.  Was even able to get a successful pump start using reel calibration.  Stations 3 and 4 also showed online today and they have not been online this consistently since 24jan23.',1675341799),(1157,451,399,'After troubleshooting with new controller, cable, cdm, power supply still could not get system to recognize any of the devices.  Explained to Bob that we need to confirm the devices are good and that not all the radios in the devices have failed and the only way to do that was to get the devices out of the current environment and test.  Either by sending them back to us or he can do it off site there.  Say this morning that all devices were working and sent an email to Bob and Kevin showing them that all is working and that they need to figure out what piece of equipment, device, etc is causing the interference so look for something that has been recently installed that was not there before the system failed which was at the time they changed the IP address on the controller.  Up until this time the system had been working without issue except for the TAC.',1675342031),(1158,448,399,'0805 all devices showed offline including CDM.',1675345487),(1159,448,399,'Enabled debug all the time so need to make sure to go in every other day or so to make sure that the disk does not fill up.  Also set the display not to blank so that you don\' t have to log in each time you go to the site.',1675348605),(1160,448,399,'CDM is timing out, maybe the connection to the CDM is not solid after Colton readjusted things.  System is trying to reopen the serial port which means it detects the usb cable but not the CDM.',1675356964),(1161,448,399,'It was strange as all I had to do to get it to stop the serial opening cycle is to restart MIM.',1675357038),(1162,448,399,'CDM keeps going offline and dropping from the port and finally it wouldn\'t come back online after restarting MIM.  Ran the command dmesg |grep tty and it verified that the controller could not longer see the usb cable and believe the messages were misleading me when it said devices says it is basically ready but not responding as it was probably seeing or using the last device status which was good to mean that it was still connected when it actually wasn\'t.  \n\nHad Mike unplug and plug into a front port to make it easier to get to as it sounds like it was difficult to get to the back ports so maybe the port it was plugged into in the back got damaged as it sounded like it was not easily seen.  Will monitor till end of day to see if it drops anymore.  Colton is sending a contractor to the site to confirm the usb connections and I asked Mike to relay to the contractor that there is a connection between the 65\' cable and the CDM  he should also check and confirm it is good.',1675371500),(1163,453,399,'After troubleshooting system if was found that the fuse in the newly installed PSM was blown so removed it from original and installed it into the newly installed PSM.  Also determined that port 4 of the main shop\'s PSM was damage SN 020922-2 so they will swapped with East Shops PSM so that the customer will not see the problem.  Will keep DR open until FCM is sent back.',1675706084),(1164,453,399,'RGA 020623-1MS is being issued for bad FCM',1675706116),(1165,454,399,'Couldn\'t start pumps at first so put MIM in debug mode and everything was reporting good so had them try a dispense.  It worked for them so left MIM running in its own window and will have to go back in later today to reboot the system so that MIM is running normally not in debug mode.',1675784814),(1166,451,399,'Customer back on original controller and all systems working including the TAC which has not worked since installation.  They were never able to figure out what was causing the interference.',1675877818),(1167,448,399,'Mark went up and readdressed all wired FCMs and turn off all terminators on the FCMs.  He then cycled power to all FCMs using radio and they all came back online and stayed online after remounting the CDM.  Still concerned due to the system having parallel RS485 buses though but is has been stable for the last 30 minutes or so.',1675886371),(1168,448,399,'Just checked system and all radio station were again offline. Dashboard was updating tanks ',1675888285),(1169,454,399,'Customer couldn\'t access their system, had them provide IP addresses of their computers and the first ping to excessively long time to return a response yet the response time was still in ms even though it took 3-5 seconds before the ping returned any results.  Explained to Mike that it was an internal network issue and he confirmed they just swapped out all the switches so they may not have them configured correctly yet to prevent the issue they are having.',1675950240),(1170,454,399,'Mike called back to say the IT person said to change the gateway to 10.215.40.253 instead of 10.215.40.254 but once that was done then they couldn\'t connect at all even though the system could be pinged from their computers.  Mike had me change it back to 10.215.40.254 as at least they could pump oil when it was set to that and Mike will call me back if there are any other issues.  System would kick me off intermittently like their network switches were not configured correctly Mike mentioned that they were having a number of network issues beside the OilCop system.',1675951658),(1171,454,399,'John their IT person called and said to change IP address from 10.215.40.31 to 10.215.40.250 and use the gateway 10.215.40.254 which was original.  Seemed to have worked as they can access the system now.  Will monitor for a couple more day before closing DR.',1675960197),(1172,448,399,'Called customer at end of day to confirm they had no issues after system was wired correctly and they said they hadn\'t.  The asked about whether the system could support a use case and said it could if the Top and multi dispense were turned on so activated those in the Admin options.  Closing DR.',1676031662),(1173,455,399,'Explained to Tim that it was perhaps caused by communications issue that resolved itself by the time I logged in.  Explained to him the next time it happens to look at the device status section of the Admin or Managers dashboard and confirm that the device is green if he get another call about this issue.  Also asked that he call back if this issue increases in frequency.',1676054447),(1174,456,399,'System would not allow me to login using the normal account, it just kept kicking me off using TV.  Tried to ssh into the computer from a local computer but disk was too full.  Had to login as Guest and then use TV File transfer to go to the application/logs directory and remove all the files with .php extensions which are just error logging files.  After cleaning up needed to reboot again to clear the system tmp files and cache that were still causing error messages in the browsers when access the system.  Updated from R34 to R38 to prevent disk from filling up again. Confirmed all working and downloaded a recent backup.',1676059979),(1175,457,399,'Called Steve at 720-975-3188, had him reboot the controller and it still did not show as online in TV.  Asked him to have IT call me so the issue could be troubleshot further.',1676479316),(1176,457,399,'No call back from their IT department yesterday and passed onto Steve at Colorado Petroleum. ',1676551601),(1177,409,399,'Sill have not heard anything back from EH Wolf concerning the rest of Green Bays TMMs in other building',1676556700),(1178,418,399,'System was running slow for manager dashboard and wo maintenance pages.  Ran sudo service mysql restart and system started responding normally.',1676557266),(1179,429,399,'Devices were returned on 1/27/23.  Found that 1 PSM pcb had a bad reed switch caused by incorrectly hooking up system during installation he other checked good so returning that one to stock.  One TMM SN 090221-2 had 4 bad solenoid ports also caused by miss wiring during system installation but TMM SN 090221-1 checked good on ports and relays so returning this item to stock.  RGA 110822-1MS.',1676557553),(1180,431,399,'Still waiting on controller to be sent back.',1676558682),(1181,434,399,'Have not heard back but checked site and saw FCM-2 was still offline.',1676559184),(1182,441,399,'Have not heard back if they installed the FCM, closing DR since there has been no communications with UDG.',1676559380),(1183,442,399,'Can\'t find another DR for this site though I could have sworn that one was created.  From the other day taled with Jeff and explained how the system works and how to wire the system so that it is more stable in the other building so the customer no longer has any issues.  Also explained how to wire the TMMs which are a constant problem at this site as they call about every two weeks asking us to reboot their controller so they start talking and updating the dashboard like they should.  Have not heard back from Jeff since we had our last discussion in which he was recommending to the customer that they hardwire the back shop and TMMS.  He is also applying to become a distributor so they can continue to support this customer as they plan to double their capacity.  Today see the system offline and am surprised they have not called to complain it is not working.  Maybe they just blocked it from TV access and it is working.',1676559848),(1184,443,399,'All hardware shows online so closing DR.',1676560127),(1185,444,399,'System is responding normally, closing DR.',1676560223),(1186,453,399,'Waiting on RGA boards to be returned.',1676560314),(1187,454,399,'System is working today, closing DR as it looks like IT issues have been resolved.',1676560387),(1188,457,399,'Still have not heard back from their IT department nor have I heard back from Steve at Colorado Petroleum.',1676901912),(1189,442,399,'Noticed that Parks Ford has been offline for the past week.  Called Jeff at ASAP who was going to do some work for them and he said they haven\'t called him about any issues.  Maybe just a network issue.',1676902787),(1190,458,399,'Found a transaction on 20feb23 for 1 5w/30 546.4Q(136.6G) which his invoice said they delivered 150G. 0w/20 522.8Q(130.7G) was also 150G on the invoice as well as 100G for Dex6 on the same day.  Will have to look further to find the Dex6 entry in the Tank Adjustment report.  He also gave 9feb23 delivery data of Dex6 50G, 5w/30 150G, and 0w/20 150G.  Will look those up in the system..\n\nMark explained that there are just too many variables for Jeff to go back to the supplier and say they shorted him.  There is temperature, tank dimensions accuracy, method of delivery, 55 gal barrels, filled by weight, but the supplier could leave as much as 2\" of oil in the bottom of the barrels and still say they delivered 55 gals, by meter on the trucks which could be calibrated for a different oil or they could not be calibrated at all.  Basically no saleman or anyone in the fluid management business will say a customer can use the data shown in their systems to contest a delivery invoice.\n\nJeff is going to email his delivery info so I can see if there is a trend, i.e. if each delivery on the invoice is 70Q off from what the system reads then he could feel more comfortable that the delivery invoice is accurate.  But as Mark mentioned there is just too many variables to confidently hold suppliers accountable if system does not match invoiced deliveries.',1677162751),(1191,459,399,'Tim Rickenbaugh 561-818-7754 cell, contacted us and walked him through solving some issues.  Had to run the command sudo service mysql restart as well as restart the system before the system would successfully start the pumps.  It could have been that I didn\'t wait long enough between trying to start the pumps and restarting mysql for the system to catch up but rebooting solved all there issues after issuing the mysql restart command.  Will monitor site for the next month or so to see if this issues comes back while the web team investigates.',1677255134),(1192,418,399,'Had to run the command sudo service mysql restart on their controller again today.  Did it before they called about an issue.  System show over 309:xx:xx for time+ when using the top command though the controller was rebooted 8 days ago.',1677255361),(1193,460,399,'Tested using reel calibration.  The system successfully started the pump and they dispensed about half a quart but no pulses were registered.  Need to have Colton go there to troubleshoot.  Mark and Mark were discussing that Colton could troubleshoot this issue when the swivel parts came as he will have to go there to do that.  They said the swevels should be in any day now.  We will have to ship as PSM and FCM pcb with the swivels so he has all the parts needed if either of them checks bad.\n\nFailing after working for almost two months after installation is basically unheard of.',1678306145),(1194,461,399,'Troublehshooting proved that the station 5 FCM had 2 bad ports, 1 and 4, 4 is connected to the 5w syn trans reel.  Also the PSM PCB had a bad reed switch.  System is out of warranty.  Moved PSM PCB from unused PSM #2 to PSM#4.  Robert will explain to customer and ADG will create quote for customer and once they sign off will call and place the order for a FCM and a PSM PCB.',1678482905),(1195,461,399,'Parts put on shelf to ship today.',1678817103),(1196,462,399,'ADG called and transferred me to a tech on site named Eric.  He at first told me the entire system was red but was actually looking at the recent WO section of the managers dashboard.  After explaining that he had to scroll down the screen to see the device status\'s he saw that all devices were online.  Had him attempt a dispense but he said there was no pressure behind the fluid coming out of the handle.\r \r Had him go to the tank room after seeing that they used the TMM relays on TMM 2 to control solenoids, not ones that we sell, and had him confirm when I activated a reel through reel calibration menu that the associated relay lit up on the face of the TMM 2 which it did.  Explain system theory of operation and that it had to be something common to all the solenoids and TMM.  TMM was working as tank levels were making the normal small adjustments so passed on that I would suspect the fuse on the TMM2 had failed or the power supply was failing and couldn\'t produce enough current to activate the relays.  Mentioned that should the fuse fail again after putting a new one in if the current one is bad would mean that one of the solenoids was shorted and he could pull the connector off the TMM board and install one relay at a time until he found the one that cause the fuse to blow and that should be his bad solenoid.  Encase the fuse was good explained also how to test the power supply using the AC setting on his meter and that anything above a few mV of AC would indicate the power supply for the TMM was weak..  If neither of these items are bad then he will have to troubleshoot the air system to ensure that it is working correctly and no one shut off a main valve.  If he doesn\'t call back then it was the fuse.  Keeping DR open for a day to see if he calls back and if not will close.',1678818076),(1197,462,399,'Need to document that they were concerned since another tech was there just a couple of days ago that his would had not caused todays failure.  Explained to Eric that there was nothing that Robert could have done to cause the issue that was present today as there is nothing connecting the two devices which he commented that he had to hear that.',1678818508),(1198,462,399,'Tech was able to get fluids working that were using relay 3 of TMM2 and relay 3 of TMM1 but he didn\'t pass on what he did to get them working.  We tried swapping the wires from relay 1 to relay 4 which was unused but they were too short so instead swapped relay 3 with relay 1 and relay 1 with relay 3 wires.  Unfortunately the tech didn\'t realize that he could remove the blue connectors and since the wires were so short he was not confident that he got them in correctly as our testing didn\'t quite show the results expected so it is a good change he was correct that he didn\'t get them in correctly.  He was in a rush so he is going to return the wires to their original locations on the relay board and confirm everything is back to the way he had it before moving the wires.  He suspects the solenoid is bad and he swapped it out with a solenoid from a tank that is not being used but he did not confirm it was good before installing it as someone could have already swapped it out in the past and didn\'t document that they installed a bad one on the unused tanks.  Erick said that he is pretty confident that the TMM board is good so is going to order a solenoid and will call back if he needs further help with the system.  Will leave DR open until we hear back from him.  ',1678826945),(1199,463,399,'Had him remove the TMM cover to confirm that the TMM had power.  We do not have access to their system through TV so could not confirm the configuration of the site.  He said that there were wires going out of the bottom connectors so assume they do have a tank sensor and he also said that wires were attached to the TMM relays and confirmed that relay 1 port was wired to a solenoid but when he sent a pic it didn\'t look like there was a solenoid attached to the pump, just a regulator filter was connected.  His picture didn\'t show the out going line nor if there was a cutoff value that may be preventing the fluid from dispensing or air.  Also had him configure a relay since he said none were configured when he went to the menu and he did confirm that when he used reel calibration for the product 15w/30 the relay light for port 1 activated on the TMM but he could still not pump fluid.  Gave him P&G Marketing and Associates Dustin Dougan contact info, dustin@pgmassociates.net, 785.764.0604.for more support.\n\nWill leave DR open for a couple of days encase they call back.',1678894466),(1200,463,399,'Looks like someone was able to go by Tri State Trucking and troubleshoot the system and found that the \"pump keys had failed\" and Oakland repaired it.  Closing DR.',1679079822),(1201,460,399,'Colton called to ask which station was having the issue.  Explained what it was, what I did to troubleshoot and what he needs to do to troubleshoot.  He said he would call back.',1679576911),(1202,460,399,'This is what Colton\'s finding were:  \n\nWent threw and checked wiring and fuses and looked for any other issues but nothing was found. Come to find out it was an issue with the laptop they were using on that bay. They switched to another computer and everything worked as it should. Thanks ',1679583563),(1203,460,399,'Colton discovered the issue was the computer by doing the following:  I didn’t swap any parts, after looking at everything on the fcm and solenoid and not seeing any issues. The technician had mentioned he had other issues with that computer so I had them do it from a couple separate computers and it worked correctly with no issues ',1679584191),(1204,464,399,'At first they were cycling power on a TMM thinking it was the controller.  They called me back once they located the controller and preformed a power cycle on it and confirmed that the CDM had power also.  They said the network connection had both yellow and green lights but still could not access the system.  Asked them to call their IT department to troubleshoot a possible network issue as they may have accidently changed something on the network that is causing the system to be inaccessible.  Pretty sure we have always been able to log into their system in the past.  They will call me back after their IT department has looked into their issue of not being able to access the controller.',1679675593),(1205,461,399,'Robert called to work with him testing the system after putting in the replacement boards.  Tested station 5 50W Synthetic Trans and got no pulses.  Moved wires to port 1 and still got no pulses.  Tested reels connected to port 2 and 3 and both worked and counted pulses.  Moved Port 3 wires to port 4 no pulses.  Tested board prior to shipment and all 4 ports were functioning correctly.  Had Robert rewire system correctly for ports 1, 2 and 3 as the wiring did not match the labels and wanted to prevent future confusion.  He will call me back once he has all the wiring corrected and has been positioned at the FCM again.',1679686804),(1206,462,399,'Jeannie ordered solenoid for this repair on SO 147792 PO 44199.  Waiting to send with RGA items',1680007235),(1207,461,399,'Waiting on Jeannie to provide either new PO or confirmation that she will put the PSM pcbs on PO 44199 that was created for the solenoid.',1680007290),(1208,465,399,'Mark helped him out and they found that the probe was pulled out of the tank a bit and when Jerry 563-209-9331, pushed it to the bottom the readings showed more oil, then they adjusted the specific gravity to get it to register the correct inches.\n\nJerry called by due to the tank now saying it was at 0 and not just low level.  Looking at pics of the probe connection it looks suspect that the white wires on both probes is securely in the connectors.  Ask Jerry to power down TMM and then confirm he had good wire connection to the connectors.  Waiting on his return call.',1680212220),(1209,465,399,'Jerry called back after doing the wire connections but no help.  Configured his tank to not use a sensor so that they could still dispense.  He provided contact info for Heartland CoOp, Jared Mills, 515-677-2256. \n500 Walnut St\nMinburn, IA 50167\nContacted Jared and explained to him what was had happened at Ditch Witch and also mentioned it looked like from the pic that the red tube on the sensor had been cut and might have been closed instead of allow air to enter but that should not have caused the senor to fail.  Told him I would send out a new probe Monday UPS on RGA .033023-1MS as a warranty item.  Jared will call me once he arrives at Ditch Witch and will walk him through a couple of troubleshooting steps to determine what is actually failed, the probe or the channel.',1680297082),(1210,466,399,'Logged into system and saw that all devices were green except for the TMM which would not have affected them as far as pumping.so let Susie know that cycling power to the TMM should take care it showing offline. She later called back after the tech got there and sent some more pics which showed that there was a missing screw from the cover and a screw had sheared off from the plate that the pcb is mounted to.  Mark explained that the only way that could have happened is if the pump didn\'t have thermal expansion built into it.  Ask the tech to send pic of pump and model number.  As of now it is not a warranty covered item.',1680548185),(1211,466,399,'Received the pics of the pump from the tech but unfortunately the bolt breaking is not covered under warranty.',1680549985),(1212,466,399,'It was decided to send them a PSM meter chamber cover, o-ring and bolt for them to repair the unit.',1680729314),(1213,466,399,'Sent parts on SO 147979 billed to AME shipped to Certified Hydraulics.',1680784031),(1214,465,399,'Sent probe out on SO 147994 SN D107325',1680795576),(1215,461,399,'Called Jeannie and she confirmed she would add the PSM pcbs to the PO.  ',1680878214),(1216,467,399,'Called Arin aback to find out if he was able to locate the controller.  He said he was and power cycled it but still could not access the system  He put in a call to their IT department and is waiting on them to return his call and troubleshoot the system.  He did confirm that the IP address we have in TV is the same as the IP address he is trying to connect to.',1681136749),(1217,467,399,'Corporate had black listed over 8000 computers on their network and oilcop happened to be one of them.  They whitelisted that device and all is good now.',1681148181),(1218,409,399,'Sill have not heard anything back from EH Wolf concerning the rest of Green Bays TMMs in other building which are still showing offline',1681762846),(1219,418,399,'Check today and system is responding very quickly.  ',1681762970),(1220,422,399,'This was implemented on both the controller and oilcopsupport.com site.',1681763024),(1221,431,399,'Still waiting on controller to be sent back. Sent email reminder today.',1681763064),(1222,434,399,'Have not heard back but checked site and saw FCM-2 was still offline',1681763139),(1223,442,399,'Found system online but Station 12 still shows failed FCM-16, user defined name FCM 15, but otherwise system looks good.',1681763382),(1224,445,399,'System checked good, closing DR.',1681763520),(1225,453,399,'Sent email asking when the RGA items will be returned.',1681763575),(1226,457,399,'Found system online today and all checkout.  closing DR.',1681763682),(1227,458,399,'Closing DR as there is nothing that can really be deemed from the reports to reconcile deliveries.',1681763732),(1228,459,399,'System was online and working normally.  Closing DR.',1681763836),(1229,461,399,'Parts were received, awaiting on AME to schedule tech.',1681763913),(1230,462,399,'Parts were received, awaiting on AME to schedule tech.',1681763924),(1231,464,399,'Had to call them back but it turned out that corporate had black listed 8000 devices on their network and out controller happened to be in the list.  Looks like they got it resolved as was able to access the controller and all seemed to be working correctly.  Closing DR.',1681764059),(1232,465,399,'Haven\'t heard that they had went to the site to do repairs or not.  Parts should have arrived already.  Tried connecting to the system but was logging in and then was kicked off and not says connection cannot be established even though the icon is showing the device as online.  Tried again and stayed connected this time.  Hydraulic tank is still configured to work without sensor but is on Re-Order level.',1681764322),(1233,465,399,'Got voice mail from Jared Mills 515-724-9299, saying it would be a good possibility that he would be going out to Ditch Witch this week to install the troubleshoot and install the sensor.',1681764654),(1234,465,3,'Jared removed 6\' probe from position one, installed new probe into position four. \nAssigned sensor four to HTB tank, enabled tank monitoring and entered Roth tank strapping table.\nCalibrated tank to level measured by Jared.\nJared is shipping defective probe to Mike.\n ',1682082176),(1235,462,399,'We do not carry this part so ADG will have to get it through another vendor, SZW-20-24VDC.  They will return solenoid sent back with other RGA items',1682362772),(1236,461,399,'Danny worked with me to troubleshoot the system and confirmed that the new board would not be damage once installed.  Once the new board was installed, tested all reels and found that one reel was not counting still.  Discovered that the PSM pcb was failed and so he replaced it with the additional spare sent.  Danny will be returning the two FCMs, solenoid which didn\'t fit, and the 3 PSM pcbs.  The PSM and FCM boards are out of warranty but the 1st FCM sent was still under warranty.  Unsure if will be able to determine what caused its failure as it was fully tested prior to shipment but was told after installation the two same channels failed as the original board. \n\nDanny wired all PSMs to the FCM in the order of the reels to prevent future confusion about which reel went to which port on the FCM.  Waiting on RGA items to be returned before closing DR.',1682363046),(1237,461,399,'Danny called and installed correct solenoid value and 15w/40 works.  Will confirm with customer all things are good now.',1683288564),(1238,469,399,'All stations techs complained it was the ow/20 oil that was giving them the issue on all stations.  Tested at station 1 and it was a hard failure, suspect PSM pcb or FCM port is bad.  Could not test station 15 but it was mentioned that it does not consistently fail and after testing station 16 again ow/20 these two stations are intermittently not displaying a count while dispensing.  Explained to Mike that the intermittent station are going to be very difficult to troubleshoot but as a start if he would please document the WO# and whether or not they manually stopped the dispense or it stopped on its own when the display stayed at zero.',1683317346),(1239,469,399,'Colton 785-418-1978 said he would be able to go to customer site either Tuesday or Wednesday of next week.',1683574726),(1240,470,399,'Was a little difficult understanding what they were trying to say but eventually the issues was that the used coolant tank was spilling out the top of the tank.  Asked that they confirm that the sensor was correctly hooked to port 3, and then confirmed that by having them pull the probe cable, which move easily, out of the tank and visually saw the tanks contents change on the dashboard.  Had them do their best to confirm that the sensor was sitting on the bottom of the tank.  They pushed as much of the cable into the tank as they could and the level barely changed from just above 3/4 full on the dashboard.\n\nThey said the tank was a 500 gallon tank, the system said the tanks capacity is 475.1 gallons with dimensions of a rectangle tanks being 60hx31w,59l.  High level warning was set to approximately 450 and since the sensor was not detecting that it was at this level there was no high level alarm.  I change the high level shutoff to 360 and High Level Warning to 340 and the system correctly alarmed.  They called a collection truck to pump the tank out and saw on the dashboard the tank level decreasing.  \n\nTold Tom that a tech will be at their place next week to look at another issue so will have him also look at this issue of why the reading is so far off from the tanks actual capacity.  The specific gravity on the used coolant product is set to 1.09.',1683828555),(1241,470,399,'Change SG for used coolant from 1.09 to 1.0000 to match the physical measurement of 3\".  One of the coolant pickup stations was mislabeled resulting in the techs pumping oil into the used coolant tanks.  Also changed the dimensions of the used coolant tank from 60x31x59 to 59.5x31.25x59.5 per Marks measurements of the double walled tanks.  They will call when it is fuller to see if needs to be calibrated more since they will not be cleaning the tank to get rid of the oil so it will always be in there making the reading slightly off.',1683910173),(1242,469,399,'Found loose wire on station 15 in FCM, green and at station 16 found loose connector on PSM and also replaced PSM pcb with pcb from PSM position 4 from station 1.  Station 1 position 4 PSM had a new board installed thinking that it was the ow/20 psm.  Also found a red wire on PSM ow/20 loose at station 1 which was possible the cause of station 1 not counting for ow/20 product when dispensing.  Note: there was a misconnection on the FCM on initial troubleshooting but system tested good when finished.  Documenting encase board fails in the future on port 1 for station 1 FCM.\n\nAlso found that a spout handle was not shutting off after the trigger was released and on one used and one coolant collection stations the solenoid was not opening after being powered.  Sent warranty replacements on RGA 051223-1MM, credit will be issued once cores are returned.',1683926672),(1243,471,399,'Logged into system and saw the East FCM and TMM were offline and told Mike that he should have them power cycle the FCM and the TMM.  Awhile later Jack Farley called 505.227.7673 called and said he had power cycled but system would still not work.  Called Mike and asked if he thought they would be able to troubleshoot the system and he said he would have to go.  Mike called back and we began troubleshooting the system.  TMM was now online but TAC and FCM, both east shop, were offline.  TAC is wireless and relies on the RAN to make it connection to the CDM.  The FCM is wired which made no sense as to why it was offline except that it could be a bad cable.\n\nAsked Mike to switch the address on the FCM just to see if the radio would reach with the RAN but the radio light on the FCM would never come on so it was not connecting to the RAN.  When Mike switched switch 8 to off for some strange reason the TAC came online.  We tested using default pins, 1234, 123456 and they gave a 255 error.  Testing with employee tech pins and they worked ever time.  Another strange issues I have not explanation as to why the defaults would not work but the employee pins did work.  The TAC remained online the rest of the time we troubleshot the FCM RS485 comms issue.  \n\nMike eventually moved the east FCM to the main building and switch it to address 2 and it came online and radio light illuminated.  Mike then connected some wire to the east FCM, set the address back to 128, and once connected to the CDM with new wire the RS485 comms light started flashing.  This pointed to the cable running to the east shop for RS485 communications somehow failed.  Suspect someone ran another cable in the same area, or some other work was done and the cable was somehow damaged so Mike will work to replace the wire.',1684268575),(1244,472,399,'Asked Dale to get ahold of IT to confirm the all network items were working.  Dave Nuss, 818.458.6941 personal cell, called from thier IT department and he said all was working up to the controller.  We went through a couple of things to ensure settings were correct on his side and then confirmed what settings needed to be setup on the replacement controller.  Sent replacement controller on SO 148924 configured with new settings or replacing controller E4:3A:6E:48:B3:1E with 70-B3-D5-OF-0E-AE.  Prev SO 140710 Inv # 173147  Previous TV ID 526886101 was deleted.   Asked Mark about how to handle this and he gave me Dustin\'s number 785-764-0604 who I called asking if he had a contact at St James I could call to explain the situation and inform them Dale requested a controller overnight.  Dustin said he would take care of contacting St James.',1684945023),(1245,472,399,'Dale called to confirm he received the replacement controller and installed successfully and all is working.  He explained that he lost some history he would like to reconcile so I told him once I receive the controller I will enter the outstanding WOs back into his current system so that he can reconcile his books.  Awaiting core controller back on RGA 052323-1MS.',1684945155),(1246,470,399,'Colton called and asked that a 24V power supply be sent to H&H Chevy as it is unknow why there is a 12V power supply hooked up to the pickup station that is not working.  Asked Mark how to handle the shipment and will send out once he responds back.',1684945399),(1247,473,399,'Moved the waste oil sensor over to port 4 of the TMM but that didn\'t change the tanks reading.  Moved the probe for the outside waste oil to port 3 and it read correctly.  Suspect bad probe on Parts Room waste oil tanks.  Outside probe is now connected to port 3 and Parts room waste oil which is reading incorrectly is connected to port 4.  Dustin is going to leave the probe from the kit he has there so they can replace it.\n\nTried users pins and each failed to log in, all giving 255 error.  Saw that there were 727 jobs trying to be pushed to the TAC which is way too many for it to receive before the data transfer timeout occurred.  Suggested they use a computer as a TAC will never work with that many jobs.\n\nThe west coolant reel was erratically counting dispense info so they moved the PSM to the east coolant reel.  The west reel had not more issue of counting erratically but now the east reel was.  Suspect bad PSM.  Dustin is going to provide a PSM out of his kit for them for this issue.\n\nDustin will get with Mark on whether or anything is under warranty.  According to action log it was setup on 20dec22.',1685479007),(1248,472,399,'Received controller and could not find anything wrong with it as it connected and was assigned an IP address immediately upon boot when connected to our network.  They must have something on their network which reassigned the IP address on the controller since it was set to DHCP instead of setting it to the previously assigned IP address as the IT tech said it should be.   ',1685541519),(1249,431,399,'Returned controller SN e4:3a:6e:48:11:b3 and returned to stock as new.',1686232164),(1250,473,399,'Checked system and it looks like all is working so sensor and psm left by Dustin has corrected their issue as I have not heard back from them.  Confirmed system is working correctly, closing DR.',1687349151),(1251,472,399,'Dale called back later and said there was another controller someplace and explained that it was probably an extra from Dustin and to call whoever called him back and tell them that the you had already received the controller.',1687350889),(1252,470,399,'Emailed Colton to find out if he had installed the power supply yet so I can close out this DR.  Awaiting on repsonse.',1687351302),(1253,453,399,'Still waiting on items to be returned.',1687351364),(1254,442,399,'Have received no calls from this site so closing DR even though I see station 15 is offline today, it must be intermittent and is always back online when they need to use it.',1687351500),(1255,418,399,'Haven\'t heard any issues and system was responding normally.  Closing DR.',1687351859),(1256,474,399,'Explained that it is due to a logic bug that didn\'t delete the associated records for a tank or product if the tank was deleted before deleting the sensors connected to it.  Developed the necessary queries to run on the DB after troubleshooting which tables had to have records deleted from them.  Ran queries on test DB first and when confirmed system still worked normally with the records gone performed the delete queries on Green Bays controller.  \n\nWhile doing this noticed that the more tanks link brought up a blank looking page but when you moved the mouse over the page the blue box showed with the tank details.  Asked the web team to look into a fix for this so it can be included in the next release that will have the MP fix in it as well as some other logic bugs fixed.\n\nLeaving DR open till the dashboard issue is fixed.',1688138415),(1257,475,399,'Shawn from ATC confirmed that their IT department had already verified all hardware including cable were good up to the controller.  Mark confirmed the controller had not ethernet adapter lights.  Controller SN 00:e0:4c:28:ec:9f  network adapter failed, replacing with SN: 70-B3-D5-OF-0E-B8.  Restored controller with backup from 10feb23 and confirmed it had the correct network settings.  Awaiting SO to ship.  ',1688760271),(1258,475,399,'ATC IT contact Nick@keystoneit.com 319-688-9319 ext 7210',1688760961),(1259,476,399,'Josh from Myers Brothers called to ask me about H&H Recon Fresh Coolant tank values and confirmed with his guesstimate of the level in inches.  Explained how he can confirm when he has time to ensure the sensor is reading the tank correctly as he said the system show it had 60 gallons when it was actually completely empty.  He then went over to H&H Chevy to troubleshoot station 3 and we confirmed through wire tap that the FCM wiring to the PSM was good.  He then checked the fuse, it was good and then once he reinstalled the pulser wires it all worked normally.  Closing DR.',1689189173),(1260,477,399,'Before I was able to talk with Brad, I changed the sensor configuration to use TMM-4 instead of TMM-3 which was offline.  The system also detected another TMM-4 with an address of 7 but Brad said they only had 3 so just informed him that somewhere in his facility there is a TMM powered up that could be used as a spare if all the outputs were good.  The FCM that was offline he realized didn\'t have a power supply connected to it so he used the power supply that he received with the TMM to power FCM 2 up and it showed up online.  Only issue with the system is that it is all wired but all the addresses are set for Radio.  Passed this information on just so they would know if it act strange it could be due to that radio and RS485 comms conflicting with each other.  Brad will call Robert Trollenger back from EH Wolf to let him know his system was back up and working.',1689189449),(1261,478,399,'Mark said that he had rebooted the system and assumed that he checked after rebooting but the problem remains.  Found out they blocked our access to their system even though it shows online so the only option was to have IT allow us to connect through a local computer using TV and then ssh into the controller.  Set up hw debug to show and it showed all devices communicating.  The tested using reel calibration and it worked correctly, then made a WO and it worked correctly, then Mark logged in to a tech computer, created a WO and then dispense successfully.  Probably the 2nd reboot fixed the issue.  Confirmed there was plenty of free space on hard.  They do keep 11 pages of WO in view which slows the WO and manager dashboard pages down a bit.  Mark will call back if issue returns.',1689357143),(1262,479,399,'Had issues at station 17 where it would give an pump unsuccessful start yet it would allow tech to pump but not show what was being dispensed.  This issues also showed when using reel calibration, unsuccessful start but then would allow the tech to pump.  So there is some timeout coded in the web pages where it will only wait for so long to see a successful message before it displays a failure message.  Have asked the web team whether or not this is the case with the pump start command.  Somehow MIM is successfully starting the pump but is not monitoring when it should shut off based on preset because unless it is set by the manager I don\'t believe this info is passed to MIM as part of the packet.  \n\nThis is what I\'m asking of the web team while I look at it in MIM:\nDo you have some timeout for the start pump command in your code were you wait only a specific amount of time to see an entry in the t_transceiver_server table before issuing the message pump start unsuccessful?  Or do you just keep monitoring until you see a response from MIM stating either a successful or unsuccessful pump start? \n\nI\'m assuming that once you post that message to the tech you don\'t look monitor the table/field you would normally monitor if it was just late coming in which is why I can see an unsuccessful pump start message yet am able to pump fluid.\n\nThe issue came up at a customer where it would say that the pump start was unsuccessful but the tech could still pump.  The bigger issue is that it wouldn\'t shut off automatically.  My understanding is that in the V1 version you don\'t sent preset info when the tech puts it in.  Do you sent preset info to MIM during the request to start the pumps when the preset is set by the manager?  Asking so I can test a theory and if it work then provide a work around for customers when they experience this until we can fix the code.\n\nNow that you are tracking the tech preset input are you sending that to MIM in your request to start pump?',1689609950),(1263,480,399,'Used reel calibration to test and it worked every time correctly giving a successful pump start message.  Gave him an overview of system functionality and he provided feedback on location of CDM in relationship to the FCMs which all have clear lines of sight to the CDM.   Explain that there is not much I can do if it is working to understand why intermittently they get an unsuccessful pump start message.  Gave him some questions to ask the next time the issue happened, and he will try and call so that I can see the failure next time it happens.  It may be a timing delay issue which was experienced at H&H Chevy where the pump actually started but the web page said it was an unsuccessful pump start.',1693408589),(1264,481,399,'It seems as though the distributor monitors the web to know when to deliver oil but did not provide anyone locally at the dealership credentials to view the tanks levels or monitor the system as there were only the default users on the system.  Gave the Parts Manager credentials as he had to go to the tank room every day and look at the gauges instead of just pulling up the web page.  I also explained to him that if sees the word invalid under the tank name he needs to reset the TMM.',1693409032),(1265,482,399,'After rebooting the controller as at first it showed offline, but before that could happened the system came back online and was able to connect.  Once connected after reboot the system intermittently lost connection with TV.  Conferencing with their IT person Hussein, it was realized after Tim pulled the power plug that he was still pinging successfully the ip address.  I told them that this indicates that some other computer on their network has the same address and that was causing the issue of it coming on and off line and why they couldn\'t access the login page.  Hussein will resolve the duplicate IP address and call if he needs any further assistance.',1693409364),(1266,479,399,'Have not heard of any further issues from H&H concerning this, will monitor for a bit longer.',1693930883),(1267,484,399,'Danny called and we began to troubleshoot.  Took them sometime to locate the controller, which is located in the center parts room on the shelf.  Also found out the TV infor or network settings was incorrect so updated those.  Was able to locate the CDM and it was just hanging by the wires.  As soon as Danny opened up the case the FCMs that were showing offline all came back online.  Suggested he look at the wiring to the connectors which he did by pulling each wire out and confirming that all looked good.  Tested a station and all work.  Soon Danny called back and said the station he was testing with the customer was not working.  Logged back in and saw the same stations were offline again.  Had him reorient the connector using the front holes and all came back online.  He sent me some pics but didn\'t provide enough details when zooming to see any obvious.  Told him about there being a site where it seems the blue connect actually had flakey contact and once it was swapped out with a spare blue connector from the RS485 terminals no more issues were detected.  Suggested that Danny also do that even though when he put the case back together the system seems to solid.  Suspect since he now had the connection on using the front holes the case was pressing down on the wires and connect and said that if he left it that way there was a good chance in the future if anyone removes the cover from the CDM the issue would return.  Suggest he swap out the blue connect with one not being used and reconfirm the wiring qs the red wire fo rthe FCM connections seem a bit odd from the pick.  Haven\'t heard back so assuming all is good now.',1693941130),(1268,485,399,'Reviewed a few items but could not find any reason why the TAC would say a WO is closed when it is open giving an error code 013.  Downloaded a backup of their data and see that there is also a copy of a bockup from May of this year which is approximately the same time that the system stop working using the TACs.  Will need to investigate further.',1695301176),(1269,485,399,'Nick called back and asked me to investigate RO 434327 where they had to manually shutoff the dispense as it was not counting what was being dispensed.  According to Nick this is an intermittent issue at their site.  Not consistent enough to troubleshoot so asked them to keep track to see if it is the same stations, etc. ',1695305368),(1270,483,399,'Tom called again, and submitted another request to Myer\'s Brothers that they send a tech there to troubleshoot.  Also asked them for confirmation of tech\'s scheduled date to be on site and ask that the tech call me after troubleshooting to see if we can determine why it has failed again so soon after being fixed.',1696427645),(1271,487,399,'This issue has progressively gotten worse in the past few days.  Yesterday could create a WO and dispense from the controller and from Davids station but not from the parts manager stations which makes no sense since they both access the same software files and programs.  Troubleshooting in progress and as a work around they are giving the techs load work order rights as that seems to work as a stop gap until the issue can be figured out.',1703872816),(1272,488,399,'Mo, 586-248-2694, confirmed that the TMM were talking correctly using RS485.  Mark had previously had them power cycle the TMMs but it did not change the Low Level Shutoff value shown on the dashboard.  Had Mo change the last value, as it is a custom tank, to a higher value and all worked, showing system was in high level shutoff.  Explained that even though it shows shutoff in the warning it would not prevent them from dispensing and is more of a nuisance message telling them not to add more to the tank.  Guesstimated that they would have to remove about 30 gallons before the system would no longer show HLSO.',1708711975),(1273,488,399,'Mo, 586-248-2694, confirmed that the TMM were talking correctly using RS485.  Mark had previously had them power cycle the TMMs but it did not change the Low Level Shutoff value shown on the dashboard.  Had Mo change the last value, as it is a custom tank, to a higher value and all worked, showing system was in high level shutoff.  Explained that even though it shows shutoff in the warning it would not prevent them from dispensing and is more of a nuisance message telling them not to add more to the tank.  Guesstimated that they would have to remove about 30 gallons before the system would no longer show HLSO.',1708711977),(1274,489,399,'Contacted Chris who explained he had to coordinate with Sonic IT and will make arrangements to raise a helpdesk ticket so that we can gane access to the controller.  Will call back when he gets more information.',1709816507),(1275,490,399,'They finally rebooted there system.  All seems to be setup correctly so need someone to go there to confirm tank dimensions and confirm overfill alert hardware is installed correctly and functional.  Mark M coordinating with Mark P.',1710166355),(1277,489,399,'Left message for Chris since I haven\'t heard anything back on getting us access.',1710166479),(1278,487,399,'Had to delete all recrods from t_adjust_workorders, t_dispenses, t_workorder_details for system to correctly match records.  This issue is caused by allowing the user to delete WOs which will either be removed or another process be implemented in future release.',1710257131),(1279,486,399,'Sent new controller to replace faulty one.  Can now connect to NMC',1710260549),(1280,483,399,'Myers Brothers went and replaced 2 sensors and one FCM',1710260627),(1281,480,399,'This is more than likely similar to the issue at United BMW and will be fixed in the next release.',1710262356),(1282,479,399,'This issue is probably the same as United BMW and will be fixed with the next release.',1710262388),(1283,475,399,'replaced controller.',1710262424),(1284,470,399,'Assuming ps was installed, not response from colton',1710262466),(1285,474,399,'SIte was reconfigured and now has two controllers',1710264120),(1286,453,399,'Item returned',1710264150),(1287,434,399,'FCM  2 is online',1710264484),(1288,409,399,'Problem was fixed after extensive troubleshooting and adding a new controller for tanks in remote building.',1710264540),(1289,491,399,'Sent email to Myers brothers on 12 Feb 2024 and again asked on 14 March 2024, they responded saying a tech would be there next week.',1710506151),(1290,492,399,'Once connected tried using reel calibration to start pumps but could not get a successful message.  Killed mim and restarted manually and then tested again and got successful pump start messages.  Left as is for the rest of the day.  Came in this morning and updated the system to R39 again since there was some sql error messages showing in cronlog and after reboot the system was acting normally.  ',1710506344),(1291,489,399,'Called Chris again and he was at the site so he will be sending me the database at least as well as sending an email to the IT department manager so that we can figure out a solution to allow us access to the oilcop system.  The you logmein but unsure if ssh is enabled on the controller as it was installed long ago.  He is also going to confirm if winspc can be used on their network.',1710509132),(1292,489,399,'Chris tried to send DB but for some reason it would not backup correctly on R34.  They cannot update the system due to it being blocked by their IT department.  Trying to worik our a solution in the meantime but have to wait on them to respond.',1710513376),(1293,490,399,'352-340-6688 Mike Parts Manager, 727-478-1531 is the sites main number.',1710515880),(1294,489,399,'The ticket Chris created for this is INC48705041, ',1710516809),(1295,489,399,'Attempted to figure out the issue using TV with Sonic but unfortunately it was too locked down.  They are going to follow up with their tier 3 IT people to see about getting the ports open.',1710784209),(1296,491,399,'Station 3 turned the issue turned out to be due to a zero kfactor being set for the reel.  Stations 19, not 28, turned out to be a loose wire in the PSM.  No board were needed that were sent on RGA 121224-1MS',1711389743),(1297,493,399,'He said pumps were not starting while talking to him but viewing the system everything was working so had him test using reel calibration the station he was saying wasn’t working.  After reviewing the logs a bit more I saw that the CDM was failing intermittently and all devices would be affected not just certain devices.  The logs showed the CDM started communicating again on its own but it does take a few seconds for all the devices to register they are available again so believe the CDM had restarted communications and the stations mentioned below just hadn’t registered in time.\n\nAdded changes to allow me to see the logs from prior days after rebooting instead of being wiped out awhile back which allowed me to guess that it was on Monday the CDM stating disconnecting from the controller for unknown reason.  Possible cause could be bad CDM, flakey usb cable, flakey usb port, all of which seem highly unlikely since the system is only a little over a year old.  \n\nI monitored the logs throughout the day yesterday and saw that it was still intermittently dropping again.  Not sure how they overfilled a vehicle because the system would have transferred the preset to the FCM so it would have stopped at the value it received even if the CDM went off line but wouldn’t have updated the screen while offline so the only way I can see that they overfilled the vehicle was if they started the dispense again but they should have known oil had already went in the vehicle so that doesn’t make much sense.  They could not tell me which RO was the one for the vehicle they overfilled so this is all I have to go off of until I get that info which Tom didn’t seem too eager to provide.\n\nThey didn’t put in the email what I text Tom exactly and didn’t explain what we discussed prior to the text below.  I called him when I notice that the CDM had dropped a couple of time in the logs to see if he was having issues and he said he wasn’t but they were slow.  \n\nI sent an email to Meyer Brothers asking when the soonest they could have someone up there since a CDM failure would be a complete system failure and knew they would not stand for that.  Meyers Brothers still hasn’t responded to my email.\n\nGot him to send me a pic of the controller and saw they had plugged the usb cable in the front of the controller so texted him to move the usb plug to the usb 2 plugs on the back showing him in a pic which ones I wanted him to plug it into. What  I said in the text was “Could be the usb port causing the issue.  If you could while slow,  power down the controller and put the …..”  \n\nHe did not power down the controller before moving the plug which I could tell because the log file grew to over 28MB which happens when you pull the usb plug out without powering down the controller or at least killing the middleware program.  Seeing this I just rebooted myself and let him know I did that without calling him out that he didn’t follow my instructions and just said there was something wrong.\n\nSince he moved the usb cable to the back of the controller the logs have showed no further CDM disconnects so will continue to monitor today. I have added code their system and included it in the code for the next release that will document the time and date of any CDM failures so I can know exactly when they happen.\n',1712758386),(1298,493,399,'Just check their system again and no further CDM failures noted in the logs and they have dispensed a number of RO’s this morning.',1712758414),(1299,493,399,'Still have not seen another occurrence of the CDM going offline today',1712776593),(1300,494,399,'Suggested troubleshooting steps are:\nInstall CDM with label side up, so that none label side is facing the floor.\nProvide an extension usb cable to move the CDM further out towards the center of the shop, directly over the wheel alignment lift.\n',1712856782),(1301,489,399,'Had Mark P use cellular dongle to allow connection to the controller.  The system was almost out of space so cleaned it up and updated from R36 to R39.  Downloaded database backup so would have current copy and wait for customer to confirm they are still having issues with overfilling at station 15.',1713793291),(1302,493,399,'Stil are not seeing any issues with the CDM losing communication with the controller since moving the usb cable to the usb 2.0 ports on the back of the controller. Customer has also not reported having any issues.  Did notice that there was at least one entry in the current cronlog cronlog_20240415113017 that showed that a start pump response was not received after the start pump command was issued but the customer has not said that he had any station now showing the count as the RO was dispensed.  ',1713794163),(1303,494,399,'Scott responded to my email today and said he was submitting a ticket to finish getting us access like united bmw.',1713795382),(1304,490,399,'Have not heard back whether or not they got someone to go there or not.  See from past emails that Certified Hydraulics Inc. took care of an issue back in Arp of 2023.  \nCertified Hydraulics Inc.\nSusie Thompson\nPO Box 605\n7737 US Hwy 27\nBranford, Fl. 32008\n386-935-3494 Office\n386-935-3495 Fax\nPresident, CFO, LDO\nsueasian@aol.com\n',1713795738),(1305,490,399,'Certified Hydraulics responded they have declined further work from AME, so email Mark P to contact AME to let them know one of their customers needs on site support.',1713804743),(1306,490,399,'Passed info onto Mark P concerning CH response and Mark said he would call CH.',1713806068),(1307,490,399,'So my understanding from TJ, retired 863-812-0701, is that Ocean Honda wants their other tank monitored so they will need a TMM and sensor as they are out of ports on the single TMM they currently have.  They don’t care about shutting pumps off according to TJ just the audio alarm and the tanks don\'t interconnect so the level would balance, they just have a hose with a T in it and no way to direct the flow of oil to the other tank when one is full.\n\nGuess that means that AME will have to contact them to initiate the sale so the customer can agree to the price, of a TMM and 6’ sensor.\n\nTech won’t be there till 5/6 or 5/7 which I’ll work with just to ensure that the tank that has the monitor will actually go off at high level.\n',1713813132),(1308,490,399,'Tech called and provided height and diameter of tanks.  Confirmed they are double walled tanks.  OD height is 75, handwritten on tank is 72\", OD diameter is 46, system setup has 44\" as diameter, Reset tank parameters to match as tank capacity reduced by approximately 20 gallons so there was a chance thanks would be overfilled with using 75\" as the height.',1715012723),(1309,495,399,'Sent 3 power supplies on SO 155344, PN 10864',1715705258),(1310,496,399,'Now that I found the mac address: e4:3a:6e:48:b2:7b, I see an entry from yesterday where it does not say all Tech, Prod, Stations WO santini2 but it was never dispensed. \n \n It shows that the WO type is load WO which normally means it was loaded from a TAC but I do not see any TACs under hardware configuration.  How did the santini2 wo get entered differently from the others, that’s the real question and the answer may lead us to the solution?  \n\nI have tried every which way, including multiple version and cannot get a system to act like the subject system.  I’m waiting on a fix for mobile pages in the R40 release.  I initially released it, Andrea updated some controllers there, but there is a bug in the mobile pages which I didn’t check after the last round of web updates that broke the pages so removed it from being able to update controllers because I know you use those pages with the tablets instead of TACs.  The next release, R41, will have a fix for the MP product displaying wrong disp amounts as well as should fix the problem your experiencing.  I hope they have it completed by the end of the week so that a release can be out next week.\n\nMy apologies for not understanding what is going on with this controller.  As mentioned it was working find until Apr 24 yet as far as I can tell nothing was changed on the controller including software from Apr 23 and Apr 24 when the issue started happening.\n\nStill investigating but without the ability to work with someone on site it will be very difficult to figure something out so would rather focus on the R41.\n',1719508227),(1311,497,399,'Jose Luna, 305-713-6428, called and said he system was down.  Had him swap the CDM usb cable to different ports and the CDM still would not show any power light.  Sent new, older model, CDM on SO 156193, but when it arrived it still did not show any power.  Thomas, 305-796-929, tried other ports and still no luck getting power to CDM.  Had them return controller, original CDM as well as shipped CDM on afore mentioned SO back on RGA 071224-1MS so that it could be troubleshot.  \n\nJobbers, ID 7405, handles the support for Pantropic Power and al requests for POs or support go to purchasing@jobbersmiami.com.',1721056800),(1312,496,399,'This is happening when using the mobile pages, will need to get the web team to fix.',1721058163),(1313,496,399,'It seems to only be an issue if MP and/or MD is enabled.  Hope this is an easy fix.  It doesn\'t have this issue in R34 so something changed in R35-R39.  It is still an issue in R43 also.',1721059983),(1314,497,399,'Sent new controller to them and tech called after the FCM and SEG would not display a green status.  After thoroughly troubleshooting the system and wires it was determined that the FCM and SEG must have bad RS485 ports due to the lighting strike that took out the controller and CDM.\n\nTech found a used FCM at the shop so is going to try that at the site before requesting a new one.  Going to send SEG as it should be communicating even if the FCM is bad.\n\nTech will update me later today.  3 hrs.',1723744948),(1315,494,399,'Have not heard back of any issues since they move the CDM using a 65\' extension cable.',1723745091),(1316,493,399,'Have not heard of any further issues with this, closing DR',1723745178),(1317,490,399,'Haven\'t heard of any issues with this after confirming that the oilcop system had the correct dimensions.',1723745274),(1318,489,399,'Still do not have access to this controller nor have they called about over dispensing.  Closing DR',1723745338),(1319,485,399,'Had to delete a number of entries in the DB since they were deleting WOs it caused the indexing to be off.  Asked them to not delete any further WO and will remove the ability to delete WOs at a later time.',1723745458),(1320,498,399,'Notice that logging in was slow and accessing pages was also slower than normal.  Disk space was ok at 65%.  This seemed to be the same characteristics that have happened at a couple of other sites where mysql would be consuming all the resources.  Running the top command this was the case.  Restarted the mysql services and things started working normally.\n\nUpdated their system to the latest release, R44 after they were close for the day on 8/14.  On 8/15 things started off just fine but then went down hill from there.  restarted the mysql services about 4-6 time and it would only be about 10-20 seconds before it was once again consuming all the resources.  Change the php.ini file that was located in the /etc/php5/apache2/ folder variables max_execution_time = 120 and max_input_time=240 and restarted mysql again but no help.  One more time restarting mysql services and the system finally started working normally and has stay functional since then which was over 6 hours ago.  Will continue to monitor.',1723753339),(1321,499,399,'Connected to the controller without any issues, all devices were green status, disk space was ok, wo management worked as expected.  Took a backup, cleaned up old open wo\'s and checked disk space which was good.  Upon further investigation it loos like around May 2nd the CDM received an impossible packet, greater than 32 bytes, hard coded to read only 32 bytes, yet the packed in the logs wax very much in excessive of 32 bytes.  Emailed Bob telling him the logs were showing that the CDM was not initializing correctly upon reboot.  Couldn\'t find any logs that showed CDM failures after reboot though or anything else that jumped out as to why they would reboot the system. \n\nExplained to Bob that it could be the port, cable or CDM and to start with changing the port first, then cable and then CDM if the problem persists.   Will leave DR open for a bit to see if they continue to report issues.',1724079521),(1322,498,399,'Asked Justin again for time on his controller to update and troubleshoot the db process issue.  He had not responded but did see an email where is was asking for pricing on a new controller.',1724079575),(1323,497,399,'Have not seen email back with PO from Jobbers yet',1724079804),(1324,499,399,'Haven\'t heard back from Quag\'s so checked site and saw that everhting is up and running.  FYI it is a wired system.  Closing DR.',1725378944),(1325,498,399,'There has not been any issues for the past two weeks with the mysql processes.  Controller has been updated to R45 and they have not reported any issues.  Configuring spare controller sent by AME to United and confirmed all ports work, rebooting does not hang up controller and software has been updated to R45.  Will close DR once they have received the replacement controller and have tested it on site.',1725379095),(1326,500,399,'Logged into system and found all devices green except for FCM 5.  Danny cycled power which did not help.  Danny removed cover and it showed that the radio light was lit as well as he had RS485 communications as the EEprom led was flashing consistently.  The system didn\'t have addresses set correctly for wired communications, only set for radio, yet the communications type for the device was set to wired.  This could cause issues and since this system has been installed for a number of years highly suspect the devices are wired in parallel instead of series.  \n\nDanny found RS485 connector not secured in place and once he pushed it on, FCM turned green.  Explained to Danny should there be an issue in the future it could be due to the devices having the incorrect addresses for being wired so keep it in the back of his mind.',1725382659),(1327,497,399,'Sent new CDM which took care of the rest of the issues.',1739800345),(1328,502,399,'After working on the TAC code believe this issue occured because the volume in the tank was too low for it to dispense the full amount.  Will have to have the site check again.',1741799785),(1329,498,399,'They have received the replacement controller but the current controller is working fine and does not hang on reboot as it once did consistently.  They have decided not to install newer controller at this time.  Closing DR.',1741799880),(1330,504,399,'Updated the system to new code due to errors showing in the system log that were fixed based on the software they were running, R46.  The system had been updated but a reboot had not been performed so the new MIM code was not running.  After a reboot the system failed to come up and could no longer connect using TV.  Had to wait over 2 hours before I could connect again with TV.\n\nMultiple reboots were done to get the system back up but since I could not access the system I could not look into the logs to figure out why the system would not start pumps.  All devices remained green but pumps would not start.  When I was finally able to connect I found that the CDM had communications errors, saying it was ready but no data could be read.  After the system was left alone for a few hours the system started working on it own but filled up the log file with this message.  Suspect a bad USB cable as the cause but difficult to troubleshoot due to how the system are installed making it necessary to have a lift available to effectively troubleshoot as well as having an extra cable on hand.  \n\nRestarted the software through the terminal and system has been running without issues for over a week.  Will need to coordinate with Distributor to have a tech there to finish troubleshooting with a new cable and CDM.  Only sending a CDM to be on the safe side.',1741800351),(1331,505,399,'Multiple reboots were done to get the system back up but since I could not access the system I could not look into the logs to figure out why the system would not start pumps.  All devices remained green but pumps would not start.  When I was finally able to connect I found that the CDM had communications errors, saying it was ready but no data could be read.  After the system was left alone for a few hours the system started working on it own but filled up the log file with this message.  Suspect a bad USB cable as the cause but difficult to troubleshoot due to how the system are installed making it necessary to have a lift available to effectively troubleshoot as well as having an extra cable on hand.  \n\nRestarted the software through the terminal and system has been running without issues for over a week.  Will need to coordinate with Distributor to have a tech there to finish troubleshooting with a new cable and CDM.  Only sending a CDM to be on the safe side.\n\nStation 2 continued to be inop but station 12 came back green but could not confirm functionality since the CDM was failing to communicate with controller.  Same issue here as what happened at Bloomfield BMW, where I could not connect to the system using TV after the reboot., also happened on Dev 1, could not connect after a reboot.  Deleted over 10 TV accounts that were no longer in use as we are at the limit of our license.  Have meeting with TV on Friday so hopefully will resolve any issues cause by TV then.\n\nRecommended that and FCM board be shipped to fix station 2, send wire to hardwire station 12, and new USB cable and CDM to fix issue with CDM not communicating with the controller after reboot.',1741800661),(1332,506,399,'Walked Payton through troubleshooting and it was determined that the installer had not wired the system correctly to match the labels.  They used Red and white for solenoid and black and green for pulser.  Found that FCM 2 had port 2 bad and FCM 3 has port 3 bad.  They opted to fix one FCM since it has a spare port to put the 15w40 oil on, FCM3.  \r \r Also noticed that their radio icons were all red x so will send them the hardware and instructions to reprogram their devices.so they have valid radio signals showing.',1741800986),(1333,507,399,'Carl sent a picture and  the burnt spot was above the sensor connection used by the probe for Used Oil tank level monitoring.  After some troubleshooting determined that the power supply was also bad for the TMM so he borrowed one from Station 5 and once the probe for Used Oil connection was removed he powered it up and all started to work, except the oil monitoring for Used Oil.\n\nSending TMM, 24V power supply and new 6\' probe to repair the system.  He will send back the bad TMM board for us to evaluate whether or not it can be repaired, if so will send it back repaired and if not will return with the bad port clearly marked as a backup encase the new TMM ever fails.',1741992509),(1334,504,399,'Have not seen any issues with the system when checking periodically since 3/12.  Will keep monitoring as we wait on AME to order the parts and coordinate with customer to have a tech troubleshoot the system and replace parts as necessary per my recommendations.\n\nBloomfield BMW, I recommend that a new 120’ USB extension cable be sent along with a CDM, to be on the safe side.  They can then replace the USB cable and do a reboot and if comes back up without any issues then they can send the CDM back unused.  Estimate 1 hr. for replacement and testing.  This should all be coordinated with the customer to block at least an hour where they won’t need access to the system.  Bloomfield has a setup where a stations can easily be put into bypass without the need for a lift, but a lift is necessary to replace the USB cable to be safe and CDM if need be.  They will also need to send back all the bad hardware so we can determine what failed and if there is anything we can do to reduce the chances of failures moving forward.',1742402638),(1335,505,399,'Colton sent me the email address, info@autoliftserv.com, to coordinate scheduling a tech to go to Ocean Honda which I have still not gotten a response to.  Mark M has sent all the parts in my recommendation except for the wire and are waiting on the sub-contractor of AME to follow up with questions in my email to them as well as a date they will be sending a tech to perform the steps in my recommendations.\n\nMy recommendation for Ocean Honda, is send an FCM board to replace the Station 2 FCM board.  Send a new 120’ USB extension cable and CDM, to be on the safe side, but start with replacing the USB cable and if all comes up correctly after reboot send back the CDM unused.  If it can be confirmed that Ocean Honda has had multiple complaints about station 12 send enough wire to hardware Station 12, otherwise monitor.  They can return what they don’t use but need them to return all bad items for testing to see if we can determine why they failed, ensure we can reproduce the issues with the same hardware and determine if there is anything we can do to prevent this from happening in the future.  This work should be coordinated with the customer to block at least 2 hours where they won’t need access to the system.  \n\nThe time-consuming step at Ocean Honda is replacing the USB cable and testing, estimating 1 hr. minimum but could be a bit more.  Wiring of Station 12 properly estimating 45 minutes.  Replacing the FCM board for station 2 estimating 15 minutes.  The system will be completely down for the USB replacement and testing.  The other two items the system will be functional except at Station 2 and if Station 12 is offline there also.  Testing of Station 2 and 12 should be able to be completed fully in 30 minutes or less after work has been done to them and the system will remain fully functional during testing.  Estimates are based on the ability of the tech to have access to a lift and can access the areas necessary without delays caused by having to work around working employees.   From what I understand from Colton there is already a lift on site, but that needs to be confirmed.\n ',1742402850),(1336,506,399,'Parts were ordered last week and am waiting on Payton to contact me how things went after replacing the parts.  Still trying to find time to get things together for him to reprogram his devices with new firmware code.',1742403116),(1337,507,399,'PrairieLand did not want to go through their original distributor so Mark M worked it out to sell to the directly  using a credit card and sold them an entire TMM instead of just the PCBA and power cord.  He also sent a new probe to them.',1742403308),(1338,501,399,'Found they were trying to use a pin that was not valid.  When they used a valid pin they didn\'t seem to have any more issues.  Update software to T86',1742403609),(1339,505,399,'Power Disconnection and Reconnection Issue: While replacing the USB cable on the controller, Colton accidentally disconnected the power, which caused me to be kicked out of the system. An issue on the customer\'s IT side prevented me from reconnecting to the controller. This site has a known issue where, if the system is rebooted, it takes a few hours before we can reconnect using TeamViewer.\n\nUSB Cable Replacement: Originally, there were two 65\' USB cables connected, with most of the second cable coiled up. Colton was able to reach the CDM with just one cable, so he installed only one, along with the new CDM that was sent. All systems started working normally, and the reel calibration pumps tested successfully.\n\nStation 2 Inoperability: The issue with Station 2 being inoperative was due to it having Station 1\'s FCM address assigned to it. Colton couldn\'t confirm Station 1\'s physical address but resolved the issue by switching dip switch 1 off and switch 2 on. Station 2 then started working.\n\nUsed Oil Tank Monitoring: The used oil tank is set up for monitoring, but there was no probe installed. Colton will ask the customer about the missing probe and whether they want to monitor it from their dashboard. If they do, they will order a new probe, and Colton will return to install it.',1742486383),(1340,508,399,'Was not able to connect using TV directly so had to log into a computer on their network and then bring up phpMyAdmin to copy the DB before after after deleting all the records from t_adjust_workorders, t_dispense, t_workorder_details.  They are going to reboot their firewall after hours today to see if that fixes the issue of not being able to connect using TV.  Will check back tomorrow to see if we can connect and if not call Matt 618-526-8550.  Brain is the manager at Cassen Dodge 618-696-9024.',1743529062),(1341,509,399,'Looked at the system and the cronlog was not populating as expected.  Could not log into their system using TV so had to log into Reconn and use ssh to get into Chevy\'s controller. Restarted the software but still could not start a pump.  Enable hardware debug and restarted software and then was seeing successful messages from all the devices.  Tested reel calibration and it worked so had Tom test and it worked.  Disabled the debug variable and restarted software and all seemed to work as normal.',1744983837),(1342,510,399,'Dustin said that nothing had changed and I explained that it was impossible for things to be working just fine and then just stop working without something changing if there were no hardware failures.  I found in the action log that a reel had been updated but the log lacked any pertinent information to know what exactly changed.  The changed happened towards the end of the day.  Of course the issue with the network at this site made things even more difficult to troubleshooting as you could only type a couple of characters or do a couple of mouse clicks before the system would lock up, basically losing communication but their IT refuses to troubleshoot what is causing the issue. Because of this it over 5 hours to troubleshoot the system to discover the web code does not know how to handle having a station with two reels with the same product.  The work around is to create another station with the duplicate product.  This clarified to the TAC user exactly which 15w40 reel he was selecting since now it ask him to choose a station instead of showing him two lines of the same product.  The code that needs to be looked at are the job.php and dispense.php files located in the admin/controller folder.  Leaving open for Engineering',1745497612),(1343,508,399,'Mark from IT did not return my phone call but left a message stating that we could still not connect.',1745497709),(1344,507,399,'Parts were sent and worked with the manager to install the new hardware and afterwards everything checked out good.',1745497759),(1345,511,399,'Found that station 10 was offline and explained they would get the message if the system detected a station FCM offline after they hit the pump start button.  Looked through the device history table and noticed that station 10 and 18 are troublesome stations going on and offline quite often.  Mike is going to call the distributor to come out and check it out.  If called suggest they wire those two stations.  Leaving open a few days.',1746461908),(1346,512,399,'There are issues with their network as they keep having to reboot the controller because they can no longer access the system.  They thought it was because they just reapplied the network settings but explained that it was more than likely the reboot and not that they reapplied the settings.  I let them know that they were far behind on software updates and said I would update it after hours to ensure it was not going to have any issues with the newest software update.  This is what I emailed him when updating it failed.\nHi Jacob,\n\nI attempted to update your controller last night, but it seems you IT is blocking the necessary port to download the files.   Please as you IT to ensure the following ports are open so that the controller can be updated.\n\nPort 3306 (allows secure backups to oilcopsuppot.com) IP 35.88.205.92\nPort 587 (emails reports)\n\nLet me know if you have any issues as it at first gave an error and then it downloaded a file, but it was corrupted but tried to install and then it failed to get the files.  Since the process is done automatically with code there could be other corrupted files but hoping not.  \n\nI tried to do the update manually but could not upload and files to the controller, must be some type of block by IT when using TeamViewer to connect.  I did some basic testing and ensured that I did get a successful pump start with using the reel calibration tool so hoping you have no issues while IT opens the ports.\n\nI also noticed looking at your log that the system was showing an issue with either your CDM, cable that connects the CDM to the computer or the usb port the CDM is plugged into.  Something to keep an eye on and will present itself after reboot where it takes a while for the system to start working.  Normally you should be able to dispense within a minute or two after a reboot.  If it has been taking longer then there is an issue and you really need to call Quag’s Equipment to have them come out and troubleshoot.\n\n',1746666467),(1347,512,399,'Jacob called back and said that he has to set the network settings as the system keeps stopping.  Looking at the logs it shows that the CDM fails to communicate. All devices are showing offline.  Jacob doesn\'t know where the controller is at so he is looking for it.  He didn\'t understand my email telling him that he needs to get Quag\'s over there to troubleshoot the failing CDM, suspect usb cable is an extension cable and it is failing. ',1746802974),(1348,512,399,'Jacob found the controller in the shop area on a desk a tech uses and the cable is that standard 15\' cable so suspect that the usb port was failing as they moved the usb cable to a new port and everything started working.  Tried to do an update and it found the file but took awhile.  Also cleared out 49 pages of open WOs which were causing the Work Order Maintenance page to load slow.  Jacob is going to confirm with IT that ports 3306 and 443 are open so the update will be successful.  Will try and update their controller again tonight.',1746804984),(1349,511,399,'Checking their system saw that all stations and devices were online.  History showed there is still an intermittent issues with a number of stations going offline for about 10 seconds.  Have received not calls that they reported the issue to the distributor.  Closing.',1747139465),(1350,506,399,'They have a RAN, SEG, FCM, Printer that all need to be updated.  Still working on directions and figuring out logistics to send them all the pickit devices to do the reprogramming.  Have to coordinate with the distributor so that they can be billed for shipping and need to confirm with Payton whether they want to attempt the reprogramming or have the distributor do it.',1747139812),(1351,513,399,'Even though the techs were assigned stations it was giving a no station error on the TAC.  Looked at the log and saw that the system was not finding any open WOs.  It was finding none because they ere assigned to a specific user in the DB that no longer existed and since the web couldn\'t find any user matching the user id in the wo details table it just showed all users but never changed the user id in the table.  They system is on T86 which has some deprecated code for the TAC removed.  Thier TACs need to be updated from what I can tell but will first test locally with the TACs I have just to confirm before sending them directions to do the update.',1748903425),(1352,514,399,'After discussing what their issues are had them disable the invoicing option in Admin Options.  That at least allowed them to get to the Work Order Maintenance page but it is still loading slow but not crashing.  Told them to reboot at the end of the day and since they are a PAG site they will have to get with their IT to configure a local computer with puTTY and WinSCP and arrange to have them send me a invite to use their remote software to log into a local computer.\n\nThey will reboot tonight and let me know how things are going tomorrow.  732-483-8561',1748959879),(1353,514,399,'Have not heard back from them yet.',1749481345),(1354,515,399,'They set me up with a tech in the Romanian area and I connected using AnyDesk.  Was able to see that the database only had a few tables in it so something happened during a restore.  Was able to use a backup file to populate the entire database and then updated software from R30 to R39 but was unable to test anything since the controller was not on site.  Had to do a manual update since the controller could not access the internet.  Tested as best I could and gave the tech my number and email encase he ran into any troubles once he installed the controller at the site.',1749660208),(1355,516,399,'It took a bit of time, this is the fourth time Matteo has called me asking for me to figure out if the system will work for their workflow.  He finally answered my questions, so I was able to understand almost all of the workflow.  They have a few items misconfigured if they want the system to work for their workflow but have to use the R39 version of the software along with a customer mim file since R39 doesn\'t have the code to work with the newer CDMs which report they are ttyACMx devices to the system instead of ttyUSBx devices.  Tested on my local system and if I\'m understanding their workflow correctly the system should be able to do what they want with these changes.  Will integrate the changes into a release so they can update their controller if need be.\n\nHave not heard back from Matteo if what I proposed will work for their workflow and I forgot to hit send/receive so didn\'t get it off to him until this morning and remember he said he was only working half a day today.',1749661194),(1356,516,399,'Matteo asked for a more specific video to show customer so created and sent to him.  Awaiting his response to see if the custom setting will work for the customer.',1749735955),(1357,517,399,'Nick confirmed that all was working on Friday when they left but today they couldn\'t access the system.  Walked him through finding the controller and he confirmed the controller had no power light.  He traced the power supply back and found the block had a green light.  When he touched it, the block was extremely warm.  Asked if he knew how to check voltage with a multimeter and explained what he should see when he measured it.  He happened to have anther 12V power supply around with a plug that fit the controller and plugged it in.  Controller came up and they were able the access the system.  Nick will call ADG to send a new power supply.  Asked Mark to send an HDMI plug with the power supply for them to also install so that their screen is not so small when logging into it.',1750094307),(1358,512,399,'Ports have been opened to allow for updates it looks like, will confirm the next time a release is available.',1750364406),(1359,519,399,'Called Jacob back and told him I saw the TMM was offline and that is why they could not dispense fluids since it controller the pumps.  He cycled power to the TMM and it came back online.  \n\nAlso noticed that the log files was over 380MB, mentioned to him it would be best if he would reboot ever couple of months.  He asked why when he reboots the controller, which he hasn\'t done for months, the TMM didn\'t come back online.  I figure he is confusing the CDM with the controller but either way explained to him that the device are not controlled by the controller so a reboot of the controller has no effect on the devices. And would need to cycle power to the individual devices if they show offline but all others show online.  ',1750364672),(1360,516,399,'Tested locally the workflow the best I understood it.  After testing some items, it was found that the new workflow for dispensing from the web will not work for the customer.  The new workflow was requested by Andrea S from Gartec so had to revert the system back to R39 and then do some custom code on the MIM file to work with the new CDM serial chips.  \n\nReverted the system from R46 back to R39 and added custom MIM file.  The system seemed to work like the customer wishes and will do more testing tomorrow and let me know.  The system did not act exactly like my local test bed so grab all the files from their system and will compare with the local test bed to see where the differences are at.',1750364964),(1361,522,399,'IT got involved since TV could not see the controller online.  Logged into a local computer and then ssh into the controller and found the disk space was 100% full.  Found various log files were very large and removed.  Once done and a reboot occurred system acted normally.  System was on R34.\n\nNeed to write cleanup code for log rotation.',1751635150),(1362,523,399,'Logged into their system and reviewed the logs.  The logs were showing successful dispenses of 0w/20 as well as there were a number of completed WO with dispense values > 0 completed today.  I suggested to Ashley that she call to confirm all is good with 0w/20 or not before making the 3-hour trip.  Waiting on her response.',1752615914),(1363,520,399,'System was back online when he called today after IT did some work due to changing the dealerships owners.  They couldn\'t get to the login page using their normal shortcut so gave them the IP address of the controller and they were able to get it.',1752768468),(1364,523,399,'Emailed Ashley to find out if things were all good at Ocean Honda and she responded with Working Good.',1752778719),(1365,521,399,'Dave went to GB and after hooking up the network dongle and it still not showing online he hooked a keyboard, mouse and monitor up to it.  The display was all garbled and tried both HDMI and VGA ports with no success.  Returning controller on RMA 071725-1MS to troubleshoot.  No hurry as it is their site and they are taking measurements manually.',1752778894),(1366,524,399,'Looked at system and log files do agree that they have reboot weekly.  \n\nNoticed in log an index error in auto_reset_reels() put in  print(\"ReelsOpen: {}\".format(ReelsOpen)) for troubleshooting.\n\nFound a serial error in the 0701 log file.',1753116059),(1367,524,399,'Bob arrived and then cycled power to the FCM but that did not help bring it back online.  Told him to look for a flashing light but he said he was going to get Mike to come with tools and then call me for help.',1753116284),(1368,525,399,'Before I returned Danial\'s call, Mark had already spoken with him. He expressed discomfort with using a lift for troubleshooting and suggested that if he’s not comfortable proceeding, he should contact DSD to come out. I also recommended that when calling DSD, he request both FCM and PSM circuit boards to avoid multiple trips and expedite getting the system back online.\n\nI sent Danial photos of the connector, instructions on how to remove it, and highlighted potential issues he might encounter. I also offered to assist remotely—if he decides to troubleshoot, he can call me once the FCM cover is off, and I’ll control the pumps while he performs the \"tap\" test.\n\nCurrently, I’m waiting to hear back from him on how he wants to proceed.',1753220264),(1369,525,399,'Troubleshot with Daniel and they found the red and white wires in the PSM were loose and once secured they got pulse counts when pumping.',1753375989),(1370,526,399,'cronlog_20250509175646.log show that the CDM disconnected from the controller, suspect they accidently disconnected it. Working fine after reboot but Tom said he did the same thing just before me and logs show that a reboot happened just before I did it.  Will monitor.  First time it happened about 5/9 and now again today 7/25',1753453849),(1371,527,399,'Based on your pictures, you are only using our system to monitor tank levels, is this correct?  In other words, you have no stations that are using our system to control the dispense of fluids.  I’m assuming this because the CDM (Communication Data Module) is right above the controller and would have to be on the other side of the brick wall to communicate effectively with the station hardware to control fluid dispensing.\n\nIf the controller is just a few feet away from the TMMs I wouldn’t think you would ever have an invalid message on your dashboard for the tanks.  There could however be some interference as the TMM should technically be at least 2 feet apart to prevent any possibility radio interference between the two but since you haven’t really had any issues until recently I believe they are just fine where they are at.\n\nAs best I can tell by the pics, the left hand TMM (Tank Monitor Module), I’m going to assume it is monitoring 4 new oil tanks or 3 new oil and 1 used oil/coolant tank and the right hand is TMM monitoring at least 1 used oil/coolant tank.  I base this on the shiny thicker black wires coming out of the bottoms of the TMM, 4 on the left and 1 on the right TMM.\n\nThe grey wires on the right hand TMM should be going to your used oil/coolant station.  Do you have one or two stations with alarms?  I have attached an attachment showing the wiring of a typical system that uses a timer to control the solenoid for the evacuation pump.  Unless the system is in alarm state, at least one relay light should be lit on the right TMM indicating that it is supplying power to the timer.  Two would be lit if you had two timers to control two separate pumps, one for used oil and the other for used coolant.\n\nNow, the LEDs on the TMM faceplate could be burnt out since you have had the since around 2018 so if you removed the cover, you should see 2 LED lit on the lower right hand side of the PCB board.  If they are burnt out we do sell replacement membranes.  You just peel off the old and stick on the new.\n\nIn the app you should confirm you have at least one entry like the following where is shows the Default State as Powered.  Unfortunately, I can guarantee they labeled then as user friendly as the following:  \n\nSince you have 5 grey wires from what I can tell from the pics coming out of the right TMM I would expect you to see two entries like the ones above.  I’m at a loss as to what the 5th wire would be connected to.\n\nI should be able to talk you through a simple test to see if it is working as long as invalid is not showing on the dashboard tanks.  If they are please just power cycle the TMM that controls the tanks with invalid messages which should take no more than 5 minutes after power cycle.  \n\nAs you can tell by the attachment the horn can be easily replaced as there is a connected inside the case which its wires connect to.  It looks like the part of the board that is burnt goes to the “horn” side and is not on the power side, so the pcb the horn connects to should be good still.\n',1753820473),(1372,528,399,'Ken explained that he needed to know how to change the IP address so walked him through it. He then called back and said the techs could not pump. I asked him if any devices showed offline and explained where to look for that information.  Walked him through how to identify which TMM was for what and he eventually cycled power on the correct TMM and it came back online.  I mentioned that if becomes a frequent issue then there are options that would improve its reliability.  \n\nHe had difficulty with changing the IP address but will attempt it later.  Notice this controller now acts like the one in Bloomfield where when we did have TV connection it would take about two hours before we could log in with TV once a reboot happened.  This was not the case before the new owners change the network.\n\n',1754516196),(1373,529,399,'Had Dave send me the controller and found the HD had failed.  Installed new and updated with very old DB which they will have to confirm once they install it if everything mapped ok.',1755199710),(1374,529,399,'They called today and had a couple of issues.  Found that I missed populating the t_tank_configurations table when they wanted me to add more tables then they originally told me, went from 33 to 45 tables.  Had issues until I rescanned for hardware and it found 2 new TMM whose ids matched the missing TMM ids so everything started working after that but took me almost 2 hours to figure it out.',1755199840),(1375,529,399,'Dave will schedule a day to be up there to trace all the sensor wires to ensure that the tanks, sensors and products are all mapped correctly. ',1755199884),(1376,526,399,'This issue has not been reported again.',1755537578),(1377,530,399,'Spent two hours with Daniel troubleshooting the system layout and investigating why three TMMs were showing offline. The labeling left by the installer was completely inaccurate, so Daniel corrected the labels while we traced and verified the actual wiring and layout.\n\nFindings:\n\nTMM 3 and TMM 4 are located in the tank room. TMM 4 is wired first in line to the CDM, followed by TMM 3.\nTMM 3 is connected (white wire) to the four TMMs at the pickup stations.\nTMM 1, located at the end of the line, was functioning correctly.\nTMMs 4, 5, and 6 were showing offline.\nTMM 2 was operational and flashing, indicating RS485 communication. However, TMMs 5 and 6 showed no RS485 activity, suggesting possible port damage—likely caused by last week’s lightning storm.\nAlthough TMM 4 showed RS485 activity, it still appeared as invalid and offline, indicating it may be partially damaged. This highlights a potential issue: RS485 lights may flash even when communication is not functioning properly, complicating future troubleshooting.\nActions Taken:\n\nSet TMM 4 to Radio mode since the CDM is mounted on the same cinder block wall. It successfully communicated with the CDM and showed good signal strength. Left it in Radio mode to ensure accurate tank readings, as tank levels were nearing shutoff thresholds.\nSet TMMs 5 and 6 to Radio mode as well. Both began working correctly.\nConfirmed that all pickup station TMMs are used solely for relay control and do not monitor tank levels.\nNext Steps:\n\nDaniel will order three replacement TMMs through DSD to replace the suspected damaged units.',1755538450),(1378,531,399,'Logged in and looked at system before returning his call.  Found a number of WOs that showed dispenses and confirmed in logs that values were being seen by the systems as the dispense happened.  Called Mike and said all seems to be good on the hardware side so suspect maybe something with the tech\'s computer is causing the issue and suggest they reboot it and if the problem persists to call back.  Have not heard back from them as of 18aug25.',1755538873),(1379,532,399,'FAE Earth moving e4:3a:6e:7a:2e:12 32GB Filcar doesn\'t want the new way the wo process flows, which was developed based on Andrea S request before leaving the company, is not the way they want it to work.  Figured out which file contained the old logic and uploaded it to the controller along with newer software and they said it work almost like they wanted want but they wanted the already dispensed data to be displayed to the techs when they bring up the WO again.  \n\nExplained that this would be an enhancement because the flow has always been to remove the already dispensed products from the screen and would have to wait for it to be changed as the entire wo flow has to be redesigned back to the old flow for it to work. \n\nThis WO should have been entered a couple of months back and forgot about it till now.',1755545042),(1380,530,399,'Dan called again today to say TMM 4, 5, and 6 were offline.  He tried cycling power but they did not come back online.  I cycled between radio and wire and for a brief second they communicated their levels but the went offline again and never came back.  Dan is calling DSD to get TMMs on order and stressed to me that he wanted me to bring up to management that they are not happy with their distributors installation team, Myer\'s brothers, and that we need to figure out a way to sell replacement parts to them directly as they have a facility team that can do the work.  I said I would bring it up.',1756133581),(1381,530,3,'8/25 Contacted by DSD, advised H&H Kia wanted to purchase 3 TMM PCBs and would like Kia facilities maintain their Oil Cop System. Because they are not happy with Myers Brothers.\n',1756141138),(1382,533,399,'Had not issues turning on pumps.  They need an HDMI dongle sent to them to plug into the controller.  WO maintenance pages loads slowly.  This is a dual core processor, which indicates it is a very old one as most for a very long time have been 4 core Celerons.  Creating indexes to help with the slow issue and disabled invoicing in the admin options temporarily until tmp table are populated.',1756147293),(1383,534,399,'With the new software they are running T86 it has a fix for the WO query where it would make the system extremely slow when invoicing was enabled.  Closed all previous WOs and marked them as invoiced from 30 July 2025 and older.',1756156263),(1384,527,399,'According to Paul AME techs came by and swapped out the TMM but never stopped to confirm it was working or not.  Paul email me today to tell me it still was not working.  This is what was determined to be wrong and the last steps I asked him to perform to confirm.  Awaiting on his response: \n\nOk good the 2 LED were on, your original TMM those were not on but if it was power cycling then they would never have come on since they didn’t have enough time to communicate to the CDM before power was lost again.  \n\nSince the new TMM was not cycling before you switched #2 to the ON position, meaning that the system was not telling it to activate a relay because it didn’t see it out there and THEN it started to cycle power once the DIP switch #2 was turned on, that leads me to believe one of your devices connected to the Relay outputs of the TMM is shorted.  The short is causing the system to cycle power but the current is not high enough to take out the fuse. \n \nMy assumption is that all your pickup stations that are controlled by this TMM do not currently work, is that correct?  I can’t seem to find the screen shot of your relay setup in this email thread; only see the screenshot I posted of my test system.  \n\nOne thing you could do without having to go over to the shop where the issue is, is to change the relay configuration from the Relay Configuration page for any relays that show Powered to Not Powered.  Once you have set all the relays for the bad TMM to Not Power, wait a couple of minutes and see if your dashboard shows the device online and you no longer see Invalid on tanks it report levels for.  If this happens then one by one turn them back to Powered waiting about a minute before turning the next one on while monitoring the Dashboard page to make sure it doesn’t show invalid before turning the next one on.  You shouldn’t have to wait more than a minute, in the worst case 5 minutes.  When you get the invalid, turn that relay back to Not Powered and see if the system recovers. \n \nIf the above steps did not solve your issue, then you will have to do the following to see if this solves the power cycling.  To confirm, remove power from the TMM and then you will need to remove all the connectors form the relay output section of the TMM.  Once they are removed plug the TMM back in and see if it still cycles power and if not then there should be 3 LED lit within a couple of minutes and you should no longer see Invalid on your dashboard.\n\nIf the TMM stops cycling power after you removed all the connectors from the relay portion of the TMM, install one at a time and see which one is causing the issue or if they all cause an issue.  \n\nIf either of the above steps works so you don’t see any Invalid message on your dashboard and you see accurate fluid levels you will have to of course call AME to come back out to troubleshoot the relay hardware.  If all the relays turn out to cause the TMM to cycle power, the TMM may have been damaged which I’m hoping is not the case, and they should order another TMM.\n',1757626610);
