INSERT INTO `discrepancies` VALUES (1,1,3,0,17,0,6,6,0,2,'Blue Lights on FCM are not working','Blue light indicators on the FCM do not power on when the reel is on. Also there is no green power light on the front. This does not affect the system, but i would like indicators to work.',1,1,6,1449171594,1454664927),(2,1,6,0,21,0,8,8,0,3,'Remote display not working','Display will not light',0,1,6,1449604122,1454664933),(3,1,0,0,62,0,1,0,1,0,'Remove Dispense ID column from Station Dashboard','Remove Dispense ID column from Station Dashboard because for anything',0,1,6,1452875647,1459541634),(4,1,1,0,27,0,12,44,0,0,'tank configuration - alarms','it\'s not possible to modify all 4 warnings and alarms of a tank if tank monitor switch is ON',1,2,6,1455895117,1459344621),(5,1,1,0,27,0,12,44,0,0,'tank configuration - alarms\' levels','there is no verification if numbers of levels are correctly set in the system: it\'s possible to set high level warning with an higher value of high level shutoff, and re-order level or low level shutoff can be set with higher values than the high level alarms',1,2,6,1455895307,1459344609),(6,8,0,0,27,0,12,44,0,0,'filter of discrepancies','clear button is not working',1,2,6,1455895427,1460383399),(7,1,1,0,27,0,12,44,0,0,'logo for login page','1) the logo in the login page is not centered (Firefox and Chrome)\n2) in administrative option there is no specification about size (pixels and MB) or allowed formats\n3) dimension is 250x100 fixed, the auto-adapting in my opinion should mantain the shape, adding transparent parts in case they\'re needed',1,1,6,1455896005,1459344599),(8,1,1,0,27,0,12,44,0,0,'change image in administrative options','1) the size in pixel is different from company logo in the login page\n2) change image and company logo should act the same way (if there is drop files to upload for one, make the same for the other)\n3) I would modify the title of the option: \"dashboard name/image\"',1,1,6,1455896479,1459344665),(9,1,1,0,27,0,12,44,0,0,'dashboard tank levels','when passing mouse on a tank, in the blue box the name of the product shows also \"[###]\"',1,1,6,1455896707,1459344639),(10,1,1,0,27,0,12,44,0,0,'system time','in the bottom part it appears \"Time: 16:45:23 (12 Hours Format)\" and this is obviously a mistake\nin system time configuration it\'s set on 12 hours format and system time states it\'s 4:45:23',1,2,6,1455897096,1459344650),(11,8,0,0,2,0,1,0,0,0,'Forgot password mail','Not getting mail while setting the forgot password',0,1,6,1456482144,1459537031),(12,1,1,0,39,0,24,26,0,0,'Place holding 0 in employee\'s password','Most of my customers set up their Tech\'s password as their employee ID number. This works good except if the employee # starts with the number 0. It will take the number but next time you go in to modify the tech\'s information the system will drop the leading 0 forcing you to re-input his password again.',1,1,6,1458219547,1459344561),(13,1,1,0,39,0,24,57,0,39,'Job recipe set up','Need the ability to apply all technicians against a particular recipe. In this case the customer has over 50 pieces of equipment they are going to assign individual recipes against and they want any of their 50 tech\'s to be able to select the recipe to service the equipment. Need to be able to select ALL when adding a tech to a recipe.',1,1,6,1458219817,1470235519),(14,1,5,0,3,1,1,0,0,0,'Tank Monitor delivery report','Tank monitor should recognize when tanks are filled.\nRecord date, time, volume before fill operations begin then record time, volume after fill operations are completed and net increase. \nWould like to make this as accurate as possible and publish the error.',1,1,6,1459290202,1484780915),(15,8,0,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'Can not delete users','Can not delete users.',0,1,6,1459342100,1470235646),(16,1,0,0,3,0,1,26,0,0,'Ver. 1.1 does not allow user to select Station fro','Ver. 1.1 does not allow user to select Station from TAC',1,1,6,1459950842,1459951063),(17,8,0,0,1,0,1,0,0,0,'Need to bcc the users in emails','Need to bcc the users in emails',1,1,6,1460183491,1460381651),(18,1,0,0,6,0,1,0,0,0,'Job Recipe Preset amount is multiplying by 4','When creating a new job recipe, if you set the preset amount for the product to any number it is automatically multiplied by 4 when you go to dispense.',1,1,6,1460479343,1460479400),(19,1,0,0,6,0,1,32,0,22,'Ticket printing issue','When two products are dispensed using the same work order number, the ticket that is printed out does not show the work order number. It just goes from the technicians name to the first product dispensed. See the attached photo',1,1,6,1460481687,1470235673),(20,1,1,0,6,0,1,0,0,0,'System not syncing up with oilcopsupport.com','On LQD_R_2_17, i cannot get any systems to sync up with oilcopsupport.com. I am creating the system on support.com and inputting the MAC address of the controller. I then go on the controller and hit synchronize database but the system never comes up online.',1,1,6,1460493711,1461005744),(21,1,1,0,21,0,8,0,0,3,'PSM Seal broke','I cut my seal becaause it was not acting correctly',2,2,6,1460555539,1460555664),(22,1,1,0,6,0,1,0,0,0,'Problems with creating a Work Order from the \"Work','LQD_R_2_17\n\nWhen creating a work order in the work order maintenance page, the user cannot select a station or product unless an Operator is first selected. Then when an operator is selected, the product cannot be selected until a station is selected first.  After selecting a product, the user can go back and change Operator and/or Station to all technicians/stations. The user should be able to select any of the options at any time when creating the work order.\n\nAlso there is a problem with the ',1,1,6,1461181937,1470235705),(23,1,0,0,6,0,1,0,0,0,'Reels getting stuck','On version LQD_R_2_17, reels are getting stuck in the \"in use\" state. After tech\'s are finished dispensing, not using a preset amount, or if the FCM is shut off during a dispense, the reel will get stuck in the \"in use\" state. The only way to get the reel reset is to find the last work order that was in use when the dispense timed out, open that wo/dispense and hit the dispense complete button. If the last work order is unknown, the only way to get the real unstuck is for an admin to delete the ',1,2,6,1461764803,1470235718),(24,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Variance report','Report/graphic that reflects difference of what the tank monitor indicates physical tank inventory vs. totaling oil cop transactions for the same product and what the inventory should be. \n\nThis will help identify if the bypass on the PSM is open and when used without the tank monitor will reflect when some one has failed to add inventory to a tank.',1,1,6,1461963304,1630521673),(25,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Question -- DNS','How difficult would it be to type a name into the URL instead of an IP address?\nIs there a such thing as a simple mini DNS server patch?',1,1,6,1461966826,1630524024),(26,1,0,0,1,0,1,8,0,0,'\"Recent work orders\" displayed from admin /support','Can a customer go to their suopport.com desktop and correctly view the work orders?',1,2,6,1463078393,1470235997),(27,8,0,0,1,0,1,72,0,0,'Oil Cop Support Demo system not working','Set up a demo system on oilcopsupport.com and the demo is not working. Can sign in but it does not function, no dispenses, cannot make changes etc...',0,1,6,1472218924,1473776504),(28,1,1,0,2,0,1,0,0,0,'Request for assistance with converting controller ','Received message from Andrea and Kevin for assistance with a controller conversion. Andrea needs a second controller to be converted from a release version to a test version. I will be available to assist at 7a.m. US central time. There may be someone available to assist earlier than that. Comment for any new details regarding this request.',1,1,6,1473215468,1473332021),(29,1,1,0,1,138,1,8,0,0,'I just tried to set the time on the controller, an','I\'m writing you with no reports or results from our tests, but only for informing you that I just tried to set the time on the controller, and nothing has changed from July, April, March, January and back to last year!!! Time is shifted of 1 hour, I set 16:45 and system sets to 15.45, whatever the fuse I set (obviously I check the \"do you want to update time?\" box).\nTime setting...such a stupid thing, but I already have 5 customers calling for this, asking how they are supposed to change time because they were not able to do it...I wrote this at least 5 times in my reports...\nSo...do we have to test seriously the new updated version? It started very very bad......',1,3,6,1473264210,1477498970),(30,1,3,0,6,3,1,77,0,56,'FCMs Dropping signal','LQD R 2_19, two FCMs lost wireless communication signal suddenly and would not reacquire the signal automatically. I did a power reset to both FCMs and still they would not reacquire the signal. There were two FCMs, one RED, and one Range Extender in the vicinity that had full connection. I tried scanning for new hardware and turning the FCMs on and off in the system and still no connection. I then reset the controller. When it booted back up the two FCMs connected right away.  \n\nWe need to look into what might be causing these FCMs to drop communication for essentially no reason, This has happened at a few shops where the FCMs will drop signal, normally the signal is reacquired automatically. If this happens during a dispense it can cause the reel to lock up.  \n\nCan we possibly look into a way to constantly monitor devices signal strength and have the data recorded to where we could find patterns that could show why an device is suddenly dropping signal?',2,2,6,1473341860,1476370023),(31,1,1,0,143,0,12,42,0,27,'test','test',0,1,6,1473345765,1473348688),(32,1,2,0,21,0,8,8,0,3,'my pump quite','ljhlkjh',0,1,6,1473360551,1473690998),(33,8,0,0,1,1,1,0,0,0,'testing comment emails','testing comment emails',1,3,6,1473776172,1473835388),(34,1,5,0,6,138,1,0,0,0,'TSM Relay does not turn off after reel calibration','When a relay on the TSM is setup to trigger on with a product/reel, if  a reel calibration is done the relay turns on as it should when you hit start dispense. When you are done and hit stop dispense the relay does not turn off. Then in order to get the relay to turn off you have to either power down the TSM or complete a regular work order dispense.',0,1,6,1475097971,1475286903),(35,8,0,0,1,1,1,0,0,0,'Testing oilcopsupport mail change','Testing - Need to add name of the person who opened the discrepancy in the email. Also We need a button on link in the email which takes it to oilcop support site directly.',0,1,6,1475159070,1475320078),(36,1,0,0,80,80,56,0,0,0,'Firmware  on TAC V2_2_1_3 problem','JOb recipies do not work on TAC when assign to Tech. It\'s work when assign to manager. it\'s work when assign to technician from PC.\n\n\nTAC firmware V2_2_1_3\nLQD T_2_25\n\nThanks to send a new firmware\n\nRegards\n\nSébastien',2,3,6,1476172400,1476348120),(37,1,4,0,80,80,56,0,0,0,'COMMUNICATION ERROR 255','System configuration whith muli product ON\nAfter dispensing it\'s not possible to re-open the W/O and dispense a different product. Message ERROR COMMUNICATION 255\n\nI Cannot testing the TAC if I have a communication Error,\n\nTAC firmware V2_2_1_3\nLQD T_2_25\n\nRegards\n\nSébastien',2,3,6,1476172452,1489409873),(38,1,4,0,80,81,56,101,0,83,'Technician gets stuck on a W / O and can not close','Problem occured today\nImpossible to take a reel\nThe technician has closed its W / O but always returns to the same.\nThe manager deleted the W / O after the technician could not connect \"Technician do not exist\"\nThe manager deleted the technician and to recreate.\nOk The TAC works',2,2,6,1476190253,1490091059),(39,1,1,0,6,6,1,0,0,0,'Daily Report Bug','LQD_T_2_26\nIn the Daily Report under system logs, there is a bug for the values in the Work Order Summary section.\n\n First in order for a value to show under W/O Opened Today, the user must create a work order and leave it open. If the user closes the work order the value goes away. This value should stay true for any work orders created in the same day no matter if the work order was closed or not. This gives the user a quick number as to how many work orders were opened in a day.\n\nTotal Opened is working as it should.\n\nFor Closed Today, the only way a value will show here is if the work order was created the same day as the daily report you are looking at. EX- If you look at the daily report on 6/25 and worker order was opened and closed on 6/25 then a value will appear, but if a work order was opened on 6/24 and closed on 6/25 there will be no value. We need this to show the value of all work orders that were closed on the same day no matter when the work order was opened.\n\nI attached a screen shot where y',1,1,6,1477424260,1487687196),(40,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'preset quantity exceeds \"max allowed preset\"','version T_2_26\nloading a new WO from WO management (manager dashboard)\npreset quantity exceeds \"max allowed preset\" but no error message is shown, the WO has been created and saved in the list\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.1.3\ncheck \"software\" report §3.2.1',1,2,6,1479198290,1486054393),(41,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'preset quantity exceeds \"max product dispense per ','version T_2_26\nloading a new WO from WO management (manager dashboard)\npreset quantity exceeds both \"max allowed preset\" (see also discrepancy #40) and \"max product dispense per WO\" but no error message is shown, the WO has been created and saved in the list\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.1.4\ncheck \"software\" report §3.2.1',1,2,6,1479198580,1486054432),(42,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'no open WO mentioned in \"WO status\" and \"summary r','version T_2_26\nloading a new WO from WO management (manager dashboard)\n\nif you create a new WO, but nobody selects it (from TAC or PC, it\'s the same), you can\'t find it in reports as an open WO. It will appear only once it will be selected by a user.\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.1.4 and §1.1.3.1\ncheck \"reports\" report §1.2',1,2,6,1479205297,1490091424),(43,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'recent WO list shown incorrectly on manager dashbo','version T_2_26\nmanager dashboard: recent WO\n\nWO in this list are shown depending on administrative options, depending on the value of \"purge closed WO\".\nThis is acting not only to closed WO, but also to still open WO: if the WO has been created before the range of time set for purging closed WO, then they are not shown in the list\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.1.4\ncheck \"software\" report §2.2 @administrative options',1,2,6,1479205908,1490092848),(44,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'recent WO sorted incorrectly on manager dashboard','version T_2_26\nmanager dashboard: recent WO\n\nthe list of recent WO is not sorted by date, or time, or last modified.\nIn 2 different days, without any modification on the system, the same WO were sorted in 2 different ways, apparently randomly.\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.1.4\ncheck \"software\" report §3.1.1',1,2,6,1479206373,1490093935),(45,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'open dispense instead of preset','version T_2_26\ndispense page on TAC, WO loaded from WO management with preset\n\nafter WO# selection and station selection (when required), system states that the WO is in open dispense mode, while the WO has been configured with a preset.\nwhen dispensing, the system automatically close at the preset value, even if it was stating \"open dispense\"\nThis is happening only when working on TAC, from PC virtual TAC system clearly shows the preset value.\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.2 (selecting WO from TAC without dispensing)\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.4 (selecting WO and dispensing from TAC): see all WARNINGs and note #4\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.3 (selecting WO from PC without dispensing)',1,2,6,1479207408,1487067891),(46,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'possibility to select a station even if the produc','version T_2_26\nWO scenario 1 and 2 - \"station\" field value on \"all assigned stations\"\nselect station on TAC\n\nafter WO# selection, system asks for station selection: depending on the stations the user is assigned to, system allows the selection of all of them.\n(i.e. user assigned to stations 1-2, system allows to select both - user assigned to stations 1-3, system allows to select both - user assigned to all stations, system allows to select all - user assigned to station 2, system allows to select only station 2)\nThe problem is that we are in scenario 1, where the WO has been already configured at least with a specific product and the preset quantity.\nSystem allows to select stations where this product is not available, while it should automatically show only the list of assigned stations where the product is present, or directly automatically select the single station where this product is available.\nIn case we are in scenario 2, there is still the possibility that product has been specified even if in open ',1,2,6,1479217835,1497428930),(47,8,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'max number of digits for discr. title','it\'s not mentioned anywhere that there is a max number of digits for discrepancies\' titles.',1,2,6,1479219129,1487068066),(48,8,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'max number of digits for discr. description','it\'s not written anywhere that description should be shorter than \"x\" digits\nThe problem is that I wrote for a while, submitted the discrepancy and found out that it has been cutted without giving error message.\nNow I have to re-write everything, trying to remember all things that I wrote earlier, which is not so easy and fast.',1,3,6,1479219312,1487068668),(49,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'automatic switch to first product of the selected ','version T_2_26\nWO scenario 1 and 2 - \"station\" field value on \"all assigned stations\"\ndispense page on TAC (after station selection - see discrepancy #46)\n\nThis is coming directly after discrepancy #46.\nIf the product is not available in the station selected by user, then system automatically selects the first product available in the selected station.',1,2,6,1479219895,1497429123),(50,8,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'\"enter\" not working in comments','in comments it\'s not working, you can see that the line changes in preview, but once submitted everything is written on the same line',1,2,6,1479220318,1487071146),(51,8,0,0,81,144,56,0,0,0,'impossible to follow discrepancies','I had to add discrepancies from this account because in this way both me and Sébastien can see them...the fact is that I cannot be e-mailed for the update/closure of the discrepancies because the address is fictitious (as my address is already in use for Gartec account)\nHow can I follow all discrepancies (especially to know that I have to answer to your comments)? could you please switch the addresses? or use my personal a.simonetto@gartec.it twice?\n\nIf I added all discrepancies from the other account, the problem would have been the same, because Sébastien\'s mail address is already in use here in Gitec account...',1,1,6,1479223745,1490126777),(52,1,0,0,81,399,56,0,0,0,'user can select a WO that he should not be able to','version T_2_26\nWO scenario 1 and 2 - \"station\" field value on \"all assigned stations\"\n\nWO has been configured for \"all technicians\" and with a preset of a specific product, which is not present in all stations.\nThe WO can be selected even by a technician assigned only to stations where this product is not present.\nThis causes a series of bugs: once the WO has been selected, the user is asked to choose a station ==> he can select only stations where he is assigned to, where the product is not available (discrepancy #46) ==> system allows the user to dispense from the selected station another product and not the preset one (discrepancy #49)\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.2.2, §1.1.3.2, §1.1.6.2, §1.2.4.4, §1.2.4.10',1,2,6,1479282934,1630524066),(53,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'useless request to select reel','version T_2_26\nWO scenario 1 and 2 - specified product from WO management\nworking on virtual TAC on PC\n\nafter WO# selection and station selection, on PC the user is asked to select the reel, even if there is only one reel available with the specified product in the selected station.\nIt\'s an useless step that should be jumped automatically\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.3.1, §1.2.6.1',1,2,6,1479284519,1487589043),(54,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'WO automatic assigned to user/station','version T_2_26\nWO scenario 1 and 2 - specified product from WO management\nworking on virtual TAC on PC\n\nif an user selects a WO and (by selecting station/reel...) arrives to the dispense page, even without starting the dispense (by clicking on START and opening the solenoid valve) and returning back, the WO is automatically assigned to that user and to the selected station.\nThe WO cannot be selected from any other user, and the user who can select it cannot select any other station.\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.3',1,2,6,1479285185,1487589618),(55,1,0,0,81,6,56,0,0,0,'TAC vs virtual TAC','software version: T_2_26\nTAC firmware version: 1.3 (NEW_TAC_v2_2_1_3.hex)\n\nsystem behavior working on TAC is different from behavior with virtual TAC on PC.\nThey must be the same. Same steps, same requests, everything.',1,3,6,1479291107,1489767625),(56,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'adjusting WO bug','version T_2_26\nWO management from manager dashboard\nthis comes after a WO has been selected from PC virtual console, with dispense not begun and WO automatically assigned to the user who selected the WO, forced to station selected by user (see discrepancy #54)\n\n1) loading WO (see TA1-001 original configuration (loading) picture)\n2) selecting WO without dispensing: see discrepancy #54\n3) when clicking on update/delete button in order to adjust the WO, the product has been changed, switching to \"all products\" (see adjust WO - assignment to all products bug picture), while the original configuration had been set to \"10W40\" product.\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.3.1\ncheck \"software\" report §3.2.2',1,2,6,1479294463,1487666783),(57,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'possibility to give a preset with \"all products\"','version T_2_26\nWO management from manager dashboard\nthis comes directly after discrepancy #56\n\nIf you\'re adding a new WO, if product is on \"all products\" value and you try to give a preset, system correctly returns an error message \"before entering preset value, product should be selected\"\nBut if the WO has been already loaded with a specific product and a preset, selected by any user without dispensing any drop of product, if you go back to WO management and try to update the WO, system will automatically switch the product value to \"all products\", leaving the preset, and not returning any error message if you click on \"update\".\n\ncheck \"software\" report §3.2.2',1,2,6,1479295327,1487666897),(58,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'product filtering not working','version T_2_26\nWO management from manager dashboard\nthis comes directly after discrepancy #57\n\nif you try to re-configure the WO with the original product, you can\'t: the product filter is not working (see picture)\n\ncheck \"software\" report §3.2.2',1,2,6,1479295597,1497435408),(59,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'useless request to select station','version T_2_26\nworking on virtual TAC on PC\nWO configured for \"all assigned stations\"\n\nwhen logged with a user assigned only to a single station, after WO# selection the user is asked to select the station (it\'s different from TAC - another reason for discrepancy #55)\nit\'s an useless step, as if the technician is assigned only to a single station, he must be addressed directly to the next step.\nIn scenario 1, where the preset is already decided, directly to dispense page.\nIn scenario 2, to the preset/open dispense request (when product already defined) or to product/reel request.\n\nSame thing in case the user is assigned to more than 1 station, but the selected WO# is configured to dispense a product available only in one single station (must be also assigned to user).\n\nIn case the product to be dispensed is not present in the stations assigned to the user, the user must not see the WO# in his list of selectable WO.',1,2,6,1479303151,1487669737),(60,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'useless request to select reel (on PC)','version T_2_26\nworking on virtual TAC on PC\n\nafter station selection, user is always asked to select the reel: but if the product is already configured by manager in WO management, user should be directly addressed to the next step (dispense page)',1,2,6,1479303377,1487669962),(61,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'useless request to select station (2)','version T_2_26\nworking on virtual TAC on PC\n\nif the list of available stations to select is simply composed by one single station, then this become an useless step that must be jumped automatically',1,2,6,1479303761,1487670345),(62,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'\"not assigned to any station\" message','version T_2_26\nworking on virtual TAC on PC\n\nusers assigned only to stations where the configured product is not present can anyway arrive to select the WO (see discrepancy #52)\non TAC, system allows the user to select one of his assigned stations (discrepancy #46) and to dispense the first product of that station (discrepancy #49)\n\nhere from PC, system acts differently: it returns an error message (check attached picture) stating that \"you are not assigned to any station\".\n\nOn one side, it\'s correct to return an error. (actually the correct thing is not to allow the user to select the WO, as it\'s configured for all assigned stations but the product is not available in the station assigned to the user - see discrepancy #52)\nOn the other side the error is wrong: the user is actually assigned to one or more station. But he can\'t dispense this WO as he\'s not assigned to a station where the product is present.\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.3.2 and §1.1.6.2',1,2,6,1479305331,1515570760),(63,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'user can dispense a product he\'s not allowed to di','version T_2_26\nselecting WO from TAC after it has been already selected from PC\n\nthis comes directly after discrepancy #62\nIn previous test on TAC, system was asking station selection and then switching automatically to first product of the selected station (check \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.2.2 and discrepancies #52,46,49).\nTEST: once received the error message \"you are not assigned to any station\" on PC, user goes to TAC and try to select the WO from there.\nNow, system acts differently and once selected the WO, the user is directly addressed to dispense page, where system allows the dispense (in open dispense - see discrepancy #45) of the configured product (which is present in a station the user is not assigned to!).\n\nbasically, user bypassed the admin configurations.\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.3.2',1,3,6,1479313626,1490109230),(64,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'suggested configuration not working','version T_2_26\nadjusting configuration of the WO after the issues created when selecting the WO from virtual TAC (discreapancies #56/57/58)\n\ninstead of restoring the original configuration of the WO (configuration changed when the WO has been selected from virtual TAC), from adjut WO we click on update and update the WO as per \"suggestion\" of the system.\nthis is the result:\nORIGINAL: Tech31/AdBlue/all assign.stations/22.0?\nUPDATED as per system\'s suggestion: Tech31/all products/refilling station/preset 22?\n\nbut when going to select the WO, it automatically takes \"AdBlue\"...even if we clicked on update configuring \"all products\"\n\ncheck \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.3.4\ncheck \"software\" report §3.2.2',1,2,6,1479726956,1497435883),(65,1,0,0,27,27,12,68,0,50,'report issue when exporting','The customer is asking regarding the chance to export reports: if he chooses to export the transaction journal, there is no report coming out. If he chooses the other options, there is no problem.\nversion LQD_R_2_17',1,2,6,1479978226,1487668356),(66,1,1,0,27,3,12,0,0,0,'communication error when re-entering in the WO','system in Saudi Arabia\ncontroller replaced this week under warranty (the previous was no more accessible with the assigned IP address - see with Angel, he tried to fix but was not possible)\n\nversion: R_19\nadmin options: multi-product = ON, multi-dispense = ON\n\nuser can load WO from TAC and dispense. He leaves WO open. He logs again on TAC, select open WO and system gives communication error.\nAlways, no matter what is the WO and no matter what is the user dispensing.\nUser needs this working because he needs to dispense 3 different oils with same WO.',1,3,6,1481796500,1510851438),(67,3,11,0,1,3,1,8,0,0,'Tank monitor dispense','Dispensed 15W/40 Press Start let the timer run out, it stopped counting at 1, then pressed Start button again, resets timer to 59 and counts down to 1 again. Note second time pressing the Start button it did not turn yellow while counting down.\n\n0W/40 Pressed the start button, it turned yellow, however the timer did not count down.\n\nSee attachment',0,1,6,1483106630,1510851480),(68,1,1,0,6,6,1,0,0,0,'Select User- Manager','I installed LQD_T_2_27 to a controller, after the install was complete, logged in as an admin on the admin dashboard, i went to the select user button to switch to Manager. When i did this a new page loaded with an error message (see attached file). I could hit the back button and it would go back to the admin dashboard. It would let me switch to Tech. Since i had just finished a software install i physically reset the controller and tried to switch to manager but still got the same error message.',1,2,6,1484751288,1484759777),(69,1,1,0,6,6,1,0,0,0,'Tank Monitor Dispensing button in Admin options','LQD_T_2_27- When I switch the Tank Monitor Solution button to ON in admin options, the Tank Monitor Dispensing button appears but there is a PHP Error box instead of an ON/OFF button. (See attached picture)',1,1,6,1484751933,1484759807),(70,1,1,0,6,6,1,0,0,0,'Switching to Tank Monitor Solution in Admin Options','LQD_T_2_27- In Administrative options menu, switch the Tank Monitor Solution button to ON, then click Apply at the bottom, I am taken to a page with 5 different errors on it. See attached pictures of the 5 errors.',1,2,6,1484752445,1484759824),(71,1,1,0,6,6,1,0,0,0,'T_2_27 Signal Strength Indicator','On LQD_T_2_27- The signal strength indicator for added devices is not showing anything. All devices have the latest firmware for T_2_27. (See attached picture) The CDM is showing connected correctly but the FCM,TAC, and TSM are just a red X.',1,1,6,1484760283,1484765682),(72,1,4,0,6,6,1,0,0,0,'Can not \"Load Work Order\" using the TAC','LQD_T_2_27- Signed in as any user (admin,manger,tech) i can not Load Work Order using the TAC. Whenever i try to load a work order the screen goes blank for about 5 seconds then i get an Error Code 255. Communication is good as i can sign in and select a work order that was already created and go through the entire dispense process. This only happens when trying to load a work order on the tac for the first time. I have tried to reset the TAC and reloaded the firmware.',2,2,6,1484850173,1484927998),(73,1,4,0,6,3,1,0,0,0,'Problem with Select Work Order- created from the CTR website','LQD_T_2_28- If i create a work order on the CTR website and i do NOT select a product, selecting any other option does not matter, when i go to select that work order on the TAC, it lets me go through the entire process of selecting the options for the WO, lets me pick a station, then lets me select a product, it then takes me to the option to begin an open dispense (does not allow me to select a preset which is ok), but when i \"press start to begin\" it goes to a blank screen for a few second then comes up with and Error Code 255 message, then if i press enter it takes me back to the dispense page where it says \"press start to begin\"  and then repeats. \n1. I believe this should be fixed to where the user can create a work order on the website and if the options are not selected on the website then they should be able to select the options on the TAC (as this can be done on the website if the same WO is selected by a user).\n2. If this is a logic issue that can not be fixed then we need to put something in the \"Adjust Work Order\" menu on the website that lets the user know they must select a product in order for the WO to be selected and dispensed at a TAC.\nI would like to make the operations for Selecting/Loading work orders at the TAC be the exact same as Selecting/Loading work orders on the website.',1,1,6,1484927978,1510850321),(74,1,1,0,6,6,1,0,0,0,'Tank Monitor Solution Dispense not counting','LQD_T_2_29- With Tank Monitor Solution and Tank Monitor Dispensing turned ON in admin option. When you hit the Start button to turn on the relay the timer does not begin to count down. It stays at 59 seconds untill you go and refresh the webpage. So the timer is counting down in the background but is not being displayed in real time. After refreshing the page the timer will show a lower number and it will start to countdown but it does so only every 3-9 seconds.  I tried to attached a video showing this process but it would not load here. In the video you can see the timer is set to 59 seconds. I hit the start button and it says the \"dispense started successfully\" but the timer stays at 59. I then go and refresh the page and the timer jumps to 52 seconds where it stay for about 6 seconds and then automatically jumps to 43 seconds. It will eventually count down all the way but in increments of 3-9 seconds.',1,2,6,1486739736,1487177793),(75,1,1,0,6,6,1,0,0,0,'Daily Report Error with Tank Monitor Solution turned ON','LQD_T_2_29-  When the Tank Monitor Solution is turned ON in admin options, if you got View Logs and click on Daily Report and error message comes up. See attached picture of the error.',1,1,6,1486740263,1487177770),(76,1,1,0,27,27,12,0,0,0,'discrepancy #40 not fully fixed','if selecting the quantity of preset from the dropdown menu of the history the browser, then the limitation can be bypassed, the system allows you to save the WO (check \"dispensing procedure test\" report §1.1.1.3)',1,2,6,1486993992,1487582936),(77,1,1,0,27,27,12,0,0,0,'discrepancy #41 not fully fixed','see also discrepancy #76\nif for one WO, configured with a product where max preset limitation is X>Y, preset quantity is set to x (with Y<x?X)\nthen it\'s possible to select from browser\'s history dropdown menu the preset value x and save the WO (or save the update in case you update a WO, without haveing an error message.\nThe system is only checking you when manually typing the value, if you select from previous values in history, there is no control.',1,2,6,1486995230,1487582981),(78,1,1,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'TAC behavior is different after the WO has been selected from virtual TAC on PC','this is very similar to discrepancy #63, but it\'s coming from a different situation:\n\n- manager creates a new WO, not assigning a specific station.\n- if a tech goes to the TAC and selects this WO, he can choose a station (if assigned to more than one)\n- if the tech selects the WO from PC (virtual TAC), he can make same choice (as discrepancy #55 has been fixed, TAC and virtual TAC steps are the same)\n\nbut if the tech (who selected a station from virtual TAC on PC) aborts the WO without dispensing, and returns to the TAC making the same WO selection from there, then the TAC is jumping station selection step, going directly to dispense page (using the station selected earlier from PC).\nOn WO management the WO is still shown as assigned to all assigned station.\n\nPlease check the video @ https://www.dropbox.com/s/dpdl2g4hf58d0o9/20170214_095032.mp4?dl=0',1,2,6,1487065380,1578762546),(79,1,1,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'impossible to test JOBS: communication error','version T_2_30 (but same error on previous versions)\nall new firmware (TAC ==> 1.4)\n\nmanager creates a new job on PC, and assigns it to one or more technicians.\nThe tech goes to TAC, login to the system and chooses 3 ==> load job recipes\nhe finds the list of the jobs assigned to him, but when selects one job, the system always returns communication error 255',1,3,6,1487349613,1497442506),(80,1,1,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'\"load job recipes\" is a wrong title','version T_2_30\n\non TAC and on PC, 3rd choice is \"load job recipes\", while actually it\'s a selection.\nIn fact, after pressing relevant button, TAC is displaying \"select job\"\non PC, system is displaying \"load job recipes\" - checking previous discrepancies about TAC and PC that should work and display same things',1,2,6,1487349887,1493021193),(81,1,1,0,27,3,12,0,0,0,'downloading reports only in pdf format','T_2_30\n\ndiscrepancy #65 has been fixed, but unfortunately it\'s possible to download only a pdf file.\n\nfor csv or txt I have to export my own report from import/export configuration.\n\nIs it possible to ask to download a pdf or a csv file?',1,1,6,1487667986,1510851512),(82,1,1,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'correct logic for autoclosure and topoff quantity','this is not to be considered a bug.\n\nIt\'s the requested specification for the logic procedure of autoclose and topoff.\n\nIt is based on the experience and customers\' feedbacks we collected in last 12 months of installations and tests.\n\nPlease check attached pdf file &#40;configurations from A to D - WIP from E to H&#41;',1,2,6,1488560264,1510851539),(83,1,4,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'Fleet Mode','Fleet Mode Yes/No\n\nEnter:   Pin#\n            Equipment # / Work Order #\n            Select Product\n            Open/Preset \"Dispense capabilities\"\n            Use typical time outs\n            Equipment# / Work Order# may have multiple dispenses daily, log each transaction.\n            Manager can set up work orders with allowable products to dispense, the maximum dispense amount or preset amount.',1,1,5,1488980821,0),(84,1,0,0,6,3,1,0,0,0,'Adding a column and button to track work orders being invoiced','Recently have had multiple customers asking for this feature. They want to be able to stay in our system and know if a work order has been billed/invoiced. So after a dispense, and the customer is billed, the manager can go through mark work orders that have been billed. Then at the end of the day they can check against all of the work orders to make sure they were all billed out and also see if any work orders were not and find out why.\nI have attached a word document showing where we need to put this feature.',0,1,6,1489426284,1510850225),(85,1,1,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'probe signal different from 0 when probe in the air','R_2_17 (2016 firmware) and T_2_30 (new firmware)\n\nin admin and manager dashboard the tank looks to have a few liters instead of being completely empty, the probe has been tested in the air and in an empty tank, placed vertically or horizontally.\nIt always returns a signal not equal to 0',1,2,6,1489505277,1497445720),(86,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'possibility to assign 2 displays to same reel','this is a not-priority for the moment\n\nthink about possibility to add a second field in reel configuration for display assignment.\n\nThis is required for some of our installations, where we have 2 sides for the cabinet and a single display is not enough or cannot be placed in a conveninet place visible for both sides.\n\nI know this could be bypassed with miniremote displays, but 1) they\'re not ready again and 2) it will always depend to the cost of every single mini-remote display',0,1,6,1489505598,1578762787),(87,1,0,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'display shows a different amount','made a 2.4 liters dispense (around 20 and a few more pulses), system shows 2.4 liters everywhere (report, WO management, ...) ticket printed by the printer is showing 2.4 but remote displays shows 2.3!\n\nthis is not affected by the small k-factor (made in order to have big quantities with few pulses, to save time), because the displays must show the same quantity the system has measured',1,1,6,1489508476,1497446092),(88,1,0,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'time printed on the ticket is wrong','if I configure the system for Paris or Rome (+1), we have 6 hours of difference from system time and printed time\n\nif I configure the system for London (0), we have 5 hours of difference from system time and printed time\n\nif I configure the system for US Central time (-6), time is correct\n\nif I configure the system for Eastern US time (-5), we have 1 hour of difference',1,2,6,1489509931,1493021260),(89,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'time zone is not correctly working','In Italy and France is 17.25. Time zone is +1\n\nIf I change time zone switching to Londo (0), system is correctly changing time to 16.25 (warning, do you want to update time NOT selected)\n\nIf I switch to US Central time (-6), system time becomes 11.25 instead of 10.25\n\nIf I switch to Eastern US time (-5), system time becomes 12.25 instead of 11.25',1,1,6,1489510131,1489576161),(90,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'translations required','we need an updated translations file to translate all last thing modified.\nWe received a translation files in August, but it\'s not complete, we need the last full one\n\nin order to put translations on TAC and on PC',0,1,6,1489596509,1510851581),(91,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'requested logic for printer','customers requires printer to print a ticket every single time there is a transaction (dispense+relevant topoff)\n\nin this moment it prints only when the WO is closed, printing a summary of all transactions.\n\ncustomers require to have a ticket everytime a tech takes oil, with printed only the single transaction he made, without caring if it\'s the first, the second or the n_th time he is dispensing',0,1,6,1489596688,1510851627),(92,1,0,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'recent WO window','this window needs some modifications:\n\n- \"view details\" is totally useless, since we can\'t go here and make modification, so it\'s better to delete this option\n- the button \"hide closed/show closed\" now is only in \"view details\", but needs to be in te dashboard window (moreover when you delete view details possibility)\n- we need to show only max 50 recent WO, no more*, always\n\n*the 50 recent WO must be selected as follows:\n- if we have more than 50 WO after \"purging date\", then show only the last 50 (open + closed, always sorted as defined by date and time of creation)\n- if after purging date there are less than 50 WO (\"n\" WO), and if before purging date all WO have been closed, then show only \"n\" WO\n- if after purging date there are less than 50 WO (\"n\" WO), and if before purging date there are \"m\" still open WO, then show first \"n\" WO and then \"min( (50-n),m)\" still open WO.',0,1,6,1490094655,1501484127),(93,1,0,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'Work Order Maintenance','in the menu it\'s written \"Work Order Maintenance\", when you click on it, the page is called \"adjust Work Order\".\nOur opinion is to have same title of the menu, Work Order Maintenance is ok.',0,1,6,1490095509,1493033734),(94,1,0,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'Work Order Maintenance','in the columns titles, \"date\" and \"time\" are referring to \"creation date\" and \"creation time\", as it\'s in recent WO window in the dashboard.\nIt should be better to specify this also in WO maintenance',0,1,6,1490095629,1493033785),(95,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'Filter for Work Order Maintenance','in WO maintenance we need to have a filter, the same we have in \"WO status\" in reporting area:\n\n- filter by date (from, to)\n- filter by name (last name)\n- filter by product\n- filter by WO#\n\nname and product filter should have a dropdown menu which shows the possibilities you have during your typing (tyiping \"SIM\" it should show \"SIMONETTO\" and in case other names starting with \"SIM\", if typing \"5W\" and you have no oil starting with \"5W\" it should show nothing or \"no products found\")\n\nfor WO# filter, it\'s required to have a \"jolly\" digit to search: if you type \"12\" it should filter only the WO starting with \"12\" (1234, 1256, 1207957, 121, ....), if you type \"*12\" where \"*\" is the jolly digit it should filter also the WO with \"12\" in the middle or at the end of their number (341244, 11223, 34512, ....)',0,1,6,1490096245,1647449514),(96,1,0,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'showing WO','both in recent WO and in WO maintenance, if the WO is a multiproduct WO, system should show this as a single line for date, time, WO#, open/closed status, update/deleting button\n\ncheck attached picture\n\nmore or less is like in WO status report',0,1,6,1490096529,1493018213),(97,1,0,0,81,80,56,0,0,0,'station filter not working in WO management','T_2_31\n\nafter creating a WO only specifying the product, you enter to update the WO and the station filter is showing the full list of stations, while the product is only available in 2 of them.\nThis is similar to #58, but with station filter instead of product filter.\n\nWe made a video for your reference, link will follow as soon as it will be uploaded on dropbox',0,1,6,1490111493,1501484266),(98,1,1,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'impossible to dispense from 3rd station if user is assigned to multiple stations','T_2_31\nthis happened during tests today. We were able before to dispense from this station, but now it\'s impossible for unknown reasons...\n\nWe create a WO assigned to 3rd station, specifying product \"AdBlue\". Leaving \"all technicians\" or specifying a tech, if technician is assigned to 3rd station and other stations, we get communication error always, when selecting the WO. If we do this with Tech03 (assigned only to station 3), he can dispense.\n\nI called at Gartec, asking my colleague to make the same steps: he does not receive communication error and he can dispense as admin.\n\nWe tried to delete the reel and the full station, creating from scratch a NEW station with same reels\' configuration...problem still occurs.\n\nthis is the link for the full database of this system giving problem: https://www.dropbox.com/s/kjkqxk4mvmhj3h2/Complete_DB_Backup_03-21-2017-16-21-57.sql?dl=0\n\n\nhttps://www.dropbox.com/s/kjkqxk4mvmhj3h2/Complete_DB_Backup_03-21-2017-16-21-57.sql?dl=0',0,3,6,1490115575,1515572967),(99,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'reaching low level shutoff dispensing from TAC in open dispense','T_2_31\ntested with 2 different k-factors: 0.1 (quick simulation) and 1.0 (real)\n\nTEST: open dispense from TAC, starting tank level = few liters more than shutoff level (shutoff level = 11 liters)\ntech start the dispense, solenoid automatically closes when the oil level reaches shutoff level ==> ok\nbut in the dashboard the level shown is 11 liters and it\'s still in yellow/re-order level\nthis means that you can start another open dispense, but when you do this, system immediately stop the solenoid valve, with a dispensed quantity at 0. In the dashboard, the level is always the same in yellow, so you can start new dispenses but without being able to dispense a single drop.\nThis means that the system recognizes that we reached the shutoff level, so it stops all new dispenses; but at the same time it does not change the level in red/shutoff and gives the possibility to continue...\nAt the beginning we thought it was a matter of k-factor, because of the bad resolution due to very low k-factor; but this is happening in the same way also with a real k-factor (1.00), so it\'s a bug of the system\n\nREQUEST: once the system stops you the first time, the level must switch to red/shutoff level without allowing new dispenses.',0,3,6,1490259970,1578762822),(100,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'reaching low level shutoff dispensing from PC in open dispense','T_2_31\ntested with 2 different k-factors: 0.1 (quick simulation) and 1.0 (real)\n\nTEST: open dispense from PC virtual TAC, starting tank level = few liters more than shutoff level (shutoff level = 11 liters)\ntech start the dispense, solenoid does NOT close when the oil level reaches shutoff level ==> it\'s possible to pump oil until the pump is not sucking anymore, filling the whole pipeline of air ==> this means that later the whole pipeline must be purged from air, losing a lot of time as if the system was brandly new\n\nMoreover, if the max open dispense limit allows you to do it, it\'s possible to count a number of pulses equal to go under 0 in the tank.\ntest parameters:\n- starting tank level = 13 liters\n- shutoff level = 11 liters\n- open dispense = 15 liters measured\n- Tank level at the end of the test = 0 (correctly, not negative)\n- transaction reported in reports area = 15 liters\n\nThis means that the system allows the user to pump more than the quanityt necessary to go under the shutoff level, it allows you to continue to pump until the pump is no more able to suck the few quantity remaining in the tank and starts to pump air.\nThere is also the possibility (if the pipeline is not too long and quite \"linear\") that air is reaching the pulser module, making gears turn very quickly and measuring very big quantities (like tens or hundreds of liters). The system will report this anomalous transaction, even if the tank corectly will reach 0 and will not become negative\n\nREQUEST: check the logic for dispensing in this situation, in this particular case the logic for TAC is more correct (even if it\'s giving the problem of discrepancy #99): system must not allow the user to go under shutoff level.',0,3,6,1490260784,1578762929),(101,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'reaching low level shutoff dispensing from TAC or PC with preset','T_2_31\n\nTEST#1: preset on TAC\nstarting condition = 15 liters\nshutoff level = 11 liters\npreset = 7 liters\nsystem allowed me to start the dispense with a preset that is greater than the max quantity I should be able to preset (current_quantity - shutoff quantity)\nAfter reaching the shutoff level, system automatically stops the solenoid. We have obviously same situation of discrepancy #99, since the system is still in re-order level and not in shutoff.\n\nTEST#2: preset from PC\nstarting condition = 16 liters\nshutoff level = 11 liters\npreset = 6 liters\nsystem allowed me to start the dispense and does not stops the solenoid once we reach the shutoff level. Same situation of discrepancy #100',0,3,6,1490261683,1578762700),(102,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'email scheduler - little mistyping and confusion with high levels','email schedule time ==> there is \"High Level Alaram\" instead of \"High Level Alarm\"\n\nin header titles in email scheduler window, \"High Level Alarm\" is ok, but \"High Level Warning\" is missing \"warning\" and could create a little confusion',0,1,6,1490262711,1510851816),(103,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'System Language & Time / Date Format','Date Format will not change  from  DD-MM-YY to  MM-DD-YY',0,1,6,1490361784,1490376047),(104,1,1,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'action journal - \"purge closed WO\" setting is affecting the results','T_2_31\n\nif the report is downloaded or sent by email with bottom \"send by email\" button, the report is listing only the actions made after purge date.\nIf the results on the browser are filtered by date, this is not happening.\nIn the email sent by email scheduler we can find the full list (from the first action registered).\n\nthe purge should affect only WO list in manager dashboard, the actions made on the system should be completely indepentent',1,1,6,1490599288,1510851857),(105,1,1,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'action journal - number of actions shown in the list','T_2_31\n\nWith current version, the report is listing only last 50 actions. If I filter by date, I can recover previous actions.\n\nWe need a switch on this window to choose if we want to see last 50 actions or all actions.\nIf the switch is set on “last 50” and we filter by date, if there are more than 50 actions in this time range system should show only the last 50 of this time range. If there are less, just show these actions.\n\nThis type of switch should be applied to all reports.',1,1,6,1490599626,1578762945),(106,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'action journal - pdf file title (sent by email)','T_2_31\nfile sent by email, both using \"send by email\" button or email scheduler.\n\nThe report sent by email is named “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM oilcop LOCATION Oilcop Action Journal Report.pdf”\n\n- The date is correct, but time is shifted of 1 hour (correct time 13.57, title time 12.57). It\'s using Windows time, not controller\'s time (tested by changing time zone on the controller, time reported is 1 hour earlier than my computer (Windows) time.\n- “oilcop LOCATION” in the middle of the title is useless as it’s been copied 2 times.\n\nCorrect title: “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM Oilcop Action Journal Report.pdf”\nwith the date and time of the system, or in case it\'s possible to use Windows time, the correct time including time zone and DST',1,1,6,1490600156,1510851897),(107,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'action journal - pdf file title (downloaded)','T_2_31\n\nThe report downloaded is called “oilcop_Action Journal Report-1.pdf”\nIt’s required that it has the same title made for the report sent by email: “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM Oilcop Action Journal Report.pdf”',1,1,6,1490600248,1510851922),(108,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'action journal - pdf file information','T_2_31\n\nIn the file, we can find only “Action Journal”\n\nIt’s required to have in the header of the page the LACATION, the date and the time; in the footer the number of the page out of the total number of pages.\nTitle in the page can stay Action Journal.\nIf data are filtered by date, please explicit the dates (check example pdf)',1,1,6,1490600911,1510852090),(109,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'report sent by email scheduler - picture','T_2_31\n\nThe picture in the email is Liquidynamics logo, while in the email sent with the \"send by email\" button the picture is the login/email file uploaded from admin options.\nThis last is the correct one that should replace Liquidynamics logo also in emails sent automatically by email scheduler',1,1,6,1490604313,1510852114),(110,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'report sent by email scheduler - mail address','T_2_31\n\nemail address appearing in email sent by the system is \"OILCOP.com\" oilcop@liquidynamics.com\n\nwe created  a new address oilcop@gartec.it that should be used in this case.\nIf you need password for the account and all configuration details (servers, ports,...) we obviously can provide them',1,1,6,1490605091,1510852051),(111,1,1,0,39,3,24,0,0,0,'Printer options','Would like the ability to use a network printer or the Transaction Printer TRP',1,1,6,1490624897,1510850370),(112,1,1,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'action journal - reported actions','T_2_31\n\nwe made various actions on the system and check the reported actions.\n\nplease check the attached file to see all details, problems, requests',1,1,6,1490625861,1578762753),(113,1,1,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'action journal - filters','T_2_31\n\nfiltering date and names is ok\n\nbut for name filtering, we need a reaserch field with a sort of dropdown menu which is automatically suggesting the results of your search (you can type the first letter and automatically a dropdown menu appears with the possible results - similar to Google research)',1,1,6,1490626877,1515574735),(114,1,1,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'action journal - not reported actions','T_2_31\n\nin action journal, some actions are not reported, but it could be great to have them: the most important is to have a reported line everytime there is a modification of the WO (re-opened, modified - switching product, changing user,...) and overall if it\'s deleted',1,1,6,1490627134,1578762730),(115,8,0,0,39,0,24,72,0,0,'Email Reports from demo site','Would like to be able to setup email schedule for reports for myself and or other customers',1,1,5,1490628833,0),(116,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'transaction journal - new columns required','T_2_31\n\nThere is the need to distinguish between dispense and topoff, so a new column is required to indicate if the reported line and quantity is a dispense or a topoff (transaction = dispense + relevant topoff).\n\nIf the odometer switch has been activated, a new column must be added to this report, since at the moment you can enter (TAC or PC) the odometer but then it does not appear anywhere.',1,1,6,1490629543,1647460179),(117,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'transaction journal - filters','T_2_31\n\nFiltering date and names is ok\n\nbut for name filtering (as in action journal), we need a reaserch field with a sort of dropdown menu which is automatically suggesting the results of your search (you can type the first letter and automatically a dropdown menu appears with the possible results - similar to Google research)\n\nA new filter is required (made as for names with dropdown showing results of the research) for the product.\n\nIn the WO filter, make same thing asked for WO maintenance (jolly digit for research) - discrepancy #95',1,1,6,1490686465,1515574985),(118,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'transaction journal - number of transactions shown in the list','T_2_31\n\nWith current version, the report is listing only last 50 transactions. If I filter by date, I can recover previous transactions.\n\nWe need a switch on this window to choose if we want to see last 50 transactions or all of them, starting from the very first one.\nIf the switch is set on “last 50” and we filter by date, if there are more than 50 transactionsin this time range system should show only the last 50 of this time range. If there are less, just show these transactions.\n\nThis type of switch should be applied to all reports.',1,1,6,1490686625,1578763380),(119,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'transaction journal - pdf file title (sent by email)','T_2_31\nfile sent by email, both using \"send by email\" button or email scheduler.\n\nThe report sent by email is named “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM oilcop LOCATION Oilcop Transaction Journal Report.pdf”\n\n- The date is correct, but time is shifted of 1 hour (correct time 13.57, title time 12.57). It\'s using Windows time, not controller\'s time (tested by changing time zone on the controller, time reported is 1 hour earlier than my computer (Windows) time.\n- “oilcop LOCATION” in the middle of the title is useless as it’s been copied 2 times.\n\nCorrect title: “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM Oilcop Transaction Journal Report.pdf”\nwith the date and time of the system or, in case it\'s possible to use Windows time, the correct time including time zone and DST',1,1,6,1490688476,1510852071),(120,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'transaction journal - download pdf','T_2_31\n\nThe report is not downloaded as per Action Journal, it opens (with Firefox) 2 tabs and the popup window for opening or saving is not showing a pdf file but an unknown file.\nYou need to save, change the extension and then you can open.\nSince it’s working good on Action Journal, it\'s not a problem due to Firefox but of the Oilcop software itself (even if with Chrome is working better).',1,1,6,1490688708,1510852139),(121,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'transaction journal - pdf file title (downloaded)','T_2_31\n\nThe report downloaded with Firefox is called “oilcop_Transaction.pdf”\nThe report downloaded with Chrome is called “oilcop_Transaction journal report.pdf”\n\n==> the name is \"created\" in a different way comparing it to Action Journal..\n\nIt’s required that it has the same title made for the report sent by email: “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM Oilcop Transaction Journal Report.pdf”\nand it\'s important the name is always the same not depending from the browser you\'re using',1,1,6,1490688913,1510852027),(122,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'transaction journal - pdf file information','T_2_31\n\nIn the file, we can find only “Transaction Journal”\n\nIt’s required to have in the header of the page the LACATION, the date and the time; in the footer the number of the page out of the total number of pages.\nTitle in the page can stay Transaction Journal.\n\nPlease refer to attachement of discrepancy #108 to view the layout of the page',1,1,6,1490689046,1510852009),(123,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'WO status - job are not distinguished from other WO#','T_2_31\n\nin WO status report, differently from WO management and from manager dashboard, there is no \"J-\" before jobs',1,1,6,1490690411,1510852161),(124,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'transaction journal - jobs are not distinguished from other WO#','T_2_31\n\nsame of discrepancy #123, but in transaction journal',1,1,6,1490692590,1510852181),(125,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'WO status - \"purge closed WO\" setting is affecting the results','T_2_31\n\nThe report should not be affected by the purge, since it’s a feature created only for the WO management, in order not to have all WO starting from the first one (maybe years!) in the dashboard and in WO management.\nIn the report area, you need to have the possibility to see everything, and in case you can filter',1,1,6,1490692780,1510851943),(126,1,0,0,81,399,56,0,0,0,'WO status - odometer','T_2_31\n\nIf the odometer switch has been activated, the user can enter (TAC or PC) the odometer value for the vehicle, but then this value does not appear anywhere!\na new column must be added to WO status report (if odometer switch is ON, otherwise do not show this column)',1,2,6,1490697242,1630524869),(127,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'WO status - filters','T_2_31\n\nAdd the dropdown research logic (see discrepancies #117 and #113) to name and product filter\n\nfilter for product: \"product\" is enough instead of \"product name\"\n\nWO# filter: make same thing asked for WO maintenance (jolly digit for research) - see discrepancy #95 and #117',1,1,6,1490697512,1578763594),(128,1,1,0,27,3,12,0,0,0,'some transaction is not reported','R_2_17 (downgraded from R_2_19)\n\nApparently the system is not reporting all transactions: if you check the last WO# open today (fluid = coolant), you won\'t find any transaction and in WO status you can\'t find it, as it\'s not delivered yet.\nBut technician is saying that he delivered around 6 liters of this fluid...is it possible to check if the system counted some pulses but did not report any transaction? I\'m remembering now that with one old version the transaction were updated after some time, maybe because they were updated with the wrong time (delay because of time zone or something like that...) One other thing, sometimes the report is saying transaction = 0, but actually they dispensed some liter.\nThey are saying is happening quite a lot in last 2 weeks.\nI checked, there are 5 transactions in last week with 0 in dispensed quantity. For WO status, I checked 1 WO@ and it looks like the topoff is to 0, but the first dispense was positive.\nI did not check more deeply because it was kicking me out continuously.',1,2,6,1490716319,1510851390),(129,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'WO status - number of WO shown in the list','T_2_31\n\nTo continue the requested philosophy of other reports, it should show last 50 WO (last 50 closed + last 50 still open).\nWe need a switch on this window to choose if we want to see last 50 WO or all WO.\nIf you want to filter by date, filtering logic should be always the same for all reports (if last 50 is selected, max only 50 results, if all is selected, all the results contained in the filtered range).',1,1,6,1490774722,1515575313),(130,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'WO status - pdf file title (downloaded)','T_2_31\n\nhe report downloaded with Firefox is called “oilcop_Workorder.pdf”\nThe report downloaded with Chrome is called “oilcop_Workorder Status report.pdf”\n\nIt’s required that it has the same title made for the report sent by email: “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM Oilcop Work Order Status Report.pdf”\nand it\'s important the name is always the same not depending from the browser you\'re using',1,1,6,1490776077,1510852205),(131,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'WO status - pdf file title (sent by email)','T_2_31\nfile sent by email, both using \"send by email\" button or email scheduler.\n\nThe report sent by email is called “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM oilcop LOCATION Oilcop Work Order Status Report.pdf”\n\nThe date is correct, but time is shifted of 1 hour (correct time 13.57, title time 12.57)\n“oilcop LOCATION” in the middle of the title is useless as it’s been copied 2 times.\n\nCorrect title “LOCATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMM Oilcop Work Order Status Report.pdf”\nwith the date and time of the system or, in case it\'s possible to use Windows time, the correct time including time zone and DST',1,1,6,1490776220,1510852257),(132,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'all reports - special digits in email objects','T_2_31\n\nplease check that special digits (for the most part, letters with accents) are all correctly reported in email objects (when language is not English)\nthis is very important for all customers',1,1,6,1490776780,1510852234),(133,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'all reports - special digits in pdf files names','T_2_31\n\nplease check that special digits (for the most part, letters with accents) are all correctly reported in pdf files names (for translated reports)\nthis is very important for all customers',1,1,6,1490776882,1510852278),(134,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'all reports - special digits in pdf file text','T_2_31\n\nplease check that special digits (for the most part, letters with accents) are all correctly reported in the whole text of pdf file &#40;for translated reports&#41;\nthis is very important for all customers',1,1,6,1490777675,1510852295),(135,1,0,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'WO status  - pdf file information','T_2_31\n\nIn the file, we can find only “Work Order Status”\n\nIt’s required to have in the header of the page the LACATION, the date and the time; in the footer the number of the page out of the total number of pages.\nTitle in the page can stay Work Order Status.\n\nPlease refer to attachement of discrepancy #108 to view the layout of the page',1,1,6,1490778265,1510852326),(136,1,0,0,81,81,56,102,0,84,'impossible to login with old controller','controller: old version 1 (orange/black)\nsystem installed more or less 2 years ago\nwe can\'t check, but it could be version R_2_14\n\nsystem worked correctly until last week\n\nthe system, concerning TACs, is now still working with no problems: techs can login on TAC, load a WO and dispense.\nBut since a few days, users (admin/managers) cannot login anymore into the system from PC:\n- they reach the login page and type PIN\n- the browsers (it happens with Chrome or Firefox, the same) are saying that the network is not a safe network\n- it appears a blank page, no dashboard\n- they cannot see anything else\n\nFirstly we thought to an issue of their LAN, maybe with some new firewalls or something...but we made the IT guy testing to login connecting directly to support LAN with a laptop: same result, not safe network and blank page.\n\ncould you please give us a possible solution?\n- or connecting via winscp\n- or replacing the controller with a new one',1,3,6,1490865904,1515575402),(137,1,0,0,81,81,56,0,0,0,'WO status - emails\' object','T_2_31\n\nThe 2 emails received by email scheduler and by sending with send button have 2 different objects.\nThey have to be the same\n\nTo be checked for all other reports',1,1,6,1490866196,1515575574),(138,1,1,0,6,0,1,38,0,26,'Work orders being attached to technician after dispense.','This is not a discrepancy but more discussion for future release. At this customers site they ran into an issue where they needed a technician to dispense, a day later, from an already created WO that had already had a dispense performed on it by a different technician. So on day 1, technician A dispensed on WO #1234. In the system that WO now became attached to technician A. So on day 2 when technician B needed to dispense from that work order, it was not available in \"Select Work Order\" when he logged in. The only way to get technician B to be able to use that work order now is if a Manager/Admin go into \"Work Order Maintenance\" and change the \"Operator\" for that WO from technician A to technician B or \"All Technicians\". \nThis is an issue that has not come up before but we want to explore possible options to prevent this issue in the future. Any Ideas you have please share on here for future reference.',1,1,5,1490988063,0),(139,1,4,0,80,80,56,0,0,0,'Listing Errors','Hello everyone,\n\nHave you got please a table that includes all numbers and error messages on TAC.\n\nThanks\n\nSébastien',0,1,6,1491293032,1493033386),(140,1,4,0,80,80,56,0,0,0,'On the software TAC IS  OFF while it communicates','Good evening,\nInstalled T_2_32 and V1.5 on TAC\n\nWarning then that the TAC is properly connected and works so it must be ON in the configuration of the components and in the menu it must be in green.\n\nIn the system menu of the components the TAC is OFF and in the menu the color is Red.',1,1,6,1491765228,1493033243),(141,1,1,0,3,0,1,8,0,0,'Multiple preset dosing amounts within job number. Used to service Bull Dozers and Track Hoe tracks','When servicing tracks one can have as many as 4 - 12 gear boxes that each needs to be filled with a small amount i.e. 2 pints. \nCustomer would like to have a job that allows them to set a preset value and the number of times a preset value can be dispensed from a work order. \nThe mechanic would select or load a Work Order with the designated Job# that has product name, preset amount and the number of preset dispense operations allowed for the job.\nJob # = input XX preset amount, input XX number of times to allow the preset amount to be dispensed. \nIn Admin options input XX Multi Dispense Timeout, this establishes how much time will elapse after the preset value is obtained, before allowing the dispense complete time out begin to counting down, when dispense complete time has elapse display returns to Mechanics home page \"Select/Load Work Order or Job #\".\nThe multi dispense timeout count down is to give the mechanic time re-position himself to perform the next preset dispense. If the Mechanic has completed the WO he needs to press Dispense complete to close the work order, otherwise he can perform additional dispense operations assigned to the WO by the manager or until the work order is closed by the Mechanic.',1,1,5,1491942082,0),(142,1,1,0,80,0,56,0,0,0,'Technician cannot select the station','with T_33\nConfiguration (AUTOCLOSE ON or OFF, multiproduct = OFF, multidispense = ON)\nTech load the WO for dispense antifreeze (present on the 3 stations) : first dispense ( on first Station Express Service ) OK\nNow, Tech select the WO : Ok But do not ask on which station to go for antifreeze (1,2 or 3)\nIt\'s a new dispense (multidispens = ON). the Tech must be able to choose the station.\n\nI try to modified the WO in menu \"WO maintenance\" to change station \"all assigned stations\" : same problem It selects the station already used',1,1,5,1492508975,0),(143,1,4,0,80,81,56,0,0,0,'technician can take another product to another station on TAC','Configuration : Autoclose = ON or OFF, Multiproducts = OFF, multidispense = ON)\nThe manager creates WO in PC : 75W90 (product only second station, all technicians, all assigned stations, 6l on preset locked)\n\nif login with Tech01 (Tech01 only assigned station 1) He can to choose the WO (Bug for me) and he can to choose the products in first station : 10W40, 0W30, antifreeze... on open dispense.\nAfter to have test in PC, (works more correctly, just for me if tech01 log this WO don\'t be available)\nThe bug is different\nre log tech01 on TAC : select WO : now arrived directly 75w90 open dispense !!!\nPlease check this configuration.\nThanks',1,1,6,1492512081,1515576340),(144,1,0,0,80,3,56,0,0,0,'Transaction Report files different to schulder email and dowload file','today 12:37\n\ncalendar I demand to sent transaction report by email at 13:30\n\nI receive the email at 12:30\n\nmy last test is at 11:56 \n18/04/2017 11:56 Test TECH00 Technicien 041804 0W30 EXPRESS SERVICE #12 5 L\n\nThe file received gives it\n18/04/17 12:56 Test TECH00 Technicien 041804 0W30 EXPRESS SERVICE #12 5 L\n\nincomprehensible !!\n\nPlease check 2 files ( receive by calendar et download directly)\n\nThanks',0,1,6,1492513292,1510851989),(145,1,0,0,80,3,56,0,0,0,'Name of product in Alert email (Re-order, shut off, high level warning, high level alarm','Can you add please the product name for the alerts Re-order, shut off, high level warning, high level alarm sent by email\n\nThanks',0,1,6,1492520260,1510852733),(146,1,4,0,144,3,1,0,0,0,'Job Recipe Issue when 2 or more of the same product/tank is on the same station','Job was setup to select a certain product (Product 1).\nStation 1 has multiple reels configured with that Product 1\nWhen the user selects the job recipe for Product 1 and gets to the reel selection, the options for selecting the reels are all 000, so the user is unable to select a reel.\nThis occured when the Product 1 came from the same tank.\n\nWas able to fix the issue and will release it as LQD_T_2_35.\nTeam is currently checking to see if this problem occurs with different configurations for select and load work orders.\n\nThank you.',1,2,6,1492618286,1510852367),(147,1,0,0,80,81,56,0,0,0,'Zigbee problem','When the CTR restarts (following reboot or power failure)\nThe CDM recognizes well the FCM (green button) by cons cannot recognize the TAC. We must electrically disconnect and reconnect the TAC to recognize.\n\nIt\'s a real problem because if the customer reboot their CTR must disconnect and reconnect the TAC otherwise COMMUNICATION ERROR 255 !!',2,1,6,1492700007,1515576719),(148,1,0,0,80,399,56,0,0,0,'Technican Unknown on Printer','Hello,\n\nVersion T_2_39\nTest with multiproduct ON.\nCreat to PC WO with 3 products\nPrinter ON\nLog \"Test Manager\"\nSelect and dispense first product\nPrint : Ok but not reconyze Technician : \"T.Unknow\"\nTry a new dispense first product : same\nSelect and dispense seconde product\nPrint : Ok and now Technician reconized : \"T.Manager\"\nCan you please modified this situation.\nWith configuration Multiproduct OFF : no problem to technician reconizing.\nPicture file attached\nThanks',0,1,6,1495193869,1666799126),(149,1,1,0,144,3,1,0,0,0,'Load Work Order Causing Communication Error','Test version T_2_39, last firmware for TAC.\nIf I switch off multiproduct, user can go to TAC and load a WO. If the switch is ON, user goes to TAC, selects “load WO” but when he presses enter for loading the WO, system returns communication error.\n\nWas unable to recreate on a different system, so it may be a setting issue. Currently requesting database where the error is occuring.',1,3,6,1495713659,1510850424),(150,1,0,0,3,3,1,113,0,95,'Pantronics, Customer installed new TAC, same problem 255 communication error','Byran,\n\nThis is the system we remoted into last week, they are having the same problem after we installed the new TAC.\nThe customer is very frustrated he is giving us a couple of days to resolve this before he request us to remove the system..\n\nOn another note maybe related We are also having communication issues with a tank monitoring system at a Minnesota car dealer ship, Angel is familiar with this issue as he remoted into last week. The dealership is getting upset because this has not worked since the system was installed three months ago.\nI am beginning to become concerned because we are getting an reputation that our system is very problematic to install, our customers don\'t have the time to help us fix their new systems..',0,3,6,1496929768,1497449707),(151,1,1,0,81,81,56,112,0,0,'autoclose not working when you make the topoff','version R_21\nTAC 1.5\nscenario 1 (WO created by manager with specified product and preset)\nautoclose ON, multiproduct OFF, multidispense ON\n\nwhen selecting the WO from TAC, if you choose to make topoff, the autoclose is not working: the WO stays open.\nIf you choose not to make topoff, it works and the WO is closed.\n\nDispensing from PC, it works.',1,1,6,1497428050,1515578367),(152,1,4,0,3,3,1,113,0,95,'Pantronics called wanting to know what does error code 9 mean.','Logged into the system everything appears to be working.\n\nDo we have a list of error codes?',1,1,6,1497531409,1499344843),(153,1,4,0,3,0,1,8,0,3,'Emergency Stop button Does not work on TAC','When pressing the E Stop button will not stop dispensing.',1,1,3,1497892731,0),(154,1,1,0,27,3,12,143,0,121,'not possible to select reel if there are 10 or more reels in the station','TOP URGENT!!! \n\nR_2_21\nTAC firmware 1.5 (hex file TAC_3_0_3)\n\nif there are 10 or more reels in one station (station X), when you try to select or load a WO and you select the station X, then you are not able to select the reel: you can try to push 0+# or 0+#+ENTER but the screen never moves on...\n\ntested with 9 reels, it works (only pushing # because it automatically knows there are less than 10 reels so one single digit and it works correctly\ntested with 10, 11, 12 reels, same result: no possibility to go ahead and dispense.\ntested both on customer site and on testing controller (in version R_2_21)\n\nthis was working 100% (this customer is working with multiproduct and multidispense, loading the WO from the TAC) on old version R_2_17 + TAC firmware 1.2',1,3,6,1498574873,1510850112),(155,1,1,0,3,0,1,8,0,3,'Index number of records in the Jobs records / importing from .csv file','For customers would have a fleet vehicles that would like to track the fluid dispensed in to vehicles by vehicle number.\nWould it be difficult to index jobs data base to automatically populate the job number field 0- 999?\nand/or import a .csv file with two maybe three fields  (Field number, alpha/numeric, alpha/numeric)',0,1,3,1498827813,0),(156,1,1,0,39,3,24,72,0,53,'Transaction history screen','Headers do not display correctly in the tank adjustment screen. See attached pic',1,1,6,1499111620,1510850049),(157,1,1,0,3,3,1,77,0,56,'Intermittent radio communications issue with FCM 6 and 7','Customer says FCM 7 looses radio communications intermittently since the installation. \nChecked system communications when arrived in the AM every thing OK.\nUpdated system to version R21, encountered issues with navigating around the controller browser connection spins taking a couple of minutes to change pages.\nBryan check out the controller attempted to install TeamViewer unsuccessful fore some reason the controller is not allowing team viewer to be installed.\nInstalled controller at the motor pool, FCM 7 would not connect, relocated the range extender from North Wall to middle of shop high on concrete pillar. FCM reconnected and desk top indicated 3 bars radio strength.\nReceived a call in the afternoon, FCM was down. Arrived at location 8:00A the next day everything had 3 bars and FCM 7 worked properly.\nRelocated Range Extender to the South east corner about 10 \' high, FCM 6 then went off line. Noticed location of the range extender did not have line of site with FCM 6. Relocated range extender to about 17\' high and west 3\', allowing the Range Extender to have line of site with FCM 6 and 7.\nEverything is now showing 3 bars for exception of FCM 2 in the South Shop its displaying 2 bars.\nTurned on Sync with OilCop support.',1,1,6,1500044148,1500565757),(158,1,1,0,3,399,1,32,0,22,'IT department says ports 80 and 8080 are open however System status indicates system offline','According to Benjamin Newton 316-315-1118 bnewton@isgtech.com he was able to \"ping out using ports 80\" not sure if that is the same thing as ports open.\nISG Tech IT service company who maintains the ParrieLand Partners wide area network.\nIs there any other questions i should ask?\nUpdated their system last week, turned on sync with Oilcopsupport.com and Synchronized Data Base. Would it make since for us to send confirmation/acknowledgement from ocsupport.com on the controller?',0,1,6,1500557782,1666799324),(159,1,5,0,3,3,1,8,0,0,'Modify the TMM to retain High Level Shutoff and High Level Warning amounts in the TMM.','In the event of a communication error the TMM will know what value to energize a relay that is programmed to activate when High Level Shutoff and High level Warning is activated.\nIf not that difficult maybe also store the Re-Order and Low level shut off values, this will also apply to the 4 input/output relay module when we develop.',0,1,6,1500987546,1510850002),(160,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Administrative Options/ Company Name','After changing Company Name a couple times, > / < symbols begin to appear.\n(Walser Wichita) Originally entered \"Walser BMW/MINI Tank Inventory System\", changed the color of font a couple of times now the only thing that can be displayed is \"Walser BMW/MINI <\"',0,1,6,1501593295,1666799352),(161,8,0,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'Restore from OilCopsupport.com data base','Would be a nice option to add someday..',0,1,5,1501593368,0),(162,1,5,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'TMM, FCM, TAC PCB LEDs not functioning properly','Have had a few questions about the Error light illuminated on the TAC, FCM and TMM.\n\nTMM Error light is continuously illuminated, Radio Link LED 6 dose not light when the radio is connected, Sensor Connected lights will not light when the probes are connected. Relay light seem to work properly.\n\nFCM RS 485-1 and RS 485- 2 LED not Illuminating: Would it be possible for RS 485 lights to illuminate when ever the RS 485 circuit is connected. This will help trouble shooting a wired RS 485 communication fault by starting at the first modal closing the end of line switch and light should illuminate open switch, move to next device close switch and light should illuminate unless something is faulty with the PCB?? \n\nTAC Error light continuously illuminated.',0,1,5,1501624468,0),(163,1,7,0,80,3,56,0,0,0,'RANGE EXTENDER NOT RECONIZE BY SCANNING','On Lqd_R_2_21\nRange Extender not reconize by scanning. add We must add it manually',2,1,6,1501685025,1578763994),(164,1,1,0,49,49,32,0,0,22,'Power failure','The tank module has no power to it. The cord has power, but no lights are on at module.',2,3,6,1501881085,1503609946),(165,1,5,0,3,3,1,38,0,26,'Tank air solenoids will not open after facility lost power for 15 minutes.','between 7:15 and 8:00 am the entire facility lost power for approximately 15 minutes.\nAppears one 6 qt. dispense occurred just before the outage, however after the outage  they tried to dispense 10 times would not dispense. \nThey contacted me, able to log in everything looked OK noted the transactions before and after the outage.\nHad them check out the TMM the relay lights would not light up when trying to pump, it appeared to be working correectly from from the mgr. desktop Station 6 turned green.\nHad them power cycle the TMMs, appears that resolved the issue the relays will now open when turned on.\nThis location has the controller connected to a UPS..',0,1,6,1501951303,1578762348),(166,1,1,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Billed/Invoice button','Have had several request to add a \"Billed or Invoiced\" button next to work order in the Mangers desktop so they click the button to indicate they added it to the customers bill.',0,1,6,1502459537,1510849305),(167,1,1,0,3,3,1,155,0,134,'(Duplicate - 1) display error.  /index.php/admin/station/reel_station_configuration','When two FCM’s are configured as three stations (see below), the reel numbers for station 2 will both indicate Reel 4.\nWhen changing the User Defined Name to 1 and 2 respectively  (Duplicate – 1) will appear next to the reassigned reel number. When deleting the User Defined Name, top Reel (FCM-1) reverts back to display 4, then deleting the User Defined Name, bottom Reel (FCM-2) reverts back to display 4 and continues to display “(Duplicate – 1)”. \nWhen testing the dispense operation everything appeared to function normally..\n\nStation 1\nFCM-1 (Inputs 1,2,3)\n\nStation 2\nFCM-1 (input 4)\nFCM-2 (input 4)\n\nStaion 3\nFCM-2 (inputs 1,2,3)',0,1,6,1502813198,1510849262),(168,1,0,0,3,3,1,32,0,22,'Volume dispensed continues to increase after dispensing handle is closed','This is a wireless installation with 6 stations.\nPrimarily happens on Station 3, Product #2\nThe example he gave was the mechanic dispensed 20.3 quarts then retracted the reel, walked back to his laptop and observed the amount increment up to 23.4 quarts.\nI will be going up there in a week or so to install 2ea. 10\' probes at that time will get TV working and check to see if there are any problematic wire connections at the PSM',0,1,6,1503669456,1578764105),(169,1,1,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'System does not produce any delivery reports and customer would like to be able to export .csv','Attached is an example of two spreadsheets that I would like to populate through the data provided by the remote tank monitoring system. \nThe first tab is a time series inventory of all the tanks in one spreadsheet. I picked a 30 minute time interval, but it would be great to have the ability to change the time interval so that we could make it shorter and longer based on the need at that time. \nThe second tab is an individual tank time series. It’s essentially the same thing as the first tab, but is only for one tank. \nThis information should be available as line graph and tabular data for exporting.\n\nWithout this type of information, the system isn’t nearly as valuable to us. \nIt loses its ability to be an audit tool in our production and inventory management work streams.',0,1,6,1503930844,1510849337),(170,1,1,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Manager dispense option','From the Managers desktop under the Stations window add a “Dispense” button between Reels and Product for each reel at each station.\n\nPressing “Dispense” will invoke the dispense page allowing the manager to press Start for an open dispense or press Preset to enter a new preset value. \n(The Preset value from the previous preset operation is recalled in the preset window, Manager can click in the window to change the preset value or press the Start button to accept the previous preset value and begin the dispense operation).\n\nAfter pressing the Start button, manager has the option to either observe the dispense or close the dispense page and select a Dispense button for a different station to start another dispense. (Able to select a reel from the same station/FCM would be nice especially if an FCM is spilt in to more than one station).\n\nAnytime a manager performs a Dispense, the transaction is logged in the transaction journal along with the managers name and a some sort of number that is automatically assigned in the work order number in the WO/Job field .\n\nDispense timeouts function as they do now. \n\nAllow system to also function with work orders as it does now .',1,1,6,1506190682,1578764073),(171,1,1,0,3,3,1,59,0,42,'Sensor 4 error ?','Jason Mitchell is having some issues with the oil cop system where we log in to a reel and select a preset and when we hit dispense it says it can’t communicate and the pump will not start.  Usually if close out and try again the system will work.\nToday we had this happen again and I went back there and noticed the light comes on the FCM and says Sensor 4 error.\nI tried all 4 reels on that FCM and even though they all work, this light comes on only when I select reel 4.  I was just curious what that indicator light means if this is something I need to address.\n\nAny ideas?',0,2,6,1506356117,1510245255),(172,1,0,0,3,3,1,164,0,142,'Radio communications','FCM 4 is off line',0,1,6,1510060591,1510849368),(173,1,0,0,3,3,1,151,0,130,'Tank monitor appeared to stop updating the web tank icon values.','Refreshed web page could not get the web tank values to change.\nChanged product specific gravity values, no change in symptom.\nPower cycled CTR seem to fix issue updated specific gravity values to match tank level in Inches.',1,1,6,1510191399,1510849430),(174,1,0,0,3,3,1,164,0,142,'Tank Monitor delivery report not working','They added 110 gallons to the 0W/20 tank and the monitor did not indicate a delivery was made.',0,1,6,1510245492,1515174424),(175,1,3,0,26,26,11,163,0,141,'FCM not counting pulses of pulse meter','Reel 2(FCM 1 Port 2), Reel 7( FCM 2 Port 3) and Reel 8( FCM 2 Port 4) are not metering at all.  As oil pumps through the meter the dispense page reads \"0.0\" the entire time.  The pulse meter on reel 2 was rewired temporarily to port 4 which then properly counted.  This demonstrates the pulse meter and wiring are not at fault but the software or hardware on the FCM.',0,1,6,1510280880,1521744883),(176,1,0,0,3,399,1,164,0,142,'Not receiving email updates or notifications','Customer has indicated they have not received any reports or notifications.\nAdd myself to receive email reports and notifications, have not received any.',0,1,6,1510420029,1666799434),(177,3,0,0,3,3,1,158,0,136,'Can not view Tank Monitor Reports from the Web site.','Can not view Tank Monitor Reports from the Web site.',0,1,6,1510420326,1515174272),(178,1,1,0,3,3,1,150,0,128,'Update T_2_37 Error: File not found','Began incrementally updating the system from T_2_33, after successful installation of T_2_36, downloaded T_2_37 after downloading update Error: File Not Found.\nShould we download and install T_2_38 ?',1,1,6,1510839896,1510842186),(179,8,0,0,80,80,56,0,0,0,'MAC Adress','Hello,\nin oilcopsupport\nI deleted a customer without deleting before the system. When I want to give back the MAC address. it already exists\nCan you please delete the MAC address\n00: e0: b4: 54: 6b: 1d\n\nThanks\nSébastien',1,1,6,1511260644,1511474755),(180,1,0,0,3,3,1,164,0,142,'Station 8 stays on, Reel 1, Prod 0W/20 will not reset','Reviewing Mgr./Work Order Maintenance    11/22/2017 WO 20122 product 0W/20  disp. 5 and is still open.\nIs the reel on and can not be reset due the work order not closed?',1,1,6,1511716858,1578764171),(181,1,1,0,3,3,1,38,0,26,'Tank History Report not working','Tank Adjustments appears to be working correctly however the Tank History report is blank.\n\nTank history report turned on. Start time 12:00AM Stop Time 12:00AM set.',1,1,6,1512144491,1578764200),(182,1,5,0,3,3,1,151,0,130,'Tank monitor modules are not communicating, not updating.','Tank monitor 1 and 2 device status is alternating from Red to Green without updating the dashboard.',0,1,6,1512747053,1529065707),(183,1,1,0,3,220,1,0,0,141,'Customer can not log into his account and see tank and transaction information','Paul@universalmitsubishi.com \nPW:   OilCop',1,1,6,1512770588,1513276901),(184,1,1,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Tank Adjustments & Tank Inventory Reports not updating','Checked 12/Start 11/Stop time \nDelivery report timeout set for 5 min.\nPlacing cursor over tank icon appears level values are updating.',0,1,6,1513084520,1515174852),(185,1,1,0,3,3,1,177,0,183,'Customer can not view inventory or tank history information','EH Wolf-  Robert pw: 123456\nCustomer: Michels Corp.\nCan not view inventory or tank history.',0,1,6,1514991938,1515173305),(186,1,5,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Tank Monitor only systems. i.e. Walser BMW/Mini, Michel\'s \"Truck Shop\" - E.H. Wolf','When selecting View Logs / Daily Reports - Tank Monitor section is not displaying any information.\nWhen selecting \"Tank History Report\" need to remove/hide \"Summary Report\" Menu selection.',1,1,6,1515173256,1578764237),(187,1,5,0,26,26,11,163,0,141,'TMM not reconnecting','Numerous times the TMM would lose connection to the OilCop system.  After power cycling the TMM it would not reconnect.  Even after a few hours the TMM would not reconnect, IT APPEARS, until either the internal reset button was used and/or the TMM was simply turned around 180 depress from the wall it is normally attached to.  Once a connection is established the TMM can be placed back on the wall and will function for weeks without fail.  The TMM consistently has 3 bars of signal.\n   Currently the TMM and FCM#3 are not communicating with the system.  After numerous attempts I was unable to get either connected to the system, which is a first.  However I was not able to gain access to the parts department to reset the CDM.  Though that was not required in the past.\n   Per our conversation, I have attached photos of the site and will later attach additional photos and site layouts for clarification.\n\nNote: this is a third attempt as previous attempts at creating a Discrepancy have failed most likely do to large file sizes.',0,1,6,1515454192,1550862935),(188,1,0,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'Tank monitor dispensing displays incorrect time.','When Tank Monitor Solution time out is set for 1 minute, 120 seconds is displayed in the Tank Level screen. \nWhen pressing the start button the displayed time value changes to the correct value, counts downs and shuts off then resets the time to 120 sec..',1,1,4,1515685221,0),(189,1,5,0,81,3,56,0,0,0,'21\' probe is giving a signal different from 0','system T_2_42\nfirmware TSM_3_0_0\n\nonce connected and configured, 2 different probes gave a signal different from 0 while they were completely out of liquid.\ndimensioning the tank as a parallelepiped with 1 square meter area, they were giving a signal of about 72-74 cm of liquid height (it was around 720-740 liters with specific gravity =1).\nPlacing the probe inside 22-23 cm of water, the signal was increasing of 210 liters more or less, meaning that the probe is working properly (considering that the specific gravity could change a little and the accuracy).\nIt looks like there is an offset instead of a null signal.\n\nChecking oilcopsupport we can see that there should be a new firmware for TSM, TSM_3_0_1 for this T version, but it\'s not available in firmware folder on dropbox.\nIf this could be the reason and firmware fixes the issue, please arrange to give us the possibility to download and load the firmware on TSM (by the end of week, on Monday we have an installation with 3 of these probes)\nOtherwise, please work on this issue as urgent.',1,3,6,1516088286,1578691893),(190,1,2,0,271,3,191,192,0,196,'No funciona','No funciona',1,1,6,1524173742,1524845554),(191,1,5,0,3,0,1,8,0,0,'Daily Start/Stop time to drive relays','If setting up Daily Start/Stop times to trigger TMM relays and Start time occurred prior too the time when someone is setting up the system, will have to wait until the Start time time occurs naturally in order for the relay to trigger. Also need to add the ability to select the days Monday - Sunday when Daily Start/Stop times are active.',1,1,5,1525124914,0),(192,1,0,0,3,3,1,18,0,10,'Had to reset reel on east station several times','Transaction 5/17, 6:35 AM WO 342757  5QT   Open dispense and appeared in the transaction logs after resetting this morning at 6:35am, interesting the transaction was 3-4 lines from top of the Transaction list in the logs, only after clicking on the date sort button did it move to the top of the list. Makes me believe the transaction occurred yesterday. \nTook a back up before resetting the reel.\nWill be at the location from 7:45am - 8:45am today..',1,1,6,1526557859,1578691820),(193,1,0,0,3,399,1,179,0,184,'Repeatedly getting 255 errors on both TAC','Corleys is saying they seem to have quite a few 255 errors on both TAC\'s.\nThey are deleting work orders and re-entering them when they get 255 error, yesterday had to delete a tech and re-enter to get it to work.\nIs it’s a coincidence deleting seems to fix the issue or if we are having some other issue?\nPre dispense timeout set at one minute..',1,1,6,1526660652,1666799506),(194,1,3,0,26,26,11,190,0,195,'Rear-end Gear Oil Mobile Tank Discrepancies','As reported to me by the parts manager(George William):\nOn 1 particular mobile tank, rear-end gear oil, we have 2 issues.\n1. Under R.O. 86001 \n   -The technician completed a preset dispense without the OilCop system recording the amount dispensed.\n\n2.Under RO 86035\n   -The parts manager loaded a RO for the technician with a preset of 28 pints.  The technician used 28 pints but required 4 more pints.  The technician was able to later log back in and dispense the 4 pints without the parts manager adding additional pints to the RO.\n\nI have reviewed the logs I have access to and can not say exactly where the issue is.  My only suspect at this time on issue number 2 is that top off feature is enabled.\n\nBackground info:\nThe OilCop should be setup so that technicians can only dispense oil that has been previously loaded by the parts department.  The Technicians should be only allowed to select a RO and dispense the preset amount set by the Parts Department.\nOn Monday the 21st I completed repairs to both mobile tanks(rear-end and transmission).  I tested the system to verify the calibration of the PSM\'s, the calibration of the inline Alemite Meters and that the solenoids were closing properly.  Both PSM\'s override\'s were closed and tightened down and new security seals were installed. No issues were observed at the time.',1,1,6,1527282965,1550862919),(195,1,6,0,39,3,24,162,0,140,'Multiple RED\'s assigned to one dispense point','On the CAT dealership installation in Omaha they need the ability to view the dispensing activity from both sides of a particular bay. Currently you cannot do this as you can only assign one Remote Display per reel. They are willing to hardware the second display if this helps.',1,1,6,1527785325,1578691940),(196,8,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Mac Address already exist','Setting up new customer in suppport.com, had to delete as Liquidynamics customer so can set up as Service Express customer. now when setting up system upon entering the Mac address Mac. address already exist.',1,1,6,1528983741,1666799585),(197,8,0,0,3,399,1,162,0,140,'Can not setup distributor with email address says already in use.','Same as discrepancy 196 however deleted distributor and reentered distributor now say email already in use.\ncorrect email address for the distributor is dan@serviceexpressco.com',0,1,6,1528985733,1666799632),(198,1,1,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'LQD T46 Reports modifications','Reports looks good..\n\nBottom of Action Journal, Transaction Journal and Work order Status can see out line of buttons along bottom of the page however font color looks like its set the same color as the button and button same color of the page.\n\nBottom of Tank History report - tank level update line items not printed..',1,1,6,1529875025,1666799686),(199,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'LQD T46 Dispense modifications.','Currently the system allows a dispense to be deleted from a work order, need to modify so after any product is dispensed the system will not allow that product to be deleted from the work order.',0,1,6,1530202394,1666799699),(200,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'LQD T46 - TAC -  Dispense modifications.','Auto Close is enable on this configuration. That did not matter from the TAC. All orders had to be closed manually.\nWhy does the computer track 0 amount dispenses on this configuration?\nDO not allow products to be deleted once any amount has been dispensed\n\nOff/On/On/On 3 was a mess. It originally started with one product, that product was changed to another product, products were added and so forth. When one uses the same order and changes its parameters drastically that is when the numbers, tank readings and journal start going crazy. Transactions that never happened were suddenly in the journals, presets were ignored and max dispense points were ignored.\n\nOff/On/On/On 5 work well until I deleted a previously dispensed product from the work order. When a product is deleted after being dispensed it disappears from the journal systems as if it never happened. The problem with this, though, is the tank readings do not change. So, the journals tell you that nothing happened, but the tanks say otherwise. If a work order is deleted in its entirety, not just a part of it, that product is then put back into its respective tank. The exception to this rule is the product we deleted BEFORE deleting the work order. That product is not put back into the tank.',0,1,6,1530555810,1666799714),(201,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'TMM-1 loss radio connection, Wireless printer loss radio connection.','TMM-1 has been operational 7 days, today lost radio communications while the TMM was holding open the 10W air solenoid valve during a dispense. Removed TMM cover no change, power cycled TMM came back up after 10 Minute. TMM-1 is installed next to TMM-2. \n\nTMM-2, TAC-1, FCM 1 & 2  and RED 1,2,3,4,5 all in the same tank room continued to have radio communications the entire time TMM-1 was not communicating. \n\nWireless printer has been working for the last 5 days with 3 bars, the printer has line of site to the Range extender 50\' away which is  about 75\' from the CDM. Power cycled the printer numerous times would not reconnect. Disconnected CDM for 2 minutes from CTR and reconnected did not immediately reconnect, they moved the printer 15\' back to the original location it had been working for the last 5 days.',1,2,6,1530567296,1578764498),(202,1,1,0,258,399,1,32,0,0,'Teamviewer Issue','Currently working on new controller for Prairieland Partners in McPherson. Have uploaded OilCop software onto an older version controller, similar to the silver ones, but black. Attempted to add the controller to the oilcop-remote via Teamviewer and was unable to do so. When opening Teamviewer the only window I can get to open is the Computers and Contacts window. I cannot get the window to open that has the steps to Open on Startup, Assign to Account and Grant Easy Access.\n\nI have deleted Teamviewer and re-downloaded via Firefox and also re-uploaded the OilCop software. I could not find that exact version of Teamviewer from their website so the one that is currently downloaded is a tad newer, but still a version of 12.',1,1,6,1531845204,1666799777),(203,1,0,0,3,3,1,210,0,212,'Missing work order 260687-042 and two transactions, 7/16/18 and 7/13/18 appears in action journal','Work order 260687-042 dose not show up in Work order maintenance, however the two transactions along with WO number appears in the transaction journal. And the two transactions are each displayed in the action journal with action = Dispense Emergency stop in HE-2 Work Order id 98 next to both of them. Also Work Order 260687-042 is listed in Open Work Orders in Work Order Status report along with 4 different 10W transactions.',0,1,6,1531846391,1538428411),(204,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Modify OilCop footer','Gartec has a large customer who is going to private label the OilCop system so to keep things simple for all Gartec systems would like to modify footer information on bottom of OilCop web pages (for all languages), remove the name Gartec and Liquidynamics from the footer leave copyright  2014.\nFor all Liquidynamics systems would like to keep the footer information the same as it is now.',0,1,6,1531917739,1538428433),(205,1,0,0,3,399,1,189,0,215,'Having a lot of 255 errors, even though all devices have 4 bars communications','255 intermittently occurs when entering PIN or work order number from the TAC.  Waiting to hear back from Tommy if we can turn off Free/open dispense for the technicians. \nFrom the search not able to access Terminal Viewer to open the debugger.',0,2,6,1532013123,1666799803),(206,1,5,0,3,3,1,151,0,130,'3-Tank Monitor only Syst. Tank Adjust. reports not updating. 1-Tank Monitor only Syst. reports works','Walser MN, Acura of Wichita and Porsche of Wichita Tank Adjustments report not up dating and Usage History desk top not updating.\n\nWichita- BMW Tank Adjustments reports working correctly and Usage History desk top are working correctly.\nAll systems have the same Admin Options settings.',0,1,6,1532096046,1538428199),(207,1,0,0,26,26,11,190,0,195,'No Delivery Report','Parts Manager George William is asking for a Delivery Report.  He would like to know how much oil was delivered by the oil company.  Essentially an automatic tank adjustment.  The tanks in question do have tank probes.\n1. Is this possible?  Tank History Report is not sufficient.\n2. Tank History Report is not visible on local OilCop system but is available on OilCopSupport.com.  Why is this?\n3. OilCopSupport Tank History Report, when selecting monthly, is showing Dates and Times that appear to be in the Future.  What timezone is this?  (Also the monthly report shows more current data, one extra day, then the weekly report)',1,1,6,1532556068,1536599657),(208,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Show date/time for multi. transactions in Recent Work order & Work Order Maintenance pages','Two transactions were pumped from the tank room at 7/30/18 approx. 7:00a; WO 111111-666 -118.0Q and 273420-022 - 346.7Q. At 10:27a this morning both reels indicated they had not timed out, had to reset both reels.\n\nAfter resetting both reels the transaction log indicates 7/30/18; 10:27a for 111111-666 – 118Q and 273420-022 - 346.7Q was dispensed. \n\nReviewing Work Order maintenance, indicates WO 111111-666 – 118Q was created 7/27/2018 and WO 273420-022 – 346.7Q was created 7/25/2018, however Work Order Maintenance indicates 357.7Q was dispensed instead of 346.7Q. Digging further into the transaction log found on 7/27/18; 3:18p WO 273420-022 dispensed 11Q thus the 357.7Q.\n\n7/30/18 at 12:04p usage info. on Mgr./Manager desktop only reflects 3 quarts was dispensed for the day.\n\nReviewing Work Order Status indicates WO 111111-666 is open and the 118.0Q transaction is recorded. WO 273420-022 is open and both the 11.0Q and 346.7Q transactions are recorded.     \n\nFrom Recent Work Order and Work Order Maintenance appears amount displayed is the combined amount if multiple dispenses occurred. Would be nice to show all transactions that occurred on the screen as we do when multiple technicians dispense, further more we should show date and time for each of the multiple transactions within a Work Order.',1,1,6,1532978816,1666799868),(209,1,0,0,3,3,1,210,0,212,'Tank Adjustments not updating','Tank history Report seems to function correctly, however Tank Adjustments is not updating.\n\nTank Monitor solution is OFF and \"Display Work Order Invoice\" is not displayed in Admin settings, if Tank Monitor solution is turned on \"Display Work Order Invoice\" is displayed and all of the previous Usage History disappears. Turn off  \"Display Work Order Invoice\" and Usage History reappears.',0,1,6,1533215317,1538428245),(210,2,9,0,258,399,1,0,0,0,'RED Test Issue','From the ADMIN page on the OilCop Jr Main Console option #23 is used to set up the address and test the Jr RED. After setting the address and saving I was unable to get the RED to activate using the test feature. The RED did work properly when I went back to the ADMIN page and selected #19, Calibrate Reels. The RED does work, but there is something awry with the test feature. There were zero issues using the test feature for the Jr Printer.',0,1,6,1533227804,1666799836),(211,1,0,0,3,3,1,151,0,130,'Tank Monitor system quit updating.','Replaced API UPS with Mini 12vdc Battery UPS Monday 7/30/18. \nChecked system this AM found system stopped updating, debugger was running when it stopped sometime yesterday, it did not indicate anything unusual.\nreplace Mini UPS with API UPS.',0,1,6,1533306363,1538428262),(212,1,5,0,3,3,1,214,0,217,'TMM not communicating','TMM quit communicating, opened the debugger, indicates Serial Port Open.\nDo not know if Serial Port Open indications is normal when first opening the debugger?\nSee attached debugger screen shot',2,3,6,1533311203,1538428368),(213,8,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'OilCop support.com... No longer receiving email notifications for new and updated discrepancies','1. Checked notifications are turned on.\n\n2. Tired to select oilcopsupport-website, however when trying to submit its is asking to Please select system.',1,2,6,1533312569,1666799900),(214,8,0,0,306,399,189,189,0,194,'Data Discrepancy','Looking for an explanation as to why the Amount Dispensed shown in the Work Order Maintenance Screen is different than the Amount Dispensed in the Recent Work Order section of the Dashboard. For the three most recent transactions.',1,1,6,1533731014,1666799935),(215,1,0,0,258,399,1,0,0,0,'T_2_47_2 Test','See attached Word document',0,1,6,1534177814,1666799959),(216,1,1,0,3,399,1,8,0,0,'T_2_47_2  Tank Monitoring Test','When product is added to tank the value added is displayed in the daily report.\nIf probe is pulled out and reinserted the value on tank history graph will increase more than tank physical volume however, tank volume displayed on the desktop is correct. \n\nDelivery report most users are familiar with displays date, time, volume begin & date, time, volume end and then displays net increase volume. If to make that happen is big thing to do maybe we could point customers to Tank adjustment log, if “Automatic” is working they can figure it out using the automatic tank adjustment logs to see better resolution than 15 minutes intervals. Some tanks will fill in 5 minutes some 20 minutes obviously depends on how fast they are pumping and size of tanks.\n\nWhat triggers tank adjustments in the Tank Adjustment report to be made Manual or Automatic? Tank Adjustment reports for United BMW Atlanta, Ga and Don Hattan Chevrolet both show “Automatic” all tanks are on the tank monitor whereas the NADA test system shows all “Manual”, even though one tank is on the monitor and three tanks are not on the monitor. Additionally Bakersfield truck center has three tanks using the monitor and two tanks not using the monitor and their reports only show manual update.. Would it be a difficult thing to show automatic updates for any tank using the monitor, even though some of the tanks are not using the monitor?',1,1,6,1534888269,1666799981),(217,1,1,0,3,0,1,8,0,0,'Record tank over fill alarm events in Action Journal','Document date, time, product tank over fill alarm events in Action Journal',0,1,5,1538484879,0),(218,1,0,0,62,399,1,0,0,0,'Duration of Tank Inventory logic for Tank History Report','Delivery report most users are familiar with displays date, time, volume begin & date, time, volume end and then displays net increase volume. If to make that happen is big thing to do maybe we could point customers to Tank adjustment log, if “Automatic” is working they can figure it out using the automatic tank adjustment logs to see better resolution than 15 minutes intervals. Some tanks will fill in 5 minutes some 20 minutes obviously depends on how fast they are pumping and size of tanks.',0,1,6,1538497783,1666800143),(219,1,0,0,62,399,1,0,0,0,'Manual/automatic Tank Adjustment','What triggers tank adjustments in the Tank Adjustment report to be made Manual or Automatic? Tank Adjustment reports for United BMW Atlanta, Ga and Don Hattan Chevrolet both show “Automatic” all tanks are on the tank monitor whereas the NADA test system shows all “Manual”, even though one tank is on the monitor and three tanks are not on the monitor. Additionally Bakersfield truck center has three tanks using the monitor and two tanks not using the monitor and their reports only show manual update.. Would it be a difficult thing to show automatic updates for any tank using the monitor, even though some of the tanks are not using the monitor?',0,1,6,1538498024,1666800173),(220,1,0,0,315,3,1,112,0,0,'Restore Backup throws a PHP error','Restore works if you select a file from the Backups listing from the webpage, but if you choose a file that is not in the listing from a local drive, network drive, media drive, etc, , a popup shows the following error:\n\n\"The uploaded file exceeds the maximum allowed size in your PHP configuration file.',1,1,6,1538656412,1578764825),(221,1,0,0,315,315,1,8,0,0,'Deletion is not removing all the necessary recrods','When a customer is deleted all the related recrods in other tables are not being deleted.  Suspect that there is no referential integrity established at the table level.',1,1,6,1538657688,1538658392),(222,1,0,0,315,399,1,8,0,0,'When a customer is deleted not all related records are also deleted from related tables','When a customer was deleted the related records in the t_system_locations were not deleted which prevented the customers mac addresses to be used when the customer was recreated using the add function.  This would suggest that referential integrity is not established at the table level.',1,1,6,1538657907,1666800206),(223,1,0,0,315,399,1,8,0,0,'PHP error is thrown when saving a New Discrepancy','When saving a New Discrepancy record without customer and customer location filled out the site throws the following in the attachement:',1,1,6,1538658660,1666800228),(224,8,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'The \"I forgot my password\" feature is not working','Appears the “I forgot my password” is not not working.',0,1,6,1539697547,1543608184),(225,1,0,0,258,315,1,0,0,0,'T_2_49 Test','A few things of note that I found while messing with the new test version:\n\n     - When an order has multiple products, why does the system return the user to the select work order page instead of the select product page? If the order still has products to be dispensed does it make \n        more sense to revert back to the remaining products in the order and skip the steps in between? It would be easier to simply select \'Back\' within the order if the user is done than trying to find an order in a \n        list and go from there.\n\n     - The \'Print\' button within the Work Order Status page did not work\n\n     - When checking the \'Check here if this is a delivery\' box when manually adding/subtracting product from a tank, it does not show as such in the daily report. It will still show as an adjustment and not a \n        delivery. \n\n     - Curious, why does tank monitor solution need to be enabled to show a delivery on the Daily Report? I added product both with tank monitor solution on/off and only saw the delivery was noted with tank \n        monitor solution turned on. I did not get any deliveries noted when adding/subtracting manually from tanks without a sensor, also.\n\n     - On the Import/Export Reports page, is it possible to add a red X next to all columns to delete that column if need be? If a user were to make a bunch of columns and later decide to remove one that user would have to backtrack and delete all the columns until they\'ve reached the one they actually want gone. The user would then have to redo all the columns they meant to keep but were forced to delete. \n\nNotes: Overall, the system runs much smoother and more snappy. The option to leave the sidebar expanded is amazing. Having less confirmation pop-ups clutter the screen is great, as well. I didn\'t run into any major issues upon review. Mark did have a question regarding multi-product w/o\'s not displaying the date and time properly and when tested it seemed to work the way it should. I\'ll re-open and run some of those orders again tomorrow to see if a change of date might trigger what he was looking for. The reports looked good. I also ran a backup, cleared the system and re-uploaded the backup without issue.',0,1,6,1541524479,1559743775),(226,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'PAG Porsche... Preset didn\'t register oil at station, overfilled car by 1 quart.','11/13/18 12:09 Tech loaded work order #360875 on station #2, preset 0W/40 8.1 Liters, pulled the trigger saw oil dispensing, looked back did not see the numbers on his computer not moving. Stopped the dispense and preset 7.0 this time the dispense stopped at 7.0 the pressed dispense complete and jumped to 7.1. This is what is displayed in the Work Order Maintenance.\nWhen the Technician test drove the car the on board computer said the engine oil was one liter too high..\n\nCan only find one transaction for WO #360875 in the transaction log 7.5 Quarts and Work Order Status \"Open work order\" indicates 7.5 Quarts dispensed. the stations are set for Liters in station configuration and reports are set for quarts.. \n\nHad Arron confirm PSM bypass was closed, and would not dispense unless the system opened the PSM. Tested with 0.5 preset and system shut off correctly.\n\nComplete DB Backup 11 -13- 2018- 17 -28-03.sql',0,1,6,1542132657,1542296999),(227,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Marine Chevrolet  Tank Monitor -1  with hard wire Range extender- 1 quit communicating','System worked for a couple of weeks after start up, now range extender-1 is now flashing from Green to Red, RSSI for tank monitor -1 and range extender-1  both have a red X and tank monitor will not communicate with system. \nTank Monitor-1 is hard wired to range extender-1, confirmed RS-485 polarity is correct and physical address dip switch are set correctly.\nSent new range extender no change in symptom.',0,1,6,1542138879,1542296368),(228,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'PAG Porsche.. Keeps one work order open for the month for topping off fluids for customer','Note: Because customer is keeping one work order open for the month that is used for topping off customers vehicles when they come in to have fluids topped off. They have multiple Products per work order and Multiple Dispense turned on, consequently they can not use Auto Close Work Order.',0,1,1,1542145025,0),(229,1,0,0,3,399,1,182,0,187,'Tech unblocked WO however did not allow to dispense','Station one, Tech Chip Nycum - Pin 6208, can open WO 387191 and go as far as selecting station then system ask to unblock  enters code however nothing happened. Action journal shows Chip Nycum Dispensed unblocked 38197 however failed to allow him to dispense product.\nThey tried multiple times to unblock before he had to used bottled oil and then they deleted to work order.\nAlso the action journal shows  Administrator “Station Reel data updated” 8 times at 10:24 and once at 10:25. That was the administrator selecting the edit button on the Stations screen and then pressing Update/Delete button, a habit he got into when the reels would need to be reset. The Admin. did say ever since the update this is the first time he has had any issues requiring him to reset the reels.\n\nAt 10:24, different Tech, station one was able to pump 0W/20 using WO 387194 \n\nAlso found the time was one hour ahead, changed time. I have found after updating a couple of systems the time was one hour ahead don’t know if it’s a daylight saving time change issue or something to do with updating to Ver. 24\n\nComplete DB Backup 11-16-2018-15-40-01.sql',0,1,6,1542381907,1666800314),(230,1,1,0,258,3,1,174,0,181,'Email Scheduler Issues','Attempted to open the \'Email Scheduler\' at this location and was redirected to a database error page.',1,1,6,1544646220,1579721857),(231,1,0,0,258,3,1,158,0,136,'User Login Issue','Was unable to log into the computer under \'oilcop\' user. Had to login as a \'guest\' to access OilCop system.',1,1,6,1544646380,1550011891),(232,1,0,0,258,399,1,112,0,0,'Reports Issue','Andrea had an issue with a Daily Report that was for December 11th. The header of the page notes that date as 11/12/2018. To Andrea this is correct. However, the title of the report notes that date as 12/11/2018. Which to Andrea would read November 12th. Per his email, it sounds like his thought process is that the system is reporting one day as another. Personally, I think that each date is the same day, but an inconsistency in the date format and it switches between Euro and American formatting.',0,1,6,1544647889,1666800336),(233,1,0,0,258,399,1,0,0,0,'Email Issues','Andrea from Gartec is receiving OilCop logs from a controller located in New Mexico. I\'ve gone through ALL of the controllers running under the \'Liquidynamics\' tab in teamviewer and was unable to find Andrea attached to any of them. Is there any other way to find out why he is receiving emails from this controller?',1,1,6,1545235916,1666800362),(234,1,0,0,258,87,1,0,0,0,'Firmware Update Issue','via Tommy\n\nSwapped from old style, yellow controller to current style controller. Tommy took a backup from their original controller that was updated to R_24 on site by the owner of the system. Tommy suspects that they did not incrementally update and, instead, jumped from their previous version straight to 24 skipping the versions in between. Tommy had attempted numerous times to find the components via the search for hardware button in the hardware config page. The search always fails and no components are found although they are on. Could the user skipping over versions while updating cause this issue? I had originally already had the new controller at R_24, does applying a backup from another controller overwrite firmware updates?',1,3,6,1548274321,1549493108),(235,1,1,0,3,316,1,210,0,212,'Can not open daily report.pdf','Beginning last Friday customer is unable open any oilcop produced .pdf files. The Error says= Adobe reader could not open \"wasn\'t correctly decoded\"\n\nThey are able to open .pdf files from other sources.',1,1,6,1548949159,1550068281),(236,1,0,0,258,399,1,0,0,0,'Controller Restart Issue','Newer batch of controllers are very inconsistent on coming back on after a computer restart. They will get stuck on the \'American Megatrends\' startup page. The best way to reboot the new controllers is to completely shut down and press the power button on the controller to turn back. Is there anything that can be done to put an end to the controllers freezing on a restart?',1,1,6,1549375621,1666800397),(237,1,0,0,3,3,1,77,0,56,'Replace controller, tried to install customer back file. Error says upload file exceeds allowable','Need to transfer fix size fix from latest T version to new controller.\nPO will follow',1,3,6,1549378026,1557837554),(238,1,0,0,258,3,1,189,0,215,'Reports not logging into support.com','Received an email from Matt from E.H. Wolf stating that there are no reports on support.com for this location. Checked myself and saw nothing, as well. Also checked the Milwaukee location and saw no reports?',1,1,6,1550174934,1573594322),(239,1,0,0,258,3,1,189,0,194,'Reports not logging into support.com','Matt from E.H. Wolf did not mention not seeing the reports from this location, but I did not see any when I checked after looking into his question regarding Wausau.',0,1,6,1550175042,1573594302),(240,1,1,0,3,3,1,230,0,234,'Work Ordered entered from TAC it will not show name of technician, as it dose from the web','Customer asked if its possible for a work order that is entered from TAC could display name of the technician who opened the work order on the managers desktop like it dose when loading the work order using the computer, instead of having to look it up on the transaction logs..',0,1,6,1550506592,1578765551),(241,1,1,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'System crashed two times this week, cycling power seems to fix it.  Open Serial Port??','Did observe open serial port on the debugger..\nDid we add the open serial port patch to the new controller?',1,3,6,1550604396,1557837470),(242,1,0,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'Tank monitor relay behavior modification','Have a customer who would like the TMM to control fluid flow into a tank by turning On and Off a 24 VDC solenoid valve. What is different there are eighteen 20 gallon tanks, they will be filled from a tank with a pump that is located 100\' feet away. Each tank will have a solenoid valve to start and stop the flow, would like to use the tank monitor relay to control each solenoid. \"Tank Re-Fill Control\" the logic is when “Low Level Shutoff” is triggered, turn on/open corresponding relay, then when “High Level Shutoff” is triggered, turn off/close the relay. This process will reoccur several times in a 24 hour period over 340 days per year.  \nWould it be difficult to add/modify   /index.php/admin/relay/relay_configuration     page? and add new “Trigger Type” called \"Tank Re-Fill Control\" or maybe prefer doing something with the second trigger??',0,1,5,1551308002,0),(243,1,1,0,3,3,1,190,0,195,'Aircraft on Ground','Can Bryan remote into Bakersfield Truck Center/Team Viewer..\nSerial port open, yet CDM is green all 6 other devices  are red??',0,1,6,1552419518,1557837490),(244,1,1,0,258,399,1,0,0,0,'Reports Formatting T_2_50','Reports do not have the location where they come from. Possible to put location in the header? Would be useful for us and customers that oversee multiples to locations to be able to easily see where a report is coming from.\n\nAction Journal: Looks good for the most part. Column titles are not aligned with the respective column of information tho. They are kind of staggered off to the side a bit and overlap.\n                         The table line also get mixed up a bit when continuing onto the next page via printing.\n\nTransaction Journal: Column titles are way off and do not line up with their respective information. Too many columns to print correctly in portrait mode?\n\nWork Order Status:\n     Completed Work Orders: Amount Dispensed and Invoiced columns overlap each other. Again, titles do not align with the correct information, either.\n\n     Open Work Orders: For whatever reason this table does not have the issues that the Completed Work Orders table does. Looks fine outside of column titles not lining up.\n\nTank Adjustments: Looks good. All columns align correctly.\n\nSummary Report: My only issue is that it looks like the two pie graphs could fit on one side of the paper instead of two. Small gripe tho.\n\nDaily Report: Table is cut off at the margin. Too many columns to fit.\n\n**Are reports meant to be printed in landscape? Seems there is too much information to fit the tables properly in portrait mode, even with zero margins.',1,1,6,1552920004,1666800514),(245,1,1,0,3,3,1,8,0,0,'Updated controller from R_2_21 to R_2_24 Pwr cycled between updates.','While installing R_2_24 threw an 130 data base error..  The system had not been set up or any data loaded, maybe R_2_24 did not know how to handle no data to convert?? see error below \nThe system is set up on our bench it is accessible Team viewer as  \"Chantilly PDI\".\n\nThe customer would like us to ship the controller back to them today if possible, we told them it would depend if the development was busy or not. DO what we can not end of the world if they have to wait till Monday.\n \n\n\nError Number: 130\nIncorrect file format \'t_adminstrative_options\'\nSELECT * FROM (`t_adminstrative_options`)\nFilename: /var/www/oilcop/helpers/util_helper.php\nLine Number: 50',1,3,6,1553882443,1554143115),(246,1,0,0,306,399,189,189,0,194,'Oil dispensed but not recorded','On Friday 4/12 at about 2:00pm tech Max Popowski dispensed approximately 11 gallons of 15W40 engine oil on Work Order 10295-02 however it was not recorded in the Transaction Journal. Only the 80W-90 shows up.',1,1,6,1555332897,1666800539),(247,1,0,0,3,3,1,141,0,119,'Updated from R_23 to R_24 caused the system to quit working for some users.','System is running on bypass, so need to fix before Monday if possible.\nThis location was updated to R_24 several months ago had similar issues. Bryan had remote in spent some time trying to resolve the issue however, was unable to finish so he had to revert back to R_23. That maybe the best thing to do now if you all are busy.   Currently daily reports will not open, seems sluggish, some technicians work properly however, some can only log in/Load Work Order - \"reply\'s valid WO\"/ will not allow station to be selected even though all users have permission to select all stations. Note: If i login from Team Viewer as one of the technician no working (password 1896) the system appears to function normally. We tried logging PW 1896 from different computer at the location no change in symptom. Tried clearing browser cache no change.\nSuspect Bryan will know best coarse of action.',1,3,6,1555520803,1557837419),(248,1,1,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'Oil Cop enhancement needs for Construction Market','Mathew Steadman and Ken Hutton put a power point together which is printed as a .pdf and uploaded for review.\n-- Oil Cop enhancement needs for Construction Market\n\nWould like to review for comment to see if we can accommodate these suggestions?',1,1,5,1556137200,0),(249,1,0,0,258,399,1,179,0,184,'Work Order Status','Corley\'s is entering work orders that are open to all technicians and not assigned to anybody in particular. The system used to log in the work order status, after the work order closed, who dispensed that order. Beginning roughly a month ago, the system now no longer does this and the work order status page shows the order was dispensed by All Technicians, not the particular individual as it used to. They are wondering if this will be the case moving forward or if this is something that can be fixed and revert back to how it once was.\n\nI did show Justin the system logs page and directed him to the transaction journal where the work orders are actually broken down by individual technicians. I think the bigger issue in the particular situation is ease of use. One click is better than four.',1,1,6,1556568316,1666800587),(250,1,1,0,3,3,1,236,0,240,'Deleted old customer user/ added new customer added says Mac address already exist','Customer  Matt Steadman   please add sytem\n\n00:e0:4c:28:ee:42',1,1,6,1557836390,1558096736),(251,1,1,0,3,3,1,189,0,0,'Is it okay to update two ASE locations with R 25, even-though they have custom code -','multi users, multi products per work order?',1,1,6,1558017504,1573594353),(252,1,1,0,3,315,1,8,0,0,'When entering users, if PIN begins with (0 zero) will allow to save however,','the leading zero is not saved therefore, system does not recognize the four digit password because the system stored only three digits.',1,1,6,1558039146,1567168780),(253,1,0,0,3,3,1,8,0,0,'Team viewer access for Gartec/Gitec to access their systems','Updated all of the OilCop systems in USA that have Teamviewer access to R_25 and a couple to T_56.\nThen looked into some of Gartec and Gitec systems noticed most of them are using  R_23 or earlier.\nWould it be possible to set Gartec up with their own Team Viewer directory?',1,1,6,1558097785,1558123832),(254,1,0,0,3,315,1,236,0,0,'Dispense not recorded','4/5/14 at 9:00am (wo-Mcardle) from computer/ethernet connection, matt tried to pump 80/90 two times and at 9:02 am (wo-mcardle 4-5-19) matt tried to pump 80/90 one time. The computer did not give indication it was dispensing, he walked to the tank room and observed 80/90 pumping. When completed the transaction was not documented in transaction journal and Work Order Maintenance showed 0 amount dispensed. Tank adjustments does reflect 399.3 Quarts was dispensed at 9:27am. Both Tank Monitor and Delivery Acknowledgement time outs are set at 1:00 Minutes. \n\nBoth TMM-2 & and FCM-2 are located in the tank room and there is a good possibility when plasma cutters are operating in the room adjacent to the tank room maybe causing the radio signal to fluctuate. \n\nWill hard wiring RS-485 communication wiring for the FCMs, TMMs and REDs fix the issue? \n\nCould this also shed some light on ASE Milwaukee “1 time” and Wausau “2 time” lost transactions?',0,1,6,1558197912,1567171803),(255,1,0,0,3,315,1,237,0,241,'When email scheduler sends daily report, \"Amount Dispensed\" on top of report reads 0 Zero','If the \"Send Daily Report\" button is pushed the report will display a value in the Amount Dispensed field.\nR_25',1,1,6,1558386684,1567171870),(256,1,0,0,3,3,1,239,0,243,'System has tank monitoring, however no information displayed for Tank Adjustments or Tank History','reports. \nR_25,\n12:00AM - 12:00AM set\nTank monitor and Delivery Acknowledgement times outs set at 1:00 Minute and turned on',0,1,6,1558440712,1573594205),(257,1,1,0,3,399,1,8,0,0,'Re:R_25, Do we need to set both Tank Monitor Solution and Delivery Acknowledgment to Yes','and same time out values for delivery reports to work properly?',0,1,6,1558525396,1666800632),(258,8,0,0,3,315,1,0,0,0,'Demo account jim@oiljobber.com  PW: 123456 says it is blocked, can the account be unblocked?','dan@distributor.com 123456\ncalvin@customer.com  123456\njim@oiljobber.com  123456\n\nAbove accounts we have setup to show features of Oilcopsupport.com, current date range for data is November 2017 - September of 2018 is there anyway we can use current data from a working system without reveling the location the data being used for those accounts?',0,1,6,1559047378,1567171908),(259,1,1,0,3,3,1,8,0,0,'email scheduler (version T_56 and R_25) sending wrong report','Hi everyone,\nwe have a problem with email scheduler (version T_56 and R_25): if you flag \"inventory\" report, instead of sending the actual inventory the system sends the adjustment report\nPlease fix this very urgently, I have a brand new customer where we finished to install this system &#40;only tank monitoring&#41; yesterday and we cannot have him complaining.\n\nI tested the same even with last T version and it\'s the same.\n\nMoreover, I tried to use the power restart command after I updated from R_24 to R_25 and it didn\'t work. Since it\'s working on T version, will it work if I force power down manually and restart the controller manually?\nthanks\nAndrea',0,1,6,1559676618,1559854330),(260,1,0,0,3,315,1,0,0,0,'Tank monitor daily report and Tank Monitor Solution time out bug','In previous releases we have to set both Tank Monitor Solution time out and Delivery Acknowledgment time outs to the same timeout value and make them both compulsory in order for the action journal, delivery report tank adjustments and tank history to work. \n\nSet up a system with R_25 software on the bench, with one CDM, TMM and TAC. Setup Test Oil 1 product and 20.8 gallon tank. Admin setting Tank Monitor solution- OFF, Tank History report – ON. Delivery Acknowledgement time out set to 1 minute and Tank Monitor Solution turned off.\n\nInsert probe into test container filled with water, Admin. and Mgr. desktop indicated 12.6 gallons and 20.8 gallon tank.  This is correct\n\n(Note: When placing a probe into a tank is the same as making a delivery. Be careful not to inadvertently pull the probe out and reinsert the probe into the tank will be the same as adding more inventory. \n\nChecking logs \nAction Journal, Tank Adjustments, recorded nothing, \nSummary report tank graphic bottom of page says 50.2 Quarts added to a 83.2 capacity tank,  “Should have indicated 12.6 gallons added to a 20.8 gallon capacity tank” \n\nDaily Report shows tank capacity 83.2 and 50.2 Quarts current inventory, “Should have indicated 12.6 gallons and 20.8 gallon tank”\n\nTank History report displays “Test Oil 1”  zero volume.\n\nThen turn on “Tank Monitor Solution time out” and set for 1 minute. \n\nRechecking logs \nAction journal shows “inventory added for Test Oil 1. Inventory value 12.6”, \nTank Adjustments show Product Test Oil 1, Automatic, amount 50.4Q,            “Should have indicated 12.6”\nSummary Report shows current inventory 50.2 Quarts, 83.2 capacity.         “Should have indicated 12.6 gallons and 20.8 gallon tank” \n\nDaily report shows 83.2Q capacity, 50.2Q current inventory, the Tank Monitor information on bottom of page should be displayed but is not populating the information.   “Should have indicated 12.6 gallons and 20.8 gallon tank”\n\nTank history indicates “Test Oil 1” 50.2 volume. “Should have indicated 12.6”\n \nThen turn  “Tank Monitor Solution” ON.\nAdmin page the same layout.\nMgr. page only displays Tank Level, Device Status and usage history.\n\nAction journal shows “inventory added for Test Oil 1. Inventory value 12.6”, \n\nTank Adjustments show Product Test Oil 1, Automatic, amount 50.4Q,                  “Should have indicated 12.6”\n   \nSummary Report shows current inventory 50.2 Quarts, 83.2 capacity.  “Should have indicated 12.6 gallons and 20.8 gallon Capacity”\n\nDaily report shows 83.2Q capacity, 50.2Q current inventory,    “Should have indicated 12.6 gallons and 20.8 gallon tank”\n    the Tank Monitor information on bottom of page should be displayed but is not populating the information.\n\nTank history indicates “Test Oil 1” 50.2 volume    “Should have indicated 12.6”\n\n\nAfter testing complete.\n\nPulled probe out of tank waited a minute, Action Journal Indicates inventory subtracted for Test Oil 1. Inventory value 12.6.\nthen reinserted probe back into tank 1, Action Journal Indicates inventory added for Test Oil 1. Inventory value 12.9\n\nPulled probe out of tank waited a minute Tank Adjustments \n06/05/2019 02:16 PM Admin One Default Test Oil 1 Test Oil 1 Automatic -50.4 Q\n\nthen reinserted probe back into tank waited a minute Tank Adjustments\n06/05/2019 02:17 PM Admin One Default Test Oil 1 Test Oil 1 Automatic 51.6 Q\n\nTank history indicates “Test Oil 1” 50.2 volume    “Should have indicated 12.6”  The graphic and tabular data is displayed correctly however, the incorrect values are displayed',0,1,6,1559763304,1567175660),(261,1,1,0,3,315,1,8,0,0,'If add name and email address from the Email Scheduler page, person added is not displayed in -','- Add/Modify Users. Try to add the same user in Add/Modify users page, the system displays “The Pin field must contain a unique value”. Will not allow the same email address to be used when trying to set up the user.If add name and email address from the Email Scheduler page, person added is not displayed in Add/Modify Users.',1,1,6,1559855158,1567168372),(262,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Tank history reports tabular data time stamp not correct.','At 7:20am the time stamp displayed 12:45 AM.\nsee attachment',1,1,6,1559909842,1573593974),(263,1,1,0,258,315,1,0,0,0,'R_2_25','Have found 2 issues so far after installing R_2_25\n\nDefault IP address is set incorrectly. The IP should read: 192.168.0.223, but is set to: 192.168.0.233. All other parameters regarding the network are good.\n\nThe default users of Andy Admin, Manny Manager and Terry Technician have the incorrect passwords set to each user.\n     The password should be:\n          Andy Admin: 123456\n          Manny Manager: 12345\n          Terry Technician: 1234\n\nWill add to discrepancy if more issues found.',1,1,6,1560784008,1567176307),(264,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Email report headings for Admiral/Filcar','When Gartec is building OilCop systems for Filcar the email reports and notifications are still arriving from oilcop@gartec.it and with Gartec logo. \n\nThey would like when the Admiral switch is turned on the Admiral/Filcar logo and email address (admiral@filcar.it) to be displayed.',1,1,6,1561559500,1573594180),(265,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Marine Chevrolet Cadillac - Useage history and transaction journal not updating','They are using the system daily and appears to dispense properly however, Admin Desktop / Usage History is not updating. \nTank adjustments indicate usage however, Transaction Journal, Work Order Status, appears to be not updating. Viewing transactions in the Transaction journal shows one transaction for the day (6/26/19)\nAppears to be something database related.',0,1,6,1561564384,1573594159),(266,1,1,0,39,3,24,72,0,0,'Another \"Ghost Dispensing\" event at ASE Wausau Wisconsin','This makes the fourth \"Ghost Dispense\" (GS) I am aware of. A GS is when the tech requests a dispense makes it all the way through the request, gets the dispense page with the display showing how much is dispensing. The problem the page never shows pause activity? The FCM opens the proper PSM they pull the trigger get product but the meter never shows any activity. This problem is not necessarily tied to the PSM as they have had the issue with different products. See attached files where I was able to correlate a tank adjustment to the time and amount of 50/50 AFC that they said they dispensed. The tech (Trent) remembered the Work Order Number 8712001 date 6/11/19 and approximate amount 10 gallons of 50 50 AFC. There is no record of the event BUT if you look at WO reports sort by WO you will find a dispense of 1.2 G of 50/50 AFC AND 7.7 gallons of Rando 40 which they say they didn\'t get on 6/11/19? Need to look in the back ground on this one. \nFeel free to give me a call with any questions. 612-406-0050.',1,2,6,1561587201,1573594139),(267,1,0,0,258,258,1,0,0,0,'Compulsory Test','Tested timeouts and compulsory configurations and found some issues. Please see attached file.',1,1,6,1561736185,1561745727),(268,1,0,0,258,258,1,0,0,0,'Compulsory Test','Tested timeouts and compulsory configurations and found some issues. Please see attached file.',1,1,6,1561736186,1561736215),(269,1,5,0,26,3,11,190,0,195,'10-30 Oil Not dispensing','Customer has reported that the 10-30 oil tank is not dispensing and that the blue light on the tank monitor is not lit.  Other oil tanks including mobile tanks may not be working either.  Customer also reported that when the system was working it can take minutes from the time they issue a preset dispense to the time it actually activates on the hardware.  While on the phone it appeared to take 30 seconds to simply cancel a work order.\nApprox a week ago we added (2) tank monitors to the mobile tanks.  A full system check was not done but the mobile tanks dispensed  I will be onsite Tuesday the 9th.',0,1,6,1562613796,1573594121),(270,1,1,0,3,3,1,112,0,0,'Emails from Admiral/Filcar OilCop systems sending incorrect email information','OilCop engineering code that allows the system to be configured as a private label system and appear as i.e. Gartec, Filcar, etc..  Issue is when the system is setup as a an Filcar/ Admiral system, email reports are arriving from oilcop@gartec.it with Gartecs logo, need to change this too the Filcar info. (see below) when the Admiral switch is turned on. This is also the case for Gartec OilCop too, the email comes from \"Oilcop.com\" which could be ok for us but must be changed for Admiral (as the email address if you enter in the details); and in the \"preview\" there\'s written \"LIQUIDYNAMICS...oilcop\" which needs to be changed, also for Oilcop removing LQD.\n\nAttached Filcar logo .PNG file.\n\n\n\n\nHello again!\nconcerning the email scheduler/the controller sending reports through emails, please find here below the email account configuration to be used:\n\nemail: admiral@filcar.it\nPassword: Luglio2019\nserver:  smtp.cloudfire.it\nport:    25\nAutenthication: yes (email and password)\nEncrypt: no\n\nplease let me know if you need something more, and how much this modification will require (they would like to install the system as soon as possible)\n\nmodifications:\n1) email address - top urgent\n2) no more \"copyright Gartec/LQD\" - top urgent\n3) admiralsupport.com - not so urgent\n4) update page: to be discussed, it always reports Liquidynamics name and logo\n\nthanks, kind regards\nAndrea\n\n\nDa: Andrea Simonetto - Gartec Srl [mailto:a.simonetto@gartec.it] \nInviato: mercoledì 10 luglio 2019 12:18\nA: \'Mark McClatchey\'\nCc: \'Mike Strong\'\nOggetto: R: oilcop / admiral\n\nHi Mark,\nuse the attached image for the homepage of Admiral support.\nAnd remove the \"video\" button\n\nthanks! kind regards\nAndrea\n\nDa: Mark McClatchey [mailto:mark@LiquiDynamics.com] \nInviato: mercoledì 26 giugno 2019 16:36\nA: Andrea Simonetto - Gartec Srl\nCc: \'Mike Strong\'\nOggetto: RE: oilcop / admiral\n\nHi Andrea,\nCan you have them send the graphic they would like to use?\n\nMark\n\nFrom: Andrea Simonetto - Gartec Srl <a.> \nSent: Friday, June 21, 2019 8:47 AM\nTo: Mark McClatchey <mark@LiquiDynamics.com>\nCc: \'Mike Strong\' <mike.strong@viaanix.com>\nSubject: oilcop / admiral\n\nHi again Mark,\nunfortunately I did not have time yet to put together the full list of things, but I have one thing which should be quite easy and fast (at least I hope that!) and that would be quite important. I already anticipated to you last time at the phone: the Admiral/Filcar thing.\n\nBasically, they now have the possibility to use the Oilcop with Admiral customized version.\nBut email are still arriving from oilcop@gartec.it with our logo, so we must change this too when the Admiral switch is turned on.\nPlease let me know which details you need to make the necessary changes to switch to a different logo and to a different email address (admiral@filcar.it)\n\nAlso, and this is valid for our Oilcop too, check the attached screenshot: the email comes from \"Oilcop.com\" which could be ok for us but must be changed for Admiral (as the email address if you enter in the details); and in the \"preview\" there\'s written \"LIQUIDYNAMICS...oilcop\" which needs to be changed, also for Oilcop removing LQD.\n\n\nAnother topic, always for Admiral/Filcar, is to think what we can do for oilcopsupport, as they cannot use it.\n\nthanks, kind regards\nAndrea',1,1,6,1563199664,1573594090),(271,1,1,0,3,399,1,8,0,0,'Karmak DMS interface','Is OilCop API Ver. 1.2 the most current version?\nNeed to send to Karmak for there review.',1,1,6,1563200525,1666800662),(272,1,1,0,3,399,1,112,0,0,'Ticket printer testing results','Hello everyone,\nyesterday Sébastien and I had the time to make some tests on the last Oilcop version.\n\nWe decided to focus on printer yesterday. You can find the report here attached.\n\nWe found a few things not correct, some are quite important because we have customers complaining for them.\nPlease let me know if you want to add discrepancies for this, and in case if you want only one or multiple.\n\nWe found a couple of bugs and issues also outside the tickets, concerning multiproduct and levels logics, even without specifically testing them. They\'re in the last column. (Actually the one concerning levels I\'m pretty sure I already pointed it out years ago, but apparently it has not been modified).\n\nPlease let me have your comments about it, thanks!\nWe will make some further test as soon as possible in July.\n\nkind regards\nAndrea',0,1,6,1563385108,1666800770),(273,8,0,0,1,1,1,0,0,0,'testing mails','Testing mails 123',0,1,6,1563540602,1563542097),(274,8,0,0,316,315,1,136,0,0,'Oilcopsupport.com Email Changes','The emails sent out are lacking some important information that is causing inefficiencies so the following needs to be fixed in the emails to reduce these.\n\n• Emails OilCop Support on creation and updates\n      o Need DR number listed in the email \n               • \"Discrepancy [###] has been updated\"\n               • “A new discrepancy [###] has been posted.”\n      o Hyperlink to send user directly to DR page\n               • Currently there is a hyperlink but hidden in emails but moving the mouse pointer to the area where it is, the user can click and be brought to the OilCop Support site.\n      o Need to include \"Assigned to:\" after \"Discrepancy Info\" section\n               • \"Engineering, comment, testing, future release\'',1,1,6,1563897230,1567176380),(275,8,0,0,316,3,1,136,0,0,'Oilcopsupport.com Discrepancy Changes','From the June 27th email\n\nThe OilCop support site discrepancy page lacks tracking the user who created the discrepancy, shows in email sent, and this needs to be fixed as well as there are times when the discrepancy has attachments that are missed due to no comments stating files were attached so the following are the changes needed.\n• Oilcop Support Discrepancy page\n               • Will track on the page \"Opened by […]\" like it does for all comments after creation\n      o Attachments tab\n               • \"Attachments\" title should be followed by the number of attachments in parenthesis if any files are attached.\n                     ? Example: \"Attachments (2)\"',1,1,6,1563897665,1573594068),(276,1,1,0,3,3,1,189,0,215,'Database filed to Synchronize','System has been unable to communicate with Team Viewer for last 30 days, customer cycled system power. Team viewer is now communicating. Take backup of system, when synchronizing data base system errors \"Database Failed to Synchronize\"',1,1,6,1563903948,1573592568),(277,1,0,0,316,3,1,136,0,0,'Admiral Copyright issue','From: Andrea Simonetto - Gartec Srl <a.> \nSent: Wednesday, July 10, 2019 4:29 AM\nTo: Mark McClatchey <mark@liquidynamics.com>\nCc: Mike Strong <mike.strong@viaanix.com>\nSubject: copyright in dashboard\nImportance: High\n\nHello Mark,\nlooks like in last T and R version the Gartec copyright has appeared again!!!!\nplease remove it immediately!\n\nkind regards\nAndrea',1,1,6,1563905153,1573594043),(278,1,0,0,316,3,1,136,0,0,'Variance Report - Download button','Added \"Download\" and \"Send by Email\" buttons to the Variance Report page',1,1,6,1563906435,1573595026),(279,1,0,0,316,3,1,136,0,0,'Variance Report - Adding the ability to see previous day\'s data','User\'s will be able to view data for previous days.',1,1,6,1563907093,1573594031),(280,1,4,0,315,3,1,136,0,0,'PO 16741 Quote Android app development to run OilCop Technicians desktop dispense page','Another date in the future will add Managers desktop and and Administration desktop',1,1,6,1564788767,1573594019),(281,1,4,0,315,3,1,136,0,0,'PO 16743 Quote tablet to replace TAC per Oilcop TAC Draft Spec July 8th 2019.','Initially Operate Technicians desktop dispense page Android Application',2,1,6,1564789562,1573594000),(282,1,0,0,3,315,1,244,0,248,'Customers home page on oilcopsupport.com will not display dispense, inventory or reports.','Installed new OilCop fluid management system at Bob Penkhus Mitsubishi in Colorado Springs, they are a customer of our distributor Colorado Petroleum. Set Bob Penkhus on oilcopsupport.com under Colorado Petroleum used the parts directors email address for mstrasner@bobpenkhus360.com  PW:123456 and enabled him with all permissions.\nEverything appears to work correctly for exception, no information is displayed on Bob Penkhus home page. One can view tank inventory by clicking on the Inventory button, however nothing shows up in reports or on the homepage. \n\nUsed this address for our distributor, Colorado Petroleum’s access to oilcopsupport.com Colorado@petroleum.com PW:123456. To set up Bob Penkus.\nIt would be appreciated if we could resolve this soon as we can, because Bo Penkhus is considering installing four more locations.',1,1,6,1566065054,1567168616),(283,3,11,0,315,3,1,136,0,0,'Autopsy Outdoor Tank Monitor Module testing in outside environment on rooftop','Monitor will communicate w/ Controller however none of the inputs 1,2,3,4 will register any probe values',2,2,6,1567014110,1567177840),(284,1,0,0,315,399,1,136,0,0,'Mecca Planning API for DMS Quote','Need an API to interface with Gartec Customer',0,1,6,1567170266,1666800797),(285,1,0,0,315,399,1,136,0,0,'Renault Trucks API for DMS system Quote','Gartec customer Renault is requesting an API to their DMS system',0,1,6,1567170617,1666800815),(286,1,5,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'20 foot probe reading incorrect level information','Appears the 20’ tank probe is reading the incorrect values, we tested using water and found the error is any ware from 7” – 9 ½” depending on the particular level. \n\nAttached is the spread sheet with the test results using water for the 20’ probe and 6’ probe.\nIn an attempt for a simple fix is there anything we can do with the algorithm to shift the entire line to match the gauge line?\n\nChecked with the probe manufacture they have not changed anything with the 20’ probe, don’t understand what could have happened.',1,1,6,1567178986,1578691550),(287,1,5,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'New tank probe slope definitions for 35\' tank probe','Mark,\nIf you were to get measurements for water, and 2 types of oil Bryan believes that would be sufficient so you could get by measuring just at every foot.  It would probably be best if you could use one light weight oil and one heavy weight oil.\nPlease raise a DR in Oilcop support using the company Viaan and reference in your PO.\nThanks….mike\n\nFrom: Mark McClatchey <mark@LiquiDynamics.com> \nSent: Wednesday, September 4, 2019 9:20 AM\nTo: Mike Strong <mike.strong@viaanix.com>\nCc: Craig Barth <craig@LiquiDynamics.com>\nSubject: RE: Adding new probe lengths\n\nMike,\nCan you confirm what measurement resolution we would need for 35’ i.e. 1”, ½”, ¼”? \nAlso if we need to collect info. for both water and one type of oil?\nThen after I collect the data, we will need a quote to have the slope information translated and added to the OilCop system.\nCraig, soon as I order/receive the probe and plot the slope information will need a PO to for Viaan to quote the modification.\nMark \n \nFrom: Mike Strong <mike.strong@viaanix.com> \nSent: Wednesday, September 4, 2019 9:04 AM\nTo: Mark McClatchey <mark@LiquiDynamics.com>\nCc: Liquidynamics - 300 <liquiddynamics@viaanix.com>\nSubject: RE: Adding new probe lengths\n\nMark,\nWe would not be able to use the 10’ probe data and would have to do a complete measurement/calibration for the 35 ft probe to ensure the slope is accurate.\nThanks….mike\n\nFrom: Mike Strong \nSent: Wednesday, September 4, 2019 8:58 AM\nTo: Mark McClatchey <mark@LiquiDynamics.com>\nCc: Liquidynamics - 300 <liquiddynamics@viaanix.com>\nSubject: RE: Adding new probe lengths\n\nOk, let me ask the question….mike\n\nFrom: Mark McClatchey <mark@LiquiDynamics.com> \nSent: Wednesday, September 4, 2019 8:42 AM\nTo: Mike Strong <mike.strong@viaanix.com>\nCc: Liquidynamics - 300 <liquiddynamics@viaanix.com>\nSubject: Adding new probe lengths\n\nMike,\nCould you check to see if we wanted to add a 35’ tank transducer to the OilCop tank monitoring system, do we have enough slope information from the 10’ transducer we can extended the same line to be used with the 35’ transducer?\nThank you,',1,1,6,1567608411,1666800853),(288,1,0,0,3,385,1,136,0,0,'Web team fixes','I believe discrepancies below are ones the web team could address.\n\nTank deliveries are shown on Daily reports after a delivery is made however, any transactions that occur the same day after the delivery are deducting from the delivery amount.  \nWhen adjusting tank inventory from the manager screen you are obligated to make a comment, however the comments are not seen anywhere in the reports.\nIn one of the updates tanks are now shown in the dashboard window in alphabetical order of product name, this is not correct. They need to be in left-to-right order according to tank number. \nWhen setting up Custom Shape Tank in “Update Tank” and Centimeters is selected the eight of tank in inches not Centimeters.',1,1,6,1570717667,1596031354),(289,1,1,0,3,3,1,112,0,0,'Buss Company / e4:3a:6e:01:55:2d will not update beyond R_2_22','Gartec has an OilCop system that will not update above R_2_22, when you log into the system from TV one can see versions R_2_17 – R_2_21 have been downloaded because Continue?  no longer has the blue hyper link color, its black. (Bus Company 2.png) However the system appears to have been updated to R_2_22 as indicated in the page footer however,  R_2_22 in the update list continues to have the blue hyper link color. Downloaded R_2_22 and performed the install process everything performed as it should, rebooted system continue to show ver. R_2_22 however, R_2_22 in the localhost/specific_version.php page has the blue hyper link color. Try to update to R_2_23 system it appears to download the update and install properly (Bus Company.png) however, after cycling the power the system continues to indicate current version of software is R_2_22.\n\nHaving no idea what I am doing logged into phpMyAdmin navigated to oilcop/t_maintenance/Columns/f_update_system/Browse, found f_flash had 9 rows of 1. (Bus Company3.png)     \n\nGuess we need someone to remote in to fix, I assume some kind of download table?? If possible my self and/or Zach would like to watch/to learn so maybe someday we could maybe address these simpler kind of kinds of issues our selfs if ??',1,1,6,1571161335,1574776915),(290,1,0,0,315,315,1,136,0,0,'To confirm calibration for 10\' and 20\' to work with Oil Cop System','To confirm calibration for 10\' and 20\' to work with Oil Cop System PO 16964 received.',1,1,6,1571235015,1571248002),(291,1,0,0,315,3,1,158,0,0,'Sensor page does not show any sensors','-Sensor Configuration 1.png page has no data displayed, then press “Add Sensor” Sensor Configuration 2.png as if your were going to add a sensor, no options are available in any of the drop down menu selection. However, the system shows tank inventory values. Indicated tank levels 3.png.',0,1,6,1571244842,1573485287),(292,1,0,0,315,315,1,0,0,0,'Cyrillic Language integration','Need to integrate Cyrillic (Russian) language into Oilcop',0,1,6,1573475391,1575982093),(293,1,1,0,3,399,1,136,0,0,'OilCop support demonstration accounts quit working two weeks ago.','Appears the calvin@customer.com, jim@oiljobber.com and dan@distributor.com demo accounts on oilcopsupport.com that angel setup no longer have a system associated with them. Do not know if it was broke because the data was supplied from the the Reliable Chevrolet system that the controller was changed because the old controller quit working or if a link was broke when fixing the system status for the Gartec system Bus Company 2. \nIs it possible for me to help maintain oilcopsupport.com using a web editor. We have added a sales representative firm with 20 sales people who all would like access to the demo account on oilcopsupport.com, so would like to have the latest OilCop version active as a demo.',1,1,6,1573497985,1666800904),(294,1,5,0,258,3,1,0,0,0,'TMM+Range Extender Hardwired Issue','Had some issues while configuring a controller for a customer.\n\nWas attempting to manually add the hardwired TMM+Range Extender to the component list, but could not get the CDM to pick up the components. I followed the provided instructions exactly.\n\nRan into some strange issues, tho. After being unable to connect the components to the system while hardwired together I decided I would try to connect them as separate components, both set to RADIO ON and addressed to 1. I found that each component would not connect to the system individually. What I mean by individually is I would plug in and power on the TMM, but leave the EXT unplugged and not powered, and vice versa, but neither component would connect. However, with both components plugged in and powered, the system would find them and I had all green bars. It seemed as though the system would only recognize them as a hardwired pair, but they were no longer hardwired together.\n\nI still could not get the two components to be recognized by the system as separate entities so I then added an FCM to the system to make sure the CDM was working properly. I also added a second TMM on another address, both of which worked as they should. Oddly, I removed turned the power off of the second TMM and changed the address of the original TMM to that of the second\'s and the system again would not recognize it. I then did the same experiment with the EXT and had the same result. Still, the two original PCBs for the TMM and EXT would only show up as ON in the system if the were not hardwired and powered at the same time.\n\nMark had mentioned something about the database and tables, so I then decided to re-clone the controller to clear out any memory that might be clashing with what I\'m trying to accomplish. After re-cloning, I set the addressed of both the original TMM and EXT and added them to the system, the CDM recognized them. After adding the components to the system individually I then powered them both down and went back through the instructions and hardwired them. I then went back into the component setup page and changed the addresses accordingly and the system now works as it should.\n\nMy main question that arose from all of this is, is there a particular order of operations that needs to happen for this setup to work properly or should the user be able to just do it or change it on the fly? That definitely wasn\'t the case in this scenario. Should I have been able to simply setup the TMM and EXT with the proper addresses for the hardwired setup and been able to turn them on and go from the beginning, or is it always the case where the user would have to add the TMM and EXT to the system separately first and only then they can change it after?\n\nApologies, this was a very strange and difficult thing to describe.',0,1,6,1574453097,1578766011),(295,1,0,0,315,315,1,190,0,195,'Bakersfield Trk. Center TMM-4 Stopped working 1.5 weeks after updating to R_30','TMM – 4 is showing up on the debugger however it is not registering under device status on the oilcop desktop. Overnighted an new TMM last Friday they installed it just now and the problem is the same showing up on the debugger not the desktop. This facility has been in operation for about a year.',1,3,6,1574870316,1574870399),(296,1,0,0,315,399,1,136,0,0,'Quote Cost to add Chinese Translation to OilCop System and OilCopsupport.com','Quote Cost to add Chinese Translation to OilCop System and OilCopsupport.com Chinese not for use with TAC',1,1,6,1575981528,1666800929),(297,1,0,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'Used Oil and Used Coolants only','“Used Oil and Used Coolant” are fluids typically collected and not dispensed from the system. Whenever a used fluid tank is full, management calls someone to pick up the used fluid. \nWould be nice to add to the daily reports when Used fluids were picked up. One possible way address is to “check” a box in “Product” page that tells system product/tank is collecting/receiving this product and cannot be assigned to a reel or station. Also will trigger line to be added to daily report, Used Oil/Coolant “Pick Up” xxx.x  gallons/quarts/liters to show that used fluids were removed from the tank. \n\nIf system did not have tank monitoring would require manager to manually input volume amount, if system was using tank monitor the monitor would automatically record the event.',0,1,5,1575990111,0),(298,1,5,0,258,3,1,189,0,215,'TMM going down?','Is there any way to look and see whether or not the TMM associated with the Rando 46 product lost connection to the system at any point within the past few weeks?\n\nTommy called on behalf of ASE and mentioned that they were having issues dispensing from that tank. Previously that morning ASE was dispensing from that tank, roughly 300 gallons, which took roughly 2.5 hours. They had to cycle the TMM before they could dispense because the system would not allow them to pump.\n\nThey are wanting to know if, when and how long the TMM lost connection to the system. Is there a way to look into this?\n\nRobert said he would be back at that location next week and will call to review.',1,2,6,1576176780,1579720836),(299,8,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'E.H Wolf can not add another system to one of their existing customers','EH Wolf is a OilCop distributor, they have a customer Michels Corporation who is installing OilCop tank monitoring in multiple locations. From EH Wolfs www.oilcopsupport desktop (rtroeller@ehwolf.com 123456) Add system/Select Customer/  https://oilcopsupport.com/index.php/create_system  no way to add another location?  \n\nNew location: Building 28      \nMac address:  00:e0:4c:2b:c3:47\n\n\"Name on Team Viewer: Building 28- E.H. Wolf\"',0,1,6,1576255741,1579721043),(300,1,0,0,3,0,1,0,0,0,'Tank monitor level out put will intermittently spike high or low','Have been observing an occasional anomaly with tank monitor systems for couple of years, where tank monitor level output intermittently spikes high or low causing erroneous readings. I suspect latest email from Andrea regarding monitor incorrectly reading 204.11cm when the tanks maximum height is 153.4cm is related to this.\n\nHave been trying to figure this out for some time, one can observe this problem occurring at the Don Hattan OilCop location in Park City regularly. \n\nViewing the Don Hattan 12/23/19 daily Variance Report it shows at 3:00 PM the tank sensor changed -499.4 Quarts and they only dispensed 40.0 Quarts.\n\nViewing the Don Hattan 12/23/19 hourly Variance Report it shows a large change in sensor volumes four different hour time stamps -212.6 / 10.3 Q dispensed,  -404.5/ 14.3 dispensed, -381.8 / 13.7Q dispensed, -566 / 20 q dispensed\n\nAny ideas how we can figure this out ?',0,1,3,1577556412,0),(301,1,1,0,3,399,1,237,0,241,'System extremely show, customer is about to pull the system out','Parks Ford ADG OilCop system, on team viewer, is running extremally slow and particularly slow when working in work order maintenance. Appears they have 3225 closed work orders and  3925 open work orders oldest work order was dated 5/24/2019. \n\nWhile waiting for the work order page to open repeatedly get a “Warning: Unresponsive script error” see Parks Ford.png\nPressing the continue button will allow the page to open then select a work order another screen opens with no graphics see Parks Ford2.png.\nHave rebooted the system, updated from Ver R2_30  to Ver R2_31 no change in symptoms.\n\nNot sure if the issue is related to too many open work orders, if I knew how to get in to the work order tables would like to delete/purge all of the open work orders 30 days or older.',1,2,6,1580252075,1666801090),(302,1,1,0,3,399,1,164,0,142,'System memory low error and becoming slow.','United BMW system has low memory error, when remoteting in, the system is behaving as if its about to shut down. Don\'t thinks its open work orders they only have two pages of open work orders. viewing from the managers work order maint page.\nWhen viewing reports system is showing data base error and possible remedy. See database attachment. \nWas able to back up the system, however there is not enough room to download the backup. The system is so full the tank gauge icons are not showing up on the desktop. See attachments for the various errors.\nsystem is currently working.',0,1,6,1580854717,1666801115),(303,1,0,0,3,399,1,220,0,225,'Can not access any reports.','When trying to access logs PAG Porsche of Monmouth OilCop system displays  Database Error Occurred. Error Number: 1030 ,    “Got error 28 from storage engine”\n\nSystem is still functioning, however the behavior seems like the controller is shutting down resources to keep its self running.\nWas able to back up the system, copy of back up and database error screen shot attached.',0,1,6,1581372209,1666801203),(304,8,0,0,315,385,1,136,0,0,'LiquiDynamics.com site needs various fixes','LiquiDynamics.com site needs to have sales map added, About Us link changed, SSL enabled, Captcha to prevent spam',1,1,6,1581765818,1596030908),(305,1,1,0,3,399,1,258,0,271,'#5531  Green bay E.H. Wolf CPU usage overloading.','Location was installed approximately 30 days ago, has eleven TMMs with 44 sensors. This is the largest tank monitoring system we have installed to date.\nBoth manager and admin desktop tank level icons are partially displayed, mouse over the tank icons blue window is slow to respond. TMM 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 11 device status are red and they are all located in the same room as the CDM.\nSystem is behaving as if its memory is full, very slow. Refreshing the desktop will temporarily allow the Icons to display information.\nAppears Firefox %CPU is running between 98% – 102% guessing something in Fire fox is overloading the processor.\nMaybe the system/CDM timing needs to be adjusted.. Might be something to ask Bryan??',0,1,6,1582142264,1666801234),(306,1,1,0,3,385,1,237,0,0,'Manager / Work order maintenance extremely slow','This is location we had to work on the data base because of amount of open WO’s.\n\nThey called today seems the system is extremely slow when working with work order maintenance, everything else seems to be snappy. TOP = CPU 6 – 8 % when opening work order maintenance page. CPU usage goes to 103% and eventually throws a Unresponsive script error. see attachment \nWe need to address this soon as we can, the manager is getting irritated. Appears they are a very fast paced facility.',0,1,6,1582837399,1596030755),(307,1,0,0,3,399,1,182,0,187,'No one can access the system','Had customer reboot the controller, system did not show up on team viewer and continues to be unresponsive.\nPlugged in USB key board in and pressed the enter button, no change in symptom.\nCustomer is overnight the controller back to LD, should have it Monday AM to put on the bench.',0,1,6,1582998267,1666801278),(308,1,1,0,3,385,1,189,0,194,'ASE Milwaukee system is down.... Data base error 1114 Tables t_adjust_work order is full','log into system says low disk space only 271.0 MB disk remaining.\nTop command, cpu usage 6.9%',1,3,6,1583166230,1596030597),(309,1,0,0,258,0,1,260,0,272,'Inventory Question','Does a report exist that this customer is able to print out that would tell him what inventory he has waiting to be dispensed on open work orders that have yet to be dispensed? I searched through the logs and only saw columns \'Amount Dispensed\' which would, understandably, be empty on the open work orders chart, since no product has been dispensed. Can we implement a printer friendly log that a customer can review and be better able to predict their inventory for future purchasing?',0,1,5,1583507576,0),(310,1,0,0,258,399,1,189,0,215,'Dispenses not logging again.','ASE Wausau is having issues with dispenses not logging in their system again.\n\nRobert described the issue that upon opening an order and clicking \'Start\' they will receive the popup \'Pump Started Unsuccessfully\' but the order will still be dispensed. When this happens that dispense will not be recorded in the logs.\n\nPlease advise.',1,1,6,1583522095,1666801341),(311,1,0,0,315,315,1,136,0,0,'PO 17322 Labor to Unsolder Radio Chip from 100812-01 & install on 100815LZ & 100816LZ MfgNo : Labor','Labor to Unsolder Radio Chip, Zipbee, from 100812-01 & install on 100815LZ & 100816LZ\nMfgNo : Labor\n\nNote:  Attempted by ESI engineers, amount unknown, but was mentioned that some or all they would not communicate afterwards.  Removed from 3 boards and then tested boards installed on with test system 216 and could not get communication to the controller through Zigbee.  Troubleshooting continues.',2,2,6,1584045610,1589921949),(312,1,1,0,3,385,1,0,0,0,'New revision controller, need to configure drivers for OilCop system','Update OilCop driver definitions.',1,3,6,1584453358,1596030502),(313,1,1,0,3,385,1,257,0,268,'Database error # 126','When selecting to view Logs / Tank Adjustments, displays database error 126. \nSee attachment',0,1,6,1584467960,1594643170),(314,1,0,0,3,399,1,150,0,128,'5W/30 and Used Oil tank not available','Reliable Chevrolet tank monitor in back of the shop that is connected to 0W/20 & Used Oil tanks quit working, to trouble shoot the issue moved front module connected to 0W/20 tank to the back shop and connect it to 5W/30 Synthetic and Used Oil Tank.\nFrom Sensor configuration try to add sensor, only tank selection available from the drop down menu is 0W/20, 5W/30 & Used Oil are not listed. \nCan we see if this is a data base issue?',0,1,6,1585162213,1666801476),(315,1,0,0,315,385,1,136,0,0,'Build 396 LD-22A-00 pcba for mini Oilbar, ref VXSO-315','Build 396 LD-22A-00 pcba for mini Oilbar, ref VXSO-315. Email sent with SO requesting PO be sent',2,1,6,1585222465,1594643034),(316,1,1,0,3,399,1,8,0,0,'Power down and Restart buttons on the managers desktop intermittently cause lockup on reboot','Power down and Power Restart buttons on the managers desktop do not function.',1,1,6,1586435355,1666801497),(317,1,0,0,3,0,1,8,0,0,'Tank Monitor solution time out must be turned on in order for tank monitor to work.','Tank monitor solution time out is used to set how long a reel will stay activated before it times out. This feature is not supposed to be  functional until Tank monitor solution is turned on in administrative options. It has been a known issue for awhile thought we had fixed it couple of month ago.. The work around for now is to leave tank monitor solution enabled.',0,1,5,1586438812,0),(318,8,0,0,315,385,1,136,0,0,'liquidynamics.com Manual website Manuals page enhancements requested','The Manuals page on the liquidynamics.com site needs to be organized better.  A Manuals Category page needs to be created to allow the webmaster to be able to categorize Manuals appropriately.  See attach for initial notes on changes requested. Ref VXSO-318',1,1,6,1586786462,1594642970),(319,9,0,0,315,385,1,0,0,0,'Steve\'s changes to Liquidynamics.com website 46731098','See attached for details about requested changes.',1,1,6,1589335952,1596030366),(320,1,0,0,315,315,1,136,0,0,'Labor to Unsolder Radio Chip from 100812-01 & install on 100815LZ & 100816LZ','Labor to Unsolder Radio Chip from 100812-01 & install on 100815LZ & 100816LZ',2,1,6,1589918702,1589918850),(321,1,0,0,258,399,1,0,0,0,'TAC Firmware Question','Noticed some strangeness with putting different TAC firmware onto boards.\n\nAfter downloading firmware onto TACs the intro page on the LCD screen will read as follows:\n TAC_1_5_3 reads ‘Admiral v1.5.3’\n        TAC_3_0_3 reads ‘Liquidynamics v1.5’\n TAC_3_0_5 reads ‘Liquidynamics v1.5.3’\n TAC_3_0_6g reads ‘OilCop v1.5.4’\n TAC_3_0_8a reads ‘Admiral v1.5.6’\n\nAm I missing something regarding why the version number on the TAC LCD screen differs from the HEX file name? Why does the version number go backwards from TAC_3_0_3 to TAC_3_0_5?\n\nMore importantly, which is truly the correct firmware that we need to install onto the boards for Gartec, Liquidynamics & Admiral going forward?',0,1,6,1590161352,1666801568),(322,1,0,0,385,385,261,8,0,0,'Finished updating to R_25 now its saying 130 Database error.','Please remote into a customers controller on the bench at our office it was R 23 just finished updating to R_25 now its saying 130 Database error. Name of the system on TV is Dennis Oil',1,1,6,1591055921,1596030383),(323,9,0,0,385,0,261,8,0,0,'OilcopSupport.com and Staging sites, liquidynamics.com and oilcopsupport.com, hosting need to change','Currently Oilcop Support.com and the staging sites for liquidynamics.com and oilcopsupport.com are being hosted by Viaanix along with support programs and services.  In a move to consolidate and control cost more effectively the websites and support programs and services needs to be moved to a site hosted by current vendor River City or to a Managed service by Strong Solutions either on AWS or Azure.  The Staging sites meant to test out fixes and enhancements before pushing the changes to the Production site.  Staging sites are the customer final sign off for changes.\n\nCost request have been request from the vendors for evaluation.',1,1,5,1591067736,0),(324,1,1,0,3,385,1,0,0,0,'Updated from R_24 to R-25 after reboot now says Database error Occurred','Currently the controller is on liquidynamics bench listed on Team Viewer as: Craftsmen Utility Trailer\n-Updated from R_24 to R-25 after reboot now says Database error Occurred, Error Number:130 Incorrect file format \'t_administrative_options\'\nSELECT * FROM (\'t_administrative_options\'\nFilename: /var/WWW/oilcop/helpers/util_helper.php\nLine Number: 50',0,1,6,1592431642,1596030426),(325,1,0,0,1,385,1,8,0,0,'When Odometer is entered from the TAC the value in the DB table is invalid','When Odometer is entered from the TAC the value in the DB table is invalid.  Does display numbers but not close to what the odometer value entered was.  Entering an odometer reading from a webpage works as designed.\n\nThis DR is for PO 17521',1,1,6,1592448012,1596030448),(326,1,1,0,3,385,1,112,0,0,'Update Security Vulnerabilities','Received email from Gartec, one of their customers is requiring we update oilcop controller security vulnerabilities ASAP!\nSee attached security report.',1,2,6,1594044554,1596030322),(327,1,0,0,385,385,261,0,0,0,'Mini Display will not program without giving an error','Using the programmer the program will error out no matter what file is used to program the mini displays. It basically states that it cannot find the attached device.when programming.  Have seen this error the last time but after regenerating the hex file it all worked.  This time that did not correct the problem.',0,1,6,1594647993,1596030273),(328,1,0,0,385,399,261,8,0,0,'Factory Reset Code Needs To Be Confirmed','Create flow charts from code analysis to determine whether or not it is correctly working as required.  \n\nEnsure there is a clear definition of what Factory Reset means and what it should do.  \n\nCurrent definition of Factory reset is ALL DB tables will be reset to default values as initially set from the factory.',1,1,6,1595832846,1666801599),(329,1,0,0,385,399,261,0,0,0,'Modify css to allow web pages to display correctly on tablets and modify Ubuntu file permissions','Modify css files and web page code so that web pages will scale correctly when view on tablets with 7\" screens.\n\nModify Ubuntu file permissions to better secure source code and application files from unauthorized changes and being viewed.',1,1,6,1596649073,1666801638),(330,1,1,0,3,385,1,0,0,0,'Security Update scope changed to include added tasks.','Add the following task to the scope:  Test procedures developed on multiple controllers.  Revise written procedures for users not as familiar with Linux systems.  Create new image for controller builds that have the security updates included.  Test building controllers with new Security Update Image.',0,1,6,1596654709,1596670720),(331,1,1,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Perform misc task for oilcop support to improve customer controller builds','Troubleshoot issues with why clonezilla does not correctly load on new controllers.  Build new image to include R32 to speed up build process.  Setup controller so that a separate image could be created that is Gartec specific and create Gartec image after Andrea sets it up.  Test upgrading Ubuntu software version to18.xx.  Troubleshoot issues with Teamviewer on software version updates.\n\nPlease Invoice this DR two weeks after Invoicing \"Security Update scope changed to include added tasks\" DR.',0,1,6,1596654899,1666801675),(332,9,0,0,385,399,261,0,0,0,'eCatalog is ready for upload but website does not support this feature.','eCatalog is ready for upload.  Currently there is not functionality for this feature and it needs to be developed.  The ecatalog can be implemented in a fairly show time frame, about 2 hours, but this is only temporary and would not allow for any updating of the catalog once implemented or the addition of any new emedia.  This temp fix also breaks the version control implemented so far so changes to the website and definition of the process needs to be developed and need a PO to implement necessary changes.',0,1,6,1597006296,1666801695),(333,1,1,0,3,3,1,258,0,271,'EHwolf can not see any tank information for their GreenBay location on oilcopsupport.com','From: Bobby Lemmer\nSent: Thursday, August 27, 2020 8:00 AM\nTo: Mark McClatchey\nCc: Robert Troeller\nSubject: Oil Cop Support Website\n\nHi Mark,\n\nI went on to the website to look at tank inventories at our Green Bay location yesterday and it did not show any tanks, including any customer tanks.  I checked again this morning and I cant see anything.  Is this something on the website side or our side that we cant see any of these?\n\nThanks,\n\nBobby Lemmer\nWarehouse Manager\nE.H. Wolf & Sons\n262-644-5030  Ext. 250',1,1,6,1598540605,1602703678),(334,9,0,0,385,3,261,0,0,0,'Update PHP and CodeIgnitor software for Liquidynamcis.com website.','The LDI.com site failed vulnerability scans and was hacked by outside entities through a CodeIgniter vulnerability according to the providers who host the site on their system.  Quoting resources to fully upgrade PHP and CodeIgniter software as well as rewrite code that is using deprecated commands, functions, etc.to get site backup in the most timely manner and demo any new user experience that may now be available after the update.',1,3,6,1599870440,1602703643),(335,2,0,0,385,385,261,0,0,0,'Research how make changes to the Oilcop Junior Source Code files','At this time it is unclear as to what IDE and compliers to use to make changes to the Oilcop Jr. firmware files.  Research is needed to so that the information can be passed on to the new developers.',1,1,6,1600633031,1601515255),(336,1,2,0,3,385,1,0,0,0,'CDM will not program','New batch of 100 CDM received from Bittele will not program.',1,1,6,1601559237,1603156237),(337,1,0,0,3,399,1,8,0,0,'Duplicate Mac address','10/7/20\nHi Mark,\njust configured a controller for Filcar, MAC address 00:e0:4c:28:ee:a5\nApparently:\n It’s a double MAC address, the other one has been configured (that time too for Filcar) in February, it was a controller received a while ago since it was R_2_24 originally, brought to 31 in February\n In the teamviewer list, it appear only 1x 00:e0:4c:28:ee:a5 (offline 1+ month)\n In oilcopsupport.com they were both appearing ON while I was syncing this one\nCould you please check the reason, how to manage, … ?\nThanks, kind regards\nAndrea',0,1,6,1602703012,1670861098),(338,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'technicians still being blocked even after R_2_25?','[2:15 PM] Mark McClatchey\n    technicians still being blocked even after R_2_25? \nDo these technicians PIN begin with Zero 0?\n No, this is happening also to new controller with “newer” versions (meaning after the 2_25 that should have fixed this issue), and now it’s not possible to add technicians with PIN starting with 0.',0,1,6,1602703079,1666801987),(339,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Controller not sending emails anymore','We have a couple of controllers not sending scheduled emails anymore (not all, only specific emails – daily report, transaction report – the triggered ones are sent normally).\nI will try to have the database tomorrow, and will test if a factory reset may change something or not.. but we need ideas about why and how to fix it\nPlease send copy of data base\nThis is the controller: 00:e0:4c:21:cf:6d\nYou can find the last backup attached to this email',0,1,6,1602703268,1670936292),(340,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Communication stopping','A lot of times we still have, even after R_2_30 or R_2_32, the devices stopping communicating with the system, FCM not opening channels giving “pump start was unsuccessful” and TAC returning error 255. Only way to fix it was factory reset, never fixed in another way (updating firmware, replacing devices – including CDM – changing addresses, …)\nThink this might be related to setting the CDM address to #1. Can you test by addressing the CDM to 0 Zero\n\nWe are currently testing this solution, unfortunately this issue is not happening in a specific occasion so will take time to see if this is fixing it or not.',0,1,6,1602703521,1666802981),(341,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Controller trying to send emails','A customer IT found that their controller is trying to send an email to Aruba provider every 10minutes, but it’s blocked from their system.\nDo you have an idea of what’s this? Oilcopsupport? What else?\nThis could be an error by googles mail server the system uses. Please provide Mac address so we can remote in to investigate\n\n00:e0:4c:28:ee:68 (Bus Company new controller)',0,1,6,1602703779,1666803159),(342,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'controllers not switching off or not rebooting from manager’s menu','This is happening quite often, I understood it was a problem from Linux.. apparently we had this issue on a controller yesterday, after factory reset (due for other problems), it returned to work. This is unfortunately not happening everytime, full of controllers that after update to R_2_25 or newer version stop switching off/rebooting, while they were doing before the update\nCan you provide a mac address we can remote into to investigate\n\nI will provide you 2 or 3 as soon as I find them back in my memory/archive. (Think one is 00:e0:4c:21:cf:25 and another one is 00:e0:4c:28:ec:cd)\nThe last one (00:E0:4C:21:CD:4C, Filcar’s showroom) has been fixed when we made factory reset 2 days ago. We made factory reset because of problem #20008LQD_OC, and customer confirmed us that this fixed also the switching off issue.',0,1,6,1602703865,1666803591),(343,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Exporting incorrect dispense units if time & date are configured to MM/DD/YY','One new bug we found is that if you have time & date configured to MM/DD/YY, no matter if you have admin options set to “liters” both for transactions and reports, but the exported txt file will send the data with “quarters” units…',0,1,6,1602706766,1666804234),(344,1,0,0,3,3,1,112,0,0,'Can we schedule how to fix my T controller?','Hi Mark,\nunfortunately I wasn’t able to test this T version, as I have no more T controller in my office: the one we have here is blocked with database error, and I need someone to fix it..\nFrom description, it would be ok if working! Doesn’t need a firmware update?',0,1,6,1602708202,1647438597),(345,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Translation file update?','has the translation file been fully updated?',0,1,6,1602710514,1666804254),(346,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'20005LQD Gartec controller IP address aren\'t recognized','Happening on at least 5 controllers of last shipment:\n1/ MAC e4:3a:6e:29:af:f4\n2/ MAC e4:3a:6e:2d:a2:34\n3/ MAC e4:3a:6e:2d:a0:81\n4/ MAC e4:3a:6e:2d:a5:45\n5/ MAC e4:3a:6e:2e:bb:4a\nAll of them are not responding to the IP address, you enter on Linux and you can see the IP configuration is correct (on the oilcop website and on the terminal with ifconfig command – check pictures). We tried changing the IP configuration (we tested 192.168.0.223, 192.168.1.120, 192.168.1.155 with relevant parameters): it switches on the controller, but it’s impossible to ping it, to connect via browser or via winscp. On the browser (not on Linux, on a PC connected to the same network), you type the IP address and it automatically switches to “localhost”, giving connection error. Both with http or https, it does not really change. Attached pictures and you can download the video here: https://wetransfer.com/downloads/ea775453ab64d86ff159b2d5954536f220200929151610/5364b046b7890893072ad458a09ee7ac20200929152144/6d80ee \n\nBelieve this is related to the latest internet security protocol update. First time entering the IP address in the URL prefix the IP address with https:// and IP address. The web page will respond with the question  “you accept the risk”. Answer YES\n\nI didn’t realize that the address was switching to “localhost”, Fabrizio told me he happened to him too with last controller he configured.\nBut, this is not helping: we were able to communicate with other controllers that have the same security update, so we know how to do with https.\nMoreover, checking the MAC addresses, the 5 we’re having problems with have been curiously shipped all together: attached your invoice with MAC addresses – I’m considering that your E43A632DA545 (which can’t be found in teamviewer list) is actually e4:3a:6e:2d:a5:45. (also, e4:3a:6e:2d:a5:45 is listed twice in teamviewer list)\nSo, couldn’t it be that something/some configuration step/anything is missing on these 5 controllers?\nI wrote it’s impossible to ping them or to connect via winscp: this is not depending on using http or https and accepting the risk…',0,1,6,1603142066,1666804603),(347,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'20003LQD_OC   technicians still being blocked even after R_2_25','no starting notes for this\nDo these technicians PIN begin with Zero 0?\n\nNo, this is happening also to new controller with “newer” versions (meaning after the 2_25 that should have fixed this issue), and now it’s not possible to add technicians with PIN starting with 0.',0,1,6,1603142699,1666804653),(348,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'20004LQD_OC controllers not switching off or not rebooting from manager’s menu','This is happening quite often, I understood it was a problem from Linux.. apparently we had this issue on a controller yesterday, after factory reset (due for other problems), it returned to work. This is unfortunately not happening everytime, full of controllers that after update to R_2_25 or newer version stop switching off/rebooting, while they were doing before the update\nCan you provide a mac address we can remote into to investigate\n\nI will provide you 2 or 3 as soon as I find them back in my memory/archive. (Think one is 00:e0:4c:21:cf:25 and another one is 00:e0:4c:28:ec:cd)\nThe last one (00:E0:4C:21:CD:4C, Filcar’s showroom) has been fixed when we made factory reset 2 days ago. We made factory reset because of problem #20008LQD_OC, and customer confirmed us that this fixed also the switching off issue.',0,1,6,1603142745,1666804676),(349,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'20006LQD_OC Controller trying to send emails','A customer IT found that their controller is trying to send an email to Aruba provider every 10minutes, but it’s blocked from their system.\nDo you have an idea of what’s this? Oilcopsupport? What else?\nThis could be an error by googles mail server the system uses. Please provide Mac address so we can remote in to investigate\n\n00:e0:4c:28:ee:68 (Bus Company new controller)',0,1,6,1603142788,1666804700),(350,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'20007LQD_OC Controller not sending emails anymore','We have a couple of controllers not sending scheduled emails anymore (not all, only specific emails – daily report, transaction report – the triggered ones are sent normally).\nI will try to have the database tomorrow, and will test if a factory reset may change something or not.. but we need ideas about why and how to fix it\nPlease send copy of data base\n\nThis is the controller: 00:e0:4c:21:cf:6d\nYou can find the last backup attached to this email',0,1,6,1603142847,1666804751),(351,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'20008LQD_OC Communication stopping','A lot of times we still have, even after R_2_30 or R_2_32, the devices stopping communicating with the system, FCM not opening channels giving “pump start was unsuccessfull” and TAC returning error 255. Only way to fix it was factory reset, never fixed in another way (updating firmware, replacing devices – including CDM – changing addresses, …)\nThink this might be related to setting the CDM address to #1. Can you test by addressing the CDM to 0 Zero\n\nWe are currently testing this solution, unfortunately this issue is not happening in a specific occasion so will take time to see if this is fixing it or not.',0,1,6,1603142887,1666804779),(352,1,0,0,3,385,1,112,0,0,'Controller in Colombia Data base','Controller in Colombia 00:e0:4c:28:2a:98 \nAttached last database backups.\n\nYesterday a technician (I’m waiting the report to understand what he did and why) made some mistakes for changing/deleting some FCM/reel…\nAnd I don’t know if before or after that, he tried to update the system, from I guess version 30 to something else…\nNow the system shows no version, in the database there is written version “0”!!! And trying to go to making an update, see the “update screen” screenshot…\nI tried to restore a database, it said successful but nothing changed in terms of version and possibility to update…',0,1,6,1603211499,1620174625),(353,8,0,0,1,399,1,0,0,0,'File system full','The file system was full from archived log files and unused system email so no more data could be written, which totaled about 2G.',2,3,6,1603927837,1630520232),(354,9,0,0,385,0,261,0,0,0,'Error happens when adding a new product.','Steve ran into an issue entering a new product, it produces an error.',0,1,2,1605197756,0),(355,9,0,0,3,385,1,0,0,0,'Setup Web hosting environment for liquidynamics.com','Setup web hosting environment to work with liquidynamics.com',1,2,6,1609256196,1620175223),(356,1,1,0,3,385,1,0,0,0,'Jordan system','appears some transactions are not completing themselves. see .pdf of completed work orders, Work Order Maintenance and Transaction journal you will see wo 46094,46066 and 46088 dispensed fluid however did not dispense complete or close work order even-though dispense complete is set to 20 minutes. While logged in changed dispense complete timeout from 20 minute to 10 minutes to see if anything changed.',1,1,6,1611236278,1620176234),(357,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Italian system','Appears everything is set up properly. Added my email address to see what reports i receive. \nAndrea\'s email - \"this system is not sending some email (some instead is correctly sent)\" Mark M---  Can you please elaborate more about the issue, what email is correctly sent? What email is not, Is it a particular user or a report that not being sent? Andrea-- I will check again next days and let you know exactly: basically they have multiple automatic reports ON, they’re receiving all alarms (low level, re-order..) – and I am receiving them too, but the daily report is not sent by the controller. If you manually send a daily report, it arrives.',1,1,6,1611236374,1666805133),(358,1,0,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Emailed Re Order Reports','OilCop Graphic takes up entire email page, leaving reorder information at bottom of page. Make the OilCop graphic smaller ribbon at the top maybe format',1,1,6,1611238992,1630521323),(359,1,0,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Emailed Re Order Reports','OilCop Graphic takes up entire email page, leaving reorder information at bottom of page. Make the OilCop graphic smaller ribbon at the top maybe format',1,1,6,1611239027,1611243100),(360,1,1,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Emailed Re Order Reports','OilCop Graphic takes up entire email page, leaving reorder information at bottom of page. Make the OilCop graphic smaller ribbon at the top maybe format',1,1,6,1611239053,1611243091),(361,1,1,0,3,3,1,0,0,0,'Emailed Re Order Report','OilCop Graphic takes up entire email page, leaving reorder information at bottom of page. Make the OilCop graphic smaller ribbon at the top maybe format',1,1,6,1611239136,1611243083),(362,1,1,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Current image we are using for Liquidynamic and Gartec is causing a PHP error in Work Order Maint.','See attachment.\nYou can find the workorder in “t_adjust_workorder”, but not in the other table “t_workorder_details”, so it gives you the error.\nAdding a new WO from WO management and/or deleting the row in “t_adjust_workorder” is obviously fixing the issue.',1,1,6,1611242934,1630520190),(363,1,1,0,3,399,1,164,0,142,'Can not update SMPT Settings','Attempted to update SMTP settings 3 times, each time system returns error that says \"The from email field can not exceed 25 characters in length\".\nSee attachments.',1,1,6,1611868390,1624969904),(364,1,1,0,3,399,1,0,0,0,'Litha Automotive','Appears to have a data base issue. On 12/23/2020 at 1:35 PM a work order was entered into the system, WO 580687 Justin Montoya Station 8 selected 5W/20. The exact same time stamp, WO is repeated on 23 pages in Manager/Work Order Maintenance. When selecting work order maintenance the browser asked to wait or stop loading the browser page.',1,1,6,1611936524,1624969709),(365,1,1,0,3,399,1,8,0,3,'Scott Robinson - Wiley equipment','During installation could not get TMM-1 to connect, originally set all devices in one sequential order not all modules were not coming on line. Re-address everything segmented by device, most devices radio linked up for exception of TMM-Waste which was TMM-1 before updating address after deleting to reenter hardware devices. After trying new address settings never used before would not connect, we hard wired TMM-Waste and it worked. So then reconfigured as wireless, same issue would not connect with radio. Then used power supply from a working FCM-4/ \"East Wall\" that had radio linked to power TMM-Waste, the radio did not link up. Reconnected original power supply to TMM-Waste waited about 15 minutes TMM-Waste connected. \nThen reinstalled power supply to FCM-4/ \"East Wall\" it has not reconnected in 24 hours.\nUsing debugger logs the controller is calling out for FCM address 1 however, FCM- address 1 is not responding to the calls. \nRemoted into location Friday feb.19th  all devices appear to be on line fore exception of FCM-4/\"East Wall\", interesting to note Waste oil tank is not registering which is connected to TMM-Waste Tanks (address 1) probe using input 1. Input 2 (Waste water) and input 3 (Waste Coolant) readout is fluctuating indicating they are active.\nTuesday 2/23/19 remoted in TMM-0W20, FCM-4/ \"East Wall\", TMM-Portable all are now off line.\nCould a bad CDM cause these issue, or would it be all or no devices would communicate? see layout attached.',0,1,6,1614117631,1624967421),(366,1,1,0,3,399,1,8,0,0,'When starting up new systems bogus transaction appaears','When setting up new systems bogus transaction appears as first transaction listed in Work Order Maintenance.\nDate created 12/31/1969 06:00 PM.\nSee attachment',0,1,6,1614617817,1624967290),(367,1,1,0,3,385,1,268,0,282,'Will not release network settings when set for DHCP','System set to DHCP yes, will not release network settings to accept new settings issued by DHCP server.',1,1,6,1615040678,1620178760),(368,2,8,0,385,399,261,0,0,0,'ESCP Oilcop Jr White Labeling','Configure the current Oilcop Jr software to specifications attached.',1,1,6,1616632494,1649086346),(369,1,0,0,385,385,261,0,0,0,'Network vulnerability scans showed Oilcop system controller has security vulnerabilities.','See attached list from Pantropic',0,1,6,1619533466,1619533895),(370,1,0,0,385,385,261,0,0,0,'Network vulnerability scans showed Oilcop system controller has security vulnerabilities.','See attached list from Pantropic',0,1,6,1619533473,1619533886),(371,1,0,0,385,0,261,0,0,0,'Network vulnerability scans showed Oilcop system controller has security vulnerabilities.','See attached list from Pantropic controller reported by their IT department.',0,1,3,1619533550,0),(372,1,1,0,385,399,261,0,0,0,'DHCP does not work correctly','Python or web code will need to be changed so that it modifies the system files correctly to allow for reserved IP address by DHCP.  Since it is the file system that is being modified it may not require any web code changes and only Python changes.',1,1,6,1620178884,1624967241),(373,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Cannot dispense from any station','The range extender on the TMM cycles between green and red status.  All devices that could be reached were power cycled as well the controller was rebooted but system still remained inactive.  No TV support but they can update the system which was at R31.  IP address of controller is 10.61.69.70, mac 00:e0:4c:ae:83:9a.  They have six stations.  Performed an reel autocalibration and the oil would only barely stream out when trigger was pulled.  The system measured 14 pulses only.  So they could dispense had them bypass the PSM.  Further troubleshooting required.',2,3,6,1624966914,1627310943),(374,1,3,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Road Machinery can\'t dispense from 15W/40 reel','Reel was missing from the station.',1,2,6,1627310318,1627310434),(375,1,3,0,399,399,1,206,0,209,'System would dispense over the amount preset and sometimes not count.','Initially they didn\'t say any specific reel had the issue but upon further investigation it was revealed that station 1 reel 2 would dispense but would not count and would over dispense fluid. Fernado called.',2,2,6,1631718202,1631718379),(376,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Tank showing low level alarm','Jason West from Murphy Tractor called to ask why they have a low level alarm when the tank has over 348 gallons of oil.',0,1,6,1631723929,1631723994),(377,1,3,0,399,399,1,267,0,281,'After power outage Express Lane FCM failed to work','Shawn Wiley called and reported they took a power hit and the entire system went down but the controller.  When power was restored all came back online work except for the express lane\'s FCM.',2,2,6,1632342992,1632343004),(378,1,3,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Walt for Peacock Ford stated techs were locking reels and over dispensing','Reported that all stations using 10W/30 product were over dispensing.',0,1,6,1633016243,1633016392),(379,1,1,0,399,399,1,220,0,0,'Security vulnerabilities on controller reported by IT','Irvin called to say that their IT department said the Oilcop controller needs to be moved to a VPN due to the outdate software exposing security vulnerabilities.',0,1,6,1633720283,1633720418),(380,1,0,0,348,399,236,236,0,240,'Report issues','I have to reset the computer daily to access reports and still get an error trying to access the tank adjustment journal.  please help',1,1,6,1636487496,1649877995),(381,1,0,0,399,399,1,237,0,241,'Dashboard wasn\'t updating tank values.','System showed all green for all devices but dashboard tanks were not updating as they normally should.  Gave no indication of values changing ever few seconds.',1,2,6,1636492099,1666798778),(382,1,1,0,3,399,1,223,0,228,'Controller will not power up.','Customer found no 12Vdc output from the power supply, tried another power supply(?) controller would not come on. They are overnighting controller, power supply and CDM - \"they dropped the CDM and broke the case\", for us to repair and overnight back to them.',2,3,6,1638192101,1638910407),(383,1,0,0,348,399,236,236,0,240,'Oil Cop is down, I cannot get it to stay green.','All components are offline< I have reset twice today.  Also could not access reports again today.   Please expedite!',1,3,6,1638909553,1639075060),(384,1,1,0,3,399,1,177,0,265,'Controller not communicating locally and oilcop support and team viewer - EH wolf','Rebooted controller, did not hear beep when powering up. plugged key board into controller pressed enter button no change in symptom. ethernet port has orange light network switch blinking, reseat both RJ45 connectors no change.\nRobert will call back when he returns from meeting..',1,2,6,1639588808,1649086323),(385,1,0,0,348,399,236,236,0,240,'Oil cop is loosing connected devices','Hi I have had to reboot twice today and the system is down again now. All of the devices show red.',0,1,6,1641839315,1649877117),(386,1,3,0,399,399,1,8,0,0,'Clearwater toyota FCM 13 shows red on the dashboard','All other FCMs and system devices are showing green, just FCM 13 is showing red',2,2,6,1641848124,1641848182),(387,1,1,0,399,399,1,266,0,280,'Users not working','Al wanted to verify the user info as he first stated that some users were not working.',0,1,6,1648041693,1648041760),(388,1,0,0,399,399,1,272,0,286,'Martin Gomez called to ask for his rights to be changed from tech to manager','Martin needed his rights change',0,1,6,1648041835,1648041865),(389,1,2,0,399,399,1,258,0,271,'RS485 buss is not stable','System has been working for awhile now without obvious issues even after they installed two new TMMs in a new building about 400 yards away from the initial installation but now the TMMs are randomly going offline then coming back on.',0,1,6,1649086268,1649878208),(390,1,5,0,399,399,1,8,0,0,'Tanks are have not been changing values as they should','A&E tech called and helped him troubleshoot the system and it looked like the TMM had failed.  He reported that the power light was flashing on and off.   Asked that since he is local to bring by to confirm TMM as good or bad.',0,1,6,1649700555,1649700965),(391,1,1,0,399,399,1,182,0,187,'System is acting very sluggish','Tim called and said that logging in takes about 30 seconds before the page will come up. Part department said that it take about a minute to switch pages after a dispense has been selected to start.',1,1,6,1649855351,1649879959),(392,1,3,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Clearwater Toyota has issue with Station 9 bays 5 and 6, 0W/16 reel not counting or stopping.','The FCM associated to station 9 has been a constant problem since installation.  They have worked on this station 4 times but no records have really been kept accurate detailing exactly what was done each of the 4 times and the customer can just say it has been worked on 4 times.  Two PSM came on RGA and one the pulser was bad but the other was just fine.  Assumption based just on this was that the first pulser was the first to be installed and was hooked up wrong, taking out the pulser which at the same time took out the port on the FCM that it was connected to.  Then it was not correctly confirmed that it was stopping correctly, assumption, so was assumed good until the techs started to use it and found that it was not stopping.  There is not one person can confirm it has ever worked.  One person says it worked for awhile and then failed before the next bit of work was done, others say it has never worked since installation.',0,1,6,1650395432,1652795802),(393,1,1,0,399,0,1,141,0,119,'Controller should not be updated','Discrepancy Title: Updated from R_23 to R_24 caused the system to quit working for some users.\nDiscrepancy info: System is running on bypass, so need to fix before Monday if possible. This location was updated to R_24 several months ago had similar issues. Bryan had remote in spent some time trying to resolve the issue however, was unable to finish so he had to revert back to R_23. That maybe the best thing to do now if you all are busy. Currently daily reports will not open, seems sluggish, some technicians work properly however, some can only log in/Load Work Order - \"reply\'s valid WO\"/ will not allow station to be selected even though all users have permission to select all stations. Note: If i login from Team Viewer as one of the technician no working (password 1896) the system appears to function normally. We tried logging PW 1896 from different computer at the location no change in symptom. Tried clearing browser cache no change. Suspect Bryan will know best coarse of action.\nComment : Can you confirm the following: 1. Do they remember the version they were on before they tried the update to R_24? Did they jump any updates? 2. Can you provide the login/names of the users that the system does not seem to be working correctly for? We would like this information so that we can see what the users are experiencing. 3. Can you provide a Admin and Manager password? 4. Do they only have one controller? Team viewer show just this one \"Cassens Dodge 2 - Neumyer\" 5. Do you remember the previous discrepancy number that was raised for the previous problem? Will try searching after posting this myself but just encase you know it off hand you can post. Bryan is currently unavailable at this time and am unsure what time today he will be free.',1,1,1,1651173847,0),(394,1,0,0,399,399,1,272,0,286,'0W/20 is not working at all station and PSM is leaking','Martin called and informed him the controller showed off line, so he rebooted and then accessed controller through TV.  The system was running out of disk space which was causing issues.  Removed all the files from the oilcop/aplication/logs directory and then change the setting in the following file to prevent the files from filling up the drive: oilcop/application/config/config.php file will have option $config[\'log_threshold\'] = 0; This should be 0 .',2,2,6,1652289868,1652289984),(395,1,1,0,399,399,1,150,0,0,'Bob from Quags called to ask if I could look at Reliable Chevrolet system','Logged into system and saw TMM offline as well as a TAC',0,1,6,1653686466,1653686618),(396,1,1,0,3,3,1,244,0,0,'System down all devices red','All devices communications was alternating from on line/ off line.\n Had Mark with Bob Penkhus move USB cable from front port to back port.\nThis appeared to resolve the issue',2,3,6,1655139904,1655139913),(397,1,1,0,399,399,1,258,0,0,'Controller is dead','Change out power supply and controller still does not power up, no fan, no network lights, no power button light.  This is at Michel\'s Truck Stop.',0,1,6,1656429261,1665146478),(398,1,5,0,399,399,1,245,0,0,'Tank not showing correct value','Ethan from C&A Equipment called to find out how to troubleshoot why the tank isn\'t showing the correct value after being filled.',0,1,6,1656511914,1656512076),(399,1,1,0,422,399,1,112,0,0,'Enhancement Gartec Email Servers, WO Search, TMM Invalid','This DR covers the development of a release to implement the changes to the new Gartec and Filcar email servers as well as implementing a basic search in the Job and Select WO screens of the Tech pages , change WO number Admin format option to allow for 20 characters instead of just 16 and finally include the change that when a TMM is offline the dashboard displays Invalid for the tasks associated to the offline TMM.',1,1,6,1657891943,1665146231),(400,8,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Add Feature to Inventory and restrict permission for Dist and Cust.','There needs to be a date/timestamp on the inventory screen showing that last time the system sync\'d with oilcopsupport.com so that the customers know when the data showing is valid from.  Also no distributer or customer should be allowed to assign Software Control permissions.',0,1,5,1659532162,0),(401,1,3,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'PSM is not showing count when dispensing','Walked Jeff through troubleshooting and found that reed switch failed.',2,2,6,1661288096,1661288152),(402,1,3,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'UDT-2 reel stopped counting FCM port 1','Jeff troubleshot and found fuse bad, order 10 replacements',2,2,6,1661288245,1662471827),(403,1,5,0,399,399,1,272,0,286,'5W/20 will not pump at all stations','5W/20 will not pump at any of the stations, all devices show green status and they can hear the pump activate when when they press the start on the dispense page.',2,2,6,1661363269,1666799001),(404,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Peacock Ford has 2404 open Work orders','I have pointed out to the parts depart this issue couple of times yet they continue to allow this to happen. Is there something we can do from admin to close and range of work orders numbers or any work orders after a defined date? \nCan you close all work orders from July 31 back to when the system was installed?',1,1,6,1661776446,1670858866),(405,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Leith Acura 1904 Open work orders','I have pointed out to the parts depart this issue couple of times yet they continue to allow this to happen. Is there something we can do from admin to close and range of work orders numbers or any work orders after a defined date?',1,1,6,1661776525,1670858952),(406,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Gahr Diesel - St James controller setup question','Dave, 818-458-6941, called to ask about how to get into the controller after installation.  Could not find any info on setting up the controller prior to sending. SO 140710 VID: 7642',0,1,6,1661796512,1670855169),(407,1,1,0,3,399,1,237,0,241,'Tank monitor quit reading','Tank values were not updating, all devices were on line.\nRebooted controller, appeared to resolve issue.\nUpdated to R36 while remoted into the system',0,1,6,1661872128,1662553289),(408,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Usage History Issue','There is an issue with Usage History that causes the loading of the dashboard to take a long time when there are a larger number of tanks with inventory data',0,1,6,1662041379,1670421624),(409,1,5,0,399,399,1,258,0,271,'All TMMs are showing offline','Currently all TMMs show offline in the completely wired system.  Issue have been progressively getting worse over the last few week ending in complete TMM failure for all tanks approximately 2 week ago.  Talked with Dave at EH Wolf on the troubleshooting steps to narrow down the problem(s) to get the system functional again.\n\nOnce the system if fully up and running, troubleshooting will begin on the tanks which have 20\' probes installed but are setup in the system as 10\' probes.  When set to 20\' probes the volume being reported is off, larger errors on smaller tanks, and they have to set unrealistic values for oil specific gravity to get them to read close to actual measured oil height.',2,3,6,1662579358,1710264540),(410,1,1,0,399,399,1,244,0,248,'Low Disk space error showed on screen','Running df -h command showed that the disk was at 100% used for sda1',1,1,6,1662755752,1663015545),(411,1,1,0,399,399,1,244,0,248,'CDM is not being found causing cronlog to grow in size and fill up hard drive.','Looked at this system last week due to limited disk space available.  Cronlog was over 6GB so deleted but disk still showed very high usage. All devices show offline due to CDM not being found.',1,2,6,1663010035,1663010064),(412,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Cannot connect to controller after reboot and Sensor is not working on 5W/30 Tank','Peacock Ford called to ask how to troubleshoot after rebooting the system they no longer could connect to it.  Mike said that he saw now lights on the network plug on the controller.  The network wire connected to the controller was hardwired under the counter so he could not easily switch to another port to see if the port was bad.  He said he would have IT get ahold of me.',2,3,6,1663011058,1668706836),(413,1,0,0,399,399,1,177,0,295,'System is not working correctly and they are overfilling tanks because of it.','Robert Troeller emailed me saying \"Mike, please look at oil cop at the Michels site in ostega MN They say it’s not working That they are over filling the tanks\"  I have never been able to connect to this site but ask Bob to contact the customer and have him reboot as the system shows online but never connects.  He just forwarded my email to tmcclish@michels.us so will wait for him to contact me.',0,1,6,1663015784,1668110533),(414,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Work Order Maintenance page load slow','Due to  the java invoice button the page loads slow that while on the controller you get a scripting error.  Leith Accura and Peacock Ford are controllers that have large amount of open WOs but only Leith Accura has an issues with the script error.  Testing by web team showed they both get errors.',1,1,6,1663069439,1664903200),(415,8,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Software Control needs its own permission assignment','Currently when you assign a user permissions to view the Software Updates they also get access to the Software control pages and shouldn\'t.  The Permissions pages needs to add a new option to assign Software Control to a user independently of the Software Updates view rights.',1,1,6,1663341962,1665431960),(416,1,1,0,3,399,1,288,0,299,'Accessing Controller very slow','Remoted in, R37, Only five open work orders.\nAccessing work order status took approximately 20 - 30 seconds.\nNeed mike to look under the hood',1,1,6,1664892214,1664894131),(417,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Need an Admin option to set Dashboard refresh frequency','For sites that have a large number of tanks it would be beneficial to have an Admin option to set the frequency of refresh so that the system is not trying to update every 2.5 seconds each tank.  Have this fast of refresh slows down the system during login since the dashboard is the first page loaded after login.',1,1,6,1664975196,1670421560),(418,1,1,0,399,399,1,288,0,0,'Andrew from Parks Chevy said their system was slow accessing workorders.','Andrew from Parks Chevy said their system was slow for workorders.  It was slow on accessing Work Order Maintenance at first but then is was normal.  Andrew also said just as the page came up he said it was working normally on his side again.  Didn\'t do anything so not sure what exactly happened.  Controller had been up for 21 days.',1,1,6,1665431814,1687351859),(419,1,2,0,3,399,1,289,0,300,'Tank monitor, station 8, 9, 11 intermittently going off line','Tank monitor, station 8, 9, 11 intermittently going off line.\nInstaller says he is going to lower the CDM because its located behind a large air handler duct.',2,2,6,1665597844,1666805374),(421,1,3,0,399,399,1,164,0,142,'Station 28 reel is always on','From email for Justin Barnes:  I have a technician that is having an issue with oil station 28 in oil cop. He is stating that his oil reel is always turned on and will not stop at the amount parts enters into oil cop. He also said that he can pump oil at any time regardless of if he is logged into oil cop.',2,1,6,1666038364,1668109389),(422,8,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Add no info message when Inventory doesn\'t have any data and TMM are invalid','Add no info message when Inventory doesn\'t have any data and TMM are invalid.  When a user changes to a different location it looks like the page is doing nothing but actually it doesn\'t have any data to display.  Now it just doesn\'t do anything on the page so we need the page to display a message stating that there is not current data available for the site selected.  \n\nWhen the sites TMMs are not working but it correctly sync with oilcop support.com there needs to be a way to notify the customer that the inventory displayed on the page may not be accurate.  One suggestion is to concatenate the word \"invalid\" to the value in the Days Remaining till empty column.  Also the code needs to be looked at to find out why this column is always blank.',0,1,6,1666187197,1681763024),(423,1,5,0,399,399,1,272,0,286,'Tank 5w/20 showing reorder level','Physically checked tank and it has over 200 gallons yet the dashboard is showing a tank level of only about 8.3 gallon which is preventing them from dispensing.  Technically they should still be able to dispense when re order alert is active but he also had the tank locked as he was trying to bypass the sensor.  Had him unlock the tank while I looked at the logs.',2,1,6,1666642532,1666642646),(424,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Add mac address along with location info to all emails and dashboard blue box fix','It is hard to know which controller is sending the emails so to make sure it is know which controller sent which email the mac address and location info from the Admin options page need to be included in the emails.  Subject line will have  Location info then mac address then report name.\n\nBody of email will have location info and mac address under the icon.',0,1,6,1666961362,1669999247),(425,1,1,0,399,399,1,112,0,0,'Job recipe won\'t start pumps for normal wo using reel does','Troubleshooting an issue with job recipes not successfully starting the pump but wo using the same reel/pump work successfully.  Controller was at R34 updated to R38 but issues with login screen constantly cycling so downgraded to R37 and get successful pump start with activating a job recipe.  Asked Andrea to confirm it is working correctly now.',0,1,6,1667390687,1669998798),(426,1,4,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'TAC does not transmit Technician info to controller','When using the TAC to dispense products, the TAC does not correctly transmit the technician info back to the controller.  This will require modification to the firmware of the TAC.  There may be a work around but will require that a python and C programmer be involved to help troubleshoot the issue to determine if there is any data in the packet that can be used to identify the user on the TAC from the controllers point of view when their info is in transmitted back when the work order is completed.',0,1,2,1667485823,0),(427,1,1,0,399,399,1,288,0,299,'Loading and saving WO\'s is extremely slow','Customer called and mentioned again after about 2 months that loading the WO page and the saving of WOs is taking a long time.  He confirmed he was getting good ping rates <1ms yet it was still slow.',1,1,6,1668539776,1668540073),(428,1,0,0,348,399,236,236,0,240,'Report issues','Reports did not generate and email today. In the past this did not rectify itself without your help.',1,1,6,1668693479,1668706895),(429,1,5,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'ADG Don Mealey Subaru TMM issues and 2 FCM not reading pulses','Troubleshot with John White 321-228-2029 John.White@autodevgroup.com on why the TMMs did not work when setup.',2,1,6,1668707630,1676557553),(430,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Pit Crew Aberdeen SD FCM not working','Customer called Jim Service manager, saying they have an FCM that wasn\'t working. System could not be found in TV.',2,2,6,1669064801,1669065143),(431,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Quags Mazda Albuquerque NM Controller go on and off line and can\'t connect with TV','Sent a replacement controller on RGA 111622-1MS suspecting that there may have been a typo in the network settings. Mike installed the new controller and the same issue happed, could not connect using TV and the system showed it online one minute and the next it was off.  Since this is a new building install asked that they get ahold of their IT department to TS and find out if they are blocking any ports.  Mike\'s number is 505.316.9720',0,1,6,1669145230,1686232164),(432,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Peacock Ford may require specific gravity calibration','They had a sensor replaced per Mike but can\'t find any of the paperwork for sensor issue and only ppw for a controller issue.  Confirmed the sensors are correctly reading but may not be accurately displaying the correct fluid levels and may require ADG to go and physically measure fluid levels and then adjust the specific gravity till the physical matches the calculated fluid height.',0,1,6,1669145439,1670854046),(433,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Victory Honda AME called about how to adjust low level shutoff','Tim Hill of AME 630-363-1986 called to ask us to contact Robert 734-546-7258 at Victory Honda Plymouth and explain to him how to change the low level shutoff on a tank so they could pump until a delivery could be made.',0,1,6,1669997269,1669997299),(434,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Dustin from ASE called concerning FCM and TMM Issue at Wausa','Dustin called and explained that when he called a couple of weeks ago about a TMM issue he was actually given the wrong site and that the site that he should have been given was the Wassau site to go and troubleshoot a TMM issue.',0,1,6,1669997468,1710264484),(435,1,0,0,399,399,1,77,0,0,'Corky called 316-807-2062 stating all stations were down','Frank gave permission to go over and help troubleshoot.  Found that all devices were offline including CDM. Found that the CDM usb cable had been unplugged from the controller and once connected all stations could dispense.  The only issues were that still there when I left were the REDs for one police station and one fire station never came online.  The discussion with the techs in those areas lead one to believe that they had issue with some water getting into them and they possibly shorted a long time ago but they never replaced them as they don\'t seem to rely on them and rely more on the preset feature of the oilcop system.\n\nTold Corky that should the techs, who were not there that use those stations with the inop REDs, say they don\'t work we will come back over and troubleshoot or get their distributor to troubleshoot.\n\nWill leave DR open for at least a week encase they call.',0,1,6,1669998255,1670854006),(436,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Victory Honda AME cannot access the controller','The controller is offline so can\'t access using TV.  AME doesn\'t know seem to have a tech that would have a mouse, keyboard, and monitor to go to the site to directly access the controller so called Robert back to see if he would be willing to install TV so that I can access his computer to run some test to see if I can determine whether or not it is a network issue or a controller issue.',0,1,6,1670247114,1670251541),(437,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Crown Volvo needed to know their controller IP address','Dave called 336.834.7349 called and said their computers were reimaged and lost their shortcuts to the controller',0,1,6,1670248667,1670248723),(438,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Victory Honda AME have reels which are \"free flowing\"','Don,  Victory is saying that their oil system is still free flowing on some stations and not 100%.  Can you confirm.\nTim Hill\nVice President\n1000 N. Opdyke Road Suite J - Auburn Hills, MI 48326\nO: 239-205-2222\nC: 630-363-1986',2,1,6,1670344213,1670853964),(439,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Leith Landrover needed firefox updated and controller','Found firfox running version 24 and should be 66, updated firefox and updated controller to R39 from',0,1,6,1670857609,1670857755),(440,1,1,0,399,399,1,245,0,0,'Leith Lincoln WO maint page loads slow.','Found that disk space at 47% which is good, but WO maintenance page loads slow, so change admin purge wo option so that not so many closed wo have to be loaded also found a large number of open WOs from 2019 and earlier.',0,1,6,1670858006,1670858585),(441,1,3,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Taylor BMW station 7 reel 2 0W/30 does not shutoff at preset value','Ray called from Universal Dist Group 9066305973 called to ask for help with a PSM they ordered for a replacement due to a reel not shutting off.  He gave me Shawn\'s number 704-560-0553 who is the tech at the site as he could not answer any questions about which station it was or what reel it was.  Called Shawn and walked him through troubleshooting and it was determined that FCM 4 port 2 was damaged during installation which is used for Station 7 reel 0w/30.',2,1,6,1671137364,1676559380),(442,1,3,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Parks Ford station 12 and 6 are intermittently failing.','Jeff Westendork, 813-765-3060 jasapequip@gmail.com, called from ASAP Equipment Repair at the request of the customer to see if they could help fixed their intermittent issues.  Parks Ford is not happy with ADG which is why they called ASAP.  ASAP is not familiar with our system but works with Sampson systems.',0,1,6,1671638749,1687351500),(443,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Peacock Ford called on Friday 12/23 saying they couldn\'t dispense','Called Mike this morning and he said that they rebooted everything and all worked afterwards.',0,1,6,1672149957,1676560127),(444,1,1,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'King\'s Cadillac accessing WO is slow','MySQL is consuming too many resources when loading the WO pages, including the dashboard.',0,1,6,1672176947,1676560222),(445,1,0,0,399,399,1,113,0,95,'Pantropic Power\'s system is completely down after lighting strike','Pantropic could not access their system after a lighting strike that took out power to their building.  They are sending back the original controller as well as a controller Jobbers has from another sears system.',0,1,6,1672947455,1681763520),(446,1,0,0,399,399,1,198,0,201,'Accura of Wichita controller has not power','Jeff 316.719.8171 called and said they could not cycle power to the controller, no green power light on the controller.',2,1,6,1673988183,1674229865),(447,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy said all techs were getting invalid ROs when loading','Received 2 calls from Tom from H&H Chevy 402-213-5480 called saying they were getting an invalid message when entering in RO#s from what I understood was the tech load work order screen.',0,1,6,1674227781,1674246288),(448,1,3,0,3,399,1,8,0,0,'DSD H-H Cheverolet Devices are RED at 6:15 AM Saturday','Logged in to check connectivity, found devices set to wireless 1,2,4,5,12,17,18,19,20,16,17,18,19,20,21,Range Extender-1,Range Extender-2 \"All Red\".  Hardwired device #12 set to wireless also is \"Red\"   All other devices are green\nWill Check later today see if Green. \nMaybe some of the power is shut off at night time.',2,2,6,1674303087,1676031662),(449,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy said they could not add another product to a RO','Mike called from H&H Chevy and said they couldn\'t add another product to a RO.  I checked and the system was not set for multi product.  Set multi product to On in Admin options.',0,1,6,1674488051,1674488057),(450,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Quality Mazda TAC Enter Key Failed','Mike called from Quags to say that one of the TAC enter keys has failed.',0,1,6,1674501278,1674501338),(451,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Reliable Chevy NM IT changed network setting making controller network settings invalid','Kevin 505-338-5848 called to say their IT dept changed the network setting and needed to know how to access the controller to change the network settings for the system.  He did not have admin passwords so gave him the pins from a 2021 backup file',0,1,6,1674663543,1675877818),(452,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'AME Zimmer Tractor Aurora called and said tank would not pump','Jeff from Zimmer Tractor called and said he was having issues with the UDT-2 tank pumping oil.  The FCM flash a blue LED quickly and then extinguish as if it had an unsuccessful pump start.',0,1,6,1675107211,1675107358),(453,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Quags Quality Mazda 0w/20 will not pump after installing new PSM','Had sent new PSM due to original leaking from under the PCB board, on RGA# 011323-1MS and after replacement Mike called to say it was not counting pulses.',0,1,6,1675705972,1710264150),(454,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Mike from Peacock Ford said their system isn\'t working','Mike explained that they lost their internet but assume it was their intranet they lost as OilCop would still work if it didn\'t have access to the internet.  They said they reset the controller a couple of times but still didn\'t work so they called.  Suspect they didn\'t wait long enough for all the devices to come back online before trying.',0,1,6,1675784736,1676560387),(455,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Recon called about a tech getting pump unsuccessful when trying to dispense','Tim called from H&H Recon asking for help as to why a tech was having issue pumping.  After confirming the techs rights and assignments it I found out that he was getting the pump unsuccessful message.',0,1,6,1676054232,1676054447),(456,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Scott Robinson could not access system, had error message about t_workorder_details being full','This is an indication of the disk being full as there is no limit to the number of records that can be stored in the db.',2,3,6,1676059805,1676059979),(457,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Bob Penkhus Mazda system has been offline for about 3 weeks','Steve from Colorado Petroleum called after finding out while there to check on some leaks that the OilCop system has been down for about 3 weeks.',0,3,6,1676479224,1681763682),(458,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Jeff from H&H Chevy asked about reports showing deliveries','Jeff called, cell 402-953-7350, asking about where he could find the reports that show the delivery of oil.  Explained to him that they are in the Tank Adjustments report as well as they should show up on the Daily report for that day.  Due to Daily reports lacking the feature to view past reports he would have to look for the email for the delivery dates Daily report.',0,1,6,1677162102,1681763732),(459,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Mullinax Ford couldn\'t get their Work Orders to load','This is similar to what used to only happen Parks Chevy but now have had 3 more customers have the same issues where a reboot is not fixing an issue with MySQL is consuming too many resources and always requires me to issue the command \"sudo service mysql restart\" and then the problem is fixed for about a month or so.',0,1,6,1677254958,1681763836),(460,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Mike H&H Chevy said Station 3 5w/30 reel is not counting.','Mike said that according to the tech it was counting up until today, 7mar23.',2,1,6,1678305876,1679584201),(461,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Cumberland Station 5 5w Trans reel doesn\'t count','Robert 239-848-5934 called and explained that the station 5 syn trans reel was not counting allowing them to overfill.',2,1,6,1678482774,1683288564),(462,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Cumberland called said they couldn\'t pump any fluids','No station would pump the fluids for work orders after pressing start on the dispense screen.',0,1,6,1678817178,1682362772),(463,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Tri State Truck called to say they could not pump fluids from any stations','Forrest Ownes, 417.818.2014 called and explained that he did not have any logins for the system and they could not pump any fluids.',2,3,6,1678894090,1679079822),(464,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Lithia Dodge Santa Fe cannot access their controller','Kayla called, 505.573.0106 saying that they cannot access the OilCop system from their computers.',0,1,6,1679675391,1681764059),(465,1,0,0,399,3,1,0,0,0,'DitchWitch Davenport called to say they couldn\'t pump oil due to low level','Dashboard showed low level but there was 29\" of oil in the tanks.',0,1,6,1680212044,1682082175),(466,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Ocean Honda FL called about a leak','Certified Hydraulic 3869353494, Susie called about a leak but provided a picture of the piping.  She also said they reported their system was inop.',0,1,6,1680547268,1681764394),(467,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Porche Monmouth NJ called and said they could not access their system','Arin called 732-483-8563 and told him that I see that their system was showing offline so asked if he could locate the controller and power cycle it.',0,1,6,1681136662,1681148180),(468,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Fix MP per Andrea description of correct functionality','MP functionality using a TAC works correctly so will fix the web code to match same functionality.',0,1,1,1682509867,0),(469,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy called and said a few stations are not showing the count during dispensing','Tested at station 1 as the tech said it happens every time now but it did work in the beginning.  Stations 15 and 16 also say they have had issues with the display not showing a count while dispensing.  The displays not showing the count have caused some overfills.',0,1,6,1683316829,1684267935),(470,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy Used Coolant tank is spilling out onto the floor.','Tom from H&H called, 402-213-5480 and said that their used coolant tank was over spilling with what seemed like oil, not coolant.   They were thinking that maybe the oil delivery person accidently put new oil in the wrong tank.',0,1,6,1683827906,1710262466),(471,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Quality Mazda East Shop TAC gives error','Mike from Quag\'s called and said that he got a call saying that the TAC in the east shop was giving an error but didn\'t say which one.',0,1,6,1684268003,1684270413),(472,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Gahr Truck from St James MO called and said they could not access controller','Dale, 573.265.5110 called and explained that they could not access the controller when they came in today even though they rebooted the system.',2,3,6,1684944801,1687350889),(473,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Kearney Fleet Yant has issues using TAC, an erratic PSM count and Oil tank reading HL always','Dustin from P&G Marketing  785-764-0604, went to Kearney City to trouble shoot the issues of a PSM used for coolant that was erratically counting, a waste oil tank that was reading high level even though there was very little oil in it and why the TAC was giving everyone a 255 error after they logged in.',0,1,6,1685478424,1687349151),(474,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'EH Wolf Green Bay needs help deleting tanks and products','Dave from EH Wolf called, 262-224-2139 and said they had ordered another controller for the other building since they couldn\'t get the RS485 to work after running a wire to the new building.  He said that he was deleting tanks and products from the original system but was only able to delete one and they it stopped allowing him to delete any more.',0,1,6,1688138169,1710264120),(475,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'ATC Ottsen Oil cannot access their controller','Mark from Ottsen Oil, 319-560-5941, called for help troubleshooting system',0,1,6,1688760173,1710262424),(476,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy called to say station 3 was not showing dispense values','Station 3 would dispense but not show how much was being dispense nor shutoff at preset value.',0,1,6,1689188531,1689189173),(477,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'ASE Wausau was having issues with Dashboard showing invalid','Brad, 715-571-5294 called to explain their issues.',0,1,6,1689189230,1689189449),(478,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Bob Penkhas Volvo can\'t get pumps to start','Mark called 719-271-6062 to say that they system would show successful pump start and then it should change to unsuccessful pump start.',0,1,6,1689356917,1689357150),(479,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy station 17 msg failed to start pump but tech could still pump','Mike called and said 5W/30 would show unsuccessful pump start but allow the tech to dispense but not show the tech how much was dispensing so would not stop at preset value.',0,1,2,1689609436,0),(480,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Matt at H&H Recon has an intermittent issue with station 6 5w/20 reel not turning on','Matt a maintenance tech for all of H&H facilities called and explained that he was asked to follow up on an issues with station 6 5w/20 reel giving an unsuccessful pump start.',1,1,1,1693408381,0),(481,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Honda Carland had issues with TMM','Tech from distributor called and asked for suggestions on where to begin troubleshooting the oilcop system due to Honda Carland overfilling a tank during delivery.',0,1,6,1693409023,1693409032),(482,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'King Cadillac cannot access the oilcop system.','Tim Shots called from King Cadillac explaining a strange page was keeping them from accessing the oilcop login page when they would put in the ip address.  Came up with some SureVue/api/v1/login page asking for credentials.',0,1,6,1693409150,1710260664),(483,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy called with an issue of their used oil tank showing zero','Tom 402-213-8480 called to explain the issue.  The tank was correctly as far as he knew before.  Saw in the logs that the tank was apparently emptied on 8/31 as it showed a subtraction of 582.8 gallons.  I also noticed that the Used Oil Station #2 device kept going on and offline intermittently.  This could be the result that the tank wiring was not modified so they were correctly wired in series when the FCMs were rewired in series.\n\nMay need to send a tech up there to troubleshoot the issue if Tom does not find anything obvious as I suggested to check to make sure the sensor was fully in the tank.  Unsure if there is a possibility that the sensor could be damaged when they empty the tank.  Waiting on Tom to get back to me on what he finds.',2,2,6,1693930821,1710260627),(484,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Cumberland is showing many stations offline','Kayla from Cumberland called to say they could not pump.  Logging in found that stations 1-9 were showing offline.  System is completely wired, TMM and FCMs.  She could not troubleshoot so had here call AME to find out when they could send someone there to troubleshoot.',2,2,6,1693940626,1693941130),(485,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'United BMW called with an issue of the TAC saying a WO is closed when they try and dispense','Justin Barnes, 404-451-6783 called and explained that for about the last 4 months their oilbars have been giving them issues where they use the TAC to dispense fluid from the oilbars but when they select Start the system gives an error that the WO is already closed.',0,1,6,1695300956,1723745457),(486,1,1,0,348,399,236,236,0,240,'No connection to the controller can be made','We have no connection to the controller, we have no network issues, I have replaced the CAT 5 cable with a brand new one and restarted the unit twice, it was off when i was alerted of the issue.   402-570-0383 Mat Steadman',2,3,6,1695740298,1710260549),(487,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Parks Ford WO creation immediately shows dispense values even though nothing been dispensed','When a manager creates a WO and sets the preset the system and then saves, the system immediately shows that the product has been dispensed but keeps the WO open.',0,1,6,1703872694,1710257131),(488,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'BMW Bloomfield MI tanks reading zero after filling up','Tank sensors for tanks 0w/20 and 0w/30 show contents as being zero even though they were just filled up.',0,2,6,1708711717,1708711977),(489,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Clearwater Toyota stated the station 15 over dispenses from preset','No access to system so must coordinate with IT Chris Killion 727-421-7180',0,1,6,1709816446,1723745338),(490,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Ocean Honda overfilled their used oil tank.','Used oil tank overfilled without setting off the alarm.  Cannot access the controller even though it shows online.  Site needs to reboot to see if that fixes the connection issue.',0,1,6,1709817584,1723745274),(491,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy station 3 and 28 were not showing dispense info on screen after successful pump start','Station 3 is consistently not showing dispense values while dispensing.  Station 28 is intermittent.',0,1,6,1710506082,1711389743),(492,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Gahr truck could get successful pump messages after rebooting.','They rebooted 3 time but could not get successful start pump messages.  Could not connect with TV until killing TV and restarting, then connected.',0,1,6,1710506237,1710506344),(493,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy showing intermittent CDM failures','Station wouldn\'t start pumps',0,1,6,1712758373,1723745177),(494,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'BMW Bloomfield per Mark M said oilbars 4, 5 and 6 intermittently will show successful pump starts','oilbars 4, 5 and 6 intermittently will show successful pump starts',0,1,6,1712779956,1723745103),(495,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Zimmer Tractor at Monroe has wrong power supplies connected to controllers','Jeff from Zimmer Tractor called, 513-340-0189, and said it looked like the power supply was bad for the controller.  After they send me a pic it was realized that the installers put the controller power supplies on the FCMs and the FCM power supplies on the controllers which are not rated high enough in amps to work correctly to charge the UPS packs.  The pack may have been damaged but he only wanted to order new power supplies for all 3 of their sites.',2,3,6,1715705215,1715705257),(496,1,0,0,399,0,1,112,0,0,'Issue with MP showing ALL tech, prod, stations','WO are not raised by the TACs and there are none listed in the hardware configuration, tech use web pages and so don\'t set All Tech, Prods, Stations.  Controller is on R39. This is customer\'s mac e4:3a:6e:48:b2:7b',0,1,1,1719506220,0),(497,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Pantropic Power can\'t dispense, all devices showing red','CDM is not showing that it has power, no power light, causing all other devices to show offline.',2,3,6,1721056479,1739800345),(498,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'United BMW cannot access WO management','Justin called to say that all of a sudden they could not longer access the WO management page.  Was working just fine the day before and noticed that things were slow today.',0,1,6,1723752940,1741799880),(499,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Quags called that Reliable Chevy was having an issues','Bob said they called Saturday about 4pm to report an issue but he didn\'t get back with them.  He asked us to see if we could log in',2,3,6,1724079200,1725378944),(500,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Cumberland FCM 5 and 6 do not have power lights showing on the FCMs','Danny from ADG called and said station 5 and 6 were not giving successful pump starts.',2,2,6,1725382294,1725382659),(501,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Quags Quality Mazda TAC giving 255 error','Add devices are showing green, TAC was working fine over an hour ago but now it gives a 255 error.  Logs show that it completes checking the pin but doesn\'t log anything else after that.',0,2,6,1734387453,1742403609),(502,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Pantropic system will dispense oil but is short','The system seems to be sending a converted value to t_server_transciever table for the preset amount.  if 5 G is set web page only sends 2.8 G.',0,1,1,1734387559,0),(503,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Gartec ARA 1965 users in t_dispense table are all the same user.','System seems to be working just fine but after a dispense has been made the system will update all the user ids in the t_dispense table to the same user.  R46',0,1,1,1734387637,0),(504,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Bloomfield BMW on reboot CDM failed to communicate','When rebooting the system after updating the system failed to come up correctly even after multiple reboots.',2,3,2,1741799979,0),(505,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Ocean Honda station 2 and 12 are inop, after reboot complete system failure','The customer called a tech to the location to figure out what was wrong with Station 2 and Stations 12 as they both showed offline.  After a reboot the system was completely inop.',2,3,2,1741800430,0),(506,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'ATC Ottsen Oil site 15w40 would not show count or stop at preset','Payton from the ATC site called and ask troubleshooting the system',2,2,2,1741800761,0),(507,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'PrairieLand John Deere system is inop','Carl Hill 785-313-5207 called and said they system was not functioning.  He said that the TMM board had a burnt spot on the label.',2,3,6,1741992293,1745497759),(508,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Cassen Dodge needs there database reset','Cassen Dodge uses repair order number that will repeat after 99999 so every time they reach this number they need their DB reset.',1,1,2,1743528843,0),(509,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy called with complete system failure','Tom called and said nothing was working but was working fine earlier.',0,1,6,1744983546,1744983837),(510,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Fed Coop P&G having issues with a job product','Dustin called and said that all went well yesterday but today when the customer started immediately having issues with the 15w20 product on the defined job 222.',0,1,2,1745496372,0),(511,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Peacock Ford getting Check FCM status message when trying to start pumps','Mike stated they were getting the message when trying to start a dispense at station 10.',0,1,6,1746461777,1747139465),(512,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Lithia Dodge of Santa Fe called asking who could come and recalibrate their system','I walked Jacob Roybal 505-428-5670 some features of the OilCop system as he was the new part manager.  I also sent him the user and installation manuals.',0,1,1,1746666280,0),(513,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Lust Chevy, Pit Crew Row, had issues with TAC','Jim deleted techs that were no longer working there and put in new techs and they started having issues with the TAC showing an error of not stations assigned',0,1,2,1748903110,0),(514,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Porsche Monmouth NJ work order maintenance screen is crashing','When they would go to the Work order maintenance screen the system would crash trying to load 70+ pages of work orders.',1,2,2,1748959703,0),(515,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Autoklass Constanta has a db issue','Matteo emailed a screenshot showing that the system could not find a table',0,1,1,1749660040,0),(516,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Filcar controller 00:e0:b4:54:fa:79 wants the system to work for their workflow','The customer builds earth movers and is using the system at 4 stations which they create WO for each vehicle they build and keep track of the fluids dispensed into the vehicle as it moves down the assembly line to ensure that all products and levels have been put in the vehicle.',0,1,1,1749660884,0),(517,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Cumberland can\'t log into the OilCop system','Nick from Cumberland 407.849.6440 called and explained that they could not log into the system.',0,1,6,1750094112,1750094307),(518,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'United BMW Tech Transaction Journal','Updated United BMW system with files to test the tech transaction journal report that they asked for.',0,1,1,1750097331,0),(519,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Lithia Dodge of Santa Fe called stating that they could not dispense','Message from Jacob said that all devices were green but they could not dispense any fluids.',0,1,6,1750364473,1750364672),(520,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Perfection Honda station 6 won\'t pump','Mike called to confirm that station 6 would pump through reel calibration.  Told him I was showing offline so he would need to troubleshoot.',0,1,6,1750765739,1752768467),(521,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'EH Wolf #5531 Green bay 00:e0:4c:28:eb:22 is not online and cannot be accessed','Received an email from Mandi Frisque: The computer in the bulk room that OilCop is used on starting having issues on 6/24.  They’ve always had the website bookmarked, but now when they try to go to it – it takes a really long time to try to load and then they get the attached message.\n \nOriginally thought this might have been a proxy/firewall issue, so worked with our IT first to see if it was something on our end.  They said there had not been any firewall updates and had me try multiple things.  They showed that the OilCop device had been online for 42 days even though we had turned off the OilCop device and restarted it several times.  After unplugging the port from the switch it’s plugged into they finally showed it offline.  However, now everything is plugged back in and the OilCop box and computer are back on, and we have been unable to get the device to show back online for IT.  So, they are thinking it’s something with the device/OilCop box.\n \nAny help with troubleshooting and getting this back online and up and running?  We’ve been unable to use for almost a week.',0,1,1,1751634807,0),(522,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Heritage Tractor MO cannot access system','Jordon called and explain they were seeing a database error page when they tried to access the system.  The error message did not provide any table information.',0,1,2,1751634989,0),(523,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'Ocean Honda FL can\'t pump 0w/20','Ashley from Certified Hydraulics called to ask if I would be available to help a tech out at Ocean Honda tomorrow.  They said they could not pump 0w/20 from any station.  She mentioned that they ran their system to low level shutoff but after they filled it, it still was not working.',0,1,6,1752615768,1752778719),(524,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Perfection Honda Quags TMM and FCM wired devices are offline','Bob didn\'t have much information concerning the issue.  Mentioned that they have had to reboot weekly on Mondays.',0,1,1,1753115022,0),(525,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Kia Station Julio/Eric 0w/20 isn\'t counting pulses, other products work as designed','H&H Kia Station Julio/Eric 0w/20 isn\'t counting pulses, other products work as designed',0,1,6,1753219934,1753375989),(526,1,0,0,399,399,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy called to say system just stopped working','Tom said it just stopped working but was working just fine.',0,1,6,1753453645,1755537578),(527,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Honda Express in IN is having issues with their used oil and coolant','Paul 317.975.6261 called a couple of weeks back asking about the invalid message on the dashboard for the tanks, used oil and coolant. He called again today with the same issue and mentioned that on the weekend the alarm went off so must have started working.  He also commented on the fact the horn is broken off and the circuit board is exposed and looks like there is a burnt spot on it.  He is sending pictures.',0,1,1,1753814714,0),(528,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Holler Ford, previously Peacock Ford shows New Oil TMM offline','Ken, an Holler IT, called 407.509.5710 to explain the techs could not pump.',2,2,1,1754515839,0),(529,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Greenbay 1 controller failed','Dave tried to connect a keyboard and monitor to the controller but the video was all scrambled.',2,3,1,1755199630,0),(530,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'H&H Kia showing invalid tanks on dashboard','Daniel called 402.517.7484 called and wanted to know what invalid meant on the dashboards for the tanks.',0,1,1,1755537533,0),(531,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'H&H Chevy called stating that station 3 was not counting','Mike called and left a message that station 3 was not counting.',0,1,1,1755538508,0),(532,1,0,0,399,0,1,0,0,0,'Gartec site Earth Movers has custom site software','Earth movers wanted the wo process from the web the old way',0,1,1,1755544639,0),(533,1,1,0,3,0,1,206,0,209,'Yokomuro Kia System will not turn on pumps','System is having memory/data base issues. Takes awhile for system to respond to action & transaction journals however when trying to access work order status web page continually cycles, have been waiting 5 minutes continues to cycle. left screen up to see if it eventually comes up.  Everything else with the system seems to work properly can observe tank values are updating properly.',0,1,1,1756144082,0),(534,1,1,0,348,0,236,236,0,240,'NMC Omaha Workorder maintenance','The work order maintenance file seems to be corrupted?  There are closed work orders listed that are marked complete and years past the 35 day limit set.  This was not like this a couple weeks ago. I go close work orders when the list gets to 4-5 pages its 10 today and they are old.',1,1,1,1756153040,0);
